window.ZGCLAB_DETAILS["news-6"]=[{"id":"news-3199","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"布里特在听证会上赞扬红石兵工厂并询问卡什·帕特尔的FBI计划","title_en":"Britt touts Redstone Arsenal, asks Kash Patel his plans for FBI in hearing - Alabama Daily News","summary_cn":"在参议院司法委员会听证会上，阿拉巴马州共和党参议员凯蒂·布里特赞扬了FBI位于亨茨维尔红石兵工厂的园区，并询问FBI局长提名人卡什·帕特尔的管理计划。帕特尔表示将“让好警察做警察”并“恢复对FBI的信任”，承诺访问红石兵工厂并保持高标准培训。听证会上民主党人就帕特尔过往言论提出尖锐质询，委员会尚未安排投票。","summary_en":"At a Senate Judiciary Committee hearing, Sen. Katie Britt, R-Ala., praised the FBI's campus at Redstone Arsenal in Huntsville and asked FBI director nominee Kash Patel about his plans for the bureau. Patel said his themes would be to 'let good cops be cops' and 'restore the trust in the FBI,' committing to visit Redstone Arsenal and maintain high training standards. Democrats sharply questioned Patel over past comments. No committee vote has been scheduled.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:28:30.891108+00:00","url":"https://aldailynews.com/britt-touts-redstone-arsenal-asks-kash-patel-his-plans-for-fbi-in-hearing","content":"Britt touts Redstone Arsenal, asks Kash Patel his plans for FBI in hearing\nJanuary 31, 2025 •\nNews,\nBy Alex Angle\nWASHINGTON – Sen. Katie Britt, R-Ala., highlighted the FBI’s campus at Redstone Arsenal in Huntsville and applauded director nominee Kash Patel’s vision for the bureau during a hearing Thursday.\nBritt started off her time during the Senate Judiciary Committee hearing explaining a plethora of positive statements she heard from Patel on how he would tackle the FBI director role throughout the other senators’ questioning.\n“You said our law enforcement officers deserve the very best,” Britt said. “You said you know and you will not allow there to be victims of government overreach because it has happened to you.”\nPatel is a lawyer who worked at the Department of Justice and in other national security jobs. He is a fierce Trump ally. He also had what critics call an ‘enemies list’ of now former government officials to target in his 2023 book. Patel called that list a “mischaracterization” during the hearing.\nMuch of the Democrats questioning before Britt’s time focused on his past comments on retribution, praising Jan. 6, 2021 rioters and his comments that he would go after journalists.\nBritt asked Patel to describe his plans for making America safe.\nPatel said his two themes for managing the FBI would be to “let good cops be cops” and to “restore the trust in the FBI.”\nThe senator used her second round of questions to focus on the FBI’s presence in Huntsville and the more than 2,000 FBI employees who work at the Redstone Arsenal campus.\n“There has been over $4 billion invested there,” Britt said. “It is truly remarkable the training that is going on there.”\nPatel told Britt he is committed to visiting those facilities in Huntsville.\n“This is a great example… of the FBI’s capabilities and infrastructure systems around the country that already exist to the tune of billions,” Patel said.\nBritt also said she wanted to ensure the funding for training remained a high priority for the FBI. Patel said he would commit to high standards at the agency.\nPatel’s exchanges with Democrats on the committee got contentious.\nSen. Mazie Hirono, D-HI, grilled Patel on whether he would go after former federal government officials, such as former FBI Director Christopher Wray.\nPatel would only say that he had “no plans in going backwards.”\nHirono pressed Patel on whether Donald Trump lost the 2020 election and he said, “President Biden’s election was certified.”\nPatel did distance himself from Trump’s pardons of Jan. 6 rioters when he told Sen. Dick Durbin, D-IL, he did not “agree with the commutation of any sentence of any individual who committed violence against law enforcement.”\nA committee vote for Patel has not been scheduled yet. After the committee votes, his nomination will go to the full Senate.","content_cn":"布里特大力宣传红石兵工厂，并在听证会上询问卡什·帕特尔对联邦调查局的计划\n2025年1月31日 •\n新闻，\n作者：亚历克斯·安格尔\n华盛顿——周四的听证会上，阿拉巴马州共和党参议员凯蒂·布里特介绍了位于亨茨维尔的红石兵工厂联邦调查局园区，并称赞了局长提名人卡什·帕特尔对该机构的愿景。\n在参议院司法委员会听证会期间，布里特首先说明，在其他参议员提问期间，她听到了帕特尔关于如何履行联邦调查局局长职责的大量积极表态。\n布里特说：“你说过，我们的执法人员应得到最好的待遇。你说过，你知道政府越权会造成受害者，而且这种事曾经发生在你身上。”\n帕特尔是一名律师，曾在司法部及其他国家安全岗位工作。他是特朗普的坚定盟友。他在2023年出版的书中还列出了一份现已离任的政府官员名单，批评者称其为“敌人名单”，用于针对这些人。帕特尔在听证会上称该名单是“曲解”。\n在布里特发言之前，民主党议员的大部分提问集中于他过去关于报复的言论、对2021年1月6日骚乱者的赞扬，以及他曾表示将追查记者的言论。\n布里特要求帕特尔说明他让美国更安全的计划。\n帕特尔说，他管理联邦调查局的两个主题将是“让优秀警察做好警察的工作”和“恢复公众对联邦调查局的信任”。\n这位参议员在第二轮提问中重点关注联邦调查局在亨茨维尔的存在，以及在红石兵工厂园区工作的2000多名联邦调查局员工。\n布里特说：“那里已经投入了超过40亿美元。那里正在进行的培训确实令人瞩目。”\n帕特尔告诉布里特，他承诺会访问亨茨维尔的这些设施。\n帕特尔说：“这是一个很好的例子……说明联邦调查局在全国各地已经拥有价值数十亿美元的能力和基础设施系统。”\n布里特还表示，她希望确保培训经费继续成为联邦调查局的高度优先事项。帕特尔说，他会承诺在该机构保持高标准。\n帕特尔与委员会民主党议员的交锋变得剑拔弩张。\n夏威夷州民主党参议员马齐·希罗诺盘问帕特尔，问他是否会追查前联邦政府官员，例如前联邦调查局局长克里斯托弗·雷。\n帕特尔只表示，他“没有倒退追查的计划”。\n希罗诺追问帕特尔唐纳德·特朗普是否输掉了2020年大选，他回答：“拜登总统的当选已经得到认证。”\n当伊利诺伊州民主党参议员迪克·德宾询问时，帕特尔表示，他并不“赞同对任何实施暴力侵害执法人员行为的个人减刑”，从而与特朗普对1月6日骚乱者的赦免拉开了距离。\n委员会尚未安排对帕特尔进行表决。委员会投票后，他的提名将提交全体参议院。","publish_source":"aldailynews.com","publish_time":"2025-01-31T13:10:37+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3139","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"布里特和图伯维尔敦促卡什·帕特尔填补红石兵工厂FBI职位","title_en":"Britt, Tuberville push for Kash Patel to fill FBI jobs at Redstone Arsenal - Alabama Daily News","summary_cn":"美国参议员凯蒂·布里特和汤米·图伯维尔致信新确认的FBI局长卡什·帕特尔，敦促其填补红石兵工厂约4000个空缺职位中的1000个。该园区占地38000英亩，目前有2000多名FBI员工。参议员们强调北园区可提供网络威胁和新兴技术培训，南园区正在建设中。帕特尔在确认听证会上承诺访问该园区并填补空缺。","summary_en":"U.S. Sens. Katie Britt and Tommy Tuberville sent a letter to newly confirmed FBI Director Kash Patel urging him to fill 1,000 of about 4,000 open FBI positions at Redstone Arsenal. The 38,000-acre campus currently employs more than 2,000 people. The senators highlighted the North Campus's state-of-the-art training for cyber threats and emerging technologies, and the South Campus under construction. Patel committed during his confirmation hearing to visiting the campus and filling the slots.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:25:12.706053+00:00","url":"https://aldailynews.com/britt-tuberville-push-for-kash-patel-to-fill-fbi-jobs-at-redstone-arsenal","content":"Britt, Tuberville push for Kash Patel to fill FBI jobs at Redstone Arsenal\nFebruary 21, 2025 •\nNews,\nBy Alex Angle\nWASHINGTON – U.S. Sens. Katie Britt and Tommy Tuberville, R-Ala., are urging newly confirmed FBI Director Kash Patel to fill 1,000 open FBI slots at Redstone Arsenal.\nBritt and Tuberville wasted no time making their request to Patel, who was confirmed Thursday afternoon. The Senate vote was 51-49. Republican Sens. Susan Collins, R-ME, and Lisa Murkowski, R-AK, joined Democrats to vote no on his confirmation.\nAlabama’s senators sent a letter to Patel Thursday asking him to fill 1,000 of about 4,000 open slots at the 38,000-acre campus in Huntsville. More than 2,000 people currently work at the FBI facilities at Redstone.\n“As threats to our nation become more sophisticated, FBI-Redstone Arsenal’s operations will need to continue growing,” Britt and Tuberville wrote.\nThe senators highlighted the FBI’s North Campus at Redstone as ready to support the openings with “state-of-the-art training to address cyber threats, emerging technologies, and the Field Offices’ investigative efforts.”\nBritt and Tuberville also mentioned the South Campus, which is under construction, as a place that will allow the FBI’s presence to grow.\n“This will send a message to our adversaries that the FBI’s leadership is back to prioritizing the pressing threats to our homeland,” the senators wrote.\nBritt and Tuberville have shown strong support for Patel who will now lead the law enforcement agency.\n“At the helm of the FBI, Director Patel will return the agency’s focus to protecting the American people from terrorists, hostile foreign actors, and violent criminals,” Britt said in a statement.\nTuberville congratulated Patel in a post on X, saying he will “clean up the FBI and ensure our government works for the PEOPLE again.”\nPatel previously worked at the Department of Justice and in other national security roles. He is a loyal Trump ally. He also had what critics call an ‘enemies list’ of now former government officials to target in his 2023 book. Patel called that list a “mischaracterization” during his confirmation hearing.\nBritt applauded the FBI’s work at Redstone Arsenal during Patel’s confirmation hearing in the Judiciary Committee last month. Patel committed to visiting the campus and filling the open slots.\n“And this is a great example, real quick, of the FBI’s capabilities and infrastructure systems around the country that already exist to the tune of billions,” Patel said. “And not only is it, I believe, a 38,000-acre sprawling campus  (…) but 4,000 seats still remain open. So, let’s go to work. I’ll come to Alabama. Let’s fill those seats.”\nPatel is set to serve a 10-year term. Former FBI Director Christopher Wray stepped down before Trump returned to office after he served in the role for seven years.","content_cn":"Britt、Tuberville 敦促 Kash Patel 填补红石兵工厂的 FBI 职位空缺\n2025年2月21日 •\n新闻，\n作者：Alex Angle\n华盛顿——美国联邦参议员 Katie Britt 和 Tommy Tuberville（阿拉巴马州共和党）敦促新近获确认的联邦调查局局长 Kash Patel 填补红石兵工厂 FBI 的1,000个空缺职位。\n\nBritt 和 Tuberville 在 Patel 于周四下午获确认后立即向其提出请求。参议院表决结果为51票对49票。共和党参议员 Susan Collins（缅因州共和党）和 Lisa Murkowski（阿拉斯加州共和党）与民主党人一道投票反对确认其任命。\n\n阿拉巴马州两位参议员周四致信 Patel，请求他填补亨茨维尔这座占地38,000英亩园区约4,000个空缺岗位中的1,000个。目前有超过2,000人在红石的 FBI 设施工作。\n\n“随着对我们国家的威胁变得更加复杂，FBI—红石兵工厂的运营将需要继续扩大，”Britt 和 Tuberville 写道。\n\n两位参议员强调，红石的 FBI 北校区已准备好通过“最先进的培训来应对网络威胁、新兴技术以及外勤办公室的调查工作”，以支持这些职位空缺的填补。\n\nBritt 和 Tuberville 还提到正在建设中的南校区，称其将使 FBI 的驻点得以扩大。\n\n“这将向我们的对手传递一个信息：FBI 的领导层重新把重点放在了对我们国土的紧迫威胁上，”两位参议员写道。\n\nBritt 和 Tuberville 一直强力支持 Patel，如今他将领导这一执法机构。\n\n“在 FBI 的领导岗位上，Patel 局长将使该机构重新聚焦于保护美国人民免受恐怖分子、敌对外国行为者和暴力犯罪分子的伤害，”Britt 在一份声明中说。\n\nTuberville 在 X 上的一篇帖子中祝贺 Patel，称他将“整顿 FBI，并确保我们的政府再次为人民服务。”\n\nPatel 此前曾在司法部工作，并担任过其他国家安全职务。他是特朗普的忠实盟友。他在2023年的著作中还列出了一份批评者所谓、针对现已离任政府官员的“敌人名单”。Patel 在其确认听证会上称该名单是“错误描述”。\n\n在上个月司法委员会举行的 Patel 确认听证会上，Britt 称赞了 FBI 在红石兵工厂的工作。Patel 承诺访问该园区并填补空缺职位。\n\n“这很快就是一个很好的例子，说明 FBI 在全国范围内已有的、价值数十亿美元的能力和基础设施系统，”Patel 说。“而且我相信，这不仅是一个占地38,000英亩、规模庞大的园区（……），还有4,000个席位仍然空缺。所以，让我们开始工作吧。我会去阿拉巴马州。让我们填满这些席位。”\n\nPatel 将任职10年。前 FBI 局长 Christopher Wray 在特朗普重返白宫前辞职，当时他已担任该职务7年。","publish_source":"aldailynews.com","publish_time":"2025-02-21T13:52:42+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1629","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"民主党称白宫关于ICE的提议“不充分”，国土安全部资金即将到期","title_en":"Democrats say White House offer on ICE is 'insufficient' as Homeland Security funding set to expire - Alabama Daily News","summary_cn":"民主党领导人称白宫提出的方案“不完整且不充分”，他们要求对特朗普的移民执法施加新限制，并威胁让国土安全部停摆。参议院民主党领袖舒默和众议院民主党领袖杰弗里斯表示，白宫的反提案既无细节也无立法文本，未回应美国人对ICE“无法无天行为”的担忧。民主党要求司法搜查令、警员身份标识、使用武力标准及停止种族定性。","summary_en":"Democratic leaders say a White House proposal is 'incomplete and insufficient' as they demand new restrictions on President Trump's immigration crackdown and threaten a Homeland Security Department shutdown. Senate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer and House Democratic leader Hakeem Jeffries said the White House counterproposal 'included neither details nor legislative text' and does not address concerns about ICE's lawless conduct. Democrats demand judicial warrants, officer identification, use-of-force standards and an end to racial profiling.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:32:45.222883+00:00","url":"https://aldailynews.com/democrats-say-white-house-offer-on-ice-is-insufficient-as-homeland-security-funding-set-to-expire","content":"Democrats say White House offer on ICE is ‘insufficient’ as Homeland Security funding set to expire\nFebruary 10, 2026 •\nNews,\nBy MARY CLARE JALONICK, KEVIN FREKING and SEUNG MIN KIM, Associated Press\nWASHINGTON — Democratic leaders say a proposal from the White House is “incomplete and insufficient” as they are demanding new restrictions on President Donald Trump’s immigration crackdown and threatening a shutdown of the Homeland Security Department.\nSenate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer and House Democratic leader Hakeem Jeffries said in a statement late Monday that a White House counterproposal to the list of demands they transmitted over the weekend “included neither details nor legislative text” and does not address “the concerns Americans have about ICE’s lawless conduct.” The White House proposal was not released publicly.\nThe Democrats’ statement comes as time is running short, with another partial government shutdown threatening to begin Saturday. Among the Democrats’ demands are a requirement for judicial warrants, better identification of DHS officers, new use-of-force standards and a stop to racial profiling. They say such changes are necessary after two protesters were fatally shot by federal agents in Minneapolis last month.\nEarlier Monday, Senate Majority Leader John Thune, R-S.D., had expressed optimism about the rare negotiations between Democrats and the White House, saying there was “forward progress.”\nThune said it was a good sign that the two sides were trading papers, and “hopefully they can find some common ground here.”\nBut coming to an agreement on the charged issue of immigration enforcement will be difficult, especially as rank-and-file lawmakers in both parties were skeptical about finding common ground.\nRepublicans have balked at the Democrats’ requests and some have demands of their own, including the addition of legislation that would require proof of citizenship before Americans register to vote and restrictions on cities that they say do not do enough to crack down on illegal immigration.\nAnd many Democrats who are furious about Immigration and Customs Enforcement’s aggressive crackdown have said they won’t vote for another penny of Homeland Security funding until enforcement is radically scaled back.\n“Dramatic changes are needed at the Department of Homeland Security before a DHS funding bill moves forward,” Jeffries said earlier Monday. “Period. Full stop.”\nTrump deals with Democrats\nCongress is trying to renegotiate the DHS spending bill after Trump agreed to a Democratic request that it be separated out from a larger spending measure that became law last week. That package extended Homeland Security funding at current levels only through Feb. 13, creating a brief window for action as the two parties discuss new restrictions on ICE and other federal officers.\nDemocrats made the demands for new restrictions on ICE and other federal law enforcement after ICU nurse Alex Pretti was shot and killed by a U.S. Border Patrol officer in Minneapolis on Jan. 24, and some Republicans suggested that new restrictions were necessary. Renee Good was shot by ICE agents on Jan. 7.\nWhile he agreed to separate the funding, Trump has not publicly responded to the Democrats’ specific demands.\nWhite House press secretary Karoline Leavitt said late last week that the Trump administration is willing to discuss some items on the Democrats’ list, but “others don’t seem like they are grounded in any common sense, and they are nonstarters for this administration.”\nDemocratic demands\nSchumer and Jeffries have said they want immigration officers to remove their masks, to show identification and to better coordinate with local authorities. They have also demanded a stricter use-of-force policy for the federal officers, legal safeguards at detention centers and a prohibition on tracking protesters with body-worn cameras.\nAmong other demands, Democrats say Congress should end indiscriminate arrests, “improve warrant procedures and standards,” ensure the law is clear that officers cannot enter private property without a judicial warrant and require that before a person can be detained, it’s verified that the person is not a U.S. citizen.\nRepublicans have said they support the requirement for DHS officers to have body-worn cameras — language that was in the original DHS bill — but have balked at many of the other Democratic asks.\n“Taking the masks off ICE officers and agents, the reason we can’t do that is that it would subject them to great harm, their families at great risk because people are doxing them and targeting them,” said House Speaker Mike Johnson, R-La., on Monday. “We’ve got to talk about things that are reasonable and achievable.”\nTennessee Sen. Bill Hagerty said on “Fox News Sunday” that Democrats are ”trying to motivate a radical left base.”\n“The left has gone completely overboard, and they’re threatening the safety and security of our agents so they cannot do their job,” Hagerty said.\nConsequences of a shutdown\nIn addition to ICE and U.S. Customs and Border Protection, the homeland security bill includes funding for the Federal Emergency Management Agency and the Transportation Security Administration. If DHS shuts down, Thune said last week, “there’s a very good chance we could see more travel problems” similar to the 43-day government closure last year.\nLawmakers in both parties have suggested they could separate out funding for ICE and Border Patrol and pass the rest of it by Friday. But Thune has been cool to that idea, saying instead that Congress should pass another short-term extension for all of DHS while they negotiate the possible new restrictions.\n“If there’s additional time that’s needed, then hopefully Democrats would be amenable to another extension,” Thune said.\nMany Democrats are unlikely to vote for another extension. But Republicans could potentially win enough votes in both chambers from Democrats if they feel hopeful about negotiations.\n“The ball is in the Republicans’ court,” Jeffries said Monday.","content_cn":"民主党人称白宫关于ICE的提议“不充分”，国土安全部资金即将到期\n2026年2月10日 •\n新闻，\n作者：玛丽·克莱尔·哈洛尼克、凯文·弗雷金、金承敏，美联社\n华盛顿——民主党领导人称白宫提出的一项提议“不完整且不充分”，他们正要求对总统唐纳德·特朗普的移民打击行动施加新限制，并威胁要让国土安全部停摆。\n参议院民主党领袖查克·舒默和众议院民主党领袖哈基姆·杰弗里斯周一晚间在一份声明中表示，白宫对他们周末提交的要求清单提出的反提案“既没有细节，也没有立法文本”，并且没有回应“美国人对ICE无法无天行为的担忧”。白宫的提议未公开发布。\n民主党人发表这份声明之际，时间已所剩无几，另一场部分政府停摆有可能于周六开始。民主党人的要求包括：必须取得司法搜查令、更好地识别国土安全部官员身份、新的使用武力标准以及停止种族定性。他们表示，在上月明尼阿波利斯两名抗议者被联邦探员开枪打死后，这些改变是必要的。\n周一早些时候，南达科他州共和党籍参议院多数党领袖约翰·图恩曾对民主党人与白宫之间罕见的谈判表示乐观，称已有“向前进展”。\n图恩说，双方交换文件是一个好迹象，“希望他们能在这里找到一些共同点”。\n但是，就移民执法这一高度敏感问题达成协议将会很困难，尤其是两党的普通议员都对找到共同点持怀疑态度。\n共和党人已对民主党人的请求表示反对，一些人还有自己的要求，包括加入一项立法，要求美国人在登记投票前提供公民身份证明，并对那些他们所称在打击非法移民方面做得不够的城市施加限制。\n许多对移民和海关执法局激进打击行动感到愤怒的民主党人表示，在执法行动被大幅缩减之前，他们不会投票支持再为国土安全部拨款一分钱。\n“在国土安全部的拨款法案向前推进之前，该部门需要发生剧烈变化，”杰弗里斯周一早些时候说。“就这样。句号。”\n特朗普与民主党人打交道\n国会正试图重新谈判国土安全部支出法案，此前特朗普同意民主党人的一项请求，将其从上周成为法律的一项更大规模支出措施中分离出来。那项一揽子方案仅将国土安全部资金按当前水平延长至2月13日，为两党讨论对ICE及其他联邦官员施加新限制创造了一个短暂窗口。\n在重症监护室护士亚历克斯·普雷蒂于1月24日在明尼阿波利斯被一名美国边境巡逻队官员开枪打死，以及一些共和党人暗示有必要实施新限制之后，民主党人提出了对ICE和其他联邦执法机构施加新限制的要求。蕾妮·古德于1月7日被ICE探员开枪打死。\n虽然特朗普同意将资金问题分离出来，但他尚未公开回应民主党人的具体要求。\n白宫新闻秘书卡罗琳·莱维特上周晚些时候表示，特朗普政府愿意讨论民主党人清单上的部分事项，但“其他事项似乎没有任何常识依据，对本届政府来说是不可接受的”。\n民主党人的要求\n舒默和杰弗里斯表示，他们希望移民官员摘下面罩、出示身份证明，并与地方当局更好地协调。他们还要求对联邦官员实行更严格的使用武力政策、在拘留中心提供法律保障，并禁止用随身摄像头追踪抗议者。\n在其他要求中，民主党人表示，国会应结束不加区分的逮捕，“改进搜查令程序和标准”，确保法律明确规定官员不得在没有司法搜查令的情况下进入私人财产，并要求在某人被拘留前核实其不是美国公民。\n共和党人表示，他们支持要求国土安全部官员佩戴随身摄像头——这一措辞原本就在国土安全部法案中——但对民主党人的许多其他要求表示反对。\n“让ICE官员和探员摘下面罩，我们不能这样做的原因是，这会\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"aldailynews.com","publish_time":"2026-02-10T12:01:08+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1501","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部停摆进入第二周，布里特重启与民主党人的对话","title_en":"DHS shutdown hits two-weeks as Britt restarts conversations with Democrats - Alabama Daily News","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部停摆进入第14天，白宫与参议院民主党人仍僵持不下，数千名联邦雇员开始拿不到工资。共和党首席谈判代表、参议员凯蒂·布里特表示本周已重启与民主党人的对话，寻求“前进路径”。民主党因联邦移民执法人员致死事件而阻挠拨款，要求限制移民执法。FEMA、TSA和海岸警卫队目前无资金运转，参议员们已离城，停摆至少将持续17天。","summary_en":"The Department of Homeland Security shutdown entered its 14th day as the White House and Senate Democrats remained at a standstill, with thousands of federal workers beginning to miss paychecks. Sen. Katie Britt, the lead Republican negotiator for DHS funding, said she has re-engaged with Democrats this week to find a pathway forward. Democrats have held up funding over deaths caused by federal immigration officers, seeking curbs on enforcement. FEMA, TSA and the Coast Guard are operating without funds, and senators left town, extending the shutdown to at least 17 days.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:34:40.167051+00:00","url":"https://aldailynews.com/dhs-shutdown-hits-two-weeks-as-britt-restarts-conversations-with-democrats","content":"DHS shutdown hits two-weeks as Britt restarts conversations with Democrats\nFebruary 27, 2026 •\nNews,\nBy Alex Angle\nWASHINGTON — The Department of Homeland Security shutdown enters its 14th day as the White House and Senate Democrats remain at a standstill.\nThousands of federal workers under DHS will begin to miss their paychecks today, with the vast majority of employees required to continue working during the funding lapse. Missed paychecks, which DHS employees are facing during a third shutdown in less than six months, could ratchet up pressure on lawmakers to find a way out of the stalemate.\nSen. Katie Britt, R-Ala., the lead Republican negotiator for DHS funding, said she has re-engaged in talks this week with Democrats to find a “pathway forward.” Much of the discussion has been between the White House and Democrats.\n“I am hopeful that those conversations can actually produce a result,” Britt told Alabama Daily News. “I’m not at liberty to talk about exactly where we are on those but (I) have re-engaged, have restarted that.”\nWhile immigration enforcement operations remain funded from money allocated in the One Big Beautiful Bill Act, the Federal Emergency Management Agency, the Transportation Security Agency and the Coast Guard are operating without funds right now.\nBritt wants to get the department’s funding up and running again next week.\n“So, I’m gonna work around the clock, this weekend, trying to get things moving in the right direction,” she said.\nOn Wednesday, Senate Minority Leader Chuck Schumer, D-N.Y., said there’s only been “crickets” from the White House after Democrats sent administration officials a counterproposal on DHS funding last Monday.\nBut a White House official told ADN that it had sent a “serious counter offer” to Democrats on Thursday.\n“Democrats need to make a move to end the shutdown before more Americans are harmed by a lack of funding for critical services like disaster relief,” the White House official said.\nDemocrats have held up DHS funding over the deaths of Alex Pretti and Renee Good by federal immigration officers in Minneapolis.\n“All (Republicans) have to do is agree with our simple ideas that every police department just about in America follows, and we’ll get it all done. Plain and simple,” Schumer told reporters.\nSenate Democrats have remained persistent in pushing for curbs on immigration enforcement.\nAccording to a DHS contingency plan, more than 20,000 workers at FEMA and more than 61,00 workers at TSA are required to work during the shutdown. This week, DHS took additional steps to deal with the funding lapse by halting all non-disaster-related FEMA response efforts and ending Global Entry service at airports. As workers miss paychecks, travel disruptions could escalate the longer the shutdown lasts.\nSenate Majority Leader Thune, R-S.D., signaled he was open to the White House finding a way to pay federal employees if the two sides cannot reach an agreement any time soon.\n“If they can figure out a way to pay government employees, absolutely,” Thune told reporters Wednesday.\nBritt echoed that getting workers paid is a priority, but she also wants to focus on funding the “entire” Homeland Security Department.\nSen. Tommy Tuberville, R-Ala., isn’t very optimistic that a deal could arise soon from the negotiations between the Democrats and the White House, saying “they’re not even close.”\n“(Democrats) have gone way out on a limb of trying to tie the hands of our law enforcement, our ICE agents,” Tuberville told ADN. “We don’t need to put them in harm’s way. We need to take and arrest as many illegals, especially the ones that are criminals, (and) get them out of this country.”\nSenators left town for the week on Thursday and will return to Washington Monday, leaving the shutdown to stretch at least 17 days.\nThis story has been updated with a comment from the White House.","content_cn":"国土安全部停摆进入两周，布里特重新与民主党展开对话\n2026年2月27日 •\n新闻，\n作者：Alex Angle\n华盛顿——随着白宫和参议院民主党人仍陷于僵局，国土安全部的停摆进入第14天。\n今天，国土安全部下属的数千名联邦工作人员将开始领不到工资，而绝大多数雇员在资金中断期间仍被要求继续工作。国土安全部员工在不到六个月内第三次面临停摆，工资拖欠可能进一步加大对议员的压力，促使他们设法打破僵局。\n负责国土安全部拨款谈判的共和党首席谈判代表、阿拉巴马州共和党参议员凯蒂·布里特表示，本周她已重新与民主党展开谈判，以寻找“前进的路径”。大部分讨论是在白宫和民主党之间进行的。\n布里特对《阿拉巴马日报》说：“我希望这些对话确实能够产生结果。我无权谈论我们目前具体进展到哪里，但我已经重新参与并重新启动了谈判。”\n虽然移民执法行动仍由《一项大而美丽的法案》中拨付的资金提供保障，但联邦紧急事务管理局、运输安全管理局和海岸警卫队目前都在无资金状态下运作。\n布里特希望下周让该部门的资金再次运转起来。\n她说：“所以，这个周末我会夜以继日地工作，努力让事情朝正确的方向推进。”\n周三，纽约州民主党参议员、参议院少数党领袖查克·舒默表示，在民主党上周一向政府官员提交国土安全部拨款反提案后，白宫方面一直“鸦雀无声”。\n但一名白宫官员告诉《阿拉巴马日报》，白宫周四已向民主党提交了一份“严肃的反提案”。\n这名白宫官员说：“民主党需要采取行动，在更多美国人因灾害救援等关键服务缺乏资金而受到伤害之前结束停摆。”\n民主党一直因联邦移民官员在明尼阿波利斯造成亚历克斯·普雷蒂和蕾妮·古德死亡一事而阻挠国土安全部拨款。\n舒默对记者说：“共和党人要做的就是同意我们提出的简单想法——几乎美国每个警察部门都遵循这些做法——我们就能把一切都完成。就这么简单。”\n参议院民主党人一直坚持推动限制移民执法。\n根据国土安全部的应急预案，联邦紧急事务管理局超过20,000名工作人员和运输安全管理局超过61,00名工作人员在停摆期间必须工作。本周，国土安全部还采取了额外措施应对资金中断，包括暂停联邦紧急事务管理局所有与灾害无关的响应工作，并终止机场的全球入境服务。随着工作人员领不到工资，停摆持续时间越长，旅行中断可能越发严重。\n南达科他州共和党参议员、参议院多数党领袖约翰·图恩表示，如果双方近期无法达成协议，他愿意让白宫寻找支付联邦雇员工资的办法。\n图恩周三对记者说：“如果他们能找到支付政府雇员工资的办法，当然可以。”\n布里特也表示，让工作人员拿到工资是优先事项，但她还希望重点为整个国土安全部提供资金。\n阿拉巴马州共和党参议员汤米·图伯维尔对民主党和白宫之间的谈判很快达成协议并不乐观，他说双方“甚至还差得很远”。\n图伯维尔对《阿拉巴马日报》说：“（民主党人）在试图束缚我们的执法人员和移民及海关执法局特工方面，已经走得太远了。我们不需要把他们置于危险之中。我们需要抓捕尽可能多的非法移民，尤其是那些罪犯，（并）把他们赶出这个国家。”\n参议员们周四离开华盛顿，前往各地度过本周，周一才会返回华盛顿，这意味着停摆至少将持续17天。\n本文已加入白宫方面的评论。","publish_source":"aldailynews.com","publish_time":"2026-02-27T14:47:05+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2939","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI局长与布里特、图伯维尔视察红石兵工厂，机构计划带来更多岗位","title_en":"FBI director tours Redstone Arsenal with Britt, Tuberville as agency plans to bring more jobs - Alabama Daily News","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔兑现对参议员凯蒂·布里特的承诺，与布里特及参议员汤米·图伯维尔一同视察了阿拉巴马州红石兵工厂的FBI设施。帕特尔承诺到年底前向亨茨维尔带来500个岗位，当地已有2000多名FBI人员。帕特尔参观了恐怖爆炸物分析中心和弹道研究设施，并观看了FBI反无人机系统演示。他称红石可成为跨机构和国际伙伴的培训场所。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel fulfilled a promise to Sen. Katie Britt by touring FBI facilities at Redstone Arsenal in Alabama alongside Britt and Sen. Tommy Tuberville. Patel has committed to bringing 500 jobs to Huntsville by year's end, where more than 2,000 FBI personnel are already located. He toured the Terrorist Explosive Device Analytical Center and the Ballistic Research Facility, and received a demonstration of the FBI's counter-drone systems. Patel said Redstone could serve as a training site for interagency and international partners.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:35:36.009150+00:00","url":"https://aldailynews.com/fbi-director-tours-redstone-arsenal-with-britt-tuberville-as-agency-plans-to-bring-more-jobs","content":"FBI director tours Redstone Arsenal with Britt, Tuberville as agency plans to bring more jobs\nApril 24, 2025 •\nNews,\nBy Alex Angle\nWASHINGTON – FBI Director Kash Patel made good on his promise to U.S. Sen. Katie Britt Wednesday with a tour of Redstone Arsenal, as the new director has committed to bringing 500 jobs to Huntsville by the end of the year.\nPatel joined Britt and fellow Sen. Tommy Tuberville for a visit to the FBI facilities.\n“I just want to let America know, part of the move to get FBI agents and intel analysts and support staff out in the field is going to come right through Redstone Arsenal,” Patel told local reporters during a press conference. “We’re going to put more and more and more people here on a permanent basis from the FBI.”\nDuring his confirmation process, Patel committed to Britt, a member of the Senate Judiciary Committee, to visit the bureau’s facilities at Redstone. He was confirmed in February.\n“Today was a great day to get to look at where we are and where we are going to go in the future,” Britt said during Wednesday’s press conference. “Director Patel is committed to making sure that the great work that is done here in Huntsville not only expands but continues to help keep Americans safe from coast to coast.”\nThe day Patel was sworn in to lead the FBI, he announced the bureau would move 500 employees to Huntsville, where more than 2,000 are already located. The announcement came just a day after Britt and Tuberville urged Patel to fill 1,000 of about 4,000 open slots at the agency’s facilities at Redstone.\n“This is a big part of his puzzle here at Redstone Arsenal, and that is the reason we’re here today for him to see what he has inherited and will inherit in the future, because it’s going to continue to grow,” Tuberville said at the press conference.\nPatel touted Redstone’s capabilities and facilities that could be used to train interagency and international partners, he said.\n“One of the things that we’ve been working on together is to tackle violent crime across the country,” Patel said. “But in order to do that, you need a place for people and experts to train, that’s right here in Redstone. You need a place for people to live in a community that’s safe, that’s right here in the state of Alabama, right here in Huntsville.”\nPatel toured the Terrorist Explosive Device Analytical Center and the Ballistic Research Facility. He and the senators also received a demonstration on the FBI’s use of Counter-Unmanned Aircraft Systems and drones.","content_cn":"FBI局长与布里特、塔伯维尔一同视察雷德斯通兵工厂，因该机构计划增加更多就业岗位\n2025年4月24日 •\n新闻，\n作者：Alex Angle\n\n华盛顿——FBI局长卡什·帕特尔周三兑现了对美国参议员凯蒂·布里特的承诺，视察了雷德斯通兵工厂。新局长已承诺在年底前为亨茨维尔带来500个就业岗位。\n帕特尔与布里特以及另一位参议员汤米·塔伯维尔一同参观了FBI设施。\n帕特尔在新闻发布会上对当地记者说：“我只是想让美国知道，让FBI特工、情报分析师和支持人员走向一线的部分行动，将直接通过雷德斯通兵工厂展开。我们将让FBI越来越多的人员长期驻扎在这里。”\n在确认任职过程中，帕特尔向参议院司法委员会成员布里特承诺，会参观联邦调查局在雷德斯通的设施。他于2月获得确认任命。\n布里特在周三的新闻发布会上说：“今天是很好的一天，我们得以了解我们目前所处的位置，以及未来将走向何方。帕特尔局长致力于确保亨茨维尔这里开展的伟大工作不仅得到扩展，而且继续帮助保护从东海岸到西海岸的美国人安全。”\n帕特尔宣誓就任FBI局长的当天，他宣布联邦调查局将把500名员工调往亨茨维尔；目前已有2000多人在当地工作。这一宣布发布的前一天，布里特和塔伯维尔曾敦促帕特尔，在雷德斯通设施约4000个空缺职位中填补1000个。\n塔伯维尔在新闻发布会上说：“这是他在雷德斯通兵工厂整体规划中的重要一环，这就是我们今天来到这里的原因——让他看看自己已经继承以及未来将继承的工作，因为这里还会继续发展壮大。”\n帕特尔称赞了雷德斯通的能力和设施，并表示这些设施可用于培训跨机构及国际合作伙伴。\n帕特尔说：“我们一直共同努力的一件事，是打击全国各地的暴力犯罪。但要做到这一点，你需要一个让人员和专家接受培训的地方，而这里的雷德斯通正是这样一个地方。你需要一个让人们生活在安全社区中的地方，这里就是阿拉巴马州、就是亨茨维尔。”\n帕特尔参观了恐怖主义爆炸装置分析中心和弹道研究设施。他与两位参议员还观看了FBI使用反无人机系统和无人机的演示。","publish_source":"aldailynews.com","publish_time":"2025-04-24T10:59:07+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1609","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部停摆即将开始，布里特请求短期延期","title_en":"Homeland Security shutdown set to begin, Britt asks for short-term extension - Alabama Daily News","summary_cn":"由于参议院民主党人阻止了为国土安全部提供至9月资金的拨款法案，该部门预计将在周六午夜后资金耗尽而停摆，且可能持续至少一周。阿拉巴马州共和党参议员凯蒂·布里特批评议员离城休假“荒谬”，并请求以一致同意方式将资金延长两周，但遭康涅狄格州民主党参议员墨菲反对。移民与海关执法局及海关与边境保护局因已有拨款将继续运作，海岸警卫队、联邦应急管理局和运输安全管理局受影响将随停摆延长而加剧。","summary_en":"Senate Democrats blocked a funding bill that would have financed the Department of Homeland Security through September, leaving the department set to run out of money just after midnight Saturday, with the lapse expected to last at least a week while lawmakers are on recess. Sen. Katie Britt, R-Ala., who has led DHS negotiations for Republicans, called it \"absurd\" that senators would be out of town and requested a two-week funding extension by unanimous consent, but Democratic Sen. Chris Murphy objected. ICE and CBP operations will continue due to prior funding, while impacts on the Coast Guard, FEMA and TSA will grow the longer a shutdown lasts.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:31:36.761156+00:00","url":"https://aldailynews.com/homeland-security-shutdown-set-to-begin-britt-asked-for-short-term-extension","content":"Homeland Security shutdown set to begin, Britt asks for short-term extension\nFebruary 13, 2026 •\nNews,\nBy Alex Angle\nWASHINGTON — The Department of Homeland Security is all but certain to shut down over the weekend as lawmakers leave Washington without reaching a deal.\nSenate Democrats blocked a funding bill Thursday that would have provided money for DHS through September. Now, the department is set to run out of money just after midnight Saturday. The funding lapse is expected to last at least a week while lawmakers are on recess.\nSen. Katie Britt, R-Ala., who has been leading DHS negotiations for Republicans, said it was “absurd” that senators will be out of town instead of discussing the issue in Washington.\n“I think we should stay here, and we should work to find a pathway forward, because I think people are depending on it,” Britt told Alabama Daily News. “I think the work that the department does is important, and I think we owe it to the people we serve to stay here and figure it out, particularly as we’re moving and working back and forth.”\nSenate Majority Leader John Thune, R-S.D., told reporters he sent senators home because they’re “not close” to reaching a compromise, but lawmakers are on notice to return if a breakthrough happens. The House is also out of session next week.\nThe White House and Democrats have traded proposals this week as the two sides worked to find agreement before the Friday deadline. But Senate Minority Leader Chuck Schumer, D-N.Y., argued the Trump administration’s offers were “not serious.”\n“The path forward is simple: negotiate serious guardrails that protect Americans, that rein in ICE and stop the violence,” Schumer said after the vote.\nDespite the near-certain shutdown, Immigration and Customs Enforcement and Customs and Border Protection operations will continue, as the One Big Beautiful Bill Act already provided $75 billion for the agencies. The impacts on other agencies under DHS, including the Coast Guard, FEMA and TSA, will become more significant the longer the shutdown lasts.\nAfter the funding bill, which needed 60 votes, was rejected in the Senate, Britt requested a short-term extension for DHS via unanimous consent.\n“Extend this funding for two more weeks, so that as we talk, that as we negotiate, TSA agents don’t miss a paycheck, so that FEMA workers who are helping to get out disaster relief to people who have been ravaged across this country (get a paycheck),” Britt said on the Senate floor.\nBut Democratic Sen. Chris Murphy of Connecticut, Britt’s counterpart on the Homeland Security Appropriations Subcommittee, objected.\n“We believe we have a constitutional obligation to only fund a Department of Homeland Security that is obeying the law, and this Department of Homeland Security is not obeying the law,” Murphy said, referencing federal immigration tactics under the Trump administration.\nIn the wake of the killing of Alex Pretti in Minneapolis, Democrats have pushed for multiple restrictions on ICE, including an end to roving patrols and requirements that federal agents wear identification and unmask. As Democrats and the White House go back and forth, neither side has revealed what changes to the department they are pushing for or are willing to accept in a final deal.\nLooking ahead, Sen. Tommy Tuberville, R-Ala., said “any negotiations with Democrats that handcuff our ICE officers’ ability to do their job is a definite no vote for me.”\nDespite Congress being out of session next week, talks are expected to continue.\n“This can get done,” Thune told reporters.\nIf DHS shuts down on Saturday, it will mark the third funding lapse in less than six months.","content_cn":"国土安全部停摆即将开始，布里特请求短期延期\n2026年2月13日 •\n新闻，\n作者：亚历克斯·安格尔\n华盛顿——随着议员们未达成协议便离开华盛顿，国土安全部几乎可以肯定将在周末停摆。\n参议院民主党人周四阻止了一项本可为国土安全部提供资金至9月的拨款法案。如今，该部门将在周六午夜刚过后资金耗尽。预计此次资金中断将至少持续一周，因为议员们正在休会。\n一直代表共和党主导国土安全部谈判的阿拉巴马州共和党参议员凯蒂·布里特表示，参议员们将离开华盛顿而不是在首都讨论这一问题，这“荒谬”。\n“我认为我们应该留在这里，努力找到前进的道路，因为我认为人们正依赖于此，”布里特对《阿拉巴马每日新闻》说。“我认为该部门所做的工作很重要，我认为我们有责任为我们所服务的人民留在这里把事情解决，尤其是当我们来回奔波、开展工作的时候。”\n参议院多数党领袖、南达科他州共和党人约翰·图恩告诉记者，他让参议员们回家，是因为他们“远未”达成妥协，但议员们已接到通知，一旦出现突破就返回。众议院下周也不开会。\n白宫和民主党人本周互换了提案，双方努力在周五最后期限前达成一致。但参议院少数党领袖、纽约州民主党人查克·舒默认为，特朗普政府提出的方案“不严肃”。\n“前进的道路很简单：谈判达成严肃的护栏措施，保护美国人，约束ICE并停止暴力，”舒默在投票后说。\n尽管停摆几乎已成定局，移民和海关执法局以及海关和边境保护局的运作仍将继续，因为《一项大而美的法案》已为这些机构提供了750亿美元。停摆持续时间越长，对国土安全部下属其他机构——包括海岸警卫队、联邦应急管理局和运输安全管理局——的影响将越显著。\n在需要60票的拨款法案于参议院被否决后，布里特通过一致同意请求为国土安全部提供短期延期。\n“把这项拨款再延长两周，这样在我们讨论、谈判期间，运输安全管理局人员不会拿不到工资，这样正在帮助向全国受灾民众发放救灾援助的联邦应急管理局工作人员（也能拿到工资），”布里特在参议院发言时说。\n但康涅狄格州民主党参议员克里斯·墨菲——布里特在国土安全拨款小组委员会的对应人物——表示反对。\n“我们认为，我们负有宪法义务，只为一个守法的国土安全部提供资金，而这个国土安全部并不守法，”墨菲说，他指的是特朗普政府时期的联邦移民执法策略。\n在亚历克斯·普雷蒂于明尼阿波利斯被杀后，民主党人推动对ICE施加多项限制，包括终止流动巡逻，以及要求联邦探员佩戴身份标识并摘下面罩。在民主党人与白宫来回交涉之际，双方均未透露他们在最终协议中推动或愿意接受对该部门作出哪些改变。\n展望未来，阿拉巴马州共和党参议员汤米·图伯维尔表示，“任何与民主党人的谈判，只要束缚我们ICE官员履行职责的能力，对我来说都绝对是反对票。”\n尽管国会下周休会，谈判预计仍将继续。\n“这件事可以完成，”图恩告诉记者。\n如果国土安全部在周六停摆，这将是不到六个月内的第三次资金中断。","publish_source":"aldailynews.com","publish_time":"2026-02-13T13:42:48+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2474","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"麦卡里研究所任命前国土安全部长加入顾问委员会","title_en":"McCrary Institute names former Homeland Security secretary to advisory board - Alabama Daily News","summary_cn":"奥本大学麦卡里网络与关键基础设施安全研究所宣布，曾在特朗普首届政府担任第六任国土安全部长的克尔斯滕·尼尔森加入其顾问委员会，前美国空军情报负责人、Scitor公司前CEO詹姆斯·霍斯金斯同时加入。该研究所专注于制定网络安全战略以保护国家基础设施，并与联邦机构和国会密切合作。尼尔森表示很荣幸加入这一以使命为导向的机构。","summary_en":"Auburn University's McCrary Institute for Cyber and Critical Infrastructure Security added two new leaders to its advisory board, including Kirstjen Nielsen, who served as the sixth Homeland Security secretary during the first Trump administration. Former U.S. Air Force intelligence leader and Scitor CEO James Hoskins also joined. The institute focuses on cybersecurity strategies to protect national infrastructure and works closely with federal agencies and Congress. Nielsen said she was honored to join the mission-driven institution.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:16:51.346678+00:00","url":"https://aldailynews.com/mccrary-institute-names-former-homeland-security-secretary-to-advisory-board","content":"McCrary Institute names former Homeland Security secretary to advisory board\nAugust 26, 2025 •\nNews,\nBy Alex Angle\nWASHINGTON — Auburn University’s McCrary Institute for Cyber and Critical Infrastructure Security added two new leaders to its advisory board, including the sixth Homeland Security secretary.\nThe institute recently announced that Kirstjen Nielsen, who served as the Homeland Security secretary during the first Trump administration, will become a board member. Nielsen is the current president of Lighthouse Strategies.\nAuburn alumnus and former U.S. Air Force intelligence leader James Hoskins also joined the board. Hoskins also served as the CEO of Scitor Corporation, a national intelligence contractor, which was acquired by SAIC.\n“Bringing on these renowned leaders in homeland and national security will only further our ability to help the McCrary Institute have a meaningful impact on our nation,” Lt. Gen. Ronald L. Burgess Jr., McCrary Institute Advisory Board chairman and former director of the U.S. Defense Intelligence Agency, said in a statement.\nThe McCrary Institute focuses on crafting cybersecurity strategies and priorities to protect the nation’s infrastructure.\n“I am deeply honored to join the board of the McCrary Institute, a dynamic and mission-driven institution that not only leads in cybersecurity innovation and education but also stands as a national resource, shaping the future of policy, research and resilience,” Nielsen said in a statement.\nThe new board members will join 13 others, including corporate executives, senior government officials and Auburn University leadership.\n“The cybersecurity mission of the McCrary Institute is national in scope and priority,” Hoskins said in a statement. “America’s future is in great hands considering the capabilities, personnel and facilities that have been assembled by McCrary with the aim to make a landmark difference.”\nThe institute works closely with federal agencies and Congress to advise and shape public policy. Research teams in Auburn and Huntsville develop and deploy cybersecurity solutions to bolster infrastructure in the Southeast and across the country.\n“(Nielsen and Hoskins) bring deep experience in national security, cybersecurity and public service — adding invaluable perspective to an already exceptional group,” Frank Cilluffo, McCrary Institute director, said in a statement. “Their advice and counsel will help us strengthen our efforts to protect the critical infrastructure that underpins our nation’s security, economy and communities.”","content_cn":"McCrary研究所任命前国土安全部长加入顾问委员会\n2025年8月26日 •\n新闻，\n作者：Alex Angle\n华盛顿——奥本大学麦克拉里网络与关键基础设施安全研究所新增两名顾问委员会领导成员，其中包括第六任国土安全部长。\n该研究所近日宣布，曾在特朗普第一届政府任内担任国土安全部长的Kirstjen Nielsen将成为委员会成员。Nielsen现任Lighthouse Strategies总裁。\n奥本大学校友、美国空军前情报负责人James Hoskins也加入了委员会。Hoskins还曾担任国家情报承包商Scitor Corporation的首席执行官，该公司后来被SAIC收购。\n“吸纳这些在国土安全和国家安全领域享有盛誉的领导者，将进一步提升我们帮助McCrary研究所对国家产生实质影响的能力，”麦克拉里研究所顾问委员会主席、美国国防情报局前局长Ronald L. Burgess Jr.中将在一份声明中说。\n麦克拉里研究所专注于制定网络安全战略和优先事项，以保护国家基础设施。\n“我深感荣幸能够加入麦克拉里研究所董事会。这是一家充满活力、以使命为导向的机构，不仅在网络安全创新和教育方面处于领先地位，也是塑造政策、研究和韧性未来的国家资源，”Nielsen在一份声明中说。\n新成员将与另外13名成员共事，这些成员包括企业高管、高级政府官员和奥本大学领导层。\n“麦克拉里研究所的网络安全使命具有国家层面的范围和优先级，”Hoskins在一份声明中说。“考虑到McCrary为实现里程碑式影响而汇聚的能力、人员和设施，美国的未来掌握在非常可靠的人手中。”\n该研究所与联邦机构和国会密切合作，为公共政策提供建议并参与塑造公共政策。奥本和亨茨维尔的研究团队开发并部署网络安全解决方案，以加强东南部及全国的基础设施。\n“（Nielsen和Hoskins）在国家安全、网络安全和公共服务方面拥有深厚经验，为这个已经非常出色的团队增添了宝贵视角，”麦克拉里研究所所长Frank Cilluffo在一份声明中说。“他们的建议和指导将帮助我们加强工作，保护支撑国家安全、经济和社区的关键基础设施。”","publish_source":"aldailynews.com","publish_time":"2025-08-26T13:02:48+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1465","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员艾伦就战争权力决议和国土安全部拨款发表声明","title_en":"Congressman Allen Issues Statement on War Powers Resolution and DHS Funding | U.S. Representative Rick W. Allen","summary_cn":"佐治亚州共和党众议员里克·W·艾伦在众议院投票反对H. Con. Res. 38战争权力决议，称其不必要地束缚政府在与伊朗敌对行动中的手脚，并投票支持H.R. 7744《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》。艾伦在声明中称伊朗应对更多美国人死亡负责，认为总统已通过向八人帮简报履行战争权力决议要求，并指责民主党近三周阻挠并关闭国土安全部，强调必须为该部门及其下属机构提供全额资金。","summary_en":"Rep. Rick W. Allen (GA-12) voted no on H. Con. Res. 38, the War Powers Resolution, saying it would unnecessarily tie the administration's hands during hostilities with Iran, and voted yes on H.R. 7744, the Department of Homeland Security Appropriations Act of 2026. In his statement, Allen said Iran is responsible for more American deaths than any other terrorist regime, argued the President fulfilled War Powers requirements by briefing the Gang of Eight, and accused Democrats of obstructing and shutting down DHS for nearly three weeks, stressing the need to fully fund the department and its agencies.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:25:12.944896+00:00","url":"https://allen.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=7143","content":"Press Releases\nCongressman Allen Issues Statement on War Powers Resolution and DHS Funding\nShare on Facebook\nShare on X\nPrint this Page\nShare by Email\nWashington,\nMarch 5, 2026\nThis evening on the House floor, Congressman Rick W. Allen (GA-12) voted no on H. Con. Res. 38, otherwise known as the War Powers Resolution, which would unnecessarily tie the hands of the Administration during hostilities with Iran. Congressman Allen also voted yes on H.R. 7744, the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Appropriations Act of 2026, which fully funds DHS and supports efforts to defend our homeland. Following tonight's floor activity, Congressman Allen released the statement below:\n\"Iran is responsible for more American deaths than any other terrorist regime in the world. The last thing we need to do is hamstring the Administration and our military leaders as they actively defend American citizens from the evolving threat that Iran poses. The President fulfilled the requirements under the War Powers Resolution by briefing the Gang of Eight before the strikes on Iran occurred. Additionally, Article II of the U.S. Constitution is clear that the President is the Commander-in-Chief of the Armed Forces and has a duty to act in defense of our nation.\n\"For that reason, I voted no on the War Powers Resolution offered by Reps. Massie and Khanna. I agree with President Trump that the Iranian regime must never obtain a nuclear weapon, and after receiving a classified briefing earlier this week on Operation Epic Fury, I am even more confident that we will achieve the objectives laid out in detail by the Administration.\n\"Further, and more important now than ever, we must fully fund the Department of Homeland Security. For nearly three weeks, Democrats have obstructed and irresponsibly shut down the department tasked with defending our homeland. That is shameful. House Republicans once again did our work to fully fund DHS—including the Coast Guard, TSA, FEMA, and Air Traffic Controllers. The longer Democrats keep DHS shut down, the more danger they impose on the American people, especially during this time of heightened uncertainty.\n\"Robin and I continue to pray for the families and loved ones of the service members we lost and all of those who continue fighting to ensure Iran’s terrorist proxies can no longer harm Americans and destabilize the Middle East.\"\nStay Connected\nEnter your email address to get the latest updates straight to your inbox.\nEmail Address\nSubmit\nStay Connected\nUse the form below to sign up for my newsletter and get the latest news and updates directly to your inbox.\nEmail Address\nSign up\nFacebook\nX\nInstagram\nYoutube\nOffice Locations\nWashington, DC Office\n462 Cannon House Office Building\nWashington, DC 20515\nPhone: (202) 225-2823\nFax: (202) 225-3377\nAugusta District Office\n2743 Perimeter Parkway\nBuilding 200, Suite 105\nAugusta, GA 30909\nPhone: (706) 228-1980\nFax: (706) 228-1954\nDublin District Office\n100 S. Church Street\nDublin, GA 31021\nPhone: (478) 291-6324\nFax: (706) 228-1954\nStatesboro District Office\n50 E. Main Street\nStatesboro, GA 30458\nPhone: (912) 243-9452\nFax: (912) 243-9453\nVidalia Satellite Office\n107 Old Airport Rd, Suite A\nVidalia, GA 30474\nPhone: (912) 243-9452\nFax: (912) 243-9453","content_cn":"新闻稿\n国会议员艾伦就《战争权力决议》和国土安全部拨款发表声明\n在Facebook上分享\n在X上分享\n打印本页\n通过电子邮件分享\n华盛顿，\n2026年3月5日\n今晚在众议院议事厅，国会议员里克·W·艾伦（佐治亚州第12选区）对H. Con. Res. 38号决议——即所谓的《战争权力决议》——投了反对票，该决议将在与伊朗的敌对行动中不必要地束缚政府的手脚。艾伦议员还对H.R. 7744号法案，即《2026年国土安全部拨款法案》投了赞成票，该法案为国土安全部提供全额资金，并支持保卫我们国土的努力。在今晚的议事活动之后，艾伦议员发表了以下声明：\n“伊朗对美国人死亡所负的责任超过世界上任何其他恐怖主义政权。我们最不需要做的，就是在政府和我们军事领导人积极保卫美国公民免受伊朗不断演变的威胁之际，束缚他们的手脚。总统在袭击伊朗之前向八人帮作了简报，履行了《战争权力决议》规定的要求。此外，《美国宪法》第二条明确规定，总统是武装部队总司令，有责任采取行动保卫我们的国家。\n“因此，我对马西和卡纳两位众议员提出的《战争权力决议》投了反对票。我同意特朗普总统的观点，即伊朗政权绝不能获得核武器，在本周早些时候收到关于‘史诗之怒行动’的机密简报后，我更加确信我们将实现政府详细阐述的各项目标。\n“此外，现在比以往任何时候都更重要的是，我们必须为国土安全部提供全额资金。近三周以来，民主党人一直在阻挠并不负责任地关闭这个负责保卫我们国土的部门。这令人羞耻。众议院共和党人再次完成了我们的工作，为国土安全部提供全额资金——包括海岸警卫队、运输安全管理局、联邦应急管理局和空中交通管制员。民主党人让国土安全部关闭的时间越长，他们给美国人民带来的危险就越大，尤其是在这个不确定性加剧的时期。\n“罗宾和我继续为失去的军人以及所有继续战斗以确保伊朗的恐怖主义代理人不再伤害美国人并破坏中东稳定的人们的家人和亲人祈祷。”\n保持联系\n输入您的电子邮件地址，即可将最新动态直接发送到您的收件箱。\n电子邮件地址\n提交\n保持联系\n使用下面的表格订阅我的通讯，直接将最新新闻和动态发送到您的收件箱。\n电子邮件地址\n注册\nFacebook\nX\nInstagram\nYoutube\n办公地点\n华盛顿特区办公室\n坎农众议院办公大楼462号\n华盛顿特区 20515\n电话：(202) 225-2823\n传真：(202) 225-3377\n奥古斯塔地区办公室\n2743 Perimeter Parkway\n200号楼，105室\n奥古斯塔，佐治亚州 30909\n电话：(706) 228-1980\n传真：(706) 228-1954\n都柏林地区办公室\n100 S. Church Street\n都柏林，佐治亚州 31021\n电话：(478) 291-6324\n传真：(706) 228-1954\n斯泰茨伯勒地区办公室\n50 E. Main Street\n斯泰茨伯勒，佐治亚州 30458\n电话：(912) 243-9452\n传真：(912) 243-9453\n维代利亚卫星办公室\n107 Old Airport Rd, Suite A\n维代利亚，佐治亚州 30474\n电话：(912) 243-9452\n传真：(912) 243-9453","publish_source":"allen.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-05T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3145","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"卡什·帕特尔以51比49参议院投票获确认出任FBI局长","title_en":"Kash Patel confirmed as FBI director in 51-49 Senate vote","summary_cn":"美国参议院以51比49的投票结果确认卡什·帕特尔出任联邦调查局局长。所有民主党人投下反对票，两名共和党人——阿拉斯加州的莉萨·穆尔科斯基和缅因州的苏珊·柯林斯——也投了反对票，凸显围绕其提名的党派分歧。帕特尔长期是特朗普的盟友，曾公开批评FBI，其确认正值该局高层人事大幅变动之际。他是首位领导这一美国顶级调查机构的印度裔美国人。","summary_en":"The U.S. Senate voted 51-49 to confirm Kash Patel as director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation. All Democrats opposed the nomination, joined by two Republicans, Lisa Murkowski of Alaska and Susan Collins of Maine, underscoring the partisan divide. A longtime Trump ally who has openly criticized the FBI, Patel takes over amid sweeping leadership changes at the bureau. He is the first Indian American to lead the nation's premier investigative agency.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:25:55.057544+00:00","url":"https://americanbazaaronline.com/2025/02/20/kash-patel-confirmed-as-fbi-director-in-51-49-senate-vote-459807","content":"Share\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\nEmail\nKash Patel, a staunch Trump ally, secures confirmation despite Democratic opposition and Republican defections.\nThe Senate voted Thursday to confirm Kash Patel as director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation, cementing a staunch ally of President Donald Trump at the helm of the nation’s top law enforcement agency. The 51-49 vote, with all Democrats opposed and two Republicans — Lisa Murkowski of Alaska and Susan Collins of Maine — breaking ranks, signals the deep partisan divide surrounding Patel’s appointment.\nA longtime Trump loyalist, Patel has openly criticized the FBI, echoing Trump’s claims of political bias within the bureau, particularly in its handling of the Capitol riot investigations. His confirmation comes amid sweeping changes at the agency, including the forced departures of multiple senior officials and the controversial involvement of an Elon Musk affiliate in key FBI operations.\nPatel, an Indian American, is the first from the community to lead the nation’s premier investigative agency.\nRELATED: ‘Enemies list’ delays Kash Patel’s Senate confirmation as FBI director (February 7, 2025)\nDuring his Senate confirmation hearing, Patel sought to allay fears of political retribution, pledging there would be no politicization at the FBI, pushing back against Democratic concerns that he would target Trump’s perceived enemies.\nRepublicans defended Patel’s appointment, arguing he would bring much-needed transparency and reform to the FBI. His confirmation is part of a broader effort by Senate Republicans to approve Trump’s key nominees, including Robert F. Kennedy Jr. as secretary of health and human services, Pete Hegseth as defense secretary, and Tulsi Gabbard as director of national intelligence.\nPatel, a former congressional aide and national security staffer, played a key role in declassifying documents that sought to undercut the FBI’s Russia investigation during Trump’s first term. His appointment follows the resignation of former FBI Director Chris Wray, whom Trump ousted after reclaiming the White House.\nREAD: Kash Patel blasts FBI for ‘endangering his life’ (August 29, 2022)\nWith Patel now in charge, the FBI faces its most significant leadership shift since Watergate, as concerns mount over the agency’s future independence.\nFacebookShare on XLinkedInWhatsAppEmailCopy Link\nFBI director Kash Patel","content_cn":"分享\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\n电子邮件\n坚定支持特朗普的卡什·帕特尔尽管遭到民主党反对及共和党议员倒戈，仍获确认任命。\n参议院周四投票确认卡什·帕特尔出任联邦调查局局长，使这位坚定的总统唐纳德·特朗普盟友执掌美国最高执法机构。表决结果为51票赞成、49票反对，所有民主党议员投反对票，两名共和党议员——阿拉斯加州的丽莎·穆尔科斯基和缅因州的苏珊·柯林斯——倒戈支持反对，显示出围绕帕特尔任命的深刻党派分歧。\n作为长期效忠特朗普的人，帕特尔曾公开批评联邦调查局，呼应特朗普关于该局存在政治偏见的说法，尤其针对其处理国会大厦骚乱调查的方式。他获确认之际，该机构正经历大规模变革，包括多名高级官员被迫离职，以及埃隆·马斯克关联的一家实体颇具争议地参与联邦调查局的关键行动。\n帕特尔是印度裔美国人，也是该群体中首位领导美国这一首要调查机构的人。\n相关阅读：“敌人名单”推迟卡什·帕特尔获参议院确认出任联邦调查局局长（2025年2月7日）\n在参议院确认听证会上，帕特尔试图消除人们对政治报复的担忧，承诺联邦调查局不会被政治化，并回应民主党关于他会针对特朗普眼中的敌人的担忧。\n共和党人为帕特尔的任命辩护，称他将为联邦调查局带来急需的透明度和改革。他的获确认是参议院共和党人批准特朗普关键提名人选更广泛努力的一部分，其中包括罗伯特·F·肯尼迪 Jr.出任卫生与公众服务部长、皮特·赫格塞思出任国防部长，以及图尔西·加巴德出任国家情报总监。\n帕特尔曾任国会助理和国家安全工作人员，在特朗普第一任期内负责解密文件，这些文件旨在削弱联邦调查局对俄罗斯干预调查。他的任命是在前联邦调查局局长克里斯托弗·雷辞职后作出的；特朗普重新夺回白宫后将雷赶下台。\n阅读：卡什·帕特尔抨击联邦调查局“危及他的生命”（2022年8月29日）\n帕特尔如今掌权之际，联邦调查局正面临水门事件以来最重大的领导层转变，人们对该机构未来的独立性日益担忧。\n在X上分享FacebookLinkedInWhatsApp电子邮件复制链接\n联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔","publish_source":"americanbazaaronline.com","publish_time":"2025-02-20T21:04:16+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3058","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"肖希尼·辛哈被任命为FBI受害者服务司助理司长","title_en":"Shohini Sinha named Assistant Director of FBI’s Victim Services Division","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局任命印度裔特工肖希尼·辛哈为受害者服务司助理司长。辛哈此前担任盐湖城分局主管特工。她于2001年加入FBI，首个岗位在密尔沃基分局从事反恐调查，此后历任反恐司监督特工、渥太华助理法律专员、底特律分局现场主管、网络入侵小组及波特兰分局助理特工主管等职，2021年任局长行政特别助理，2023年7月起执掌盐湖城分局。","summary_en":"The Federal Bureau of Investigation has named Indian American special agent Shohini Sinha as assistant director of the Victim Services Division. Sinha most recently served as special agent in charge of the Salt Lake City Field Office. She joined the FBI in 2001, first assigned to the Milwaukee Field Office on counterterrorism investigations, and later held roles including supervisory special agent in the Counterterrorism Division, assistant legal attaché in Ottawa, field supervisor in Detroit, and assistant special agent in charge in Portland.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:19:13.729968+00:00","url":"https://americanbazaaronline.com/2025/03/17/shohini-sinha-named-assistant-director-of-fbis-victim-services-division-460769","content":"Share\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\nEmail\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation has named Indian American special agent Shohini Sinha as the assistant director of the Victim Services Division. Sinha most recently served as the special agent in charge of the Salt Lake City Field Office.\nSinha joined the FBI as a special agent in 2001. She was first assigned to the Milwaukee Field Office, where she worked in counterterrorism investigations, according to an FBI press release. She also served temporary assignments at the Guantanamo Bay Naval Base, the FBI Legal Attaché Office in London, and the Baghdad Operations Center.\nRELATED: ‘Enemies list’ delays Kash Patel’s Senate confirmation as FBI director (February 7, 2025)\nSinha was promoted in 2009 to supervisory special agent and transferred to the Counterterrorism Division in Washington, D.C. She served as program manager of Canada-based extraterritorial investigations and facilitated liaison efforts with Washington-based Canadian liaison officers.\nIn 2012, Sinha was promoted to assistant legal attaché in Ottawa, Canada, working counterterrorism matters in collaboration with the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Canadian Security Intelligence Service.\nIn 2015, she was promoted to field supervisor in the Detroit Field Office, where she led squads responsible for investigating international terrorism matters.\nIn early 2020, Sinha transferred to the Cyber Intrusion squad, which worked both national security and criminal cyber intrusion matters. Later in 2020, she was promoted to assistant special agent in charge for national security matters, and later criminal matters, in the Portland Field Office.\nREAD: Kash Patel blasts FBI for ‘endangering his life’ (August 29, 2022)\nSinha was selected to serve as the executive special assistant to the director in 2021. She has been serving as the special agent in charge of the Salt Lake City Field Office since July of 2023.\nPrior to her employment with the FBI, Sinha worked as a therapist and later as an administrator for a private, not-for-profit clinic. She earned a bachelor’s degree in psychology and a master’s degree in mental health counseling from Purdue University in Indiana.\nFacebookShare on XLinkedInWhatsAppEmailCopy Link\nfbi Shohini Sinha Victim Services Division","content_cn":"分享\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\n电子邮件\n联邦调查局任命印度裔美国人、特别探员肖希妮·辛哈（Shohini Sinha）为受害者服务处助理主任。辛哈最近担任盐湖城外勤办事处特别探员主管。\n辛哈于2001年加入联邦调查局，成为特别探员。根据联邦调查局的一份新闻稿，她最初被派往密尔沃基外勤办事处，在那里从事反恐调查。她还曾临时派驻关塔那摩湾海军基地、联邦调查局驻伦敦法律专员办公室以及巴格达行动中心。\n相关报道：“敌人名单”推迟了卡什·帕特尔获参议院确认出任联邦调查局局长（2025年2月7日）\n2009年，辛哈晋升为主管特别探员，并调往位于华盛顿特区的反恐处。她曾担任加拿大境外调查项目经理，并协助与驻华盛顿的加拿大联络官开展联络工作。\n2012年，辛哈晋升为驻加拿大渥太华助理法律专员，与加拿大皇家骑警和加拿大安全情报局合作处理反恐事务。\n2015年，她晋升为底特律外勤办事处的外勤主管，领导负责调查国际恐怖主义事务的小组。\n2020年初，辛哈调入网络入侵小组，该小组同时处理国家安全和刑事网络入侵事务。2020年晚些时候，她晋升为波特兰外勤办事处负责国家安全事务、后来负责刑事事务的助理特别探员主管。\n阅读：卡什·帕特尔抨击联邦调查局“危及他的生命”（2022年8月29日）\n2021年，辛哈获选担任局长执行特别助理。自2023年7月以来，她一直担任盐湖城外勤办事处特别探员主管。\n在加入联邦调查局工作之前，辛哈曾担任治疗师，后来又担任一家私人非营利诊所的行政人员。她获得了印第安纳州普渡大学的心理学学士学位和心理健康咨询硕士学位。\n在Facebook上分享在X上分享LinkedInWhatsApp电子邮件复制链接\n联邦调查局 肖希妮·辛哈 受害者服务处","publish_source":"americanbazaaronline.com","publish_time":"2025-03-17T17:05:27+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2668","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部建立全国公民身份数据库","title_en":"Department of Homeland Security builds national citizenship database","summary_cn":"据报道，美国国土安全部首次建立了一个全国公民身份数据库，整合移民机构和社会保障局的信息，并与政府效率部合作。该数据库是SAVE项目的扩展。批评者警告其缺乏透明度，可能被滥用来针对无证移民和美国公民，引发隐私和公民权利担忧。","summary_en":"The Department of Homeland Security has reportedly built a national citizenship database for the first time, combining information from immigration agencies and the Social Security Administration, in collaboration with DOGE. The database is an expansion of the SAVE program. Critics warn it lacks transparency and could be misused to target undocumented immigrants and US citizens, raising privacy and civil rights concerns.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:51:01.864823+00:00","url":"https://americanbazaaronline.com/2025/07/01/department-of-homeland-security-builds-national-citizenship-database-464502","content":"Share\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\nEmail\nPresident Donald Trump and his administration are leaving no stone unturned when it comes to persecuting citizens of the United States. The Department of Homeland Security (DHS) has reportedly for the first time built a national citizenship database that combines information from immigration agencies and the Social Security Administration.\nThe DHS database was created in collaboration with the Department of Government Efficiency (DOGE), previously led by tech billionaire Elon Musk, in an effort to bridge the gaps between disparate information sources to make it easier to determine whether someone is a citizen, according to NPR, which first reported the details of the database.\nIn response to a request for comment, the DHS said: “Integration with the Social Security Administration (SSA) significantly improves the service offered by Save.”\nREAD: Immigrants will now have their social media posts monitored for antisemitism (April 10, 2025)\nThis database is the latest in a string of moves made by Trump to detain and deport citizens of the U.S. without due process.\nThe database is the result of an expansion of the Systematic Alien Verification for Entitlements (SAVE) program, made up of smaller databases within the homeland security department, and an integration with information from the Social Security Administration.\nWhat this database could lead to and how it could be misused is something that the government seems to be conveniently ignoring.\n“The premise of noncitizen voter fraud is one that officials, including President Trump, have used as a pretext to discredit and intimidate entire communities,” said Citlaly Mora, spokesperson for immigration legal project Just Futures Law.\n“This database is the latest iteration of Doge’s attempt to weaponize the data of the millions of people that live in the U.S. They are building this database without transparency and without consulting the public about how their data will be used, a brazen violation of our privacy rights. Given this administration’s track record of failing to follow proper processes, we should all be concerned.”\nTrump continues to adopt an aggressive stance on immigration, prioritizing large-scale deportations and stricter enforcement. His administration reinstated and expanded expedited removal procedures, allowing immigrants to be deported without court hearings.\nREAD: Biden removes Trump road block for poor immigrants (September 9, 2022)\nThrough Executive Order 14159, Trump directed federal agencies to cut funding to sanctuary cities, restricted public benefits for undocumented immigrants, and expanded local police cooperation with ICE under Section 287(g). Operation Safeguard—a multi-agency initiative—mobilizes ICE, National Guard units, and local law enforcement to detain and deport undocumented immigrants, especially those with prior criminal charges. The administration has used military aircraft to deport some migrants, and ICE operations have significantly increased since January.\nThe Trump administration’s creation of a centralized citizenship database marks a significant escalation in immigration enforcement. While officials claim it improves efficiency, critics warn it could be misused to target both undocumented immigrants and U.S. citizens without due process. The lack of transparency and public oversight raises serious privacy and civil rights concerns.\nCoupled with aggressive deportation policies and surveillance tactics, this system risks becoming a tool for widespread discrimination and intimidation. As technology and government power converge, it is crucial to demand accountability and safeguards to protect individual rights and prevent abuse against vulnerable communities across the country.\nFacebookShare on XLinkedInWhatsAppEmailCopy Link\nCitizenship Database civil liberties Department of Homeland Security (DHS) deportation immigration enforcement privacy rights Trump administration","content_cn":"分享\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\n电子邮件\n唐纳德·特朗普总统及其政府在迫害美国公民方面可谓无所不用其极。据报道，国土安全部（DHS）首次建立了一个全国公民身份数据库，将移民机构和社会保障局的信息结合起来。\n据首次报道该数据库详情的美国国家公共电台（NPR）称，DHS与政府效率部（DOGE）合作创建了这一数据库。DOGE此前由科技亿万富翁埃隆·马斯克领导，旨在弥合不同信息来源之间的空白，从而更容易确定某人是否为公民。\n针对置评请求，DHS表示：“与社会保障局（SSA）的整合显著改善了SAVE所提供的服务。”\n阅读：移民现在将因反犹主义而受到社交媒体帖子监控（2025年4月10日）\n这一数据库是特朗普一系列行动中的最新一步，这些行动旨在不经正当程序拘留和驱逐美国公民。\n该数据库源于对系统性外国人资格核验（SAVE）计划的扩展。该计划由国土安全部内部的多个较小数据库组成，并整合了社会保障局的信息。\n这一数据库可能导致什么后果，以及它可能被如何滥用，似乎是政府刻意忽视的问题。\n移民法律项目“正义未来法”（Just Futures Law）发言人西特拉莉·莫拉说：“非公民选民欺诈这一前提，是包括特朗普总统在内的官员用来诋毁和恐吓整个社区的借口。”\n“这一数据库是DOGE试图将居住在美国的数百万人的数据武器化的最新版本。他们在缺乏透明度、也未就数据如何使用征求公众意见的情况下建立这一数据库，这是对我们隐私权的公然侵犯。鉴于本届政府一贯未能遵循适当程序，我们都应对此感到担忧。”\n特朗普继续对移民采取强硬立场，将大规模驱逐和更严格的执法置于优先位置。他的政府恢复并扩大了快速驱逐程序，允许在没有法庭听证的情况下驱逐移民。\n阅读：拜登为贫困移民扫清特朗普设置的障碍（2022年9月9日）\n通过第14159号行政命令，特朗普指示联邦机构削减对庇护城市的资金，限制无证移民获得公共福利，并依据第287(g)条扩大地方警方与移民及海关执法局（ICE）的合作。“保障行动”（Operation Safeguard）是一项多机构倡议，动员ICE、国民警卫队部队和地方执法部门拘留并驱逐无证移民，尤其是那些此前曾被提出刑事指控的人。本届政府已使用军用飞机驱逐一些移民，自1月以来，ICE行动显著增加。\n特朗普政府建立集中式公民身份数据库，标志着移民执法力度的重大升级。官员们声称这能提高效率，但批评者警告称，它可能被滥用，在不经正当程序的情况下针对无证移民和美国公民。缺乏透明度和公众监督，引发了严重的隐私与公民权利担忧。\n再加上激进的驱逐政策和监控手段，这一系统有沦为广泛歧视和恐吓工具的风险。随着技术与政府权力汇合，要求问责并建立保障措施至关重要，以保护个人权利，防止全国各地的弱势社区遭受侵害。\nFacebook在X上分享LinkedInWhatsApp电子邮件复制链接\n公民身份数据库 公民自由 国土安全部（DHS）驱逐 移民执法 隐私权 特朗普政府","publish_source":"americanbazaaronline.com","publish_time":"2025-07-01T18:17:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1990","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"劳拉·卢默称FBI局长卡什·帕特尔为“奴隶”？","title_en":"Laura Loomer calls FBI Director Kash Patel a slave?","summary_cn":"极右翼人物劳拉·卢默在社交平台X上抨击美国联邦调查局（FBI）局长卡什·帕特尔访问卡塔尔并签署两份谅解备忘录，指责其无视卡塔尔对印度移民工人的待遇，并称其与资助哈马斯等极端组织的政府往来。文章介绍了帕特尔与卡塔尔内政大臣的会晤内容，以及卢默的背景和帕特尔的履历。","summary_en":"Far-right figure Laura Loomer attacked FBI Director Kash Patel on X over his visit to Qatar and the signing of two memoranda of understanding, accusing him of ignoring Qatar's treatment of Indian migrant workers and engaging with a government she claims funds extremist groups. The article details Patel's meeting with Qatar's interior minister and provides background on both Loomer and Patel.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:00:39.039724+00:00","url":"https://americanbazaaronline.com/2025/12/10/laura-loomer-calls-fbi-director-kash-patel-a-slave-471359","content":"Share\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\nEmail\nFar-right personality Laura Loomer insulted FBI Director Kash Patel after his recent deals with the Saudis. Loomer criticized Patel after he signed two Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs) with Qatar’s Ministry of Interior during an official visit to Doha.\nLoomer accused Patel of turning a blind eye to Qatar’s alleged treatment of Indian migrant workers and slammed him for engaging with a government she claims bankrolls extremist groups like Hamas.\nLoomer said on X: “You are an Indian. Do you know the Qataris make Indians like you slaves under Kafala? They build their buildings with Indian slave labor. Did you tell the Qataris to stop enslaving your people and funding terrorists? This is just so shameful… I advocated for you and now you’re in Qatar.” She added that Patel’s presence in Doha was a “let down.”\nPatel met Sheikh Khalifa bin Hamad bin Khalifa Al-Thani, Qatar’s Minister of Interior and Commander of the Internal Security Force on Tuesday, where both sides signed agreements aimed at strengthening cooperation on training, intelligence sharing, and capacity building.\nREAD: Kash Patel vows to hunt down those who seek to harm Americans (February 21, 2025)\nLaura Loomer is an American political activist and media personality known for her far-right views and confrontational style. Born on May 21, 1993, in Tucson, Arizona, she graduated from Barry University in 2015 with a degree in broadcast journalism. Loomer first gained national attention through online activism and her involvement with conservative media organizations.\nShe became widely known for public disruptions, protests, and commentary targeting immigration policies, tech companies, and political opponents. Her rhetoric led to bans from several major social-media and payment platforms, including Twitter (now X), Facebook, and PayPal, due to violations of their content rules. Loomer ran twice for the U.S. House of Representatives in Florida, in 2020 and 2022, but did not win either race.\nShe warned that this unusual partnership will result in the “Islamification of our country and Islamic terrorists endangering the lives of Americans.”\nREAD: FBI cuts ties with Anti-Defamation League following conservative backlash (October 3, 2025)\nKash Patel became the ninth Director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) when he was sworn in on Feb. 21, after a narrow 51-49 Senate confirmation vote. Patel, a native of Garden City, New York, holds a bachelor’s degree in criminal justice and history from the University of Richmond, a juris doctor from law school, and a certificate in international law from the University College London Faculty of Laws. Before leading the FBI, he served as a public defender, a national-security prosecutor at the U.S. Department of Justice, and in staff roles on congressional intelligence committees. His appointment drew major attention because of his previous work in politically aligned roles and his longstanding criticism of the bureau.\nThe recent interaction between Loomer and Patel underscores the tension between federal officials and far-right activists over international security partnerships. Patel’s visit to Qatar and the signing of two Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs) focused on training, intelligence sharing, and capacity building.\nWhile Patel’s actions represent official diplomatic and security cooperation, public perception is shaped by partisan commentary and social media amplification.\nFacebookShare on XLinkedInWhatsAppEmailCopy Link\nFBI director Kafala system Kash Patel Laura Loomer Memoranda of Understanding migrant workers Qatar visit","content_cn":"分享\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\n电子邮件\n极右翼人物Laura Loomer在FBI局长Kash Patel最近与沙特方面达成交易后侮辱了他。Loomer批评Patel在正式访问多哈期间与卡塔尔内政部签署了两份谅解备忘录（MoU）。\nLoomer指责Patel对卡塔尔据称对待印度移民工人的方式视而不见，并抨击他与一个她声称资助哈马斯等极端组织的政府打交道。\nLoomer在X上说：“你是印度人。你知道卡塔尔人在卡法拉制度下把像你这样的印度人变成奴隶吗？他们用印度奴隶劳工建造他们的建筑。你有没有告诉卡塔尔人停止奴役你们的人民和资助恐怖分子？这太可耻了……我曾为你发声，而现在你在卡塔尔。”她补充说，Patel出现在多哈令人“失望”。\n周二，Patel会见了卡塔尔内政部长兼国内安全部队司令Sheikh Khalifa bin Hamad bin Khalifa Al-Thani，双方签署了旨在加强培训、情报共享和能力建设合作的协议。\n阅读：Kash Patel誓言追捕那些试图伤害美国人的人（2025年2月21日）\nLaura Loomer是一名美国政治活动人士和媒体人物，以其极右翼观点和对抗性风格而闻名。她于1993年5月21日出生于亚利桑那州图森市，2015年毕业于Barry University，获得广播新闻学学位。Loomer最初通过网络行动主义及其参与保守派媒体组织而获得全国关注。\n她因针对移民政策、科技公司和政治对手的公开扰乱、抗议和评论而广为人知。由于违反这些平台的内容规则，她的言论导致她被多个主要社交媒体和支付平台封禁，包括Twitter（现为X）、Facebook和PayPal。Loomer曾于2020年和2022年两度竞选佛罗里达州联邦众议员，但两次均未获胜。\n她警告称，这种不寻常的合作关系将导致“我们国家的伊斯兰化，以及伊斯兰恐怖分子危及美国人的生命”。\n阅读：保守派反弹后，FBI切断与反诽谤联盟的关系（2025年10月3日）\nKash Patel在2月21日以参议院51票对49票的微弱确认票数宣誓就任，成为联邦调查局（FBI）第九任局长。Patel出生于纽约州Garden City，拥有里士满大学刑事司法和历史学学士学位、法学院法学博士学位，以及伦敦大学学院法学院国际法证书。在领导FBI之前，他曾担任公设辩护人、美国司法部国家安全检察官，并在国会情报委员会担任工作人员。他的任命因其此前在政治立场一致的职位上任职，以及长期批评该局，而引起广泛关注。\nLoomer与Patel最近的互动突显了联邦官员与极右翼活动人士在国际安全伙伴关系问题上的紧张关系。Patel访问卡塔尔并签署两份谅解备忘录（MoU），重点涉及培训、情报共享和能力建设。\n尽管Patel的行动代表正式的外交与安全合作，公众看法仍受到党派评论和社交媒体放大的影响。\nFacebook 在X上分享 LinkedIn WhatsApp 电子邮件 复制链接\nFBI局长 卡法拉制度 Kash Patel Laura Loomer 谅解备忘录 移民工人 卡塔尔访问","publish_source":"americanbazaaronline.com","publish_time":"2025-12-10T18:26:01+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1942","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"联邦调查局副局长辞职，未透露原因","title_en":"FBI Deputy Director steps down, does not reveal reason","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局副局长丹·邦吉诺表示将于明年1月离职，但未说明原因。邦吉诺于2025年3月17日在局长卡什·帕特尔手下就任，此前由特朗普总统于2025年2月任命。他在社交媒体发文中感谢特朗普、司法部长邦迪和局长帕特尔。邦吉诺曾任纽约市警察局警官和美国特勤局特工，后成为保守派媒体人物，其非传统晋升路径引发关注。文章还讨论了高层人事变动对联邦调查局战略重点和公众看法可能产生的影响。","summary_en":"FBI Deputy Director Dan Bongino said he will leave his role in January but did not reveal why. Bongino joined the FBI's senior leadership under Director Kash Patel on March 17, 2025, after being appointed by President Donald Trump in February 2025. In a social media post, he thanked Trump, Attorney General Pam Bondi and Director Patel. A former NYPD officer and Secret Service agent turned conservative media figure, Bongino's nontraditional path drew attention. The article also discusses how senior leadership changes may affect the bureau's strategic priorities and public perception.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:40:57.546312+00:00","url":"https://americanbazaaronline.com/2025/12/18/fbi-deputy-director-steps-down-does-not-reveal-reason-471831","content":"Share\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\nEmail\nThe leadership at the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) has been shaken up. Dan Bongino has said he will leave his role as the FBI’s deputy director in January.\nDan Bongino (born December 4, 1974) is an American law-enforcement veteran, conservative political commentator, and the 20th Deputy Director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI). He joined the FBI’s senior leadership under Director Kash Patel on March 17, 2025, after being appointed by President Donald Trump in February 2025. The deputy director is the bureau’s second-highest official, assisting the director in overseeing day-to-day operations and management of the FBI.\nAnnouncing his decision to step down in Wednesday’s social media post, Bongino wrote: “I will be leaving my position with the FBI in January. I want to thank President Trump, AG [Pam] Bondi, and Director [Kash] Patel for the opportunity to serve with purpose.\nREAD: Laura Loomer calls FBI Director Kash Patel a slave? (December 10, 2025)\n“Most importantly, I want to thank you, my fellow Americans, for the privilege to serve you. God bless America, and all those who defend her.”\nBefore his appointment, Bongino served as a New York City Police Department officer from 1995 to 1999 and later as a special agent with the U.S. Secret Service from 1999 to 2011. During his Secret Service career, he worked on criminal investigations, served as an instructor, and was assigned to the Presidential Protective Division, helping protect Presidents George W. Bush and Barack Obama. After leaving government service, he became a prominent conservative media figure, hosting “The Dan Bongino Show” and running unsuccessfully for Congress several times.\nBongino’s appointment drew attention because he did not rise through the FBI as a career agent.\nIn a post on X, he thanked President Trump, as well as the director of the FBI and the U.S. attorney general “for the opportunity to serve with purpose.” Bongino did not say in his post why he was stepping down.\nREAD: FBI cuts ties with Anti-Defamation League following conservative backlash (October 3, 2025)\nBongino’s tenure as Deputy Director of the FBI has been brief but highly visible, drawing attention due to his nontraditional path from media into one of the bureau’s top leadership positions. His announcement that he plans to step down in January underscores the evolving nature of leadership within the FBI and the challenges faced by senior officials navigating both public scrutiny and internal responsibilities. Bongino’s career reflects a blend of law enforcement experience, federal service, and public commentary, highlighting the diverse backgrounds that can intersect with national security leadership roles.\nChanges in senior leadership, such as Bongino’s planned departure, often prompt discussions about the FBI’s strategic priorities and internal direction. The bureau relies on continuity and experience at the top levels to maintain effective operations across its field offices and investigative divisions. While the agency has a long history of adapting to new challenges, transitions in leadership can temporarily affect decision-making and public perception. Observers will be watching closely to see how the bureau navigates the period following Bongino’s resignation and whether any new appointments will signal shifts in organizational focus or policy emphasis.\nFacebookShare on XLinkedInWhatsAppEmailCopy Link\nBongino resignation Dan Bongino Donald Trump FBI Deputy Director Federal Bureau of Investigation Kash Patel","content_cn":"分享\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\n电子邮件\n美国联邦调查局（FBI）的领导层发生变动。丹·邦吉诺表示，他将于1月卸任FBI副局长一职。\n丹·邦吉诺（生于1974年12月4日）是美国执法界资深人士、保守派政治评论员，也是美国联邦调查局（FBI）第20任副局长。他于2025年2月被总统唐纳德·特朗普任命，并于2025年3月17日在局长卡什·帕特尔领导下加入FBI高层领导团队。副局长是该局的第二高官员，协助局长监督FBI的日常运营和管理。\n邦吉诺在周三的社交媒体帖子中宣布了卸任决定，他写道：“我将于1月离开FBI的职位。我要感谢特朗普总统、司法部长[帕姆]邦迪以及局长[卡什]帕特尔给予我带着使命感服务的机会。\n阅读：劳拉·卢默称FBI局长卡什·帕特尔是奴隶？（2025年12月10日）\n“最重要的是，我要感谢你们，我的美国同胞们，感谢你们给予我为您们服务的殊荣。上帝保佑美国，保佑所有捍卫她的人。”\n在被任命之前，邦吉诺于1995年至1999年担任纽约市警察局警官，随后于1999年至2011年担任美国特勤局特工。在特勤局任职期间，他从事刑事调查工作，担任教官，并被分配到总统保护处，协助保护乔治·W·布什总统和巴拉克·奥巴马总统。离开政府服务后，他成为知名的保守派媒体人物，主持《丹·邦吉诺秀》，并多次竞选国会议员但未成功。\n邦吉诺的任命引起关注，因为他并非作为职业特工在FBI内部逐级晋升。\n在X平台上的一篇帖子中，他感谢了特朗普总统，以及FBI局长和美国司法部长“给予我带着使命感服务的机会”。邦吉诺在帖子中没有说明他卸任的原因。\n阅读：FBI在保守派强烈反对后切断与反诽谤联盟的关系（2025年10月3日）\n邦吉诺担任FBI副局长的任期短暂但备受瞩目，因其从媒体进入该局最高领导层之一的非传统路径而引发关注。他宣布计划于1月卸任，凸显了FBI领导层的演变性质，以及高级官员在应对公众审视和内部职责时所面临的挑战。邦吉诺的职业生涯体现了执法经验、联邦服务和公共评论的结合，凸显了可与国家安全领导角色产生交集的多元背景。\n高级领导层的变动，如邦吉诺计划中的离职，往往会引发关于FBI战略优先事项和内部方向的讨论。该局依赖高层的连续性和经验，以维持其各外地办事处和调查部门的有效运作。尽管该机构在适应新挑战方面有着悠久历史，但领导层的过渡可能会暂时影响决策和公众认知。观察人士将密切关注该局在邦吉诺辞职后如何度过这一时期，以及任何新任命是否会预示组织重点或政策重心的转变。\nFacebook在X上分享LinkedInWhatsApp电子邮件复制链接\n邦吉诺辞职 丹·邦吉诺 唐纳德·特朗普 FBI副局长 联邦调查局 卡什·帕特尔","publish_source":"americanbazaaronline.com","publish_time":"2025-12-18T16:49:36+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1878","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"丹·邦吉诺在短暂且充满争议的任期后离开联邦调查局","title_en":"Dan Bongino leaves FBI post after a brief, controversial tenure","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局副局长丹·邦吉诺在任职不到一年后离职，成为近年任期最短的副局长之一。他于2025年12月宣布离任，称是个人决定。批评者指其缺乏联邦调查局经验，担忧其任命加深该局政治化印象。局长卡什·帕特尔公开赞扬其贡献。邦吉诺离任后，安德鲁·贝利成为该局仅剩的副局长。","summary_en":"FBI Deputy Director Dan Bongino left his post after less than a year, one of the shortest tenures in recent memory. He announced his exit in December 2025, calling it a personal decision. Critics cited his lack of FBI experience and warned his appointment deepened perceptions of politicization. Director Kash Patel publicly praised his contributions. With Bongino gone, Andrew Bailey remains the Bureau's sole deputy director.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:20:05.932552+00:00","url":"https://americanbazaaronline.com/2026/01/05/dan-bongino-leaves-fbi-post-after-a-brief-controversial-tenure-472614","content":"Share\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\nEmail\nDan Bongino’s departure adds to the sense of churn at the top of the FBI. Serving less than a year as deputy director, his stint stands out as one of the shortest in recent memory. He signaled his exit in December 2025, framing the move as a personal decision to step away from government and re-enter civilian life. Still, the timing underscores how unsettled the Bureau’s leadership has been, even as it faces heightened scrutiny and political pressure.\nHis brief tenure was dogged by questions that never fully went away. Critics repeatedly pointed to his lack of prior FBI experience, while others warned that his appointment risked deepening perceptions of politicization inside the bureau. Those concerns were not limited to partisan critics, drawing scrutiny from lawmakers as well as unease among career officials within the agency.\n“It was a busy last day on the job. This will be my last post on this account…Tomorrow I return to civilian life. It’s been an incredible year thanks to the leadership and decisiveness of President Trump. It was the honor of a lifetime to work with Director Patel, and to serve you, the American people. See you on the other side,” Bongino wrote on X, while highlighting his experience as well as showering praise on FBI Director Kash Patel.\nREAD: Laura Loomer calls FBI Director Kash Patel a slave? (December 10, 2025)\nEven so, Bongino received a public show of support from Patel, who praised his impact in a post on X. Patel said Bongino helped “orchestrate a record year” for the FBI, pointing to efforts that disrupted 1,800 gangs and criminal enterprises, located thousands of child victims, and led to the seizure of more than 2,000 kilos of fentanyl, among other outcomes.\n“FBI is saving lives, protecting innocent kids, and taking deadly drugs off our streets at levels not seen in decades. None of it would’ve been possible without Dan’s leadership and support. And he paved the way for even better things to come,” Patel wrote, thanking Bongino.\nWhy did Don Bongino suddenly quit FBI?\nBongino’s background also set him apart from his predecessors. A former Secret Service agent, he came into the job without any prior experience at the FBI before being tapped by Trump for the Bureau’s No. 2 role. According to the FBI Agents Association, the position had been filled by a career FBI official for more than a century before Bongino, making his appointment a sharp break from long-standing tradition.\nREAD: FBI cuts ties with Anti-Defamation League following conservative backlash (October 3, 2025)\nMedia reports, citing current and former officials, pointed to growing frustration among career agents over the leadership style of Patel and Bongino, including their approach to decision-making and public messaging. Some officials questioned whether the two fully grasped the Bureau’s culture and operational norms. That internal unease was compounded by sustained scrutiny from lawmakers and commentators, reinforcing a broader perception of instability and dissatisfaction within the FBI during their time in senior roles.\nBongino has also spoke openly about the personal cost of the job. In an earlier interview with Fox News, he said the role had taken a heavy toll on his private life. “I gave up everything for this,” Bongino said, describing the long hours he and Patel were putting in. “I stare at these four walls all day in DC, by myself, divorced from my wife, not divorced, but I mean separated, and it’s hard. I mean, we love each other, and it’s hard to be apart,” he added.\nWith Bongino now out of the picture, the leadership structure shifts again. Andrew Bailey, who was appointed co-deputy director in September 2025, is left as the Bureau’s remaining deputy director, marking another transition at the top as the FBI seeks stability.\nFacebookShare on XLinkedInWhatsAppEmailCopy Link\nDan Bongino Donald Trump FBI Agents Association FBI Deputy Director FBI leadership Kash Patel","content_cn":"分享\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\n电子邮件\n\n丹·邦吉诺的离任进一步加剧了联邦调查局高层的人事动荡。他担任副局长不到一年，这段任期成为近来最短的任期之一。他在2025年12月发出离职信号，将这一决定描述为个人选择：离开政府，重新回归平民生活。然而，离任时机凸显出，即使联邦调查局面临更严格的审查和政治压力，其领导层仍有多么不稳定。\n\n他的短暂任期一直受到一些始终未能完全消退的质疑困扰。批评者反复指出他此前缺乏联邦调查局经验，另一些人则警告称，他的任命可能加深外界对该局内部政治化的看法。这些担忧并不局限于党派批评者，国会议员以及该机构内部的职业官员也对此进行了审视并感到不安。\n\n邦吉诺在X上写道：“这是忙碌的最后一个工作日。这将是我在这个账号上的最后一篇帖子……明天我将回归平民生活。感谢特朗普总统的领导和果断，这一年令人难以置信。能与局长帕特尔共事、为美国人民服务，是一生的荣誉。我们彼岸再见。”他在强调自身经历的同时，也大力赞扬了联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔。\n\n阅读：劳拉·卢默称联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔为奴隶？（2025年12月10日）\n\n即便如此，邦吉诺仍获得了帕特尔公开表达的支持。帕特尔在X上的一篇帖子中称赞了他的影响力。帕特尔说，邦吉诺帮助联邦调查局“创下了创纪录的一年”，包括挫败1800个帮派和犯罪组织、找到数千名儿童受害者，以及查扣超过2000公斤芬太尼等成果。\n\n帕特尔写道：“联邦调查局正在以数十年来未见的程度挽救生命、保护无辜儿童，并将致命毒品从我们的街道上清除。如果没有丹的领导和支持，这一切都不可能实现。而且，他为未来更好的成果铺平了道路。”他向邦吉诺表示感谢。\n\n丹·邦吉诺为何突然辞去联邦调查局职务？\n\n邦吉诺的背景也使他区别于前任。他曾是特勤局特工，在被特朗普选中担任该局二号人物之前，没有任何联邦调查局工作经验。据联邦调查局特工协会称，在邦吉诺之前，该职位一个多世纪以来一直由职业联邦调查局官员担任，因此他的任命彻底打破了长期传统。\n\n阅读：联邦调查局在保守派反弹后与反诽谤联盟断绝关系（2025年10月3日）\n\n媒体援引现任和前任官员的话称，职业特工对帕特尔和邦吉诺的领导方式日益感到沮丧，包括他们在决策和对外沟通方面的做法。一些官员质疑两人是否真正理解联邦调查局的文化和行动规范。这种内部不安又因国会议员和评论员持续审查而加剧，进一步强化了外界对两人在高级职位任职期间联邦调查局不稳定和不满情绪的广泛看法。\n\n邦吉诺也曾公开谈到这份工作的个人代价。在此前接受福克斯新闻采访时，他说这份工作给自己的私人生活带来了沉重负担。“我为此放弃了一切，”邦吉诺说，并描述了他和帕特尔长时间工作的情况。他补充说：“我整天一个人盯着华盛顿特区的这四面墙，和妻子分开了，不是离婚，我是说分居，这很难。我的意思是，我们彼此相爱，但分开很难。”\n\n如今邦吉诺离开，领导层结构再次发生变化。安德鲁·贝利于2025年9月被任命为共同副局长，目前成为联邦调查局仅剩的副局长，标志着该局高层又一次交接，而联邦调查局正寻求稳定。\n\nFacebook\n在X上分享\nLinkedIn\nWhatsApp\n电子邮件\n复制链接\n\n丹·邦吉诺 唐纳德·特朗普 联邦调查局特工协会 联邦调查局副局长 联邦调查局领导层 卡什·帕特尔","publish_source":"americanbazaaronline.com","publish_time":"2026-01-05T17:05:05+00:00"}},{"id":"news-418","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"劳拉·卢默称“我想成为新任国土安全部长”","title_en":"‘I would like to be the new DHS Secretary,’ says Laura Loomer","summary_cn":"活动人士劳拉·卢默在X平台公开呼吁特朗普总统撤换现任国土安全部长马克韦恩·穆林，由她接任，并承诺将移民和海关执法局改造成“准军事力量”以加速大规模驱逐。她批评国土安全部现有领导层执行强硬移民政策不够迅速。文章还提到穆林此前在州长协会活动上区分合法与非法入境、暗示调整就业签证的言论引发强硬派不满。白宫和国土安全部未就此正式回应。","summary_en":"Activist Laura Loomer publicly urged President Donald Trump on X to replace current Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin with her, promising to turn ICE into a 'paramilitary force' to speed up mass deportations. She claimed DHS leadership has failed to execute the administration's hardline immigration agenda quickly enough. The article also notes Mullin's earlier remarks at a National Governors Association event distinguishing legal from illegal entry and floating employment-visa adjustments, which drew criticism from hardliners. Neither the White House nor DHS issued formal responses.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:45:46.727914+00:00","url":"https://americanbazaaronline.com/2026/08/06/i-would-like-to-be-the-new-dhs-secretary-says-laura-loomer-485913","content":"Share\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\nEmail\nActivist and social media personality Laura Loomer has launched a public push to take over leadership of the Department of Homeland Security (DHS), urging President Donald Trump to replace current Secretary Markwayne Mullin with a far more aggressive approach to border enforcement.\nPosting publicly on X, Loomer “promises” to convert Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) into a “paramilitary force” to speed up mass deportations.\nShe claimed that existing leadership at DHS has failed to execute the administration’s hardline anti-immigration platform with sufficient speed or intensity, challenging that she “will get the job done.”\nNetizens under her post have mixed reactions and opinions to Loomer’s statement.\nWhile some criticize her actions, calling her “crazy” arguing she is on the wrong side of the issue, others are calling her brave and promising their votes to her.\nREAD: Laura Loomer brands Marjorie Taylor Greene ‘traitor’ over new movement (August 2, 2026)\nThe public pitch showcases an escalating dispute among conservative political figures over the nation’s immigration priorities.\nThis directly relates to activists focusing much of their criticism on Mullin, a former U.S. senator from Oklahoma and Cherokee Nation citizen who was appointed to lead the agency earlier this year.\nHardline conservative commentators, including Steve Bannon and Loomer, voiced their opposition towards Mullin after he spoke at a National Governors Association gathering in Oklahoma City.\nIn his address, he suggested distinguishing between legal and illegal entry and floated potential adjustments to employment-based visa programs to address labor shortages.\nCritics labeled the remarks overly permissive, while Mullin maintained that he remains committed to strict border security and removing undocumented immigrants.\nLoomer argued that Mullin had failed to drive rapid increases in deportation numbers.\nDespite the internal political debate, federal authorities have continued large-scale immigration sweeps.\nAlthough Loomer holds no official government post, she has maintained a visible profile among administration supporters, frequently visiting Mar-a-Lago and traveling alongside high-profile political figures.\nREAD: Marjorie Taylor Greene highlights rise in medical tourism as Americans seek treatment abroad (June 18, 2026)\nShe has previously spearheaded public social media campaigns against administration personnel that coincided with high-level staff exits and revoked nominations.\nTrump has publicly described Loomer as a dedicated supporter, while acknowledging that he considers input from various outside allies on personnel choices.\nLoomer’s public career has long drawn scrutiny over her use of incendiary rhetoric and conspiracy theories, which previously led to bans across major social platforms before her account on X was restored.\nNeither the White House nor DHS representatives issued formal statements responding directly to Loomer’s public campaign.\nWhether her post will prompt official consideration remains unconfirmed, but the public dispute underscores the mounting pressure from immigration hardliners demanding stricter enforcement across federal agencies.\nFacebookShare on XLinkedInWhatsAppEmailCopy Link\nDHS Secretary Donald Trump ICE deportation policy Laura Loomer Markwayne Mullin","content_cn":"分享\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\n电子邮件\n活动人士兼社交媒体人物劳拉·卢默已发起公开行动，争取接管国土安全部（DHS）的领导权，敦促唐纳德·特朗普总统撤换现任部长马克韦恩·马林，并采取对边境执法更为激进的方式。\n\n卢默在X上公开发帖，“承诺”将移民与海关执法局（ICE）改造成一支“准军事部队”，以加快大规模驱逐出境。\n\n她声称，国土安全部现有领导层未能以足够的速度或力度落实政府强硬的反移民纲领，并表示她“会把事情办成”。\n\n她帖文下的网民对卢默的声明反应和看法不一。\n\n一些人批评她的行为，称她“疯狂”，认为她站错了立场；另一些人则称她勇敢，并承诺会投票给她。\n\n阅读：劳拉·卢默因新运动称玛乔丽·泰勒·格林为“叛徒”（2026年8月2日）\n\n这番公开表态凸显了保守派政治人物之间围绕美国移民政策优先事项不断升级的争端。\n\n这与活动人士将大部分批评集中在马林身上直接相关。马林曾任来自俄克拉何马州的美国参议员，也是切罗基民族公民，今年早些时候被任命领导该机构。\n\n包括史蒂夫·班农和卢默在内的强硬保守派评论人士，在马林于俄克拉何马城举行的全国州长协会聚会上发表讲话后，表达了对他的反对。\n\n他在讲话中建议区分合法与非法入境，并提出可能调整就业类签证项目，以应对劳动力短缺。\n\n批评者称这些言论过于宽松，而马林坚持表示，他仍致力于严格的边境安全和遣返无证移民。\n\n卢默认为，马林未能推动驱逐人数迅速增加。\n\n尽管存在内部政治争论，联邦当局仍持续开展大规模移民突击搜查。\n\n尽管卢默并无任何正式政府职务，她仍在政府支持者中保持显著影响力，经常造访海湖庄园，并与知名政治人物一同出行。\n\n阅读：玛乔丽·泰勒·格林强调医疗旅游兴起，美国人赴海外寻求治疗（2026年6月18日）\n\n她此前曾主导针对政府人员的公开社交媒体活动，这些活动恰逢高级工作人员离职及提名被撤销。\n\n特朗普曾公开称卢默是忠诚的支持者，同时承认他会考虑各种外部盟友对人事选择的意见。\n\n卢默的公开职业生涯长期因使用煽动性言辞和阴谋论而受到审视；这些行为此前导致她被多个主要社交平台封禁，之后她的X账号恢复。\n\n白宫和国土安全部代表均未就卢默的公开行动直接发表正式声明。\n\n她的帖文是否会促使官方考虑仍未得到确认，但这场公开争端凸显了移民强硬派日益加大的压力，他们要求各联邦机构采取更严格的执法措施。\n\nFacebook在X上分享LinkedInWhatsApp电子邮件复制链接\n\n国土安全部部长 唐纳德·特朗普 ICE 驱逐出境政策 劳拉·卢默 马克韦恩·马林","publish_source":"americanbazaaronline.com","publish_time":"2026-08-06T16:02:42+00:00"}},{"id":"news-222","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国公民及移民服务局纪念9·11袭击25周年","title_en":"USCIS marks 25th anniversary of September 11 attacks","summary_cn":"美国公民及移民服务局（USCIS）纪念9·11袭击25周年，缅怀近3000名遇难者及救援人员。该局在社交平台X发文称袭击“永远改变了美国”，并表示将继续通过维护合法移民体系完整性来承担责任。USCIS于2003年作为国土安全部的一部分成立，负责管理合法移民和入籍体系。全美各地举行了纪念仪式和默哀活动。","summary_en":"U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS) marked the 25th anniversary of the September 11 attacks, honoring nearly 3,000 victims and first responders. In a post on X, USCIS said the attacks \"forever changed America\" and pledged to safeguard the integrity of the lawful immigration system. USCIS was established in 2003 as part of the Department of Homeland Security. Memorial ceremonies and moments of silence were held across the United States.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T19:56:47.718059+00:00","url":"https://americanbazaaronline.com/2026/09/11/uscis-marks-25th-anniversary-of-september-11-attacks-487966","content":"Share\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\nEmail\nThe U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS) marked the 25th anniversary of the September 11 attacks on Friday, honoring the nearly 3,000 people killed and the first responders, service members and public servants who responded to the tragedy.\nIn a post on X, USCIS said the attacks “forever changed America” and reshaped how the country protects its homeland.\n“Today, as we mark the 25th anniversary of the September 11, we remember the nearly 3,000 lives lost and honor the courage of the first responders, service members, public servants, and everyday Americans who answered tragedy with bravery and resolve,” the agency said.\nREAD: No more 60 days? DHS targets H-1B, L-1 and other foreign workers (September 10, 2026)\nUSCIS said the anniversary also carries significance for its work overseeing the country’s lawful immigration system.\n“At USCIS, we carry that responsibility forward by safeguarding the integrity of our lawful immigration system and serving the American people with vigilance and purpose,” the agency said.\nThe agency ended its message with: “We remember. We honor. We will never forget.”\nThe September 11, 2001, attacks killed 2,977 people when al-Qaida terrorists hijacked four commercial aircraft and crashed them into the World Trade Center in New York, the Pentagon in Virginia and a field near Shanksville, Pennsylvania. The attacks fundamentally altered U.S. national security, immigration and foreign policy.\nREAD: DHS changes green card rules for children born to foreign government employees (September 5, 2026)\nUSCIS was established in 2003 as part of the Department of Homeland Security following the restructuring of the federal government after the September 11 attacks. Its responsibilities include administering the country’s lawful immigration and naturalization system.\nAcross the United States on Friday, communities held memorial ceremonies, moments of silence and readings of victims’ names to mark the 25th anniversary. At the National September 11 Memorial in New York, seven moments of silence were observed, including a new tribute to people who later died from illnesses linked to exposure to toxic debris after the attacks.\nThe anniversary has also renewed attention to the long-term consequences of September 11, including the health impact on first responders and survivors and the broader changes to U.S. security policies that followed the attacks.\nFacebookShare on XLinkedInWhatsAppEmailCopy Link\n9/11 attacks 9/11 first responders September 11 anniversary September 11 victims U.S. immigration system USCIS","content_cn":"分享\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nPinterest\n电子邮件\n美国公民及移民服务局（USCIS）于周五纪念9月11日袭击事件25周年，缅怀近3,000名遇难者，以及应对这场悲剧的急救人员、军人和公共服务人员。\nUSCIS在X平台的一则帖子中表示，这些袭击“永远改变了美国”，并重塑了该国保护国土的方式。\n该机构表示：“今天，在我们纪念9月11日25周年之际，我们缅怀近3,000名逝去的生命，并致敬以勇气和坚毅回应这场悲剧的急救人员、军人、公共服务人员和普通美国人的勇气。”\n阅读：不再是60天？国土安全部瞄准H-1B、L-1及其他外国劳动者（2026年9月10日）\nUSCIS表示，这一周年纪念对其监督国家合法移民体系的工作也具有重要意义。\n该机构表示：“在USCIS，我们通过维护合法移民体系的完整性，并以警觉和使命感服务美国人民，来延续这一责任。”\n该机构以如下文字结束其讯息：“我们铭记。我们致敬。我们永不忘记。”\n2001年9月11日，基地组织恐怖分子劫持四架商用飞机，撞向纽约世界贸易中心、弗吉尼亚州五角大楼及宾夕法尼亚州尚克斯维尔附近的一处田野，造成2,977人死亡。这些袭击从根本上改变了美国的国家安全、移民和外交政策。\n阅读：国土安全部修改外国政府雇员所生子女的绿卡规则（2026年9月5日）\nUSCIS于2003年在9月11日袭击事件后联邦政府重组期间，作为国土安全部的一部分成立。其职责包括管理国家的合法移民和入籍体系。\n周五，全美各地社区举行纪念仪式、默哀和受害者姓名宣读活动，以纪念25周年。在纽约国家9月11日纪念馆，举行了七次默哀，其中包括一项新的悼念活动，纪念袭击后因接触有毒残骸相关疾病而去世的人们。\n此次周年纪念也重新引发了对9月11日长期后果的关注，包括对急救人员和幸存者的健康影响，以及袭击后美国安全政策发生的更广泛变化。\nFacebook 在X上分享 LinkedIn WhatsApp 电子邮件 复制链接\n9/11袭击 9/11急救人员 9月11日周年纪念 9月11日受害者 美国移民体系 USCIS","publish_source":"americanbazaaronline.com","publish_time":"2026-09-11T18:21:13+00:00"}},{"id":"news-575","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"“我被冻住了”——洛杉矶无证男子面临国土安全部180万美元罚款","title_en":"'I Was Frozen' -- Undocumented LA Man Faces $1.8 Million DHS Penalty | ACoM","summary_cn":"美国社区媒体ACoM报道，洛杉矶一名来自墨西哥的无证移民“安赫尔”收到国土安全部（DHS）信件，因其未遵守驱逐令被处以180万美元罚款，按每日998美元、五年法定最低标准计算。报道称联邦政府已向全国逾6.5万名移民发出类似信件，总额约360亿美元，依据是1996年一项极少使用的法律。安赫尔因早年误信“公证人”而错过抗辩，如今担心资产被扣押、工资被扣发及家庭被拆散。","summary_en":"American Community Media reports that an undocumented Los Angeles man from Mexico, identified as Ángel, received a Department of Homeland Security letter imposing a $1.8 million fine for failing to comply with a deportation order, calculated at $998 per day with a five-year statutory minimum. The report says the federal government has sent more than 65,000 such letters nationwide, totaling roughly $36 billion, under a rarely used 1996 law. Ángel, who was misled by a notario years ago, now fears asset seizure, wage garnishment and family separation.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:03:46.589634+00:00","url":"https://americancommunitymedia.org/immigration/i-was-frozen-undocumented-la-man-faces-1-8-million-dhs-penalty","content":"ImmigrationNews Exchange\n‘I Was Frozen’ — Undocumented LA Man Faces $1.8 Million DHS Penalty\nBy Araceli Martinez\nJul 17, 2026\nImage published under CC License 1.0\nShare\nFacebookLinkedinEmail\nLatest Content\n00:00:00\nNews Briefings\nRural Health Care at a Breaking Point: Who Can Afford to Stay Healthy?\nSep 17, 2026\nSep 18 | Rural Americans face rising healthcare costs, coverage losses, hospital closures, and longer travel for urgent care as experts examine affordability, access, and solutions for communities nationwide under growing financial pressure.\nstate’s agriculture industry.\nRead more\nImmigration\nHow the AI Surveillance Dragnet Is Powering Mass Deportation\nSep 17, 2026\nThe government’s deportation efforts are increasingly relying on the deployment of surveillance tools that experts say directly threaten Americans' civil liberties.\nRead more\nAuthor Related\nImmigration\nOne Year After Glass House Farms Raid, Residents Say Fear and Trauma Remain\nJul 14, 2026\nCommunity members say the July 10, 2025 raid in Ventura County left lasting scars but also fostered a greater sense of solidarity in response.\nRead more\nGender and Sexuality\n‘In the Eye of the MAGA Hurricane’ – Bamby Salcedo on Defending Trans Rights in Trump’s America\nJun 15, 2026\nThe veteran activist says hard-won rights are being stripped from the trans community even as violence targeting trans people is on the rise.\nRead more\nAt the end of May a letter arrived in the mail for Ángel, who has called Los Angeles home for more than two decades. The letter, from the Department of Homeland Security, informed him that he was being fined $1.8 million for failing to comply with a deportation order.\nÁngel (we are not using his real name because he is undocumented), says the days and weeks since the letter arrived have been filled with anguish.\n“I was frozen when I got the letter,” he said. “I couldn’t eat. My appetite left. I felt cornered.” He added, “I began wondering over and over again what was going to happen to me. I don’t have money to pay that amount. What will happen to my family if they deport me?”\nRecent reporting by the Marshall Project shows the federal government has sent out more than 65,000 such letters to immigrants across the country who, like Ángel, have outstanding deportation orders. In Ángel’s case, the $1.8 million is based on a $998 per-day fine with a five-year statutory minimum.\nIn administering the fines — which amount to some $36 billion in total — the Trump administration has revived a rarely used 1996 law that allows for financial penalties for immigrants who fail to comply with court issued orders.\nBeware notarios\nÁngel is 47 and has worked in construction since he first came to Los Angeles from Mexico. With a lump in his throat, the husband and father of three — ages 21, 18 and 12, all U. S. citizens — takes long pauses during the interview. Between sobs, he says his problems began when he visited a local notario in 2001 shortly after arriving in the country.\n“He promised me a work permit, a social security number, and then residency,” Ángel recounted. “I had only been in the country for a year at the time, and in my ignorance, I foolishly believed him.”\nA copy of the DHS letter sent to Ángel. The Trump administration has revived a rarely used 1996 law to begin levying steep financial penalties on undocumented immigrants.\nIn Mexico and other parts of Latin America, notarios are state-appointed attorneys with broad legal authority, which is not the case here in the US. That confusion has led to legal and financial pitfalls as well as numerous scams targeting unsuspecting immigrants.\nIn Ángel’s case, it was three years later, in 2004, when an immigration judge denied his asylum petition and handed down a deportation order, that he understood his mistake.\n“I wasn’t the only one, there were hundreds,” explained Ángel, who paid the notario $4000 for his “services.” According to Ángel, the notario never explained that he would be filing an asylum petition on his behalf.\nApproval rates in asylum cases for Mexican nationals has historically hovered at below 10%.\nThe judge in the case told Ángel he could choose to self-deport or have agents come to his home. “I responded that I would leave on my own account,” he said.\nInstead, he remained in the country, motivated by the need to support his parents in Mexico. A year later, in 2005 he got married and started his own family.\n“I have a very good job. I pay my taxes. My wife has always volunteered in our children’s schools,” said Ángel. “I have never had problems with the police; I have perfect credit…”\nShattered dreams\nTwo weeks after receiving the first DHS letter, Ángel received a second notifying him that his debt would be sent to a collection agency.\n“Since then, I’ve visited many lawyers trying to find a solution, but nothing can be done. One lawyer wanted to charge me $5,000 to file an appeal; another $8,000 to file for bankruptcy, but that option isn’t available, because bankruptcy isn’t an option when you owe the government.”\nHe eventually made the decision to cancel his bank accounts, moving his savings and his vehicles under his children’s names to prevent them from being seized.\n“They have also told me that they can garnish up to 25% of my salary, and that would affect me because I am the only provider in the family.”\nÁngel says he expects the Trump administration to send him another letter with a court summons, and that ultimately, a judge will determine his fate.\n“If my children had already finished their studies, I would feel more at ease returning to Mexico,” he said. “My daughter wants to study to be a teacher, and my oldest son dreams of becoming a drone engineer. Deporting me would mean shattering their dreams.”\nProtect your assets\nAlex Gálvez is an immigration attorney working in Los Angeles. He said the first thing immigrants who receive these letters should do is beware of scams by lawyers who offer to appeal the fine for more than a million dollars.\n“There is nothing to appeal; and we are seeing lawyers who are charging up to $4,500 to file an appeal that is not going to stop the fine or cancel the deportation,” he explained. “What they should do is protect their assets, especially those who own homes, and create a trust to prevent their property from being seized or confiscated.”\nHe added he has seen cases of immigrants who received these letters only to have agents with Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) show up at their door shortly after.\n“What happened is that ICE detained them as they left their homes,” he said. “I’ve seen it.”\n‘The goal is to break them’\nJuan José Gutiérrez, director of the Full Rights for Immigrants Coalition, said these fines serve two purposes; the first is to continue terrorizing the immigrant community.\n“All that’s left is for them to take away what little savings they have,” he said.\nThe second, he said, is to get people to self-deport, fulfilling the government’s campaign pledge of mass deportation. “The goal is to emotionally break undocumented immigrants so that, filled with panic, they leave.”\nFor his part, Ángel, devastated and with no way to fix his immigration status, says his greatest wish is to connect with other immigrants who have received the fines.\n“So far, I haven’t been able to contact anyone. Talking to someone who is living through the same nightmare as me would help me a lot.”\nThis story was produced as part of “Aquí Estamos/Here We Stand,” a collaborative reporting project of American Community Media and community news outlets statewide.\nTagsCaliforniaDHSHere We StandICELatinoLos AngelesPolicy HWS","content_cn":"移民新闻交流\n“我整个人僵住了”——洛杉矶无证男子面临国土安全部180万美元罚款\n作者：阿拉塞利·马丁内斯\n2026年7月17日\n图片依据CC 1.0许可协议发布\n分享\nFacebookLinkedinEmail\n最新内容\n00:00:00\n新闻简报\n农村医疗保健濒临崩溃：谁还负担得起保持健康？\n2026年9月17日\n9月18日 | 随着专家在全国范围内审视在日益加大的财政压力下 affordability、可及性和解决方案，美国农村居民面临医疗费用上涨、保险覆盖丧失、医院关闭以及紧急护理需要长途跋涉等问题。\n该州的农业产业。\n阅读更多\n移民\n人工智能监控天网如何助推大规模驱逐\n2026年9月17日\n政府的驱逐行动日益依赖监控工具的部署，专家称这些工具直接威胁美国人的公民自由。\n阅读更多\n作者相关\n移民\n玻璃屋农场突袭一年后，居民称恐惧与创伤仍在\n2026年7月14日\n社区成员表示，2025年7月10日在文图拉县发生的突袭留下了持久的伤痕，但也促成了更强的团结意识。\n阅读更多\n性别与性取向\n“身处MAGA飓风之眼”——班比·萨尔塞多谈在特朗普治下的美国捍卫跨性别权利\n2026年6月15日\n这位资深活动人士表示，跨性别群体来之不易的权利正被剥夺，而针对跨性别者的暴力却在上升。\n阅读更多\n五月底，一封寄给安赫尔（Ángel）的信件送到了他手中，他已在洛杉矶生活了二十多年。这封信来自国土安全部，通知他因未遵守驱逐令而被罚款180万美元。\n安赫尔（因他是无证移民，我们未使用其真名）说，自这封信到来后的日子里，他充满了痛苦。\n“我收到信时整个人僵住了，”他说。“我吃不下饭。食欲全无。我感到走投无路。”他补充道，“我开始一遍又一遍地想，我会遭遇什么。我没有钱支付那笔金额。如果他们把我驱逐出境，我的家人会怎样？”\n马歇尔计划最近的报道显示，联邦政府已向全国像安赫尔一样有未执行驱逐令的移民发出了超过65,000封此类信件。在安赫尔的案例中，180万美元是基于每天998美元的罚款，并设有五年法定最低期限。\n在实施这些罚款——总额约360亿美元——的过程中，特朗普政府重启了一项很少使用的1996年法律，该法律允许对未遵守法院命令的移民处以经济处罚。\n当心“公证人”\n安赫尔47岁，自从从墨西哥来到洛杉矶后一直从事建筑工作。这位三个孩子（分别为21岁、18岁和12岁，均为美国公民）的父亲在采访中喉咙哽咽，长时间停顿。他在抽泣之间说，他的问题始于2001年，当时他刚到美国不久，就去找了当地的一位“公证人”（notario）。\n“他向我承诺会办工作许可、社会安全号码，然后是居留权，”安赫尔回忆道。“我当时只在这个国家待了一年，出于无知，我愚蠢地相信了他。”\n寄给安赫尔的国土安全部信件副本。特朗普政府重启了一项很少使用的1996年法律，开始对无证移民征收高额经济罚款。\n在墨西哥和拉丁美洲其他地区，“公证人”（notarios）是由国家任命的律师，拥有广泛的法律权限，而在美国并非如此。这种混淆导致了法律和财务上的陷阱，以及众多针对毫无戒心的移民的骗局。\n在安赫尔的案例中，直到三年后的2004年，一名移民法官驳回他的庇护申请并下达驱逐令时，他才明白自己犯了错。\n“我不是唯一一个，有数百人，”安赫尔解释道，他为这位“公证人”的“服务”支付了4000美元。据安赫尔说，这位“公证人”从未解释过他将代表自己提交庇护申请。\n墨西哥国民的庇护案件批准率历来徘徊在10%以下。\n该案的法官告诉安赫尔，他可以选择自行离境，或者让探员到他家来。“我回答说我会自行离开，”他说。\n然而，他留在了这个国家，动力来自需要赡养在墨西哥的父母。一年后，2005年，他结婚并组建了自己的家庭。\n“我有一份很好的工作。我缴税。我的妻子一直志愿服务……\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"americancommunitymedia.org","publish_time":"2026-07-17T15:03:57+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2571","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国监督组织启动爱泼斯坦记录调查，要求公开司法部与联邦调查局审查详情","title_en":"American Oversight Launches Epstein Records Investigation, Seeks Details on DOJ and FBI Review of Investigative Holdings - American Oversight","summary_cn":"美国监督组织宣布对司法部和联邦调查局审查杰弗里·爱泼斯坦刑事案件相关调查材料一事展开调查。此前有报道称，联邦调查局人员被指示标记任何提及特朗普的记录，司法部长邦迪也曾告知特朗普其名字多次出现在爱泼斯坦文件中。该组织已提交《信息自由法》请求，要求获取审查培训材料、最终指令及内部异议备忘录等记录。","summary_en":"American Oversight launched an investigation into the DOJ and FBI's review of investigative holdings related to Jeffrey Epstein's criminal case. Following reports that FBI personnel were instructed to flag records mentioning President Trump, and that Attorney General Bondi told Trump his name appears multiple times in Epstein files, the watchdog filed FOIA requests seeking training materials, final directives, and internal dissent memos related to the review.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:03:07.896781+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/american-oversight-launches-epstein-records-investigation-seeks-details-on-doj-and-fbi-review-of-investigative-holdings","content":"News\nJuly 29, 2025\nAmerican Oversight Launches Epstein Records Investigation, Seeks Details on DOJ and FBI Review of Investigative Holdings\nWe’re seeking records following reports that FBI personnel were instructed to flag Epstein files for Trump references.\ngovernment transparencyTrump administration accountability\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nSHARE\nOn Tuesday, American Oversight launched an investigation into the Department of Justice (DOJ) and the Federal Bureau of Investigation’s (FBI) review of investigative holdings relating to Jeffrey Epstein’s criminal case. Following news that Sen. Dick Durbin’s office was informed that FBI personnel “were instructed to ‘flag’ any records in which President Trump was mentioned,” and reports that Attorney General Pam Bondi informed Trump in May that his name appears multiple times in the Epstein files, the nonpartisan watchdog filed Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) requests seeking records that could shed light on how these sensitive materials were reviewed. The review conducted by DOJ and the FBI reportedly involved hundreds of FBI employees and federal prosecutors who were pulled off other assignments and asked to work around the clock to conduct multiple rounds of reviews of Epstein-related files.\n“In a functioning democracy, no one — not even the most powerful — should be shielded from public scrutiny,” said Chioma Chukwu, Executive Director of American Oversight. “Jeffrey Epstein called Donald Trump his ‘closest friend’ for a decade — and now, the public is being asked to trust that law enforcement handled this case without bias or special treatment. That’s not good enough. When the stakes are justice and public trust, we don’t need secrecy. We need sunlight. And we intend to get it.”\nAmerican Oversight is seeking records from the DOJ and the FBI that reflect training materials provided to personnel involved in reviewing Epstein-related investigative holdings, including materials addressing redaction procedures, flagging specific content, and operational security. The nonpartisan watchdog also requested final directives or guidance shared with agency staff as well as any internal complaints or dissent memoranda regarding the conduct of the review.","content_cn":"新闻\n2025年7月29日\nAmerican Oversight启动爱泼斯坦记录调查，寻求有关司法部和联邦调查局审查调查档案的细节\n在有报道称联邦调查局人员被指示标记爱泼斯坦文件中提及特朗普的内容后，我们正在寻求相关记录。\n政府透明度　特朗普政府问责\n咨询 press@americanoversight.org\n分享\n周二，American Oversight启动了针对司法部（DOJ）和联邦调查局（FBI）审查与Jeffrey Epstein刑事案件有关的调查档案的调查。继有消息称Dick Durbin参议员办公室获悉，联邦调查局人员“被指示‘标记’任何提及特朗普总统的记录”，以及有报道称司法部长Pam Bondi于5月告知特朗普，他的名字在爱泼斯坦文件中多次出现后，这家无党派监督机构提交了《信息自由法》（FOIA）请求，寻求可能揭示这些敏感材料如何被审查的记录。据报道，司法部和联邦调查局进行的审查涉及数百名联邦调查局员工和联邦检察官，他们被从其他任务中抽调出来，并被要求昼夜不停地对爱泼斯坦相关文件进行多轮审查。\n“在一个正常运作的民主制度中，任何人——即使是最有权势的人——都不应免于公众监督，”American Oversight执行主任Chioma Chukwu表示。“Jeffrey Epstein曾在十年间称Donald Trump为他‘最亲密的朋友’——如今，公众被要求相信执法部门在处理本案时没有偏见或特殊待遇。这还不够。当事关正义与公众信任时，我们不需要保密。我们需要阳光。而我们打算得到它。”\nAmerican Oversight正在寻求司法部和联邦调查局的记录，以反映向参与审查爱泼斯坦相关调查档案的人员提供的培训材料，包括涉及删节程序、标记特定内容和行动安全的材料。这家无党派监督机构还要求提供与机构工作人员分享的最终指令或指导意见，以及任何关于审查执行情况的内部投诉或异议备忘录。","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2025-07-29T20:04:45+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2482","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国监督组织获国土安全部惊人承认：不再保存诺姆等高层官员短信","title_en":"American Oversight Obtains Startling DHS Admission: It No Longer Preserves Text Messages for Noem, Other Top Officials - American Oversight","summary_cn":"美国监督组织称，国土安全部在回应其《信息自由法》请求时承认，自2025年4月起不再保存部长诺姆及其他高级领导人的短信，且已无法搜索短信记录。该组织认为此举涉嫌违反联邦透明和记录保存法律，时间点恰逢外界对基尔马·阿布雷戈·加西亚被错误驱逐一事加强审视之际。","summary_en":"American Oversight said DHS admitted in response to its FOIA requests that it has not preserved text messages for Secretary Kristi Noem and other senior leaders since April 2025 and can no longer search them. The watchdog argues this may violate federal transparency and recordkeeping laws, noting the timing coincides with heightened scrutiny over the wrongful deportation of Kilmar Abrego Garcia.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:17:53.315469+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/american-oversight-obtains-startling-dhs-admission-it-no-longer-preserves-text-messages-for-noem-other-top-officials","content":"News\nAugust 22, 2025\nAmerican Oversight Obtains Startling DHS Admission: It No Longer Preserves Text Messages for Noem, Other Top Officials\nDHS decision to halt text message retention coincided with timing of scrutiny over Kilmar Abrego Garcia’s wrongful deportation.\ngovernment transparency\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nSHARE\nNew York Times: “Homeland Security Dept. Says It Hasn’t Kept Text Message Data Since April”\nAmerican Oversight slammed the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) after the agency informed the nonpartisan watchdog that it can no longer search for text messages belonging to Secretary Kristi Noem and other senior leaders — and that it has not preserved any text messages created since April — timing that appears to coincide with heightened public scrutiny over the wrongful deportation of Kilmar Abrego Garcia.\nThese startling admissions, revealed in DHS’s response to American Oversight Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) requests, raise serious concerns about the agency’s compliance with federal transparency and recordkeeping laws, including FOIA and the Federal Records Act, especially in the wake of the Signalgate scandal.\n“DHS’s admissions are as alarming as they are unacceptable. It appears the Trump administration has learned nothing from Signalgate about its obligation to retain the text communications of senior officials, and Secretary Noem is no exception,” said Chioma Chukwu, Executive Director of American Oversight. “The law is clear: text messages are federal records, and DHS cannot simply decide it will no longer maintain or search them. We will not allow this blatant attempt by one of the nation’s largest law enforcement agencies to shield itself from oversight and accountability while carrying out some of the administration’s most dangerous and unconstitutional initiatives to be swept under the rug.”\nIn July, American Oversight submitted a FOIA request seeking the text, Signal, and email communications of Noem and other top DHS officials related to the National Guard’s questionable Los Angeles deployment to quell protests over its mass deportation agenda. In its July 23 response, DHS stated that “text message data generated after April 9, 2025, is no longer maintained.”\nTo test whether the agency was in fact retaining these communications, American Oversight submitted a follow-up FOIA request on August 21 seeking text messages sent or received by DHS leaders in July 2025. Just two and a half hours later, DHS responded with a categorical “no records” determination, stating that it “no longer has the capability to conduct a search of text messages.”\nDHS’s decision to stop preserving or searching text messages after April 9 appears to have coincided with heightened public scrutiny of the Trump administration’s wrongful deportation of Kilmar Abrego Garcia, a Salvadoran national living in Maryland who was mistakenly sent in March to a notorious mega-prison in El Salvador. According to public reporting and whistleblower accounts, DHS officials were engaged in significant internal discussions during this period about compliance with the Supreme Court’s orders — including through text messages — raising serious concerns that the agency’s failure to preserve or produce these records may have shielded critical communications from oversight and accountability.\nWith more than 260,000 employees and 80,000 law enforcement officers, DHS plays a central role in some of the federal government’s most controversial actions, including mass detention and deportation operations that have run roughshod over the rights of immigrants and American citizens alike. The department’s new position suggests that critical records may not be preserved or accessible for lawful oversight, leaving the public in the dark about decisions with sweeping consequences for civil rights and public safety.\nThe irony is stark: DHS and its components, including Customs and Border Protection, recently received a dramatic increase in funding, and have unprecedented access to the phones and communications of ordinary people — conducting record-high searches of travelers’ devices at the border — while simultaneously claiming it cannot access or search the official text messages of its own senior leadership.","content_cn":"新闻\n2025年8月22日\n美国监督组织获得国土安全部惊人承认：不再保存诺姆及其他高官的短信\n国土安全部停止保留短信的决定，恰逢公众对基尔马尔·阿布雷戈·加西亚遭错误驱逐一事的审查加剧。\n政府透明度\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\n分享\n《纽约时报》：“国土安全部称自4月以来一直未保存短信数据”\n美国监督组织抨击国土安全部（DHS）。此前，该机构告知这个无党派监督组织，它已无法再搜索属于部长克里斯蒂·诺姆及其他高级领导人的短信，并且自4月以来创建的任何短信都未被保存——这一时间点似乎与公众对基尔马尔·阿布雷戈·加西亚遭错误驱逐的高度关注相吻合。\n这些惊人的承认内容披露于国土安全部对美国监督组织依据《信息自由法》（FOIA）提出的请求所作的回应中，引发了人们对该机构是否遵守联邦透明度和记录保存法律的严重担忧，包括《信息自由法》和《联邦记录法》，尤其是在“信号门”丑闻之后。\n“国土安全部的承认既令人震惊，也不可接受。特朗普政府似乎没有从‘信号门’事件中吸取任何关于其有义务保存高级官员短信通信的教训，诺姆部长也不例外，”美国监督组织执行董事Chioma Chukwu表示。“法律非常明确：短信属于联邦记录，国土安全部不能简单地决定不再维护或搜索这些记录。我们不会允许这个全国最大的执法机构之一，在实施政府最危险、最违宪的一些举措的同时，公然试图逃避监督和问责，而这些事情也不能被掩盖。”\n7月，美国监督组织提交了一份《信息自由法》请求，要求提供诺姆及其他国土安全部高官与国民警卫队备受质疑的洛杉矶部署有关的短信、Signal和电子邮件通信；此次部署旨在平息针对其大规模驱逐议程的抗议。在7月23日的回应中，国土安全部表示，“2025年4月9日之后生成的短信数据不再保存。”\n为检验该机构是否确实保留这些通信，美国监督组织于8月21日提交了后续《信息自由法》请求，要求提供国土安全部领导人在2025年7月发送或接收的短信。仅仅两个半小时后，国土安全部就作出绝对的“无记录”裁定，称其“已不再具备搜索短信的能力”。\n国土安全部在4月9日之后停止保存或搜索短信的决定，似乎与公众对特朗普政府错误驱逐基尔马尔·阿布雷戈·加西亚一事的高度关注相吻合。阿布雷戈·加西亚是居住在马里兰州的萨尔瓦多国民，3月被错误送往萨尔瓦多一所臭名昭著的超级监狱。据公开报道和举报人叙述，国土安全部官员在这一时期就遵守最高法院命令进行了大量内部讨论——其中包括通过短信进行的讨论——这引发了严重担忧：该机构未能保存或提供这些记录，可能使关键通信逃避了监督和问责。\n国土安全部拥有超过26万名雇员和8万名执法人员，在联邦政府一些最具争议的\n这些行动，包括大规模拘留和驱逐行动，肆意践踏了移民和美国公民的权利。该部门的新立场表明，关键记录可能不会被保存，或无法被依法监督获取，使公众无法了解那些对公民权利和公共安全具有广泛影响的决策。\n\n讽刺意味十分明显：国土安全部及其下属机构，包括海关与边境保护局，最近获得了大幅增加的资金，并前所未有地获取普通人的手机和通信信息——在边境对旅客设备进行创纪录数量的检查——与此同时却声称无法访问或搜索其自身高级领导层的官方短信。","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2025-08-23T01:08:21+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1808","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国监督组织反对政府试图抹去特朗普-联邦调查局爱泼斯坦调查访谈记录案中的关键事实","title_en":"American Oversight Opposes Government Effort to Erase Key Facts in Records Case on Trump FBI Epstein Investigation Interview - American Oversight","summary_cn":"美国监督组织反对特朗普政府提出的动议，该动议要求从其针对司法部和联邦调查局的诉讼中删除事实指控。该诉讼寻求获取总统在政府调查杰弗里·爱泼斯坦及其同伙吉斯莱恩·麦克斯韦尔期间接受访谈的任何记录。联邦调查局以隐私为由拒绝确认或否认此类记录的存在。该组织称，被质疑的指控基于特朗普、司法部长邦迪和联邦调查局局长帕特尔的公开声明、一份联合备忘录、参议员德宾的信件以及大量公开报道。","summary_en":"American Oversight opposed the Trump administration's motion to strike factual allegations from its lawsuit against the Department of Justice and the FBI seeking any interview records of the president in connection with the government's investigation of Jeffrey Epstein and Ghislaine Maxwell. The FBI has refused to confirm or deny the existence of such records, citing privacy concerns. The group said the challenged allegations are grounded in public statements by Trump, Attorney General Bondi and FBI Director Patel, a joint memorandum, a letter from Sen. Durbin and extensive public reporting.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:31:23.686286+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/american-oversight-opposes-government-effort-to-erase-key-facts-in-records-case-on-trump-fbi-epstein-investigation-interview","content":"News\nJanuary 16, 2026\nAmerican Oversight Opposes Government Effort to Erase Key Facts in Records Case on Trump FBI Epstein Investigation Interview\nTrump Administration Trying to Hide Its Own Public Comments in Suit Challenging FBI’s Refusal to Confirm Whether President Was Interviewed About Epstein\nTrump administration accountability\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nSHARE\nOn Friday, we opposed the Trump administration’s motion to strike factual allegations from our lawsuit against the Department of Justice (DOJ) and the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) seeking any interview records of the president in connection with the government’s investigation of convicted sex offender Jeffrey Epstein and his associate Ghislaine Maxwell.\nThus far, the FBI has refused to confirm or deny the existence of such records, citing privacy concerns — even though Trump’s ties to Epstein and Maxwell are a matter of longstanding and widespread public record.\n“If the president of the United States was questioned by federal investigators in the Epstein case, the American people have a right to know,” said our Executive Director Chioma Chukwu. “Instead of making good on its promise to be the most transparent administration, the Trump administration is asking the court to erase its own public statements about the Epstein investigation from the record to stymie our litigation and delay the release of basic facts. That is a slap in the face to the victims and an insult to the public’s right to the truth.”\nIn the court filing opposing the administration’s motion to strike, we explained that the challenged allegations are grounded in public statements by President Trump, Attorney General Pam Bondi, and FBI Director Kash Patel, a joint DOJ–FBI memorandum describing the administration’s review of Epstein-related materials, a letter from Senator Richard Durbin, and extensive public reporting on Trump’s relationship with Epstein. The filing explains that this factual background is directly relevant to evaluating the FBI’s refusal to confirm or deny the existence of responsive records.\nOur underlying Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) request specifically sought FBI 302s and other records memorializing interviews of Trump during the Epstein investigation. After the FBI issued a “Glomar” response during the first Trump Administration — neither confirming nor denying the existence of responsive records — we appealed to the DOJ’s Office of Information Policy, which upheld the FBI’s refusal. Having exhausted all administrative remedies, we are now seeking judicial intervention.\nLast month, we opposed a similar government motion in our lawsuit seeking records on the DOJ and the FBI’s politicized review of files related to Epstein. The litigation was sparked when the agencies failed to produce records responsive to FOIA requests seeking guidance, instructions, and internal communications related to the administration’s claimed “exhaustive review” of Epstein investigative materials.\nIn July 2020, we filed a FOIA request for FBI Form 302s — reports used by agents to summarize witness interviews — and related records documenting any interviews of Trump during the 2006–2008 investigation. That investigation resulted in a controversial non-prosecution agreement with Epstein that was negotiated by then-U.S. Attorney Alex Acosta, who later served in Trump’s first cabinet. Again, the FBI has refused to confirm or deny the existence of such records.\nMaxwell, who in 2021 was found guilty of conspiring with Epstein to sexually abuse and exploit underage girls, was recently moved to a lower-security federal prison in Texas by the Trump administration. The transfer came just days after she met with Deputy Attorney General Todd Blanche, who previously served as one of Trump’s personal criminal defense attorneys. In 2020, when asked by a reporter whether he expected Maxwell to reveal the names of powerful men tied to Epstein’s alleged sex-trafficking ring, Trump replied that he didn’t know and added, “I just wish her well.”\nThe government’s latest request to erase facts from the public record comes amid continued revelations of Trump’s connections to Epstein, including reports that Trump’s name appeared repeatedly in internal government reviews of Epstein-related records and that Trump personally wrote and illustrated a suggestive note included in a book given to Epstein. While Trump has publicly downplayed his relationship with Epstein, he acknowledged in 2002 that Epstein was a “terrific guy” who enjoyed the company of “beautiful women as much as I do, and many of them are on the younger side.”","content_cn":"新闻\n2026年1月16日\n美国监督组织反对政府试图在特朗普FBI爱泼斯坦调查访谈记录案中抹除关键事实\n特朗普政府试图在质疑FBI拒绝确认总统是否就爱泼斯坦接受访谈的诉讼中隐藏其自身的公开言论\n特朗普政府问责\n查询请联系press@americanoversight.org\n分享\n周五，我们反对特朗普政府提出的动议，该动议要求从我们对司法部（DOJ）和联邦调查局（FBI）提起的诉讼中删除事实性指控。该诉讼寻求获取总统在与政府对已定罪性犯罪者杰弗里·爱泼斯坦及其同伙吉斯兰·麦克斯韦的调查相关的任何访谈记录。\n迄今为止，FBI一直以隐私为由拒绝确认或否认此类记录的存在——尽管特朗普与爱泼斯坦和麦克斯韦的关系是长期且广泛公开记录在案的事实。\n“如果美国总统在爱泼斯坦案中接受了联邦调查人员的询问，美国人民有权知道，”我们的执行主任奇奥玛·楚库说。“特朗普政府非但没有兑现其成为最透明政府的承诺，反而要求法院将其自己关于爱泼斯坦调查的公开声明从记录中抹去，以阻挠我们的诉讼并拖延基本事实的公布。这是对受害者的侮辱，也是对公众知情权的冒犯。”\n在反对政府删除动议的法庭文件中，我们解释说，受到质疑的指控依据的是特朗普总统、司法部长帕姆·邦迪和FBI局长卡什·帕特尔的公开声明、一份描述政府对爱泼斯坦相关材料审查情况的司法部—FBI联合备忘录、参议员理查德·德宾的一封信，以及关于特朗普与爱泼斯坦关系的广泛公开报道。该文件解释说，这一事实背景与评估FBI拒绝确认或否认存在相关记录直接相关。\n我们依据《信息自由法》（FOIA）提出的基本请求，具体寻求获取FBI 302表格及其他记录特朗普在爱泼斯坦调查期间接受访谈的文件。在FBI于特朗普第一任期内作出“格洛马”式回应——既不确认也不否认存在相关记录——之后，我们向司法部信息政策办公室提出上诉，该办公室维持了FBI的拒绝。在穷尽所有行政救济后，我们现在寻求司法干预。\n上个月，我们在另一起诉讼中反对了政府提出的类似动议，该诉讼寻求获取关于司法部和FBI对爱泼斯坦相关文件进行政治化审查的记录。该诉讼源于这些机构未能提供响应FOIA请求的记录，这些请求寻求与政府所称对爱泼斯坦调查材料进行“详尽审查”相关的指导、指示和内部通信。\n2020年7月，我们提交了一份FOIA请求，要求获取FBI 302表格——探员用来总结证人访谈的报告——以及记录2006至2008年调查期间对特朗普任何访谈的相关记录。该调查最终导致与爱泼斯坦达成了一项有争议的不起诉协议，该协议由时任美国联邦检察官亚历克斯·阿科斯塔谈判达成，他后来在特朗普的第一届内阁中任职。FBI再次拒绝确认或否认此类记录的存在。\n麦克斯韦于2021年被判与爱泼斯坦合谋对未成年女孩实施性虐待和性剥削罪名成立，最近被特朗普政府转移至得克萨斯州一所安全级别较低的联邦监狱。此次转移发生在她会见副司法部长托德·布兰奇几天后，布兰奇此前曾担任特朗普的私人刑事辩护律师之一。2020年，当记者问特朗普是否预计麦克斯韦会披露与爱泼斯坦涉嫌性交易团伙有关的有权势男性的名字时，特朗普回答说他不清楚，并补充说：“我只希望她过得好。”\n政府最新提出的从公开记录中抹除事实的请求，正值特朗普与爱泼斯坦关联的更多披露不断出现之际，包括有报道称特朗普的名字在政府对爱泼斯坦相关记录的内部审查中反复出现，以及特朗普亲自撰写并绘制了一则带有暗示性的便条，该便条被收录在送给爱泼斯坦的一本书中。虽然特朗普公开淡化他与爱泼斯坦的关系，但他在2002年承认\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2026-01-16T22:21:10+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1383","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国监督组织寻求紧急法院命令，要求公布司法部/联邦调查局审查爱泼斯坦文件的记录","title_en":"American Oversight Seeks Emergency Court Order to Release Records About DOJ/FBI Review of Epstein Files - American Oversight","summary_cn":"美国监督组织提交初步禁令动议，要求司法部和联邦调查局迅速公布有关其处理杰弗里·爱泼斯坦调查文件记录的信息，这些记录可能揭示包括提及特朗普总统在内的政治敏感材料是否受到特殊对待。动议提出之际，司法部长邦迪因处理爱泼斯坦调查而面临立法者压力，包括众议院监督委员会发出闭门作证传票。该组织称，司法部和联邦调查局迄今未提供所要求的记录。","summary_en":"American Oversight filed a motion for a preliminary injunction to compel the DOJ and FBI to quickly release records regarding their handling of investigative files related to Jeffrey Epstein, records that could shed light on whether politically sensitive materials, including references to President Trump, received special treatment. The motion comes as Attorney General Pam Bondi faces pressure from lawmakers over her handling of the Epstein investigation, including a subpoena for closed-door testimony before the House Oversight Committee. The group says DOJ and FBI have not produced the requested records.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:18:11.833318+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/american-oversight-seeks-emergency-court-order-to-release-records-about-doj-fbi-review-of-epstein-files","content":"News\nMarch 17, 2026\nAmerican Oversight Seeks Emergency Court Order to Release Records About DOJ/FBI Review of Epstein Files\nWe asked the court to compel the production of records ahead of Attorney General Bondi’s closed-door Epstein deposition.\nTrump administration accountability\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nDocket Number\n25-3200\nSHARE\nMonday, American Oversight filed a motion for a preliminary injunction to compel the U.S. Department of Justice (DOJ) and Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) to quickly release records regarding the agency’s handling of investigative files related to convicted sex offender Jeffrey Epstein — records that could shed light on whether politically sensitive materials, including references to President Donald Trump, received special treatment.\nThe motion comes as Attorney General Pam Bondi faces mounting pressure from lawmakers over her handling of the Epstein investigation — including a subpoena for closed-door testimony before the House Oversight Committee, following a bipartisan vote citing alleged slow-walking, improper redactions, and removal of documents from public view. The deposition is reportedly expected to take place within 30 days. Last week, a bipartisan group of senators also requested a Government Accountability Office probe into the DOJ’s handling of Epstein files, citing concerns over the incomplete release of legally mandated documents.\nWe filed the motion as part of our ongoing Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) lawsuit seeking records regarding instructions and training given to personnel reviewing Epstein-related investigative materials. The requested records are urgently needed ahead of Bondi’s deposition, so Congress and the public can assess how the review was conducted and whether the Justice Department complied with its obligations under the federal law requiring transparency in the Epstein investigation.\n“The Justice Department and the FBI must disclose to the American people how they handled the review of the Epstein files and the extent to which documents implicating President Trump received special treatment,” said Chioma Chukwu, Executive Director of American Oversight. “This administration promised transparency but delivered the opposite: botched releases, quiet withdrawals, and misleading statements from senior officials. That’s why we’re asking the court to order the immediate release of these records ahead of Bondi’s testimony — so Congress can evaluate her candor against the documentary evidence and the public can determine whether the law was followed or whether political interests were protected over the public’s right to know.”\nThe lawsuit seeks records about the Justice Department’s internal review of Epstein-related investigative materials conducted in 2025, including training or instructions provided to personnel reviewing the files, internal directives or protocols governing how the review was carried out, communications among senior officials regarding the process, and any complaints or dissent from personnel involved in reviewing the investigative holdings.\nWe filed the underlying FOIA requests in July 2025 after reports and congressional inquiries raised concerns that FBI staff were instructed to flag mentions of Trump, further deepening concerns about political interference. To date, DOJ and FBI have not produced the requested records. DOJ’s Office of Legal Counsel told us on March 13, 2026 that it has no responsive records.\nIn December, DOJ and FBI asked the court to strike factual allegations from our lawsuit that were drawn from public statements by top officials — including Trump’s own Attorney General, Pam Bondi, agency documents, media reporting, and correspondence from Congress. A federal judge rejected this effort after we argued it was a brazen attempt to keep the public in the dark about how the Epstein file review was conducted and who it was designed to protect.\nLast November, Congress passed the Epstein Files Transparency Act, which required DOJ to release all unclassified records related to Epstein by Dec. 19, 2025. President Trump signed it into law shortly after. Despite the clear mandate, DOJ released only a portion of the files by the deadline, drawing criticism from lawmakers across the political spectrum and from survivors seeking greater transparency.\nSubsequent releases and public reporting have indicated that tens of thousands of records remain withheld, including records on a woman’s claims against Trump, fueling questions about whether DOJ has fully complied with the law and whether Bondi’s statements to Congress about the completeness of the releases were accurate.In Monday’s filing, we argue that the records it seeks could help answer key questions about how the review of Epstein-related files was conducted, including whether certain categories of records were singled out for special handling and whether the DOJ followed the transparency requirements enacted by Congress. Our motion asks the court to order DOJ to expedite the production of records, so that lawmakers and the public have the information necessary to evaluate the department’s conduct before Bondi’s upcoming deposition.","content_cn":"新闻\n2026年3月17日\n美国监督组织寻求紧急法院命令，要求公布司法部/联邦调查局审查爱泼斯坦文件的记录\n我们请求法院在司法部长邦迪就爱泼斯坦案闭门作证之前，强制要求提交相关记录。\n特朗普政府问责\n查询邮箱：press@americanoversight.org\n案卷编号\n25-3200\n分享\n周一，美国监督组织提交了一项初步禁令动议，要求强制美国司法部（DOJ）和联邦调查局（FBI）尽快公布有关该机构处理已定罪性犯罪者杰弗里·爱泼斯坦相关调查文件的记录——这些记录可能揭示包括涉及总统唐纳德·特朗普在内的政治敏感材料是否受到了特殊对待。\n该动议提出之际，司法部长帕姆·邦迪正因处理爱泼斯坦调查一事面临来自立法者日益增大的压力——包括众议院监督委员会发出传票要求其闭门作证，此前两党投票 citing 了所谓的拖延、不当涂黑以及将文件从公众视野中移除等行为。据报道，该作证预计将在30天内进行。上周，一个两党参议员小组还要求政府问责局对司法部处理爱泼斯坦文件的情况展开调查，理由是担心法律规定的文件未完整公布。\n我们提交该动议是我们正在进行的《信息自由法》（FOIA）诉讼的一部分，该诉讼寻求获取有关审查爱泼斯坦相关调查材料的人员所获指示和培训的记录。在邦迪作证之前，这些被请求的记录迫切需要，以便国会和公众能够评估审查是如何进行的，以及司法部是否遵守了联邦法律规定的在爱泼斯坦调查中保持透明的义务。\n“司法部和联邦调查局必须向美国人民披露他们如何处理爱泼斯坦文件的审查，以及涉及特朗普总统的文件在多大程度上受到了特殊对待，”美国监督组织执行主任奇奥马·楚库说。“本届政府承诺透明，却带来了相反的结果：搞砸的公布、悄无声息的撤回，以及高级官员的误导性声明。这就是为什么我们请求法院在邦迪作证之前下令立即公布这些记录——以便国会能够根据书面证据评估她是否坦诚，公众能够判断法律是否得到遵守，或者政治利益是否被置于公众知情权之上。”\n该诉讼寻求获取有关司法部2025年对爱泼斯坦相关调查材料进行内部审查的记录，包括向审查文件人员提供的培训或指示、指导审查如何进行的内部指令或规程、高级官员之间关于该过程的通信，以及参与审查调查资料的人员提出的任何投诉或异议。\n我们在2025年7月提交了相关的《信息自由法》请求，此前有报道和国会调查引发担忧，称联邦调查局工作人员被指示标记提及特朗普的内容，进一步加深了人们对政治干预的担忧。迄今为止，司法部和联邦调查局尚未提交所请求的记录。司法部法律顾问办公室于2026年3月13日告诉我们，它没有响应记录。\n去年12月，司法部和联邦调查局要求法院删除我们诉讼中取自高级官员公开声明的 factual 指控——包括特朗普自己的司法部长帕姆·邦迪、机构文件、媒体报道以及国会来信。一名联邦法官驳回了这一要求，此前我们辩称，这是公然试图让公众对爱泼斯坦文件审查如何进行以及旨在保护谁一无所知。\n去年11月，国会通过了《爱泼斯坦文件透明法》，要求司法部在2025年12月19日之前公布所有与爱泼斯坦相关的非机密记录。特朗普总统随后不久签署了该法案。尽管有明确要求，司法部在截止日期前只公布了部分文件，招致了来自各政治派别立法者以及寻求更大透明的幸存者的批评。\n随后的公布和公开报道表明，仍有数万份记录被扣留，包括关于一名女性对特朗普的指控的记录，fu\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2026-03-17T13:58:43+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2290","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"American Oversight 就特朗普在爱泼斯坦调查中的访谈记录起诉司法部和联邦调查局","title_en":"American Oversight Sues DOJ and FBI for Records of Any Trump Interviews in Epstein Investigation - American Oversight","summary_cn":"2025年10月7日，监督组织 American Oversight 起诉美国司法部与联邦调查局，要求公开特朗普在2006至2008年爱泼斯坦调查中接受访谈的记录。该组织称，FBI 以隐私为由拒绝确认是否存在此类记录，属于“格洛玛”回应。此前其依据《信息自由法》申请 FBI 302 访谈报告，行政申诉被驳回后诉诸法院。诉讼还提及爱泼斯坦案相关争议及特朗普与爱泼斯坦的公开关联。","summary_en":"On October 7, 2025, American Oversight sued the U.S. Department of Justice and the FBI for records of any interviews of President Donald Trump during the 2006–2008 Jeffrey Epstein investigation. The group said the FBI refused to confirm or deny the existence of such records, citing privacy concerns, in a Glomar response. After its FOIA request for FBI Form 302 interview reports was upheld on administrative appeal, it sought judicial intervention. The suit also cites broader controversies over the Epstein case and Trump's publicly documented ties to Epstein.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:03:24.373784+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/american-oversight-sues-doj-and-fbi-for-records-of-any-trump-interviews-in-epstein-investigation","content":"News\nOctober 7, 2025\nAmerican Oversight Sues DOJ and FBI for Records of Any Trump Interviews in Epstein Investigation\nWe’re challenging the FBI’s refusal to confirm whether President Trump was interviewed.\ngovernment transparencyTrump administration accountability\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nSHARE\nOn Tuesday, we sued the Department of Justice (DOJ) and the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) for any interview records of President Donald Trump in connection with the government’s investigation of convicted sex offender Jeffrey Epstein and his associate Ghislaine Maxwell.\nThe lawsuit comes two weeks after Arizonans elected Adelita Grijalva, whose swearing-in could provide the decisive signature for a bipartisan discharge petition to force a floor vote on releasing the Epstein files, to Congress — a move Trump opposes and is actively lobbying Republican lawmakers to abandon. Speaker Mike Johnson has yet to schedule Grijalva’s swearing-in.\nIn July 2020, we filed a Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) request for FBI Form 302s — reports used by agents to summarize witness interviews — and related records documenting any interviews of Trump during the 2006–2008 investigation. That investigation resulted in a controversial non-prosecution agreement with Epstein that was negotiated by then-U.S. Attorney Alex Acosta, who later served in Trump’s first cabinet. The FBI refused to confirm or deny the existence of such records, citing privacy concerns — even though Trump’s ties to Epstein and Maxwell are a matter of longstanding and widespread public record.\nMaxwell, who in 2021 was found guilty of conspiring with Epstein to sexually abuse and exploit underage girls, was recently moved to a lower-security federal prison in Texas by the Trump administration. The transfer came just days after she met with Deputy Attorney General Todd Blanche, who previously served as one of Trump’s personal criminal defense attorneys. In 2020, when asked by a reporter whether he expected Maxwell to reveal the names of powerful men tied to Epstein’s alleged sex-trafficking ring, Trump replied that he didn’t know and added, “I just wish her well.”\n“The American people deserve to know whether the president of the United States was questioned by federal investigators about his ties to one of the nation’s most notorious sexual predators,” said Chioma Chukwu, Executive Director of American Oversight. “Trump spent years promising transparency in the Epstein case if he returned to office. Instead, he’s wielded the power of the federal government to keep the truth hidden. Real accountability demands full disclosure — and that starts with releasing these records.”\nThe lawsuit comes amid continued revelations of Trump’s connections to Epstein, including reports that Trump’s name appeared repeatedly in internal government reviews of Epstein-related records and that Trump personally wrote and illustrated a suggestive note included in a book given to Epstein. While Trump has publicly downplayed his relationship with Epstein, he acknowledged in 2002 that Epstein was a “terrific guy” who enjoyed the company of “beautiful women as much as I do, and many of them are on the younger side.”\nThe complaint, filed in the U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia, asks the court to compel the DOJ and the FBI to conduct adequate searches for responsive records and to release any non-exempt documents.\nOur FOIA request specifically sought FBI 302s and other records memorializing interviews of Trump during the Epstein investigation. After the FBI issued a “Glomar” response during the first Trump Administration — neither confirming nor denying the existence of responsive records — we appealed to the DOJ’s Office of Information Policy, which upheld the FBI’s refusal. Having exhausted all administrative remedies, we are now seeking judicial intervention.\nEarlier this month, we sued the DOJ and the FBI for failing to release records related to the Trump administration’s controversial review of materials about Epstein, including his connections to the president. That suit seeks to answer unresolved questions about how Attorney General Pam Bondi and FBI Director Kash Patel may have intervened in or steered the review of the Epstein files — and why the process appeared designed to protect Trump by instructing FBI personnel to flag records mentioning the president.","content_cn":"新闻\n2025年10月7日\n美国监督组织起诉司法部和联邦调查局，要求提供爱泼斯坦调查中任何特朗普问询记录\n我们正在质疑联邦调查局拒绝确认特朗普总统是否曾被问询。\n政府透明度 特朗普政府问责\n查询：press@americanoversight.org\n分享\n周二，我们起诉了司法部（DOJ）和联邦调查局（FBI），要求提供在政府对已定罪性犯罪者杰弗里·爱泼斯坦及其同伙吉斯莱恩·麦克斯韦的调查中，对总统唐纳德·特朗普的任何问询记录。\n这起诉讼提起的两周前，亚利桑那州选民选举阿德利塔·格里哈尔瓦进入国会，她的宣誓就职可能为一项两党解除请愿书提供决定性签名，以迫使就公布爱泼斯坦文件进行全院投票——此举特朗普反对，并正在积极游说共和党议员放弃。议长迈克·约翰逊尚未安排格里哈尔瓦的宣誓就职。\n2020年7月，我们提交了一份《信息自由法》（FOIA）请求，要求获取联邦调查局302表格——探员用来总结证人问询的报告——以及记录2006至2008年调查期间对特朗普任何问询的相关记录。那项调查最终导致与爱泼斯坦达成一项有争议的不起诉协议，该协议由时任美国检察官亚历克斯·阿科斯塔谈判达成，他后来在特朗普的第一届内阁任职。联邦调查局以隐私为由拒绝确认或否认此类记录是否存在——尽管特朗普与爱泼斯坦和麦克斯韦的关系是长期且广泛公开记录在案的事项。\n麦克斯韦于2021年被判与爱泼斯坦合谋对未成年女孩实施性虐待和性剥削罪名成立，最近被特朗普政府转移到得克萨斯州一所安全级别较低的联邦监狱。此次转移发生在她与副总检察长托德·布兰奇会面几天后，布兰奇此前曾担任特朗普的私人刑事辩护律师之一。2020年，当记者问特朗普是否预计麦克斯韦会披露与爱泼斯坦涉嫌性交易团伙有关联的权贵人物姓名时，特朗普回答说不知道，并补充说：“我只希望她过得好。”\n“美国人民有权知道，美国总统是否曾因与我国最臭名昭著的性侵犯者之一的关系而接受联邦调查人员问询，”美国监督组织执行主任奇奥马·楚库说。“特朗普多年来承诺，如果他重返公职，将在爱泼斯坦案中实现透明。相反，他却动用联邦政府的权力掩盖真相。真正的问责要求全面披露——而这首先要公布这些记录。”\n这起诉讼提起之际，有关特朗普与爱泼斯坦关系的披露不断涌现，包括有报道称特朗普的名字在政府对爱泼斯坦相关记录的内部审查中反复出现，以及特朗普亲自撰写并绘制了一则带有暗示性的便条，该便条被收录在一本送给爱泼斯坦的书中。虽然特朗普公开淡化他与爱泼斯坦的关系，但他在2002年承认，爱泼斯坦是个“了不起的家伙”，喜欢有“漂亮女人作伴，和我一样，而且其中许多人都偏年轻。”\n该诉状提交至美国哥伦比亚特区联邦地区法院，要求法院强制司法部和联邦调查局对相关记录进行充分检索，并公布任何非豁免文件。\n我们的FOIA请求特别要求获取联邦调查局302表格以及其他记录特朗普在爱泼斯坦调查期间问询情况的文件。在联邦调查局于特朗普第一届政府期间作出“格洛玛”式回应——既不确认也不否认相关记录是否存在——之后，我们向司法部信息政策办公室提出上诉，该办公室维持了联邦调查局的拒绝。在穷尽所有行政救济后，我们现在寻求司法干预。\n本月早些时候，我们起诉司法部和联邦调查局，指控其未能公布与特朗普政府有争议地审查爱泼斯坦相关材料（包括其与总统的关系）有关的记录。那起诉讼旨在回答尚未解决的问题：司法部长帕姆·邦迪和联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔可能如何干预或主导了对爱泼斯坦文件的审查——以及为什么这一过程似乎旨在通过指示联邦调查局人员标记提及总统的记录来保护特朗普。","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2025-10-07T17:02:06+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2033","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"American Oversight 敦促国土安全部停止 SAVE 系统非法扩张，担忧数据隐私与合法选民被清除","title_en":"American Oversight Urges DHS to Halt Unlawful Expansion of SAVE System Citing Data Privacy, Eligible Voter Purge Concerns - American Oversight","summary_cn":"2025年12月1日，American Oversight 提交公众意见，反对国土安全部大幅扩张“系统性外国人权益验证”（SAVE）系统的提案。该组织警告，将 SAVE 变成美国人敏感个人信息的大型数据库会带来数据安全风险，并可能导致合法注册选民被错误清除。意见指出，该计划可能违反《隐私法》，且各州已开始用 SAVE 进行批量选民名单核查，可能误伤归化公民。该组织还与 Campaign Legal Center 合作起诉了 DHS、USCIS 和 SSA。","summary_en":"On December 1, 2025, American Oversight submitted a public comment opposing the Department of Homeland Security's proposal to dramatically expand the Systematic Alien Verification for Entitlements (SAVE) program. The group warned that turning SAVE into a sweeping repository of Americans' sensitive personal information poses data security risks and could wrongfully remove lawfully registered voters from the rolls. It said the plan may violate the Privacy Act and that states have begun using SAVE for bulk voter list checks despite documented error risks. American Oversight also sued DHS, USCIS, and the SSA with the Campaign Legal Center.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:58:42.141183+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/american-oversight-urges-dhs-to-halt-unlawful-expansion-of-save-system-citing-data-privacy-eligible-voter-purge-concerns","content":"News\nDecember 1, 2025\nAmerican Oversight Urges DHS to Halt Unlawful Expansion of SAVE System Citing Data Privacy, Eligible Voter Purge Concerns\nTransforming SAVE into a sweeping repository of Americans’ personal information threatens data security and could wrongfully remove lawfully registered voters from the rolls.\nTrump administration accountabilityvoting rights\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nSHARE\nMonday, American Oversight submitted a public comment opposing the U.S. Department of Homeland Security’s (DHS) proposal to dramatically expand the Systematic Alien Verification for Entitlements (SAVE) program. We warned that transforming SAVE into a sweeping repository of Americans’ highly sensitive personal information poses serious risks to data security and threatens to wrongfully remove lawfully registered voters from the rolls.\n“When an administration consistently signals that it believes too many people are participating in our elections, we have to pay close attention to what it builds in the name of ‘integrity,’” said Chioma Chukwu, Executive Director of American Oversight. “So when DHS creates a massive database of personal information and moves to share it across agencies, it’s not just a technical issue — it’s a human one. Millions could have their private details exposed, their eligibility wrongly questioned, or their right to vote challenged. This plan heightens the risk of data breaches, identity theft, and inaccurate voter purges, putting people’s privacy and their voice in our democracy at risk.”\nThe proposed overhaul comes amid DHS’s ongoing effort to consolidate sensitive personal data into SAVE, historically a limited tool used only to verify specific immigration-related information for benefits eligibility. As we noted in our comment, DHS’s new plan would unlawfully repurpose Americans’ personal data, potentially violate the Privacy Act, and expand a flawed system that can easily misidentify naturalized citizens as noncitizens. States have begun using SAVE to conduct bulk voter list checks, despite these well-documented potential errors — a shift that could result in eligible voters being swept up in inaccurate purges.\nIn partnership with Campaign Legal Center, we recently sued DHS, USCIS, and the Social Security Administration for records about the expanded SAVE system’s development and implementation. Additionally, last month, we released records showing DHS sought nationwide access to driver’s license and passport information as part of the Trump administration’s sweeping push to use the SAVE system for “voter roll maintenance” efforts targeting virtually nonexistent noncitizen voting.\nRead The Full Letter","content_cn":"新闻\n2025年12月1日\n美国监督组织敦促国土安全部停止SAVE系统的非法扩张，援引数据隐私与合格选民被清除的担忧\n将SAVE转变为美国人个人信息的庞大存储库威胁数据安全，并可能错误地将合法登记的选民从选民名册中移除。\n特朗普政府问责投票权\n查询press@americanoversight.org\n分享\n周一，美国监督组织提交了一份公开评论，反对美国国土安全部（DHS）大幅扩张“系统性外国人福利资格验证”（SAVE）计划的提案。我们警告称，将SAVE转变为美国人高度敏感个人信息的庞大存储库，对数据安全构成严重风险，并可能错误地将合法登记的选民从选民名册中移除。\n“当一届政府持续释放信号，表明其认为参与我们选举的人过多时，我们就必须密切关注它以‘诚信’之名构建的东西，”美国监督组织执行主任奇奥玛·楚库（Chioma Chukwu）表示。“因此，当国土安全部建立一个庞大的个人信息数据库并推动在各机构间共享时，这不仅仅是一个技术问题——而是一个关乎人的问题。数百万人的私人信息可能被曝光，他们的资格可能被错误质疑，或者他们的投票权可能受到挑战。这一计划加剧了数据泄露、身份盗窃和不准确选民清除的风险，使人们的隐私及其在我们民主中的声音面临危险。”\n这项拟议的全面改革出台之际，国土安全部正持续努力将敏感个人数据整合到SAVE中。SAVE历来只是一个有限工具，仅用于核实与福利资格相关的特定移民信息。正如我们在评论中指出的，国土安全部的新计划将非法地将美国人的个人数据挪作他用，可能违反《隐私法》，并扩大一个容易将归化公民错误识别为非公民的有缺陷系统。尽管这些潜在错误已有充分记录，各州已开始使用SAVE进行大规模选民名单核查——这一转变可能导致合格选民被卷入不准确的清除行动中。\n我们近期与竞选法律中心（Campaign Legal Center）合作，起诉了国土安全部、美国公民及移民服务局（USCIS）和社会保障局，要求获取有关扩张后的SAVE系统开发与实施的记录。此外，上个月，我们公布了记录，显示国土安全部寻求在全国范围内获取驾照和护照信息，这是特朗普政府全面推动利用SAVE系统进行“选民名册维护”努力的一部分，而该努力针对的是几乎不存在的非公民投票。\n阅读完整信函","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2025-12-01T20:01:45+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2420","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国监督组织就科里·莱万多夫斯基影子角色起诉国土安全部","title_en":"American Oversight Sues DHS for Records on Corey Lewandowski’s Shadow Role - American Oversight","summary_cn":"美国监督组织起诉国土安全部，要求公开有关科里·莱万多夫斯基在该机构影子角色的记录，包括其特别政府雇员身份。该组织称，莱万多夫斯基被描述为部长诺姆的“事实上的幕僚长”，却规避基本透明和监督要求，对政策、合同和人事决定施加广泛影响。国土安全部数月来未回应多项《信息自由法》请求。","summary_en":"American Oversight sued DHS for records about Corey Lewandowski's shadow role at the agency, including his status as a Special Government Employee. Described as Secretary Noem's de facto chief of staff, Lewandowski has reportedly evaded transparency and oversight while wielding influence over policy, contracts, and personnel. The lawsuit follows months of DHS stonewalling on multiple FOIA requests.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:12:03.827229+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/corey-lewandowski-dhs-public-records-foia-lawsuit","content":"News\nSeptember 10, 2025\nAmerican Oversight Sues DHS for Records on Corey Lewandowski’s Shadow Role\nAs DHS wages war on American cities, secrecy around Lewandowski continues the Trump Administration’s assault on the public’s right to know.\nattacks on FOIATrump administration accountability\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nSHARE\nOn Wednesday, American Oversight sued the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) for failing to release records that could answer numerous questions about Corey Lewandowski’s shadowy role at the agency, including his status as a Special Government Employee (SGE). Despite being described as DHS Secretary Kristi Noem’s “de facto chief of staff,” Lewandowski has evaded basic transparency and oversight requirements while reportedly exercising sweeping influence over policy, contracts, and personnel decisions.\nThe secrecy around Lewandowski’s role in the Trump administration — including his apparent misuse of the SGE designation that is intended for individuals who provide temporary, limited service to the government — reflects the administration’s broader hostility toward transparency. Recent reports suggest concern about his murky role is growing among at least some inside the White House.\nOur lawsuit follows months of stonewalling by DHS, which has failed to respond to multiple Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) requests seeking Lewandowski’s communications, calendars, and other records. DHS’s refusal to release records about his activities obscures whether he has exceeded the legal time limits on his appointment, avoided using government email to conduct official business, and directed agency business that may benefit his private associates.\n“It is telling that this White House — which has shown an aversion to the rule of law — has reportedly grown weary of Mr. Lewandowski’s attempts to game the system at DHS,” said Chioma Chukwu, Executive Director of American Oversight. “At a time when DHS is waging war on American cities, its refusal to provide basic transparency poses an increasing threat to the public’s right to know and our democracy. Transparency laws exist for a reason: When powerful operatives like Lewandowski are allowed to wield government authority behind closed doors, public trust is undermined and accountability erodes.”\nReports indicate that Lewandowski has acted as Secretary Noem’s “gatekeeper,” routed meetings through himself, directed personnel decisions, and even exercised veto power over contracts exceeding $100,000 — all while eschewing use of his government email and phone number to conduct official business and avoiding badge swipes that would document his time in government buildings. Despite these responsibilities, DHS claims he has worked only 69 days this year (228 days have elapsed since Secretary Noem was confirmed; Lewandowski began working there shortly after), well under the 130-day cap for SGEs — a count that insiders describe as a “gross undercount.”\nLewandowski has also failed to file a public financial disclosure report, raising concerns about whether he is complying with ethics rules that prohibit SGEs from engaging in outside work that conflicts with official duties. DHS’s secrecy has left unanswered questions about whether Lewandowski maintains private clients with interests before the agency.","content_cn":"新闻\n2025年9月10日\nAmerican Oversight起诉国土安全部，要求提供有关科里·莱万多夫斯基隐秘角色的记录\n随着国土安全部向美国城市发起战争，围绕莱万多夫斯基的秘密持续成为特朗普政府对公众知情权的攻击。\nFOIA攻击 特朗普政府问责\n咨询：press@americanoversight.org\n分享\n周三，American Oversight起诉国土安全部（DHS），原因是该部门未能公开可回答有关科里·莱万多夫斯基在该机构隐秘角色的诸多问题的记录，包括他的特别政府雇员（SGE）身份。尽管莱万多夫斯基被称为国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的“事实上的幕僚长”，但据报道，他广泛影响政策、合同和人事决定，同时规避了基本的透明度和监督要求。\n围绕莱万多夫斯基在特朗普政府中角色的秘密——包括他明显滥用SGE这一 designation；该身份本 intended for individuals who provide temporary, limited service to the government——反映了政府对透明度更广泛的敌意。近期报道显示，至少白宫内部一些人对其模糊角色的担忧正在加剧。\n我们的诉讼是在国土安全部数月拖延之后提起的。该部门未回应多项《信息自由法》（FOIA）请求，这些请求要求提供莱万多夫斯基的通信、日程和其他记录。国土安全部拒绝公开有关其活动的记录，使人无法得知他是否超出了任命的法定时间限制，是否为开展公务而避免使用政府电子邮件，以及是否指挥了可能使其私人关系人受益的机构事务。\nAmerican Oversight执行主任乔马·楚库说：“据报道，这个对法治表现出厌恶的白宫似乎已经厌倦了莱万多夫斯基先生试图在国土安全部钻制度空子的做法，这一点很能说明问题。在国土安全部向美国城市发起战争之际，它拒绝提供基本透明度，正日益威胁公众的知情权和我们的民主。透明度法律之所以存在是有原因的：当像莱万多夫斯基这样的权势操盘手被允许在幕后行使政府权力时，公众信任会受到削弱，问责也会被侵蚀。”\n报道称，莱万多夫斯基一直充当诺姆部长的“守门人”，通过自己安排会议，指挥人事决定，甚至对金额超过10万美元的合同行使否决权——与此同时，他避开使用政府电子邮件和电话号码处理公务，也避免刷证件，以免留下其在政府大楼内工作时间的记录。尽管承担这些职责，国土安全部声称他今年只工作了69天（诺姆部长获确认以来已经过去228天；莱万多夫斯基在此后不久开始在那里工作），远低于SGE的130天上限；知情人士称这一统计“严重少算”。\n莱万多夫斯基还未提交公开财务披露报告，引发了人们对他是否遵守伦理规定的担忧；这些规定禁止SGE从事与其公务冲突的外部工作。国土安全部的保密留下了未解问题：莱万多夫斯基是否仍维持着在该机构有利益关系的私人客户。","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2025-09-10T21:39:40+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2148","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部承认就诺姆及高层短信提供“错误”信息，尚未确认遵守法律","title_en":"DHS Admits It Provided “Erroneous” Information on Texts of Noem and DHS Brass, Hasn’t Confirmed It Followed Law - American Oversight","summary_cn":"2025年11月6日，American Oversight 在针对国土安全部的诉讼中披露，政府承认此前声称诺姆部长等高层官员短信未保存的说法“有误”。该组织称，DHS 尚未提供证据证明所请求记录已依法保存。法庭文件显示，DHS 承认于2025年4月停用短信归档系统，现依赖官员手动保存，但未确认诺姆、副部长埃德加及顾问劳、莱万多夫斯基是否遵守20天转移期限。国家档案局已要求 DHS 调查可能的记录非法销毁。","summary_en":"On November 6, 2025, American Oversight revealed in its lawsuit against the Department of Homeland Security that the government admitted its earlier assertion that text messages of Secretary Kristi Noem and other top officials were no longer preserved was 'erroneous.' The group said DHS has not provided evidence that requested records were preserved as required by law. Court filings show DHS disabled its text-archiving system in April 2025 and now relies on officials to manually preserve messages, but has not confirmed whether Noem, Deputy Secretary Troy Edgar, and advisers Rob Law and Corey Lewandowski followed the 20-day transfer deadline. NARA has directed DHS to investigate potential unauthorized destruction of records.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:16:50.534778+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/dhs-admits-it-provided-erroneous-information-on-texts-of-noem-and-dhs-brass-hasnt-confirmed-it-followed-law","content":"News\nNovember 6, 2025\nDHS Admits It Provided “Erroneous” Information on Texts of Noem and DHS Brass, Hasn’t Confirmed It Followed Law\nThursday, following a court filing in American Oversight’s lawsuit against the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) over the agency’s initial claim that it failed to preserve the text messages of Secretary Kristi Noem and other top agency officials, we revealed the government has admitted its assertion that text messages were no longer preserved was “erroneous” […]\ngovernment transparencyTrump administration accountability\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nDocket Number\n25-3699\nSHARE\nThursday, following a court filing in American Oversight’s lawsuit against the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) over the agency’s initial claim that it failed to preserve the text messages of Secretary Kristi Noem and other top agency officials, we revealed the government has admitted its assertion that text messages were no longer preserved was “erroneous” — though the government has yet to provide evidence that the records we requested have been preserved as required by law.\n“DHS has now admitted that it provided inaccurate information about whether Secretary Noem’s and other top agency officials’ text messages were properly preserved,” said Chioma Chukwu, Executive Director of American Oversight. “We’re talking about messages exchanged amid major national controversies — from the deployment of military forces on American streets to inhumane immigration crackdowns and deportations carried out in defiance of court orders. The public deserves to know whether these records still exist, and whether officials destroyed evidence of how those decisions were made. After misleading us for months, DHS wants us to trust that the law is being followed. But the agency has not turned over the records we requested nor has it provided details about whether senior officials’ text messages have been preserved in accordance with the law. It’s time for transparency — not more empty assurances.”\nToday’s court filing contains declarations by government defendants, which include an explicit acknowledgement from DHS that the agency’s repeated claims to us that it no longer preserved the text messages of Secretary Noem and other top DHS officials were “erroneous.” Beyond that, the declarations describe DHS’s general policies for records management but do not state unequivocally that those policies have been followed. The agency acknowledges that it disabled its text-archiving system in April 2025, and now relies on individual officials to manually capture and forward their own messages — a practice that, by law, must be completed within 20 days of the original record being created. Yet DHS has not confirmed whether Secretary Noem, Deputy Secretary Troy Edgar, and senior advisers Rob Law and Corey Lewandowski have followed the law.\nThe agency also has not stated whether any forensic searches have been conducted on the officials’ devices or provided any other evidence that those messages still exist. Meanwhile, the National Archive and Records Administration’s (NARA) declaration confirms it instructed DHS on Sept. 3 to investigate the potential unauthorized destruction of records and notify NARA within 30 days of the outcome of that investigation — and as of Oct. 30, DHS still had not responded to that directive.\nIn July, we submitted a FOIA request seeking the text, Signal, and email communications of Noem and other top DHS officials related to the National Guard’s questionable Los Angeles deployment to quell protests over the administration’s mass deportation agenda. In its July 23 response, DHS stated that it could not search for responsive records because “text message data generated after April 9, 2025, is no longer maintained.”\nWe submitted follow-up FOIA requests on Aug. 21 seeking the July 2025 text messages of Noem and other DHS leaders as well as records reflecting those messages. Just two and a half hours later, DHS responded with a categorical “no records” determination for each request, stating that it “no longer has the capability to conduct a search of text messages.”\nIn October, we filed a lawsuit against DHS based on the agency’s previous assertion that it failed to preserve text messages from Secretary Noem and other top DHS officials as required by law. We also filed suit against the agency for failing to release text messages and other records that could shed light on DHS’s role in decisions ranging from military strikes and National Guard deployments in American cities to inhumane immigration enforcement and the upheaval of government operations.","content_cn":"新闻\n2025年11月6日\n国土安全部承认就诺姆及国土安全部高层的短信提供了“错误”信息，尚未确认其遵守了法律\n周四，在“美国监督”诉国土安全部（DHS）一案中，针对该机构最初声称未能保存部长克里斯蒂·诺姆及其他机构高层官员短信的说法，我们披露政府已承认其关于短信不再被保存的断言是“错误的”[…]\n政府透明度 特朗普政府问责\n查询 press@americanoversight.org\n案卷编号\n25-3699\n分享\n周四，在“美国监督”诉国土安全部（DHS）一案中，针对该机构最初声称未能保存部长克里斯蒂·诺姆及其他机构高层官员短信的说法，我们披露政府已承认其关于短信不再被保存的断言是“错误的”——尽管政府尚未提供证据表明我们要求的记录已依法得到保存。\n“国土安全部现在已承认，它就诺姆部长及其他机构高层官员的短信是否得到妥善保存提供了不准确的信息，”美国监督执行主任奇奥玛·楚库说。“我们谈论的是在重大全国性争议期间往来的信息——从在美国街头部署军队，到以违抗法院命令的方式实施不人道的移民打击和驱逐。公众有权知道这些记录是否仍然存在，以及官员是否销毁了有关这些决定如何作出的证据。在误导我们数月之后，国土安全部想让我们相信法律得到了遵守。但该机构既没有交出我们要求的记录，也没有提供有关高层官员短信是否已依法保存的细节。现在是透明的时候了——而不是更多空洞的保证。”\n今天的法庭文件包含政府被告的声明，其中包括国土安全部明确承认，该机构一再向我们声称其不再保存诺姆部长及其他国土安全部高层官员短信的说法是“错误的”。除此之外，这些声明描述了国土安全部记录管理的一般政策，但并未明确表示这些政策得到了遵守。该机构承认，它于2025年4月停用了其短信归档系统，现在依赖个别官员手动捕获并转发自己的信息——依法，这种做法必须在原始记录创建后20天内完成。然而，国土安全部尚未确认诺姆部长、副部长特洛伊·埃德加以及高级顾问罗布·劳和科里·莱万多夫斯基是否遵守了法律。\n该机构也未说明是否对官员的设备进行了任何取证搜索，或提供任何其他证据表明这些信息仍然存在。与此同时，国家档案与记录管理局（NARA）的声明证实，它于9月3日指示国土安全部调查可能未经授权销毁记录的行为，并在调查结果出炉后30天内通知NARA——而截至10月30日，国土安全部仍未对该指令作出回应。\n7月，我们提交了一份《信息自由法》请求，寻求诺姆及其他国土安全部高层官员与国民警卫队备受质疑的洛杉矶部署有关的短信、Signal和电子邮件通信。该部署旨在镇压针对政府大规模驱逐议程的抗议。在7月23日的回复中，国土安全部表示，它无法检索相关记录，因为“2025年4月9日之后生成的短信数据不再保存”。\n我们于8月21日提交了后续《信息自由法》请求，寻求诺姆及其他国土安全部领导人2025年7月的短信以及反映这些短信的记录。仅两个半小时后，国土安全部就对每项请求作出了一概“无记录”的裁定，称其“不再具备检索短信的能力”。\n10月，我们基于国土安全部此前声称其未能依法保存诺姆部长及其他国土安全部高层官员短信的说法，对该机构提起诉讼。我们还因该机构未能公布短信及其他可能揭示国土安全部在相关决策中所起作用的记录而对其提起诉讼，这些决策包括\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2025-11-06T20:55:41+00:00"}},{"id":"news-879","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"邦迪作证前夕，American Oversight就司法部与FBI审查爱泼斯坦文件起诉特朗普政府","title_en":"On Eve of Bondi Testimony, American Oversight Sues Trump Admin for Records on DOJ and FBI Review of Epstein Files - American Oversight","summary_cn":"在司法部处理爱泼斯坦文件之际，监督组织American Oversight对司法部和联邦调查局提起诉讼，要求公开依据《信息自由法》于2026年3月申请的相关记录，包括涉嫌指示“标记”涉及特朗普材料的记录、内部审查规程及高级官员通信。诉讼还质疑司法部拒绝加急处理及FBI未作回应。该组织称，尽管国会通过《爱泼斯坦文件透明法》，司法部仅按期公布部分文件，数万份记录被扣留，引发对是否完全守法的质疑。","summary_en":"Ahead of former Attorney General Pam Bondi's testimony, American Oversight sued the Department of Justice and the FBI seeking records requested in March 2026 under the Freedom of Information Act, including alleged instructions to 'flag' materials mentioning President Trump, internal review protocols and senior officials' communications. The suit also challenges DOJ's denial of expedited processing and the FBI's failure to act. The group says that despite the Epstein Files Transparency Act, DOJ released only part of the files by the deadline, with tens of thousands of records withheld, raising questions about full compliance.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:24:38.071979+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/epstein-files-lawsuit-foia-bondi-testimony","content":"News\nMay 28, 2026\nOn Eve of Bondi Testimony, American Oversight Sues Trump Admin for Records on DOJ and FBI Review of Epstein Files\nLawsuit seeks records about alleged instructions to “flag” Trump-related files, internal review protocols, and communications among senior DOJ and FBI officials.\ngovernment transparency\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nDocket Number\n26-1832\nSHARE\nAhead of former Attorney General Pam Bondi’s scheduled testimony before the House Oversight Committee regarding the Department of Justice’s (DOJ) handling of the Epstein Files, American Oversight filed suit against DOJ and the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) seeking records about the government’s review and release process for the files, including records concerning alleged instructions to “flag” materials mentioning President Donald Trump.\nThe lawsuit seeks records requested in March 2026 through the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) that could shed light on how senior DOJ and FBI officials managed the review and release process after Congress enacted the Epstein Files Transparency Act, including records from the past year concerning internal review protocols, communications about withheld materials, and messages exchanged through encrypted or third-party platforms. The suit also challenges DOJ’s denial of expedited processing and the FBI’s failure to act on such requests despite ongoing congressional investigations, mounting public scrutiny, and growing evidence that records concerning allegations against Trump may have been withheld from earlier releases.\n“Despite mounting calls for information, the American people still do not have basic answers about how DOJ and the FBI handled the Epstein Files review,” said Chioma Chukwu, Executive Director of American Oversight. “The administration repeatedly claimed it was conducting a transparent and exhaustive review, yet public reporting suggests the review process included undisclosed review protocols, missing materials, and apparent efforts to single out records connected to President Trump. This review took place under Attorney General Pam Bondi’s leadership, and the public has a right to know whether political considerations compromised a process that was supposed to comply with federal law and deliver transparency.”\nToday’s lawsuit builds on our ongoing effort to uncover how DOJ and FBI officials handled the review and release of Epstein-related records as scrutiny over the process intensified. Since we first sought records in 2025, Congress passed the Epstein Files Transparency Act; DOJ released additional records under mounting public pressure; and reporting and newly released documents raised further questions about undisclosed review protocols, withheld materials, and whether records concerning allegations against Trump were treated differently from other files.\nLast September, we filed suit for records from March about DOJ’s internal review of Epstein-related investigative materials. We filed the previous underlying FOIA requests in July 2025 after reports and congressional inquiries raised concerns that FBI staff were instructed to flag mentions of Trump, further deepening concerns about political interference.\nIn December, DOJ and the FBI asked the court to strike factual allegations from our initial lawsuit that were drawn from public statements by top officials — including Bondi, agency documents, media reporting, and correspondence from Congress. A federal judge rejected this effort after we argued it was a brazen attempt to keep the public in the dark about how the Epstein file review was conducted and who it was designed to protect.\nLast November, Congress passed the Epstein Files Transparency Act, which required DOJ to release all unclassified records related to Epstein by Dec. 19, 2025. President Trump signed it into law shortly after. Despite the clear mandate, DOJ released only a portion of the files by the deadline, drawing criticism from lawmakers across the political spectrum and from survivors seeking greater transparency.\nSubsequent releases and public reporting have indicated that tens of thousands of records were withheld in 2025, including records of allegations against Trump that DOJ released only after public pressure, in early March 2026. The chaotic response has fueled questions about whether DOJ has fully complied with the law and whether Bondi’s previous statements to Congress about the completeness of the releases were accurate.","content_cn":"新闻\n2026年5月28日\n在邦迪作证前夕，美国监督组织起诉特朗普政府，要求提供司法部和联邦调查局审查爱泼斯坦文件的记录\n诉讼寻求有关据称指示“标记”与特朗普相关文件、内部审查规程以及司法部和联邦调查局高级官员之间通信的记录。\n政府透明度\n查询邮箱：press@americanoversight.org\n案卷编号\n26-1832\n分享\n在前司法部长帕姆·邦迪按计划就司法部（DOJ）处理爱泼斯坦文件一事向众议院监督委员会作证之前，美国监督组织对司法部和联邦调查局（FBI）提起诉讼，要求提供有关政府对相关文件审查和发布流程的记录，包括涉及据称指示“标记”提及总统唐纳德·特朗普的材料的记录。\n该诉讼寻求通过《信息自由法》（FOIA）于2026年3月申请获取的记录，这些记录可能揭示在国会颁布《爱泼斯坦文件透明度法》后，司法部和联邦调查局高级官员如何管理审查和发布流程，包括过去一年中有关内部审查规程、关于被扣留材料的通信，以及通过加密或第三方平台交换的信息。该诉讼还质疑司法部拒绝加快处理，以及联邦调查局在国会调查持续进行、公众监督日益加强、且越来越多证据表明有关针对特朗普的指控的记录可能被排除在早前发布之外的情况下，仍未对这些请求采取行动。\n“尽管要求提供信息的呼声日益高涨，美国人民仍然对司法部和联邦调查局如何处理爱泼斯坦文件审查缺乏基本答案，”美国监督组织执行主任奇奥马·楚库说。“政府一再声称正在进行透明而彻底的审查，但公开报道表明，审查过程包括未披露的审查规程、缺失的材料，以及显然试图单独挑出与特朗普总统有关的记录。这次审查是在司法部长帕姆·邦迪的领导下进行的，公众有权知道政治考量是否损害了一个本应遵守联邦法律并实现透明度的过程。”\n今天的诉讼建立在我们持续努力的基础上，旨在揭露随着对该过程审查的加剧，司法部和联邦调查局官员如何处理爱泼斯坦相关记录的审查和发布。自我们于2025年首次寻求记录以来，国会通过了《爱泼斯坦文件透明度法》；司法部在日益增大的公众压力下发布了更多记录；报道和新公布的文件进一步引发了关于未披露审查规程、被扣留材料，以及有关针对特朗普的指控的记录是否与其他文件受到不同对待的问题。\n去年9月，我们提起诉讼，要求获取当年3月有关司法部对爱泼斯坦相关调查材料进行内部审查的记录。在报道和国会质询引发担忧，即联邦调查局工作人员被指示标记提及特朗普的内容后，我们于2025年7月提交了此前的基础《信息自由法》请求，这进一步加深了人们对政治干预的担忧。\n12月，司法部和联邦调查局请求法院删除我们最初诉讼中取自高级官员公开声明的部分事实指控——包括邦迪的声明、机构文件、媒体报道以及国会来函。在我们主张这是公然试图让公众无法了解爱泼斯坦文件审查如何进行及其旨在保护谁的之后，一名联邦法官驳回了这一请求。\n去年11月，国会通过了《爱泼斯坦文件透明度法》，要求司法部在2025年12月19日前公布所有与爱泼斯坦相关的非机密记录。特朗普总统随后不久将其签署成为法律。尽管有明确要求，司法部仍只在截止日期前公布了部分文件，招致跨政治光谱的议员以及寻求更大透明度的幸存者的批评。\n随后的公布和公开报道表明，2025年有数万份记录被扣留，其中包括针对特朗普的指控记录，司法部直到2026年3月初在公众压力下才予以公布。这种混乱的应对引发了质疑：司法部是否完全遵守了法律，以及邦迪此前向国会所作的关于公布完整性的陈述是否准确。","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2026-05-28T15:11:23+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1273","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"独家：内部邮件显示国土安全部首席律师建议特工“直接动手打”抗议者","title_en":"Exclusive: Internal Emails Reveal Top DHS Attorney Suggested Agents Should ‘Start Hitting’ Protesters - American Oversight","summary_cn":"American Oversight通过《信息自由法》获得的内部邮件显示，时任国土安全部代理总法律顾问约瑟夫·马扎拉在2025年6月一次高级官员邮件往来中，就洛杉矶国民警卫队部署的法律策略建议联邦特工本应“直接动手打”抗议者，并称应逮捕“所有跑不掉的人”。该组织称获得两个版本记录，其中一份显示机构曾试图删节但未成功。执行主任奇奥马·楚库表示，此类言论令人质疑政府最高层对言论自由与公共安全的立场。","summary_en":"Internal emails obtained by American Oversight through the Freedom of Information Act show that then-acting DHS General Counsel Joseph Mazzara, in a June 2025 exchange among senior officials about the legal strategy for deploying National Guard troops to Los Angeles, suggested federal agents should have 'just started hitting' protesters and should have arrested 'everyone that couldn't get away.' The group says it obtained two versions of the records, one showing an attempted but failed redaction. Executive Director Chioma Chukwu said such remarks raise serious questions about the government's stance on free speech and public safety.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:38:55.269550+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/exclusive-internal-emails-reveal-top-dhs-attorney-suggested-agents-should-start-hitting-protesters","content":"News\nMarch 27, 2026\nExclusive: Internal Emails Reveal Top DHS Attorney Suggested Agents Should ‘Start Hitting’ Protesters\nTrump admin’s attempted redaction of damning portions of records raises alarming questions about use-of-force mindset at DHS\nimmigrationTrump administration accountability\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nSHARE\nFriday, we released newly-obtained internal Department of Homeland Security (DHS) emails revealing that the agency’s top attorney at the time suggested federal agents in Los Angeles should have “just started hitting” protesters during a 2025 demonstration against Trump’s inhumane immigration policies. The emails, which we obtained through the Freedom of Information Act, were first reported this morning by the Los Angeles Times.\nThe records show that then–acting DHS General Counsel Joseph Mazzara made the remarks in a June 2025 email exchange among senior officials discussing legal strategy related to the Trump administration’s controversial deployment of National Guard troops to Los Angeles — which a federal court later ruled was illegal. In the same message, Mazzara suggested agents should have arrested “everyone that couldn’t get away,” raising concerns about how senior legal officials viewed both protest activity and the appropriate use of force.\nNotably, we obtained two versions of the records. One set indicates that the agency had attempted but failed to properly redact Mazzara’s comments. In the other version, the statement had been successfully redacted, demonstrating that the agency may never have intended for the public to see the remarks.\n“Statements like this should alarm anyone who expects federal officials to respect free speech and keep the public safe. When an agency’s most senior lawyer responds to demonstrations by suggesting officers should ‘just start hitting’ people, it raises serious questions about the mindset shaping the government’s legal arguments and decision-making at the highest levels,” said our Executive Director Chioma Chukwu. “It’s no wonder the Trump administration wanted these comments redacted. They reveal a level of hostility toward protesters that is deeply at odds with the government’s obligation to protect civil liberties — and there’s no FOIA exemption that justifies hiding them. These types of attitudes don’t exist in a vacuum; they shape how authority is exercised amid increased tension, especially for immigrant families — many of whom are navigating the Trump administration’s inhumane mass deportation agenda with fear and uncertainty. Rhetoric like this reinforces concerns that aggressive and abusive tactics, rather than rule of law, may guide decisions that directly affect our safety, rights, and ability to participate in public life.”\nThe release comes amid continued scrutiny of the Trump administration’s use of federal forces in domestic settings and its handling of protest activity, including incidents in which demonstrators were injured or killed during enforcement actions.\nIn February, we released a tranche of records — obtained through a FOIA request and subsequent lawsuit against Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) — detailing troubling training practices and a more than 300 percent escalation in use-of-force incidents by ICE officers soon after President Trump returned to the White House. The records showed that senior ICE officials were aware as early as March 2025 that officers were using dramatically more force against civilians, months before officers shot and killed two U.S. citizens in Minneapolis.\nThe same records also revealed that ICE failed to publicly acknowledge the fatal shooting of 23-year-old U.S. citizen Ruben Ray Martinez in South Padre Island, Texas, in March 2025, until we obtained and released the documents. Reporting on the case raised serious questions about discrepancies between ICE’s internal account and what was initially communicated to Martinez’s family, underscoring broader concerns about transparency and whether additional incidents have gone undisclosed.\nThe materials further show that, even as official training instructed officers that entering a residence generally requires a judicial warrant or consent, instructors were directed to tell cadets that the use of controversial administrative warrants to enter homes was “under review” — aligning with recent whistleblower testimony that officers were given guidance suggesting they could enter homes without a judicial warrant while avoiding formal documentation of that instruction.","content_cn":"新闻\n2026年3月27日\n独家：内部邮件披露国土安全部首席律师建议特工应“开始动手打”抗议者\n特朗普政府试图对记录中具有破坏性的部分进行涂黑处理，引发了对国土安全部使用武力心态的令人担忧的质疑\n移民 特朗普政府问责\n查询请致信 press@americanoversight.org\n分享\n上周五，我们公布了新获取的国土安全部（DHS）内部邮件，披露该机构时任最高律师曾建议洛杉矶的联邦特工在2025年一场反对特朗普不人道移民政策的示威活动中“直接开始动手打”抗议者。这些邮件是我们通过《信息自由法》获取的，《洛杉矶时报》今晨率先报道。\n记录显示，时任国土安全部代理总法律顾问约瑟夫·马扎拉（Joseph Mazzara）是在2025年6月的一封邮件往来中发表上述言论的，当时高级官员正在讨论与特朗普政府备受争议地向洛杉矶部署国民警卫队相关的法律策略——联邦法院后来裁定该部署违法。在同一封邮件中，马扎拉建议特工应当逮捕“所有跑不掉的人”，这引发了人们对高级法律官员如何看待抗议活动及适当使用武力的担忧。\n值得注意的是，我们获取了两个版本的记录。其中一个版本显示，该机构曾试图对马扎拉的言论进行涂黑处理，但未能妥善完成。在另一个版本中，该言论已被成功涂黑，这表明该机构可能从未打算让公众看到这些言论。\n“任何期望联邦官员尊重言论自由并保障公众安全的人，都应该对这样的言论感到震惊。当一个机构最高级别的律师在回应示威活动时建议执法人员‘直接开始动手打’人，这引发了对其塑造政府法律论据和最高层决策的心态的严重质疑，”我们的执行主任奇奥玛·楚库（Chioma Chukwu）表示。“难怪特朗普政府想要涂黑这些言论。它们暴露出对抗议者一定程度的敌意，这与政府保护公民自由的义务严重相悖——而且没有任何《信息自由法》豁免条款能为隐藏这些言论提供正当理由。这类态度并非凭空存在；它们塑造了在紧张局势加剧时权力如何被行使，尤其是对移民家庭而言——其中许多人正怀着恐惧和不确定感应对特朗普政府不人道的大规模驱逐议程。这样的言论强化了人们的担忧，即激进和滥用的手段、而非法治，可能主导那些直接影响我们安全、权利和参与公共生活能力的决策。”\n此次公布之际，特朗普政府在国内使用联邦力量及处理抗议活动的方式持续受到审视，包括示威者在执法行动中受伤或死亡的事件。\n今年2月，我们公布了一批记录——通过《信息自由法》请求及随后对移民和海关执法局（ICE）提起的诉讼获得——详细披露了令人不安的培训做法，以及特朗普总统重返白宫后不久ICE官员使用武力事件激增超过300%的情况。记录显示，ICE高级官员早在2025年3月就知晓官员对平民使用武力的程度大幅上升，而这比官员在明尼阿波利斯开枪打死两名美国公民早了数月。\n同一批记录还显示，ICE未能公开承认2025年3月在得克萨斯州南帕德里岛23岁美国公民鲁本·雷·马丁内斯（Ruben Ray Martinez）遭枪杀一事，直到我们获取并公布了相关文件。对该案的报道引发了严重质疑，即ICE内部说法与最初向马丁内斯家属传达的内容之间存在出入，凸显了对透明度以及是否还有其他事件未被披露的更广泛担忧。\n这些材料进一步显示，即便官方培训教导官员进入住所通常需要司法搜查令或当事人同意，教官却被指示告诉学员，使用备受争议的行政搜查令进入住宅的做法“正在审查中”——这与近期举报人的证词相符，即官员获得的指导暗示他们可以在没有司法搜查令的情况下进入住宅，同时避免正式文件\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2026-03-27T21:35:24+00:00"}},{"id":"news-819","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"记录显示诺姆疑似将国土安全部资源用于政治目的，American Oversight寻求《哈奇法》调查","title_en":"American Oversight Seeks Hatch Act Investigation After Records Reveal Noem's Apparent Use of DHS Resources for Political Purposes - American Oversight","summary_cn":"American Oversight向美国特别检察官办公室提交投诉，要求调查前国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆及其幕僚是否违反《哈奇法》。投诉称，依据《信息自由法》获得的记录显示，诺姆及国土安全部人员于2025年6月使用纳税人资助的差旅前往田纳西州纳什维尔参加共和党州长协会活动，并利用官方Flickr账号宣传该活动及其他党派政治活动。投诉还提及围绕一项2.2亿美元广告宣传及购置湾流公务机计划的争议。","summary_en":"American Oversight filed a complaint with the U.S. Office of Special Counsel seeking an investigation into whether former Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem and her staff violated the Hatch Act. The complaint alleges that records obtained under FOIA show Noem and DHS staff used taxpayer-funded travel in June 2025 to attend a Republican Governors Association event in Nashville, Tennessee, and used the agency's official Flickr account to publicize that and other partisan events. It also cites controversy over a $220 million ad campaign and plans to acquire Gulfstream jets.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:22:43.768816+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/kristi-noem-hatch-act-inquiry","content":"News\nJune 4, 2026\nAmerican Oversight Seeks Hatch Act Investigation After Records Reveal Noem’s Apparent Use of DHS Resources for Political Purposes\nThursday, American Oversight submitted a complaint to the U.S. Office of Special Counsel (OSC) requesting an investigation into whether former Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem and members of her staff violated the Hatch Act. The complaint alleges that Noem and her staff used taxpayer-funded travel to attend a partisan Republican Governors Association (RGA) event and […]\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nSHARE\nThursday, American Oversight submitted a complaint to the U.S. Office of Special Counsel (OSC) requesting an investigation into whether former Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem and members of her staff violated the Hatch Act. The complaint alleges that Noem and her staff used taxpayer-funded travel to attend a partisan Republican Governors Association (RGA) event and used official Department of Homeland Security (DHS) communication channels to promote partisan political activities. Noem now serves in the Trump administration as Special Envoy for the Shield of the Americas, a newly created role focused on hemispheric security initiatives.\nThe complaint is based on records we obtained through the Freedom of Information Act (FOIA), which indicate that Noem and DHS staff traveled to Nashville, Tennessee, in June 2025 to attend an RGA conference — a partisan political organization dedicated to electing Republican governors. According to the records, attendance at the RGA event appears to have been the primary purpose of the trip. We are requesting that OSC investigate whether taxpayer-funded travel and other government resources were improperly used for political activity and whether any required reimbursements were made.\nThe complaint also asks OSC to investigate DHS’s use of its official Flickr account to publicize Noem’s attendance at the RGA conference and other partisan political events, including the Mackinac Republican Leadership Conference. Federal guidance prohibits agencies from using official social media accounts to promote partisan political activities.\n“Public resources exist to serve the public — full stop. They are not a vehicle for subsidizing partisan activity, promoting political allies, or elevating the personal political brand of government officials,” said our Executive Director Chioma Chukwu. “Americans should not be left to question whether their tax dollars are being used to underwrite partisan events or whether official government channels were used to amplify them. The public deserves a full accounting of how these resources were used and whether federal law was violated.”\nDuring her tenure at DHS, Noem drew bipartisan scrutiny from lawmakers over her use of DHS resources for political self-promotion. During her March 2026 Senate testimony just days before she was removed from her DHS post and named Special Envoy for the Shield of the Americas, Sen. John Kennedy pressed Noem over a controversial taxpayer-funded ad campaign that featured her prominently, asking whether “spending $220 million was appropriate” and telling her the ads were “effective in your name recognition.” Reports also noted that the campaign featured Noem on horseback near Mount Rushmore, that DHS bypassed the normal competitive bidding process, and that firms tied to Noem’s political circle received work on the campaign.\nQuestions about Noem’s use of taxpayer-funded resources extend beyond the advertising campaign. In early 2026, lawmakers also scrutinized DHS plans to acquire a pair of Gulfstream jets for executive travel, a proposal critics characterized as an unnecessary luxury expenditure that appeared designed to support Noem’s travel and public profile. The records we uncovered raise a related concern: that DHS resources may have been used not only to elevate Noem’s own political profile, but also to support partisan political allies and organizations.\nThe Hatch Act prohibits executive branch employees from using their official authority or influence to affect the outcome of an election and restricts the use of taxpayer-funded resources for partisan political activities. While certain Senate-confirmed officials are permitted to engage in some political activity while serving in office, federal law and OSC guidance require that public resources not be used to subsidize those activities.\nWe are requesting that OSC investigate whether DHS resources were improperly used to support partisan political activities and whether federal restrictions governing those activities were violated.","content_cn":"新闻\n2026年6月4日\n记录揭示诺姆疑似利用国土安全部资源从事政治目的后，美国监督组织寻求《哈奇法》调查\n周四，美国监督组织（American Oversight）向美国特别检察官办公室（OSC）提交了一份投诉，要求调查前国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆及其工作人员是否违反了《哈奇法》。投诉指控诺姆及其工作人员使用纳税人资助的差旅参加了一场党派性的共和党州长协会（RGA）活动，并……\n垂询：press@americanoversight.org\n分享\n周四，美国监督组织向美国特别检察官办公室（OSC）提交了一份投诉，要求调查前国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆及其工作人员是否违反了《哈奇法》。投诉指控诺姆及其工作人员使用纳税人资助的差旅参加了一场党派性的共和党州长协会（RGA）活动，并利用国土安全部（DHS）的官方沟通渠道宣传党派政治活动。诺姆现于特朗普政府中担任“美洲之盾”特使，这是一个新设立的职位，专注于半球安全倡议。\n该投诉基于我们通过《信息自由法》（FOIA）获得的记录，这些记录显示诺姆及国土安全部工作人员于2025年6月前往田纳西州纳什维尔参加一场RGA会议——该组织是一个致力于选举共和党州长的党派政治组织。根据记录，参加RGA活动似乎是此次出行的主要目的。我们要求OSC调查纳税人资助的差旅及其他政府资源是否被不当用于政治活动，以及是否进行了任何必要的报销。\n投诉还要求OSC调查国土安全部使用其官方Flickr账户宣传诺姆出席RGA会议及其他党派政治活动（包括麦基诺共和党领导力会议）的行为。联邦指导意见禁止各机构利用官方社交媒体账户宣传党派政治活动。\n“公共资源的存在是为了服务公众——仅此而已。它们不是用来补贴党派活动、宣传政治盟友或提升政府官员个人政治品牌的工具，”我们的执行主任奇奥玛·楚库表示。“美国人不应该被置于这样的疑问之中：他们的税款是否被用来资助党派活动，或者官方政府渠道是否被用来放大这些活动。公众理应获得关于这些资源如何被使用以及联邦法律是否遭到违反的完整交代。”\n在诺姆任职国土安全部期间，她因利用国土安全部资源进行政治自我宣传而受到两党议员的审视。在2026年3月她即将被免去国土安全部职务并被任命为“美洲之盾”特使前几天举行的参议院作证中，参议员约翰·肯尼迪就一场以她为主角、由纳税人资助的争议性广告宣传活动向诺姆施压，质问她“花费2.2亿美元是否合适”，并告诉她这些广告“在你的知名度方面很有效”。报道还指出，该宣传活动展示了诺姆在拉什莫尔山附近骑马的形象，国土安全部绕过了正常的竞争性招标程序，与诺姆政治圈有关联的公司获得了该宣传活动的工作。\n关于诺姆使用纳税人资助资源的问题不仅限于广告宣传活动。2026年初，议员们还审视了国土安全部计划购置两架湾流喷气式飞机用于行政出行的计划，批评者将这一提议描述为不必要的奢侈开支，似乎旨在支持诺姆的出行和公众形象。我们发现的记录引发了一个相关担忧：国土安全部资源可能不仅被用来提升诺姆本人的政治形象，还被用来支持党派政治盟友和组织。\n《哈奇法》禁止行政部门雇员利用其官方权力或影响力影响选举结果，并限制将纳税人资助的资源用于党派政治活动。虽然某些经参议院确认的官员在任职期间被允许从事某些政治活动，但联邦法律和OSC指导意见要求公共资源不得被用来补贴这些活动。\n我们要求OSC调查国土安全部资源是否被不当","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2026-06-04T20:05:41+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2072","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"诉讼促使国土安全部通知诺姆等高层官员妥善保存记录","title_en":"Lawsuit Spurs DHS Notice to Noem, Other Top Officials Demanding Proper Records Preservation - American Oversight","summary_cn":"2025年11月21日，American Oversight 在针对国土安全部的诉讼新法庭文件中披露，因诉讼压力，DHS 已发出通知，要求诺姆部长等高层官员“保存与本案诉讼标的相关的文件和电子记录”。该组织称，政府虽声称已归档并搜索多数官员设备，但无法确认这些官员保存了所有响应其《信息自由法》请求的记录。此前 DHS 承认其关于高层短信未保存的初始说法“有误”。该组织继续要求透明，并关注 DHS 是否遵守《联邦记录法》的20天电子记录转移要求。","summary_en":"On November 21, 2025, American Oversight revealed in a new court filing in its lawsuit against the Department of Homeland Security that, as a result of the litigation, DHS issued a notice demanding that Secretary Kristi Noem and other top officials 'preserve documents and electronic records that relate to the subject matter of the complaint.' The group said that while the government claims it has archived and searched most officials' devices, it cannot confirm those officials preserved all records responsive to American Oversight's FOIA requests. This follows DHS's admission that its initial assertion that top officials' text messages were no longer preserved was 'erroneous.' The group continues to press for transparency and scrutiny of DHS compliance with the Federal Records Act's 20-day electronic records transfer requirement.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:03:31.035797+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/lawsuit-spurs-dhs-notice-to-noem-other-top-officials-demanding-proper-records-preservation","content":"News\nNovember 21, 2025\nLawsuit Spurs DHS Notice to Noem, Other Top Officials Demanding Proper Records Preservation\nDHS now says it has instructed officials to preserve their communication records.\ndocument preservation requirements\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nSHARE\nOn Friday, following a new court filing in American Oversight’s lawsuit against the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) over the agency’s initial claim that it failed to preserve the electronic messages of Secretary Kristi Noem and other top agency officials, the nonpartisan watchdog revealed that as a result of its litigation, DHS has issued a notice demanding that these officials “preserve documents and electronic records that relate to the subject matter of the complaint in this case.”\nAdditionally, while the Trump administration now claims it has archived and searched most of these officials’ devices, it is unable to confirm that those officials preserved all records responsive to American Oversight’s FOIA requests. This follows the government’s recent admission that its initial assertion that the electronic messages of top DHS officials were no longer preserved was “erroneous.”\n“Weeks after admitting it provided ‘erroneous’ information about whether Secretary Noem and other senior DHS officials’ text messages were saved, DHS has finally put these officials on notice to follow the law and properly preserve these records, which belong to the American people,” said Chioma Chukwu, Executive Director of American Oversight. “These messages may shed light on decisions that profoundly impacted the lives of real families’ futures, led to wrongful deportations, and put vulnerable communities at risk. The public deserves to know the truth about the government’s actions, and we will continue pressing for answers and transparency.”\nAs part of today’s filing, the government has agreed to provide American Oversight with its forthcoming response to the National Archive and Records Administration’s (NARA’s) Sept. 3 letter directing DHS to investigate and explain how its record-retention policies for text messages comply with the Federal Records Act (FRA). DHS’s response should finally clarify whether its policies, as implemented, meet those legally mandated standards. NARA directed DHS to respond to its request for additional information within 30 days of the outcome of that investigation, which came during the government shutdown.\nImportantly, federal law requires custodians to transfer electronic records from their devices into a searchable system within 20 days. DHS’s own declarations confirm that its current policies fall short of this requirement: neither its guidance nor its declarations identify any deadline — let alone the 20-day legal mandate — for transferring non-email electronic records from employee devices. Based on DHS’s earlier declarations, that transfer does not appear to have occurred for the text messages potentially responsive to American Oversight’s FOIA requests. And because DHS relies on employees to screenshot and self-archive many electronic messages — a method that is not centrally searchable, as the government’s declaration explains — this deficiency extends far beyond the records at issue here, affecting any electronic communication archived outside the government’s forensic tools. If accurate, this would mean DHS failed to follow a core requirement of the FRA — one specifically designed to prevent the loss of electronic messages — to ensure that messages are captured and transferred to a searchable location.\nWhile DHS’s new declaration claims that most of the DHS officials’ devices were archived as of Nov. 14, the officials themselves did not attest that they preserved all records potentially responsive to American Oversight’s FOIA requests. If DHS responds to NARA as instructed — by explaining how its electronic message retention policies ensure text messages and messages on third-party platforms like Signal are “captured, managed and preserved” with their metadata so that DHS can “access and retrieve . . . electronic records, through electronic searches” — it should include clarification about how DHS ensures custodians’ compliance with the 20-day transfer deadline. Months after DHS first misled American Oversight about whether the records existed at all, the agency still has not demonstrated that the messages were preserved — making NARA’s demanded explanation all the more important.\nIn July, American Oversight submitted a FOIA request seeking the text, Signal, and email communications of Noem and other top DHS officials related to the National Guard’s questionable Los Angeles deployment to quell protests over the administration’s mass deportation agenda. In its July 23 response, DHS stated that it could not search for responsive records because “text message data generated after April 9, 2025, is no longer maintained.”\nAmerican Oversight submitted follow-up FOIA requests on Aug. 21 seeking the July 2025 text messages of Noem and other DHS leaders as well as records reflecting those messages. Just two and a half hours later, DHS responded with a categorical “no records” determination for each request, stating that it “no longer has the capability to conduct a search of text messages.”\nIn October, American Oversight filed a lawsuit against DHS based on the agency’s previous assertion that it failed to preserve text messages from Secretary Noem and other top DHS officials, as required by law. The nonpartisan watchdog also filed suit against the agency for failing to release text messages and other records that could shed light on DHS’s role in decisions ranging from military strikes and National Guard deployments in American cities to inhumane immigration enforcement and the upheaval of government operations.","content_cn":"新闻\n2025年11月21日\n诉讼促使国土安全部向诺姆及其他高级官员发出通知，要求妥善保存记录\n国土安全部现表示已指示官员保存其通信记录。\n文件保存要求\n咨询请联系press@americanoversight.org\n分享\n周五，在“美国监督”（American Oversight）针对国土安全部（DHS）的诉讼中提交新法庭文件后——该诉讼源于该机构最初声称未能保存部长克里斯蒂·诺姆（Kristi Noem）及其他机构高级官员的电子信息——这家无党派监督机构披露，由于其诉讼，国土安全部已发出通知，要求这些官员“保存与本案诉状主题事项相关的文件和电子记录”。\n此外，尽管特朗普政府现在声称已归档并检索了这些官员的大部分设备，但它无法确认这些官员保存了所有响应“美国监督”《信息自由法》（FOIA）请求的记录。此前，政府最近承认其最初关于国土安全部高级官员电子信息已不再保存的说法是“错误的”。\n“在承认其就诺姆部长及其他国土安全部高级官员的短信是否被保存提供了‘错误’信息数周后，国土安全部终于通知这些官员遵守法律并妥善保存这些属于美国人民的记录，”美国监督执行主任奇奥玛·楚库（Chioma Chukwu）表示。“这些信息可能揭示那些深刻影响真实家庭未来、导致错误驱逐出境、并使脆弱社区面临风险的决定。公众有权知道政府行为的真相，我们将继续追问答案并要求透明。”\n作为今日提交文件的一部分，政府已同意向“美国监督”提供其即将对国家档案与记录管理局（NARA）9月3日信函的回应。该信函指示国土安全部调查并解释其短信记录保存政策如何符合《联邦记录法》（FRA）。国土安全部的回应应最终澄清其政策在实际执行中是否符合这些法律规定的标准。NARA指示国土安全部在该调查结果出炉后30天内回应其补充信息请求，而该调查恰逢政府停摆期间。\n重要的是，联邦法律要求保管人须在20天内将设备中的电子记录转入可检索系统。国土安全部自己的声明证实，其现行政策未达到这一要求：无论是其指南还是其声明，均未指明任何将非电子邮件电子记录从员工设备中转移的截止期限——更不用说20天的法律强制要求。根据国土安全部此前的声明，对于可能响应“美国监督”《信息自由法》请求的短信，这一转移似乎并未发生。而且，由于国土安全部依赖员工自行截屏并自行归档许多电子信息——正如政府声明所解释的，这种方法无法进行集中检索——这一缺陷远远超出本案所涉记录，影响到任何在政府取证工具之外归档的电子通信。如果属实，这将意味着国土安全部未能遵守《联邦记录法》的一项核心要求——该要求专门旨在防止电子信息丢失——以确保信息被捕获并转移到可检索的位置。\n尽管国土安全部的新声明声称，截至11月14日，国土安全部官员的大部分设备已被归档，但官员本人并未证实他们保存了所有可能响应“美国监督”《信息自由法》请求的记录。如果国土安全部按指示回应NARA——解释其电子信息保存政策如何确保短信以及Signal等第三方平台上的信息连同其元数据被“捕获、管理和保存”，以便国土安全部能够“通过电子检索……访问和取回……电子记录”——那么它应澄清国土安全部如何确保保管人遵守20天转移截止期限。在国土安全部首次就这些记录是否存在误导“美国监督”数月之后，该机构仍未证明这些信息已被保存——这使得NARA所要求的解释更加重要。\n7月，“美国监督”提交了一份《信\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2025-11-21T21:45:43+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2712","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国监督组织诉国土安全部、海关与边境保护局、移民与海关执法局、公民及移民服务局和劳工部——移民执法政策指令与通讯","title_en":"American Oversight v. DHS, CBP, ICE, USCIS, and DOL — Immigration Enforcement Policy Directives and Communications - American Oversight","summary_cn":"美国监督组织（American Oversight）于2025年6月20日对国土安全部、海关与边境保护局、移民与海关执法局、公民及移民服务局及劳工部提起诉讼，要求强制公开与移民执法行动相关的通讯和政策指令，涉及在工作场所、宗教场所等敏感地点实施突袭、使用I-9审计等策略，可能揭示当局的逮捕和驱逐优先事项。案件编号25-1932，目前仍在审理中。","summary_en":"American Oversight filed a lawsuit on June 20, 2025 against the Department of Homeland Security, Customs and Border Protection, Immigration and Customs Enforcement, U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services, and the Department of Labor, seeking to compel the release of communications and policy directives related to immigration enforcement actions, including raids at sensitive locations such as worksites and places of worship and the use of I-9 audits, which could shed light on the administration's arrest and deportation priorities. Docket Number 25-1932; status open.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:35:27.555829+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/litigation/american-oversight-v-dhs-cbp-ice-uscis-and-dol-immigration-enforcement-policy-directives-and-communications","content":"Legal Action\nJune 20, 2025\nAmerican Oversight v. DHS, CBP, ICE, USCIS, and DOL — Immigration Enforcement Policy Directives and Communications\nLawsuit filed by American Oversight against the DHS, CBP, ICE, USCIS, and the DOL seeking to compel the release of communications and policy directives related to immigration enforcement actions.\nFederalimmigrationweaponization of government\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nStatusopen\nDocket Number\n25-1932\nSHARE\nLawsuit filed by American Oversight against the Department of Homeland Security, Customs and Border Protection, Immigration and Customs Enforcement, U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services, and the Department of Labor seeking to compel the release of communications and policy directives related to immigration enforcement actions, such as raids at sensitive locations like worksites and places of worship and the use of I-9 audits and other tactics, which could shed light on the administration’s arrest and deportation priorities.","content_cn":"法律行动\n2025年6月20日\nAmerican Oversight 诉 DHS、CBP、ICE、USCIS 和 DOL——移民执法政策指令与通信记录\nAmerican Oversight 对 DHS、CBP、ICE、USCIS 和 DOL 提起诉讼，寻求强制公开与移民执法行动有关的通信记录和政策指令。\n联邦移民政府武器化\n咨询 press@americanoversight.org\n状态：开放\n案卷编号\n25-1932\n分享\nAmerican Oversight 对国土安全部、海关与边境保护局、移民与海关执法局、美国公民及移民服务局以及劳工部提起诉讼，寻求强制公开与移民执法行动有关的通信记录和政策指令，例如在工作场所和宗教礼拜场所等敏感地点开展突击行动，以及使用 I-9 审计和其他策略；这些资料可能揭示本届政府在逮捕和驱逐出境方面的优先事项。","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2025-06-20T15:14:48+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2587","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国监督组织诉国土安全部、海关与边境保护局、移民与海关执法局和公民及移民服务局——移民登记要求","title_en":"American Oversight v. DHS, CBP, ICE, and USCIS — Immigrant Registration Requirements  - American Oversight","summary_cn":"American Oversight于2025年7月24日发布诉讼登记，要求国土安全部及其CBP、ICE、USCIS机构公开移民登记相关记录，包括第14159号行政命令。页面列出案号25-2390、状态为open；该状态不等于已经作出裁决。","summary_en":"American Oversight filed a lawsuit on July 24, 2025 against the Department of Homeland Security, Customs and Border Protection, Immigration and Customs Enforcement, and U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services, seeking to compel the release of records related to immigrant registration, including Executive Order 14159 titled 'Protecting the American People Against Invasion.' Docket Number 25-2390; status open.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:25:39.770010+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/litigation/complaint-american-oversight-v-dhs-cbp-ice-and-uscis-immigrant-registration-requirements","content":"Legal Action\nJuly 24, 2025\nAmerican Oversight v. DHS, CBP, ICE, and USCIS — Immigrant Registration Requirements\nLawsuit filed by American Oversight against DHS, CBP, ICE, USCIS seeking to compel the release of records related to immigrant registration.\nFederalimmigration\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nStatusopen\nDocket Number\n25-2390\nSHARE\nLawsuit filed by American Oversight against the Department of Homeland Security, Customs and Border Protection, Immigration and Customs Enforcement, and U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services seeking to compel the release of records related to immigrant registration, including Executive Order 14159 titled “Protecting the American People Against Invasion.”\nRead the complaint here.","content_cn":"法律行动\n2025年7月24日\n美国监督组织诉国土安全部、海关与边境保护局、移民与海关执法局和美国公民及移民服务局——移民登记要求\n美国监督组织针对国土安全部、海关与边境保护局、移民与海关执法局及美国公民及移民服务局提起诉讼，寻求迫使其公开与移民登记有关的记录。\n联邦移民\n咨询 press@americanoversight.org\n状态：开放\n案卷编号\n25-2390\n分享\n美国监督组织针对国土安全部、海关与边境保护局、移民与海关执法局及美国公民及移民服务局提起诉讼，寻求迫使其公开与移民登记有关的记录，包括题为“保护美国人民免受入侵”的第14159号行政命令。\n在此阅读起诉书。","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2025-07-24T15:39:29+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3146","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国监督组织谴责卡什·帕特尔获确认领导联邦调查局","title_en":"American Oversight Condemns Confirmation of Kash Patel to Lead Federal Bureau of Investigation - American Oversight","summary_cn":"美国监督组织（American Oversight）发表声明，谴责卡什·帕特尔获确认出任联邦调查局局长。该组织称多年来一直调查帕特尔的记录与通讯，并采取多项法律行动要求公开特别检察官关于特朗普处理机密文件的报告。该组织临时执行主任奇奥马·丘库表示，尽管帕特尔有激烈言论、政治攻击且缺乏执法管理经验，参议院仍予以确认，并誓言继续追究其责任，反对将FBI政治化。","summary_en":"American Oversight issued a statement condemning the confirmation of Kash Patel as director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation. The group said it has investigated Patel for years and taken multiple legal actions to bring to light the special counsel's report on Trump's alleged mishandling of classified documents. Interim Executive Director Chioma Chukwu said the Senate confirmed Patel despite his record of vitriol, political attacks, and lack of law enforcement management experience, vowing to keep holding him accountable and opposing politicization of the FBI.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:25:54.493996+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/press-release/american-oversight-condemns-confirmation-of-kash-patel-to-lead-federal-bureau-of-investigation","content":"News\nFebruary 20, 2025\nAmerican Oversight Condemns Confirmation of Kash Patel to Lead Federal Bureau of Investigation\nAmerican Oversight’s condemnation of Patel follows extensive investigation into Patel’s problematic record and communications\nTrump administration accountabilityTrump appointees\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nSHARE\nFollowing a turbulent nomination process for Kash Patel, President Donald Trump’s controversial pick for Director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI), today American Oversight condemned his confirmation to be the next head of the powerful law enforcement agency.\nAmerican Oversight has investigated Patel for years — including most recently taking multiple legal actions to bring to light the special counsel’s report on Trump’s alleged mishandling of classified documents, which potentially involved Patel — and will continue to hold him accountable for any attempts to weaponize the FBI, politicize law enforcement, and use his new post to enact Trump’s promised “retribution” against his political enemies.\n“Despite his record of vitriol, political attacks, and complete lack of law enforcement management experience, the Senate voted to confirm Kash Patel as FBI Director without full disclosure of his role in one of the most consequential criminal investigations in our nation’s history,” said American Oversight interim Executive Director Chioma Chukwu. “With Congress failing to act as a check on an out-of-control executive branch, the need for independent watchdogs like American Oversight is more important than ever. We will continue fighting for the release of the special counsel’s report and remain committed to holding Patel and the administration accountable.”\nJust days ago, American Oversight submitted an expedited motionasking Judge Aileen Cannon to dissolve her Jan. 21 order barring the Department of Justice from releasing Volume Two of Special Counsel Jack Smith’s report on President Trump’s mishandling of classified documents, or confirm that the order expired when all remaining criminal charges in the case were dismissed in January.\nThat motion followed American Oversight’s Feb. 10 lawsuit and motionfor a preliminary injunction against the DOJ, demanding the swift release of the report. The report could have exposed highly critical details about Patel. Despite this, DOJ claimed it could not release the report until Judge Cannon lifted her order.\nIn 2021, American Oversight sued for communications records of top Trump administration officials from the time of the Jan. 6 insurrection, including Patel’s communications. One of the lawsuits revealed that the Pentagon had failed to preserve senior officials’ text messages, leading to the department announcing a change in policy.\nThe nomination and confirmation of Patel, who rose through the ranks of the Trump administration as an avowed loyalist to the president, raises serious concerns about how Trump could weaponize the FBI for his promised “retribution” against his political enemies.\nPatel has promoted conspiracy theories about the 2020 election as well as the “deep state,” which he has pledged to purge of “government gangsters.” In public statements, Patel has said he plans to “find the conspirators” in both government and in the media. “Yes, we’re going to come after the people in the media who lied about American citizens, who helped Joe Biden rig presidential elections,” he said. “We’re going to come after you. Whether it’s criminally or civilly, we’ll figure that out.” Patel’s confirmation as FBI director puts him in charge of a federal law enforcement agency that he could use to target his enemies list of critics and high-ranking officials.","content_cn":"新闻\n2025年2月20日\n美国监督组织谴责确认卡什·帕特尔领导联邦调查局\n美国监督组织在对帕特尔的问题记录和通信展开广泛调查后，谴责对其的确认\n特朗普政府问责 特朗普任命官员\n咨询：press@americanoversight.org\n分享\n在卡什·帕特尔经历动荡的提名程序后——这位总统唐纳德·特朗普颇具争议的联邦调查局（FBI）局长人选——美国监督组织今日谴责确认他担任这一强大执法机构的下一任负责人。\n美国监督组织多年来一直在调查帕特尔——最近还采取了多项法律行动，以公开特别检察官关于特朗普涉嫌不当处理机密文件的报告，该事件可能涉及帕特尔——并将继续追究他任何企图将联邦调查局武器化、将执法政治化，以及利用新职位实施特朗普承诺对政治敌人进行“报复”的行为。\n美国监督组织代理执行主任奇奥马·楚库说：“尽管卡什·帕特尔有充满恶意的言论记录、政治攻击记录，并且完全缺乏执法管理经验，参议院仍在未充分披露他在我国历史上最重要的刑事调查之一中的作用的情况下，投票确认他担任联邦调查局局长。国会未能对失控的行政部门发挥制衡作用，使得美国监督组织这样的独立监督机构比以往任何时候都更加重要。我们将继续争取公开特别检察官的报告，并将继续致力于追究帕特尔和本届政府的责任。”\n就在几天前，美国监督组织提交了一项加急动议，请求艾琳·坎农法官撤销其1月21日发布的命令。该命令禁止司法部公开特别检察官杰克·史密斯关于特朗普不当处理机密文件的报告第二卷；或者确认该命令已于1月该案所有剩余刑事指控被撤销时失效。\n这项动议是在美国监督组织2月10日对司法部提起诉讼并申请初步禁令之后提出的，诉讼要求迅速公开该报告。报告本可能披露有关帕特尔的高度批评性细节。尽管如此，司法部声称，在坎农法官解除其命令之前，它无法公开报告。\n2021年，美国监督组织起诉要求公开特朗普政府高级官员在1月6日叛乱期间的通信记录，其中包括帕特尔的通信。一宗诉讼揭露五角大楼未能保存高级官员的短信，促使该部门宣布改变政策。\n帕特尔的提名和确认引发了严重担忧：作为一名公开效忠总统、在特朗普政府内部逐级晋升的人，他可能会如何利用联邦调查局武器化，以对政治敌人实施特朗普承诺的“报复”。\n帕特尔曾散布有关2020年选举以及“深层政府”的阴谋论，并承诺清除其中的“政府恶棍”。帕特尔在公开声明中说，他计划在政府和媒体中“找出阴谋者”。他说：“是的，我们要追究那些对美国公民撒谎、帮助乔·拜登操纵总统选举的媒体人士。我们要追究你们。无论是刑事还是民事，我们会想办法。”帕特尔获确认为联邦调查局局长后，负责领导一个联邦执法机构，而他可能利用该机构针对其敌人名单中的批评者和高级官员。","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2025-02-20T20:49:41+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1510","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国监督组织谴责与特朗普机密文件调查相关的FBI探员遭清洗","title_en":"American Oversight Slams Purge of FBI Agents Tied to Investigation of Trump’s Mishandling of Classified Documents - American Oversight","summary_cn":"美国监督组织就FBI局长卡什·帕特尔解雇约10名参与特朗普机密文件调查的FBI雇员发表声明，批评此举是报复性清洗。声明指出，解雇发生在法官坎农永久禁止公开特别检察官杰克·史密斯报告第二卷数日之后，认为这损害公众对机构的信任，将总统个人利益置于美国人民之上。","summary_en":"American Oversight issued a statement condemning FBI Director Kash Patel's firing of roughly 10 FBI employees tied to the investigation into Trump's handling of classified documents. The group called it a retaliatory purge, noting it came days after Judge Cannon permanently blocked release of Volume II of Special Counsel Jack Smith's report, and said it damages public trust in institutions.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:53:32.253665+00:00","url":"https://americanoversight.org/press-release/american-oversight-slams-purge-of-fbi-agents-tied-to-investigation-of-trumps-mishandling-of-classified-documents","content":"News\nFebruary 26, 2026\nAmerican Oversight Slams Purge of FBI Agents Tied to Investigation of Trump’s Mishandling of Classified Documents\nThe FBI firings come just days after Judge Cannon granted Trump’s motion to permanently block the full release of Jack Smith’s report on the classified documents investigation.\nTrump administration accountabilityweaponization of government\nInquiriespress@americanoversight.org\nSHARE\nWednesday, responding to news that Federal Bureau of Investigations (FBI) Director Kash Patel fired roughly 10 FBI employees tied to the investigation into President Trump’s alleged mishandling of national security documents — just days after Judge Aileen Cannon granted the president’s motion to permanently bar release of Volume II of Special Counsel Jack Smith’s report on the matter — we released the following statement slamming the retaliatory purge and ongoing efforts to bury the truth:\n“Director Patel’s removal of career public servants who were carrying out a lawful investigation into the president’s willful mishandling of classified records raises profound questions about what he is trying to hide. That he purged agents for simply doing their jobs just days after Judge Cannon permanently barred the release of Volume II of Special Counsel Jack Smith’s report — a taxpayer-funded report detailing the evidence and charging decisions in that case — is indefensible,” said our Executive Director Chioma Chukwu. “The public was promised the most transparent administration in history. Instead, they are witnessing retaliation against law enforcement and a coordinated effort to ensure that the truth never sees the light of day. This kind of interference damages trust in our institutions and shows that FBI leadership is putting the president’s personal interests ahead of the American people.”\nIn December, Smith spent more than eight hours testifying behind closed doors before the House Judiciary Committee. There, he revealed that his investigation produced “proof beyond a reasonable doubt” that President Trump unlawfully attempted to overturn the 2020 election and that he had uncovered “powerful evidence” that the president willfully retained highly classified documents after leaving office.\nLast week, in an extension of her unprecedented deference to President Trump, Judge Cannon granted motions filed by the president and his co-conspirators to permanently block the release of Volume II of Smith’s final report, preventing the public from accessing the full account of the evidence and the report’s findings. In a separate order, Judge Cannon also denied our joint motion with the Knight First Amendment Institute seeking a stay of proceedings while our appeal of her decision preventing our participation in the criminal proceedings to seek the report’s release is pending with the Eleventh Circuit Court of Appeals. Our appeal of the denial of an earlier motion to intervene is currently before the Eleventh Circuit, with oral arguments tentatively scheduled in June.","content_cn":"新闻\n2026年2月26日\nAmerican Oversight 抨击清洗参与调查特朗普不当处理机密文件案的 FBI 探员\nFBI 解雇行动发生在卡农法官批准特朗普永久阻止完整公开杰克·史密斯关于机密文件调查报告的动议仅数日后。\n特朗普政府问责\n政府武器化\n咨询\npress@americanoversight.org\n分享\n周三，针对联邦调查局（FBI）局长卡什·帕特尔解雇约10名参与调查特朗普总统涉嫌不当处理国家安全文件的 FBI 雇员的消息——此事发生在艾琳·卡农法官批准总统永久禁止公开特别检察官杰克·史密斯就此事撰写的报告第二卷仅数日后——我们发布以下声明，谴责这种报复性清洗以及持续掩埋真相的努力：\n“帕特尔局长罢免那些正在对总统故意不当处理机密记录一事开展合法调查的职业公务员，引发了关于他试图隐瞒什么的深刻疑问。他在卡农法官永久禁止公开特别检察官杰克·史密斯报告第二卷——这份由纳税人资助、详细说明该案证据和起诉决定的报告——仅数日后，就因探员只是履行职责而清洗他们，这是站不住脚的，”我们的执行主任 Chioma Chukwu 表示。“公众曾被承诺将迎来史上最透明的政府。但他们看到的却是对执法人员的报复，以及一项确保真相永不见天日的协调行动。这种干预损害了公众对我们机构的信任，并表明 FBI 领导层正将总统的个人利益置于美国人民利益之上。”\n12月，史密斯在众议院司法委员会进行了超过八小时的闭门作证。他在那里披露，他的调查产生了“排除合理怀疑的证据”，证明特朗普总统曾非法试图推翻2020年选举；他还发现了“有力证据”，证明该总统在离任后故意保留高度机密文件。\n上周，卡农法官延续其对特朗普总统前所未有的迁就，批准了总统及其共同谋划者提出的动议，永久阻止公开史密斯最终报告的第二卷，从而阻止公众获得该报告中完整的证据叙述和调查结论。在另一项命令中，卡农法官还驳回了我们与奈特第一修正案研究所共同提出的动议；该动议请求在我们就其阻止我们参与刑事诉讼以寻求公开该报告的裁决向第十一巡回上诉法院提出上诉期间，中止诉讼程序。我们对较早前一项介入动议被驳回所提出的上诉目前正在第十一巡回上诉法院审理，口头辩论暂定于6月举行。","publish_source":"americanoversight.org","publish_time":"2026-02-26T21:26:49+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3155","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"特朗普痴迷移民清洗致国土安全部探员与资金从打击芬太尼、枪支和人口贩运转向","title_en":"Trump Obsession with Immigrant Purge Leads to Diversion of DHS Agents & Funds Away from Fighting Fentanyl, Guns and Human Trafficking - America's Voice","summary_cn":"美国之声援引《今日美国》报道指出，国土安全部下令其6000名调查部门探员将重点从毒品、恐怖主义和人口贩运转向驱逐非法移民。文章批评此举削弱对芬太尼走私、卡特尔、网络攻击等跨国威胁的调查，认为特朗普政府将反移民置于公共安全之上，代价高昂。","summary_en":"America's Voice cites a USA Today report that the Department of Homeland Security ordered its 6,000-agent investigations division to shift focus from drugs, terrorism and human trafficking to deporting undocumented immigrants. The piece argues this undermines investigations into fentanyl smuggling, cartels and other transnational threats, prioritizing anti-immigrant goals over public safety.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:05:40.731634+00:00","url":"https://americasvoice.org/press_releases/trump-obsession-with-immigrant-purge-leads-to-diversion-of-dhs-agents-funds-away-from-fighting-fentanyl-guns-and-human-trafficking","content":"tags: Press Releases\nTrump Obsession with Immigrant Purge Leads to Diversion of DHS Agents & Funds Away from Fighting Fentanyl, Guns and Human Trafficking\nby AV Press Releases on February 18, 2025\nShare This:\nWashington, DC — Last week, we highlighted the high cost of the Trump administration’s anti-immigrant obsessions and plans for indiscriminate mass deportations above all. Over the weekend, a USA Today story, “Thousands of DHS agents shift to deportation instead of drugs, weapons and human trafficking,” underscored the point and adds to the growing mountain of evidence that even real public safety threats are being deprioritized in the process.\nAccording to Vanessa Cárdenas, Executive Director of America’s Voice:\n“The Trump administration’s obsession to purge America of immigrants knows no bounds and comes at a very high cost to us all. As the USA Today story makes clear, DHS agents have been diverted from combating real threats to public safety like the scourge of fentanyl, among other dangerous drugs, gun running and stopping human traffickers from conducting their evil trade. Instead, Trump is prioritizing a quid pro quo deal with the Mayor of New York over immigration, and spending millions on mindless anti-immigrant ads – all at taxpayer expense and real threats.”\nLast week, we noted that among the many high costs of the Trump administration’s obsession include: trampling on the rule of law; pardoning or ignoring actual criminal behavior; subverting many other policy priorities and actual public safety threats – including taking critical resources away from key domestic priorities and drug enforcement, combatting fentanyl and terrorism investigations – in favor of a focus on indiscriminate mass deportations; the negative economic and inflationary impacts of deporting key workers; and a failure to pursue real solutions to a broken immigration system in favor of chaos and cruelty. The USA Today story, by reporter Josh Meyer, adds more details, noting in part:\n“The Department of Homeland Security has ordered its entire investigations division – composed of 6,000 agents – to divert focus on drug dealers, terrorists, and human traffickers and shift priority to the Trump administration’s mission of deporting people in the U.S. illegally, USA TODAY has learned. The new focus for DHS’s Homeland Security Investigations agency (HSI), current and former officials say, is in keeping with recent executive orders signed by President Donald Trump that demand a wholesale shift in federal law enforcement resources toward immigration crackdowns and removal.\nBut they warn the shift will undermine high-profile investigations into some of the most dangerous transnational threats Americans face, including Mexican drug cartels smuggling deadly fentanyl across the border from Mexico.\n…Kenneth MacDonald, another former HSI supervisory agent and a former White House official, said other critical threats could go uninvestigated by HSI, which he described as the second largest U.S. federal investigative law enforcement agency after the FBI. Those include child exploitation crimes, cyberattacks and Dark Web financial schemes, Iranian and Chinese nuclear traffickers, Russian organized crime, trade fraud and sanctions investigations.\n…The directive could also threaten ongoing investigations and prosecutions, many of which are multi-agency efforts that have been years in the making – like several ongoing cases against the Sinaloa Cartel and other Mexican and Chinese transnational crime syndicates, current and former officials said.”","content_cn":"标签：新闻稿\n特朗普对清除移民的执念，导致国土安全部探员和资金从打击芬太尼、枪支及人口贩运中被转移\n由AV新闻稿于2025年2月18日发布\n分享：\n华盛顿哥伦比亚特区——上周，我们强调了特朗普政府反移民执念以及不惜一切代价推行不加区分的大规模驱逐计划所造成的高昂代价。周末，《今日美国》的一篇报道《数千名国土安全部探员转向驱逐出境，而非毒品、武器和人口贩运》，突出了这一点，并为越来越多的证据再添一笔：在此过程中，即使是真正的公共安全威胁也正被降级处理。\n\n据America’s Voice执行主任Vanessa Cárdenas称：\n\n“特朗普政府将美国清除移民的执念毫无边界，对我们所有人都代价极高。正如《今日美国》的报道所清楚表明的，国土安全部探员已从打击真正威胁公共安全的事物中被转移，包括芬太尼这一祸害、其他危险毒品、枪支走私，以及阻止人口贩子从事其邪恶交易。相反，特朗普正将移民问题上的交换条件交易置于与纽约市市长的关系之上，并花费数百万美元投放无脑的反移民广告——这一切都由纳税人买单，并以真实威胁为代价。”\n\n上周，我们指出，特朗普政府这一执念的众多高昂代价包括：践踏法治；赦免或无视实际的犯罪行为；颠覆许多其他政策优先事项和真正的公共安全威胁——包括从关键国内优先事项、禁毒、打击芬太尼及恐怖主义调查中抽走关键资源——转而专注于不加区分的大规模驱逐；驱逐关键劳工造成的负面经济和通胀影响；以及放弃寻求解决破损移民制度的真正方案，转而制造混乱和残酷。《今日美国》记者Josh Meyer的报道补充了更多细节，部分内容如下：\n\n“《今日美国》获悉，美国国土安全部已命令其整个调查部门——由6,000名探员组成——从毒贩、恐怖分子和人口贩子身上转移重点，优先执行特朗普政府驱逐非法居留在美国人员的任务。现任和前任官员称，国土安全部国土安全调查局（HSI）的新重点符合唐纳德·特朗普总统近期签署的行政命令，这些命令要求将联邦执法资源全面转向移民严打和遣返。\n\n但他们警告称，这一转变将削弱针对美国人面临的一些最危险跨国威胁的高调调查，其中包括墨西哥贩毒集团从墨西哥越境走私致命芬太尼。\n\n……另一名前HSI主管探员、前白宫官员Kenneth MacDonald表示，HSI可能不会调查其他关键威胁；他将HSI描述为仅次于FBI的美国第二大联邦调查执法机构。这些威胁包括儿童剥削犯罪、网络攻击和暗网金融计划、伊朗和中国的核材料贩运者、俄罗斯有组织犯罪、贸易欺诈和制裁调查。\n\n……现任和前任官员称，该指令还可能威胁正在进行的调查和起诉，其中许多是历经多年形成的多机构合作——例如针对锡那罗亚贩毒集团以及其他墨西哥和中国跨国犯罪集团的数起正在进行的案件。”","publish_source":"americasvoice.org","publish_time":"2025-02-18T17:52:14+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2866","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"前FBI局长贝壳照片帖引发争议","title_en":"Seashell photo post by former FBI director sparks controversy | Amu TV","summary_cn":"前FBI局长詹姆斯·科米在Instagram发布贝壳排列成“8647”的照片，被批评者解读为暗示对特朗普总统的暴力，随后删除。特勤局表示正在审查，现任FBI局长卡什·帕特尔称正与特勤局联系并提供支持。科米称未意识到数字关联暴力，反对任何形式的暴力。","summary_en":"Former FBI Director James Comey deleted an Instagram post showing seashells spelling '8647,' which critics read as suggesting violence against President Trump. The Secret Service said it is reviewing the matter, and current FBI Director Kash Patel said the bureau is in contact with the Secret Service. Comey said he did not realize the numbers' violent association and opposes violence.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:29:54.804429+00:00","url":"https://amu.tv/174408","content":"US\nSeashell photo post by former FBI director sparks controversy\nby Habib Mohammadi\nMay 16, 2025\n28 Views\nFacebook Twitter LinkedIn Whatsapp Print Share via Email\nWASHINGTON — Former FBI Director James B. Comey is under investigation by the U.S. Secret Service following a now-deleted social media post that critics, including senior Republican officials, claim suggested harm toward President Donald J. Trump.\nComey, who led the FBI from 2013 to 2017, posted a photo to Instagram earlier this week showing a line of seashells arranged to spell out the number “8647.” He captioned the image: “Cool shell formation on my beach walk.” While seemingly innocuous to some, the number sparked backlash after commentators noted that “86” is sometimes used as slang for “eliminate” or “kill,” and “47” is widely used as shorthand for Trump, the 47th president of the United States.\nThe post was swiftly condemned by conservative figures, including Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi Noem, who accused Comey of inciting violence. “Disgraced former FBI Director James Comey just called for the assassination of Trump,” Noem wrote on X, formerly known as Twitter. White House Deputy Chief of Staff Dan Scavino went further, describing the post as “a plea to bad actors/terrorists to assassinate the POTUS.”\nComey later deleted the photo and said in a follow-up post that the interpretation had not occurred to him. “I didn’t realize some folks associate those numbers with violence,” he wrote. “It never occurred to me, but I oppose violence of any kind so I took the post down.”\nThe Secret Service confirmed it is reviewing the matter. “We vigorously investigate anything that can be taken as a potential threat against our protectees,” spokesman Anthony Guglielmi said in a statement. “We are aware of the social media posts by the former FBI Director, and we take rhetoric like this very seriously.”\nCurrent FBI Director Kash Patel acknowledged the situation, stating on social media that the agency is in contact with the Secret Service and would provide support. “Primary jurisdiction is with the Secret Service on these matters,” Patel added.\nComey, who was dismissed by Trump in 2017 during the FBI’s investigation into Russian interference in the 2016 election, has been a frequent target of criticism from the Trump camp. The tension between the two dates back to Comey’s oversight of the Clinton email investigation, which many Democrats and some Republicans believe influenced the outcome of the 2016 election.\nPresident Trump, who has survived two assassination attempts in the past year, is currently on a diplomatic tour in the Middle East. His eldest son, Donald Trump Jr., also weighed in, accusing Comey on X of “casually calling for my dad to be murdered.”\nAs of Friday evening, Comey had not issued further public comment beyond his explanation and removal of the original post.\nShare This Post:\nFacebook Twitter LinkedIn Whatsapp Print Share via Email\nRelated Posts\nImmigration, US\nUS deports 12 Afghan nationals to Central African Republic\nAugust 30, 2026\nUS\nWho is Aisha Wahab, the first Afghan American elected to Congress?\nAugust 21, 2026\nPolitics, US\nHegseth says US efforts to remake Afghanistan, Iraq cost thousands of lives\nJuly 22, 2026\nPolitics, US\nEx-MP Zahir Qadeer extradited to US\nJuly 11, 2026\nSearch\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nLanguage\nEnglish\nفارسی\nپښتو\nLatest\nSeptember 18, 2026\nAmu 8pm News\nAmu TV 8pm News 17 Sep 2026\nThe visit by senior Turkish and Qatari security officials to Kabul was made at Pakistan’s\nSeptember 18, 2026\nAmu 6pm News\nAmu TV 6pm News 17 Sep 2026\nSeptember 17, 2026\nSports\nIndia defeat Afghanistan by 127 runs to complete 3-0 T20I sweep\nSeptember 17, 2026\nPolitics\nExclusive: Turkish, Qatari officials in Kabul at Pakistan’s request","content_cn":"美国\n前联邦调查局局长发布贝壳照片引发争议\n哈比卜·穆罕默迪\n2025年5月16日\n28次浏览\nFacebook Twitter LinkedIn Whatsapp 打印 通过电子邮件分享\n\n华盛顿——美国特勤局正在调查前联邦调查局局长詹姆斯·B·科米此前发布的一则现已删除的社交媒体帖子。包括共和党高层官员在内的批评者声称，该帖子暗示要伤害总统唐纳德·J·特朗普。\n\n2013年至2017年担任联邦调查局局长的科米本周早些时候在Instagram上发布了一张照片，显示一排贝壳排列成数字“8647”。他为照片配文：“我在海滩散步时看到的酷贝壳排列。”对一些人来说，这看似无害，但评论人士指出，“86”有时被用作“消灭”或“杀死”的俚语，而“47”则被广泛用作特朗普这位美国第47任总统的简称，因此该数字引发了强烈反弹。\n\n这则帖子很快遭到保守派人士谴责，其中包括国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，她指责科米煽动暴力。诺姆在X（前身为推特）上写道：“声名狼藉的前联邦调查局局长詹姆斯·科米刚刚呼吁刺杀特朗普。”白宫副幕僚长丹·斯卡维诺进一步称，这则帖子是“向不法分子/恐怖分子发出的刺杀美国总统的请求”。\n\n科米后来删除了这张照片，并在后续帖子中表示，他此前没有想到这种解读。他写道：“我没有意识到有些人会把这些数字与暴力联系起来。这从未在我脑中出现过，但我反对任何形式的暴力，所以删除了这条帖子。”\n\n特勤局证实正在审查此事。发言人安东尼·古列尔米在一份声明中说：“对于任何可能被视为针对我们受保护对象的潜在威胁，我们都会进行有力调查。我们已注意到前联邦调查局局长发布的社交媒体帖子，并且非常严肃地对待此类言论。”\n\n现任联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔承认了这一情况，他在社交媒体上表示，该机构正与特勤局保持联系，并将提供支持。帕特尔补充说：“这类事务的主要管辖权在特勤局。”\n\n2017年，特朗普在联邦调查局调查俄罗斯干预2016年大选期间解雇了科米。科米一直是特朗普阵营批评的对象。两人之间的紧张关系可追溯到科米负责监督希拉里·克林顿电子邮件调查之时；许多民主党人和一些共和党人认为，该调查影响了2016年大选结果。\n\n曾在过去一年中躲过两次刺杀企图的特朗普总统目前正在中东进行外交访问。他的长子小唐纳德·特朗普也在X上发表评论，指责科米“漫不经心地呼吁杀害我父亲”。\n\n截至周五晚间，除解释并删除原帖外，科米尚未发表进一步公开评论。\n\n分享此帖子：\nFacebook Twitter LinkedIn Whatsapp 打印 通过电子邮件分享\n\n相关文章\n移民，美国\n美国将12名阿富汗国民驱逐至中非共和国\n2026年8月30日\n美国\n艾莎·瓦哈卜是谁？首位当选国会议员的阿富汗裔美国人\n2026年8月21日\n政治，美国\n赫格塞思称美国重塑阿富汗、伊拉克的努力导致数千人丧生\n2026年7月22日\n政治，美国\n前议员扎希尔·卡迪尔被引渡至美国\n2026年7月11日\n\n搜索\n订阅我们的新闻通讯\n语言\n英语\n波斯语\n普什图语\n\n最新\n2026年9月18日\n阿穆8点新闻\n阿穆电视台2026年9月17日8点新闻\n土耳其和卡塔尔高级安全官员访问喀布尔，是应巴基斯坦要求进行的\n2026年9月18日\n阿穆6点新闻\n阿穆电视台2026年9月17日6点新闻\n2026年9月17日\n体育\n印度以127分击败阿富汗，完成T20I系列赛3比0横扫\n2026年9月17日\n政治\n独家：土耳其、卡塔尔官员应巴基斯坦要求抵达喀布尔","publish_source":"amu.tv","publish_time":"2025-05-16T11:32:21+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1031","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国会通过2026年国土安全部拨款法案","title_en":"Congress Enacts 2026 Department of Homeland Security Act |\nPassenger Transport","summary_cn":"国会于4月30日通过《2026年国土安全及进一步追加拨款法案》（P.L. 119-86），为美国国土安全部内与移民无关的机构提供资金至2026年9月30日。该法案为2026财年交通安全拨款计划提供8840万美元，较2025财年增加470万美元（6%）。法案还为负责与获得2025财年TSGP拨款公共交通机构对接的工作人员提供薪资；此前国土安全部停摆期间，FEMA工作人员无法向交通机构发放已授予的TSGP资金。","summary_en":"Congress enacted the Homeland Security and Further Additional Continuing Appropriations Act, 2026 (P.L. 119-86) on April 30, funding non-immigration agencies within the U.S. Department of Homeland Security through September 30, 2026. The Act provides $88.4 million for the Transit Security Grant Program in FY26, a $4.7 million (6 percent) increase over FY25. It also funds staff working with public transit agencies awarded FY25 TSGP grants, after FEMA staff were unable to disburse awarded funds during the DHS shutdown.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:20:34.197694+00:00","url":"https://aptapassengertransport.com/congress-enacts-2026-department-of-homeland-security-act","content":"Congress Enacts 2026 Department of Homeland Security Act\n5/4/2026\nShare\nCongress enacted the Homeland Security and Further Additional Continuing Appropriations Act, 2026 (P.L. 119-86), April 30, which funds through Sept. 30, 2026 those agencies within the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) that are not related to immigration.\nThe Act provides $88.4 million for the Transit Security Grant Program (TSGP) in FY26, an increase of $4.7 million (6 percent) from the FY25 enacted level.\nThe legislation also provides salaries for the staff responsible for working with public transit agencies that were awarded FY25 TSGP grants. During the DHS shutdown, FEMA staff were unable to provide awarded TSGP funds to transit agencies for draw down.\nRead APTA’s January 14, 2026 letter to House and Senate Homeland Security Appropriations Committee leaders.\nRead the DHS Appropriations Act, 2026 (P.L. 119-86, Division A).\nUse APTA’s Advocacy Tools\nIt has never been more important to make the case to Congress for public transportation investment. That is why APTA has created a one-stop shop explaining key advocacy tools, such as the APTA Industry Footprint and My Economic Impact tool, for APTA members to engage with their Members of Congress both on Capitol Hill and in their congressional districts and states.\nAPTA’s Industry Footprint shows how many riders use public transportation; recent major grant awards; and the manufacturing, construction, and engineering firms advancing public transportation projects in each congressional district and state.\nThe My Economic Impact tool uses a public transit agency’s budget data to calculate the economic impact of its transit service.\nView APTA’s Advocacy Tools Summary. View APTA’s Online Advocacy Toolkit.","content_cn":"国会颁布《2026年国土安全部法案》\n2026年5月4日\n分享\n国会于4月30日颁布《2026年国土安全及进一步追加持续拨款法案》（P.L. 119-86），为美国国土安全部（DHS）内与移民无关的机构提供资金，直至2026年9月30日。\n该法案为2026财年交通安全拨款计划（TSGP）提供8840万美元，较2025财年通过的拨款水平增加470万美元（6%）。\n该立法还为负责与获得2025财年TSGP拨款的公共交通机构合作的工作人员提供薪资。在DHS停摆期间，联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）工作人员无法向交通机构提供已获批的TSGP资金以供提取。\n阅读APTA于2026年1月14日致众议院和参议院国土安全拨款委员会领导人的信函。\n阅读《2026年DHS拨款法案》（P.L. 119-86，A部分）。\n使用APTA的倡导工具\n让国会了解公共交通投资的重要性从未如此关键。因此，APTA创建了一站式平台，介绍APTA行业足迹和“我的经济影响”等主要倡导工具，帮助APTA成员在国会山以及各自的国会选区和州内与国会议员开展互动。\nAPTA行业足迹展示每个国会选区和州的公共交通乘客数量、近期重大拨款项目，以及推动公共交通项目发展的制造、建筑和工程企业。\n“我的经济影响”工具利用公共交通机构的预算数据，计算其交通服务的经济影响。\n查看APTA倡导工具摘要。查看APTA在线倡导工具包。","publish_source":"aptapassengertransport.com","publish_time":"2026-05-04T14:12:59+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2140","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"迪尔伯恩 FBI 突袭引发阿拉伯裔美国人社区愤怒与质疑","title_en":"FBI raids in Dearborn spark outrage, doubt in Arab American community","summary_cn":"2025年11月7日，《阿拉伯美国新闻》报道，三名19至20岁的阿拉伯裔美国人因涉嫌策划受ISIS启发的万圣节袭击在迪尔伯恩被捕，面临恐怖主义相关指控。FBI局长卡什·帕特尔在X上宣布挫败袭击，引发媒体关注。辩护律师否认阴谋，称当事人是“电子游戏和休闲枪械爱好者”，批评官方“鲁莽的歇斯底里”。当地阿拉伯裔和穆斯林社区领袖质疑FBI行动，担忧种族定性和伊斯兰恐惧症，指责政府使用诱捕策略。","summary_en":"On November 7, 2025, The Arab American News reported that three Arab Americans aged 19–20 were arrested in Dearborn and charged with terrorism-related offenses for allegedly planning an ISIS-inspired Halloween attack. FBI Director Kash Patel announced on X that the plot was thwarted, drawing intense media attention. Defense attorneys denied any conspiracy, calling the men 'video-game and recreational firearm enthusiasts' and criticizing official 'reckless hysteria.' Local Arab and Muslim community leaders questioned the FBI operation, voicing concerns about racial profiling and Islamophobia, and accused the government of using entrapment tactics.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:51:29.355525+00:00","url":"https://arabamericannews.com/2025/11/07/fbi-raids-in-dearborn-spark-outrage-and-doubt-in-the-arab-american-community","content":"Mohamed Ali (left) and his brother, Ayoub Nasser, shop at a firearms store in the Detroit area in September.\nHomeCommunity FBI raids in Dearborn spark outrage and doubt in the Arab American community\nPosted: Friday 11.07.2025 3:23 pm\nThe Arab American News\nCommunity, Local, U.S.A\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nWhatsapp\nEmail\nThree young Arab Americans charged with terrorism-related offenses after alleged ISIS-inspired Halloween plot; community leaders decry “reckless hysteria” and “Islamophobic targeting”\nDEARBORN — Three young Arab Americans, aged between 19 and 20, are facing terrorism-related charges after being arrested by the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) at two separate homes in Dearborn on the morning of Friday, October 31, allegedly for planning an ISIS-inspired terrorist attack targeting gay and transgender bars in Ferndale during Halloween.\nFederal raids and FBI announcement\nIn an atmosphere of secrecy and confusion, federal agents launched coordinated predawn raids targeting two homes on Horger Street and Middlepointe Street in east Dearborn, as well as a storage unit in Inkster. Within hours, FBI Director Kash Patel posted on the social-media platform X, announcing that the agency had thwarted a potential Halloween-night terrorist attack.\nHis brief statement ignited intense media attention and local concern, particularly since the raids followed weeks of incitement and negative portrayals of the majority-Arab and Muslim city of Dearborn.\nConfusion persisted for three days, as rumors spread about the arrest of a “terror cell.” The picture began to clear when only two defendants appeared before a federal court in Detroit: Mohmed Ali and Majed Mahmoud, both 20-years-old. Three others were interrogated but not charged initially.\nOn Wednesday, federal prosecutors expanded the indictment to include a third Dearborn resident, Ayob Ismail Nasser, 19, the younger brother of Mohmed Ali. Both were arrested at the family’s home on Horger Street. The updated indictment also revealed another alleged target — the Cedar Point amusement park in Sandusky, Ohio.\nFederal agents search a house on Horger Street in East Dearborn on the eve of Halloween.\nFederal charges and defense responses\nThe three defendants were charged with conspiracy to provide material support to a terrorist organization and possession of firearms that could be used in a terrorist act.\nThe first charge carries up to 20 years in federal prison, the second up to 15 years.\nDefense attorney Hussein Bazzi, representing Nasser, “categorically denied” any involvement by his client.\nIn a statement to the Detroit News, Bazzi said there was “no credible evidence that any attack was planned, discussed or even intended”, stressing that “there was no such conspiracy.” He criticized statements made by the FBI director and senior officials as “reckless and irresponsible, and not based on evidence”, adding that “Washington pressure may have been the decisive factor in filing charges.”\nAccording to federal prosecutors, the suspects had obtained weapons and ammunition, trained at firing ranges and searched for LGBTQ bars and nightclubs in Detroit suburbs during September for a possible Halloween attack. The 72-page criminal complaint claims they were inspired by the so-called Islamic State (ISIS), a charge the defense strongly denies.\nFederal investigators said they relied on months of surveillance, including a camera mounted on a pole outside a Dearborn home, interception of encrypted messages and analysis of social-media posts.\nJohn Miller, CNN’s chief intelligence analyst, reported that an undercover FBI agent had entered an encrypted chatroom months earlier after suspecting that some participants were in the U.S. and others abroad, potentially linked to ISIS.\nThe Detroit Free Press reported that the FBI’s surveillance of Ali, Mahmoud and a third juvenile suspect began nearly a year ago and intensified after a group call recorded by an informant in July.\nAuthorities claim Mahmoud recently purchased more than 1,600 rounds of ammunition for AR-15-style rifles, that the men practiced reloading quickly and that their repeated references to “Pumpkin Day” led agents to believe an attack was planned for Halloween weekend.\nProsecutors also allege that a juvenile active in the chats consulted a “local extremist cleric” about when to perform a “righteous act”, though his identity was not disclosed.\nNasser is accused of scouting possible targets in Ferndale and across the Midwest, using encrypted apps to share ISIS-related material. Surveillance footage allegedly shows him visiting Cedar Point on September 18–19, arriving six hours before the park opened.\nWhen his home was searched on Halloween morning, investigators found a computer that had been used to check whether the park would be crowded that weekend.\nStatements from U.S. officials and defense\nU.S. Attorney General Pam Bondi said the suspects had a “detailed plan to launch an attack on U.S. soil”, adding on X, “This plot was thwarted before innocent lives were lost.”\nDespite the seizure of tactical vests, backpacks, AR-15 rifles, ammunition, loaded handguns and GoPro cameras, defense attorney Amir Makled — representing Mohmed Ali — rejected any suggestion of a terrorist plot, calling the FBI’s operation “hysteria and fear-mongering.”\nMakled told the Associated Press that the young men were American citizens aged 16–20 who were “video-game and recreational firearm enthusiasts” and that the FBI had acted prematurely.\nHe said the online conversations cited by agents were typical of bragging among gamers.\n“If these young men were in forums they shouldn’t have been in, we’ll see,” he said, “but I don’t believe any of their activity was illegal.”\nHe emphasized that all weapons were legally purchased and that the case involved “a small group of young men interested in recreational firearms, not a terrorist cell.”\nMakled also expressed concern about the rise in anti-Arab and anti-Muslim rhetoric in Michigan, particularly in Dearborn, following the FBI announcement. Speaking to CNN, he said he was “confident that when the facts are objectively reviewed, it will be clear there was no plan for a mass attack or coordinated conspiracy of any kind.”\nLocal reaction and civil rights concerns\nThe surprise raids and Patel’s statement sparked deep anxiety in the Dearborn community, where many doubted the official narrative and viewed the FBI operation as part of a broader pattern of federal targeting of Arab and Muslim Americans.\nNasser Beydoun, president of the Arab American Civil Rights League (ACRL), said the government appeared to be “depicting the situation in the worst possible light.”\n“Until the defendants are convicted, we presume them innocent,” he said. “Dearborn is a safe, welcoming and diverse community, but these sensational headlines have a direct and damaging impact on our city.”\nBeydoun expressed concern that “the racism against Arabs and Islamophobia we’ve faced since September 11, 2001 — and again after October 7, 2023 — may never end.”\n“Look at the national media and what they’re doing to Dearborn — the attacks, the lies,” he said. “Anything like this fuels hatred of Muslims and paints Dearborn as if it were some kind of Islamic-law capital.”\nNabih Ayad, civil rights attorney and founder of the ACRL, criticized the sensational media coverage of the FBI’s operation.\n“As soon as someone says ‘Dearborn’ and ‘terrorism’ it becomes an irresistible story for the media,” he said, adding that Arabs and Muslims in Dearborn “have earned the right to distrust the government.”\nAyad accused federal authorities of using pre-emptive and entrapment tactics to target Arab and Muslim youth, including through undercover agents and paid informants. He said the government monitors Arab Americans as “pre-suspects” while failing to equally surveil White extremists who have committed real acts of terror.\n“How many terrorist attacks has this community ever committed?” He asked rhetorically. “And the answer is ‘zero.’”\nDawud Walid, executive director of the Council on American Islamic Relations (CAIR)–Michigan, said he spoke to numerous community members after the news broke.\n“Every comment I heard was, ‘Here we go again — the government is setting up or entrapping young people,’” Walid said, noting the FBI’s long history of using informants and taxpayer money to “manufacture” terror plots.\nTags\nAmir Makled\narab american news\nArab-American Civil Rights League\nCAIR-Michigan\nCedar Point\nDearborn\nFBI\nFerndale\nHussein Bazzi\nnabih ayad\nnasser beydoun\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nWhatsapp\nEmail\nNext article\nDearborn does not want or need wards!\nPrevious article\nPolitical violence undermines our democracy","content_cn":"穆罕默德·阿里（左）和他的兄弟阿尤布·纳赛尔九月在底特律地区一家枪械店购物。\n首页社区 迪尔伯恩的FBI突袭在阿拉伯裔美国人社区引发愤怒与质疑\n发布时间：2025年11月7日星期五下午3:23\n《阿拉伯裔美国人新闻报》\n社区、本地、美国\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nWhatsapp\nEmail\n三名年轻的阿拉伯裔美国人因涉嫌受ISIS启发的万圣节阴谋被控与恐怖主义相关的罪名；社区领袖谴责“鲁莽的歇斯底里”和“伊斯兰恐惧症式的针对”\n迪尔伯恩——三名年龄在19至20岁之间的年轻阿拉伯裔美国人正面临与恐怖主义相关的指控。他们于10月31日星期五上午在迪尔伯恩两处不同的住宅中被联邦调查局（FBI）逮捕，据称他们策划在万圣节期间对芬代尔市针对同性恋和跨性别者的酒吧发动一场受ISIS启发的恐怖袭击。\n联邦突袭与FBI的宣布\n在秘密与混乱的气氛中，联邦探员于黎明前发动协调突袭，目标包括迪尔伯恩东部霍尔格街和中点街的两处住宅，以及英克斯特的一个储物单元。数小时内，FBI局长卡什·帕特尔在社交媒体平台X上发帖，宣布该机构挫败了一起潜在的万圣节之夜恐怖袭击。\n他的简短声明引发了媒体的强烈关注和当地的担忧，尤其是因为这些突袭发生在此前数周针对迪尔伯恩这座以阿拉伯裔和穆斯林为主的城市的煽动和负面描绘之后。\n混乱持续了三天，有关一个“恐怖小组”被捕的谣言四起。当只有两名被告在底特律联邦法院出庭时，情况才开始明朗：穆罕默德·阿里和马吉德·马哈茂德，两人均为20岁。另外三人被审讯，但最初未被起诉。\n周三，联邦检察官扩大起诉范围，将第三名迪尔伯恩居民、19岁的阿尤布·伊斯梅尔·纳赛尔列入其中，他是穆罕默德·阿里的弟弟。两人均在该家庭位于霍尔格街的住所被捕。更新后的起诉书还披露了另一个据称的目标——俄亥俄州桑达斯基的雪松点游乐园。\n联邦探员在万圣节前夕搜查迪尔伯恩东部霍尔格街的一处住宅。\n联邦指控与辩护方回应\n三名被告被控共谋向恐怖组织提供物质支持，以及持有可用于恐怖行为的枪支。\n第一项指控最高可判处20年联邦监禁，第二项最高可判处15年。\n代表纳赛尔的辩护律师侯赛因·巴齐“断然否认”其当事人有任何参与。\n巴齐在给《底特律新闻报》的声明中表示，“没有可信证据表明策划、讨论甚至意图实施任何袭击”，并强调“不存在这样的共谋”。他批评FBI局长和高级官员的言论“鲁莽且不负责任，并非基于证据”，并补充说“华盛顿的压力可能是提出指控的决定性因素”。\n据联邦检察官称，嫌疑人已获取武器和弹药，在射击场训练，并在九月搜寻底特律郊区的LGBTQ酒吧和夜总会，以图在万圣节发动可能的袭击。这份72页的刑事起诉书声称他们受到所谓“伊斯兰国”（ISIS）的启发，辩护方强烈否认这一指控。\n联邦调查人员表示，他们依靠数月的监视，包括安装在迪尔伯恩一处住宅外杆子上的一台摄像头、对加密信息的截获以及对社交媒体帖子的分析。\nCNN首席情报分析师约翰·米勒报道称，一名FBI卧底探员数月前进入一个加密聊天室，此前他怀疑一些参与者在美国境内，另一些在国外，可能与ISIS有关联。\n据《底特律自由新闻报》报道，FBI对阿里、马哈茂德和第三名未成年嫌疑人的监视始于近一年前，并在七月一名线人录下的一次群组通话后加强。\n当局声称，马哈茂德最近为AR-15式步枪购买了1600多发弹药，这些人练习快速装弹，且他们反复提及“南瓜日”，使探员相信他们策划在万圣节周末发动袭击。\n检察官还声称，一名活跃于聊天中的未成年人曾就何时实施“正义之举”咨询一名“当地极端主义神职人员”，但其身份未予披露。\n纳赛尔被指控在芬代尔及整个中西部侦察可能的目标\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"arabamericannews.com","publish_time":"2025-11-07T20:23:03+00:00"}},{"id":"news-255","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS + Yahoo title resolution via Reader","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike Falcon传感器本地权限提升零日漏洞（FalconFlank）","title_en":"CrowdStrike Falcon Sensor Local Privilege Escalation Zero-Day (FalconFlank) - Arctic Wolf","summary_cn":"Arctic Wolf Labs报告，2026年9月3日有研究人员公开披露CrowdStrike Falcon Sensor零日漏洞FalconFlank，利用Office恶意宏修复流程中的TOCTOU竞争条件，可实现SYSTEM级权限提升。该漏洞影响启用宏移除策略的Windows 11 25H2和Server 2025。CrowdStrike尚未发布补丁，建议客户禁用相关宏修复策略作为临时缓解措施。","summary_en":"Arctic Wolf Labs reports that on September 3, 2026, a researcher publicly disclosed a CrowdStrike Falcon Sensor zero-day dubbed FalconFlank, exploiting a TOCTOU race condition in the Office malicious macro remediation workflow to achieve SYSTEM-level privilege escalation. It affects Windows 11 25H2 and Server 2025 with the macro removal policy enabled. CrowdStrike has not yet issued a patch and recommends disabling the affected macro remediation policy as an interim workaround.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T05:52:48.616962+00:00","url":"https://arcticwolf.com/resources/blog/crowdstrike-falcon-sensor-local-privilege-escalation-zero-day-falconflank","content":"Back to blog\nCrowdStrike Falcon Sensor Local Privilege Escalation Zero-Day (FalconFlank)\nFalconFlank is a CrowdStrike Falcon zero-day vulnerability that enables SYSTEM-level privilege escalation. Learn the risks, affected environments, and recommended mitigation steps.\nSeptember 4, 2026\nby\nArctic Wolf Labs\n6 min read\nIn this article: Select\nThreat Summary\nOn September 3, 2026, a security researcher known as Nightmare Eclipse/Chaotic Eclipse publicly disclosed a zero-day dubbed ‘FalconFlank’ which abuses the Office malicious macro remediation workflow in CrowdStrike Falcon Sensor. The attack leverages a time-of-check to time-of-use (TOCTOU) race condition, allowing an attacker with code execution on a vulnerable system to hijack the Falcon macro remediation routine. This results in DLL side-loading and execution as  NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM.\nThe exploit is effective against fully-updated versions of Windows 11 (25H2) and Server 2025, provided CrowdStrike Falcon is running in Phase 3 Optimal Protection with the macro removal policy enabled. The PoC is publicly available on GitHub and can be leveraged by moderately skilled threat actors with development capability to achieve SYSTEM-level privileges. At the time of writing, no attacks have been reported.\nCrowdStrike has not yet issued a public advisory or patch but recommends (via internal tech alert) that customers disable the affected macro remediation policy as an interim workaround. Detection is challenging. Hash-based antivirus signatures are easily bypassed, and only behavior-based monitoring, such as unusual SYSTEM processes spawned by csfalconservice.exe, abnormal DLL loads, or the presence of FalconFlank.exe can highlight malicious activity.\nRecommendations\nImmediate Actions:\nDisable the ‘Microsoft Office file Suspicious Macro Removal’ policy via the CrowdStrike Falcon console (Phase 3 policy setting). This is the only vendor-approved workaround and removes the attack vector for FalconFlank. Confirm policy propagation to all endpoints.\nDisclosure from CrowdStrike: “Customers remain protected through the Cloud Anti-malware for Microsoft Office Files settings.”\nShort-Term Defensive Measures:\nEnforce Group Policy or endpoint controls to block macros from the Internet and disable all macros with notification in Microsoft Office (as a compensating control).\nRestrict the creation of NTFS symbolic links by non-privileged users where possible.\nLong-Term/Strategic:\nEngage with CrowdStrike support to request direct advisory updates and private notifications about patch timelines and remediation steps.\nRetain enhanced endpoint monitoring and centralize event logs (Sysmon, SIEM, EDR detection) to catch adaptation of the attack or follow-on tools.\nEducate users on risks of macro-enabled Office documents; maintain regular security awareness campaigns focused on social engineering and macro attacks.\nMonitor for new advisories, patches, or CVEs from CrowdStrike and downstream OS security advisories, acting as soon as fixes are published.\nTemporary Workarounds\nOfficially documented workaround: Disable the ‘Microsoft Office file Suspicious Macro Removal’ policy from the Falcon console for all vulnerable Windows endpoints. This removes the primary FalconFlank exploit vector while retaining other protective capabilities.\nEnforce Office macro-restriction policies: Use Group Policy to block macros from the internet, set VBAWarnings to 4 (disable all macros with notification), restrict trusted locations and startup paths in Office.\nReferences:\nhttps://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/new-crowdstrike-falconflank-zero-day-grants-system-privileges/\nhttps://thehgtech.com/articles/falconflank-crowdstrike-falcon-lpe-analysis.html\nhttps://github.com/MSNightmare/FalconFlank\nhttps://intelfusions.com/news/falconflank-falcon-macro-remediation-lpe\nhttps://socradar.io/blog/falconflank-crowdstrike-falcon-0day-poc\nPopular Topics\nAdversary Research\nCyber Attacks and Breaches\nCyber Insurance\nEndpoint Security\nIncident Response\nManaged Detection and Response\nRegulatory Compliance\nSecurity Awareness\nSecurity Bulletins\nTechnical Briefs\nThreat Research\nVulnerability Management\nView all posts\nShare this post:\nWhat to read next\nBack to Blog\n4 min readWe Need to Pace AI Development. We Can’t Pace AI Defense\nSeptember 15, 2026 View Post 4 min readIntroducing Aurora® MDR Connect: A New Way for MSPs to Deliver Modern Security Operations\nSeptember 15, 2026 View Post 5 min readAstra Just Raised the Bar for AI-Enabled Attacks. Here’s What That Means for Defenders\nSeptember 11, 2026 View Post 3 min readBuilding an Agentic SOC So Your Team Doesn’t Have To\nSeptember 11, 2026 View Post","content_cn":"返回博客\nCrowdStrike Falcon Sensor 本地权限提升零日漏洞（FalconFlank）\nFalconFlank 是一个 CrowdStrike Falcon 零日漏洞，可实现 SYSTEM 级权限提升。了解其风险、受影响环境以及建议的缓解措施。\n2026年9月4日\n作者\nArctic Wolf Labs\n阅读时长 6 分钟\n本文内容：选择\n威胁摘要\n2026年9月3日，一位名为 Nightmare Eclipse/Chaotic Eclipse 的安全研究人员公开披露了一个名为“FalconFlank”的零日漏洞，该漏洞滥用了 CrowdStrike Falcon Sensor 中的 Office 恶意宏修复工作流。该攻击利用检查时间与使用时间（TOCTOU）竞态条件，使在易受攻击系统上拥有代码执行能力的攻击者能够劫持 Falcon 宏修复例程。这导致 DLL 侧加载并以 NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM 身份执行。\n只要 CrowdStrike Falcon 以第 3 阶段最佳保护（Phase 3 Optimal Protection）运行且启用了宏移除策略，该漏洞利用对完全更新的 Windows 11（25H2）和 Server 2025 版本均有效。该概念验证（PoC）已在 GitHub 上公开，具备开发能力的中等技能威胁行为者即可利用其获得 SYSTEM 级权限。截至撰写本文时，尚未有攻击报告。\nCrowdStrike 尚未发布公开公告或补丁，但（通过内部技术警报）建议客户禁用受影响的宏修复策略作为临时变通方案。检测颇具挑战性。基于哈希的防病毒签名很容易被绕过，只有基于行为的监控——例如由 csfalconservice.exe 生成的异常 SYSTEM 进程、异常的 DLL 加载，或 FalconFlank.exe 的存在——才能揭示恶意活动。\n建议\n立即行动：\n通过 CrowdStrike Falcon 控制台禁用“Microsoft Office 文件可疑宏移除”策略（第 3 阶段策略设置）。这是唯一经厂商认可的变通方案，可消除 FalconFlank 的攻击途径。确认策略已传播至所有端点。\nCrowdStrike 的声明：“客户仍可通过 Microsoft Office 文件的云端反恶意软件设置受到保护。”\n短期防御措施：\n通过组策略或端点控制阻止来自 Internet 的宏，并在 Microsoft Office 中禁用所有宏并发出通知（作为补偿性控制措施）。\n在可能的情况下，限制非特权用户创建 NTFS 符号链接。\n长期/战略性措施：\n与 CrowdStrike 支持团队沟通，请求直接公告更新以及有关补丁时间表和修复步骤的私下通知。\n保持增强的端点监控并集中化事件日志（Sysmon、SIEM、EDR 检测），以捕捉攻击的变种或后续工具。\n对用户进行有关启用宏的 Office 文档风险的教育；定期开展以社会工程和宏攻击为重点的安全意识宣传活动。\n监控 CrowdStrike 及下游操作系统安全公告发布的新公告、补丁或 CVE，并在修复发布后立即采取行动。\n临时变通方案\n官方记录的变通方案：在 Falcon 控制台中为所有易受攻击的 Windows 端点禁用“Microsoft Office 文件可疑宏移除”策略。这可在保留其他保护能力的同时消除 FalconFlank 的主要利用途径。\n强制执行 Office 宏限制策略：使用组策略阻止来自 Internet 的宏，将 VBAWarnings 设置为 4（禁用所有宏并发出通知），限制 Office 中的受信任位置和启动路径。\n参考资料：\nhttps://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/new-crowdstrike-falconflank-zero-day-grants-system-privileges/\nhttps://thehgtech.com/articles/falconflank-crowdstrike-falcon-lpe-analysis.html\nhttps://github.com/MSNightmare/FalconFlank\nhttps://intelfusions.com/news/falconflank-falcon-macro-remediation-lpe\nhttps://socradar.io/blog/falconflank-crowdstrike-falcon-0day-poc\n热门主题\n对手研究\n网络攻击与入侵\n网络保险\n端点安全\n事件响应\n托管检测与响应\n法规合规\n安全意识\n安全公告\n技术简报\n威胁研究\n漏洞管理\n查看所有文章\n分享此文章：\n接下来阅读\n返回博客\n阅读时长 4 分钟 我们需要放慢 AI 发展步伐。我们无法放慢 AI 防御步伐\n2026年9月15日 查看文章 阅读时长 4 分钟 推出 Aurora® MDR Connect：MSP 交付现代安全运营的新方式\n2026年9月15日 查看文章 阅读时长 5 分钟 Astra 刚刚提高了 AI-En 的标准\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"arcticwolf.com","publish_time":"2026-09-04T15:33:53+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1771","ktid":1001190,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001190","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"大西洋理事会文章称TRIPP有望重塑南高加索地缘政治","title_en":"TRIPP poised to reshape the geopolitics of the South Caucasus – Atlantic Council article","summary_cn":"亚美尼亚通讯社报道，美国智库大西洋理事会发表文章，称穿越亚美尼亚南部长约27英里的TRIPP走廊有望重塑南高加索地缘政治格局。文章由大西洋理事会欧亚中心副主任安德鲁·达涅里与约克敦研究所高级研究员约瑟夫·爱泼斯坦撰写，认为该项目可能成为特朗普第二任期重要外交成果，美方提供前期资金并通过过境费和商业机会获得回报，亚美尼亚则凭少数股权、税收和关税获益。文章还提及俄罗斯在亚美尼亚选举前散布虚假信息。","summary_en":"Armenpress reports that a U.S. think tank, the Atlantic Council, published an article arguing that TRIPP, a roughly twenty-seven-mile route through southern Armenia, is poised to reshape the geopolitics of the South Caucasus. Written by Andrew D'Anieri of the Atlantic Council's Eurasia Center and Joseph Epstein of the Yorktown Institute, the piece says the project could become one of President Trump's most impressive second-term foreign policy achievements, with Washington providing upfront capital and earning returns via transit fees and commercial opportunities, while Armenia benefits from its minority stake, taxes and customs duties. It also notes Russia has targeted Armenia's PM with fake news ahead of elections.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:35:02.350260+00:00","url":"https://armenpress.am/en/article/1240259","content":"Politics12:19, 22 January 2026TRIPP poised to reshape the geopolitics of the South Caucasus – Atlantic Council article6 minute readAn article published by the U.S. think tank Atlantic Council highlighted the benefits of the TRIPP project in Armenia.The article titled How Trump’s ‘TRIPP’ triumph can advance US interests in the South Caucasus is written by Andrew D’Anieri, associate director of the Atlantic Council’s Eurasia Center, and Joseph Epstein, director of the Turan Research Center and senior fellow at the Yorktown Institute.“A twenty-seven-mile stretch of land running through southern Armenia is poised to reshape the geopolitics of the South Caucasus,” the article says.According to the experts, TRIPP “could go down as one of US President Donald Trump’s most impressive foreign policy achievements of his second term.”“The agreement envisions the United States government providing upfront capital to develop the route and making a financial return via the TDC [TRIPP Development Company] over the life of the project through transit fees and commercial opportunities along the route, in addition to construction contracts to US companies. Armenia will earn revenue based on its minority stake in the TDC, plus taxes and customs duties along TRIPP. It’s an arrangement that should work well for both parties. The White House can tell Americans that they are getting an economic return for US diplomatic engagement in the South Caucasus and opening new opportunities for US companies. At the same time, [Armenian Prime Minister] Pashinyan can sell the agreement as a means of attracting high-quality Western infrastructure investment—something he had pursued through his Crossroads of Peace initiative—that can help position Armenia as a regional transport hub, all while maintaining control over Armenian territory,” it said. “TRIPP could provide spillover benefits to Washington, Yerevan, and the broader Caspian region, as well. The US government has been quietly supportive of the Middle Corridor, a multi-modal trade route that connects Central Asia to Turkey and Europe via the Caspian Sea and infrastructure chokepoints in Azerbaijan and Georgia. Washington and its European partners see the Middle Corridor as a way for overland trade with Asia to bypass Russia, including the potential export of critical minerals and rare earths from Central Asia. The South Caucasus and Central Asian countries seek prosperity through better integration with global markets. TRIPP provides another route across the Caucasus, increasing transport volume capacity as Azerbaijan and Kazakhstan work to build port capacity to meet trade demand. The successful implementation of TRIPP would make it cheaper and faster to ship products and critical raw materials from Central Asia to Europe and beyond.”According to the authors, \"understanding that a peace deal with Azerbaijan was the only way to remove Russian leverage and therefore achieve true independence, the Armenian prime minister staked his political future on such a deal.\"\"Simultaneously, he inked major defense deals with India, France, Greece, and Cyprus, among others. But the United States is the only power capable of truly offering Armenia an exit ramp from Russian domination. By conducting peace negotiations under US auspices and placing US interests directly over TRIPP, Pashinyan and Aliyev have protected the most sensitive part of the deal with a US deterrent. But more than that, they tied the success of the peace process to closer relations with Washington.\"The article also noted that Russia has targeted the Armenian PM with fake news ahead of this year’s election. “Moscow will almost certainly seek to expand these efforts ahead of the election.”The Trump Route for International Peace and Prosperity (TRIPP) is a connectivity project in Armenia, envisaged under the U.S.-brokered Armenian-Azerbaijani joint declaration signed in Washington, D.C. The project is expected to unlock strategic economic opportunities, create long-term benefits by promoting infrastructure investment, and enhance regional connectivity. TRIPP is part of the Crossroads of Peace project, and an Armenian-American joint enterprise is expected to develop the route.Armenian Foreign Minister Ararat Mirzoyan and U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio earlier this month approved the joint statement on the TRIPP Implementation Framework.   Read the article in: العربيةFrançaisՀայերենРусский中文Section PoliticsLocation Armenia","content_cn":"政治 2026年1月22日 12:19 大西洋理事会文章：TRIPP有望重塑南高加索地缘政治 阅读时间6分钟 美国智库大西洋理事会发表的一篇文章强调了TRIPP项目在亚美尼亚的益处。这篇题为《特朗普的“TRIPP”胜利如何推进美国在南高加索的利益》的文章由大西洋理事会欧亚中心副主任安德鲁·达涅里和土兰研究中心主任、约克敦研究所高级研究员约瑟夫·爱泼斯坦撰写。文章称：“一条穿越亚美尼亚南部、绵延二十七英里的土地，有望重塑南高加索的地缘政治。”据这些专家称，TRIPP“可能成为美国总统唐纳德·特朗普第二任期内最令人印象深刻的外交政策成就之一”。“该协议设想美国政府提供前期资金来开发这条路线，并在项目存续期内通过TDC[TRIPP开发公司]以过境费和沿线商业机会获得财务回报，此外还有授予美国公司的建设合同。亚美尼亚将根据其在TDC中的少数股权获得收入，外加TRIPP沿线的税收和关税。这一安排对双方都应十分有利。白宫可以向美国人表示，他们从美国在南高加索的外交参与中获得了经济回报，并为美国公司开辟了新机遇。与此同时，[亚美尼亚总理]帕希尼扬可以将该协议宣传为吸引高质量西方基础设施投资的一种手段——这正是他通过‘和平十字路口’倡议所追求的目标——这有助于将亚美尼亚定位为区域交通枢纽，同时保持对亚美尼亚领土的控制，”文章称。“TRIPP还可能为华盛顿、埃里温以及更广泛的里海地区带来溢出效益。美国政府一直默默支持中间走廊，这是一条多式联运贸易路线，经里海以及阿塞拜疆和格鲁吉亚的基础设施瓶颈，将中亚与土耳其和欧洲连接起来。华盛顿及其欧洲伙伴将中间走廊视为与亚洲进行陆路贸易以绕开俄罗斯的一种方式，包括从中亚潜在出口关键矿产和稀土。南高加索和中亚国家寻求通过更好地融入全球市场来实现繁荣。TRIPP提供了另一条穿越高加索的路线，在阿塞拜疆和哈萨克斯坦努力建设港口能力以满足贸易需求之际，增加了运输量能力。TRIPP的成功实施将使从中亚向欧洲及其他地区运输产品和关键原材料变得更便宜、更快捷。”据作者称，“亚美尼亚总理明白，与阿塞拜疆达成和平协议是消除俄罗斯杠杆、从而实现真正独立的唯一途径，因此他将自己的政治前途押在了这样一项协议上。”“与此同时，他与印度、法国、希腊和塞浦路斯等国签署了重大防务协议。但美国是唯一有能力真正为亚美尼亚提供摆脱俄罗斯支配出路的大国。通过在美国主持下进行和平谈判，并将美国利益直接置于TRIPP之上，帕希尼扬和阿利耶夫以美国的威慑力保护了协议中最敏感的部分。但不仅如此，他们还将和平进程的成功与同华盛顿的更紧密关系联系在一起。”文章还指出，俄罗斯在今年选举前以假新闻针对亚美尼亚总理。“莫斯科几乎肯定会寻求在选举前扩大这些行动。”“特朗普国际和平与繁荣之路”（TRIPP）是亚美尼亚的一个互联互通项目，依据在美国斡旋下于华盛顿特区签署的亚美尼亚-阿塞拜疆联合声明而设想。该项目预计将释放战略经济机遇，通过促进基础设施投资创造长期利益，并增强区域互联互通。TRIPP是“和平十字路口”项目的一部分，预计将由一家亚美尼亚-美国合资企业开发这条路线。亚美尼亚外交部长阿拉拉特·米尔佐扬和美国国务卿马尔科·鲁比奥本月早些时候批准了关于TRIPP实施框架的联合声明。   阅读本文的其他语言版本：阿拉伯语 法语 亚美尼亚语 俄语 中文 栏目 政治 地点 亚美尼亚","publish_source":"armenpress.am","publish_time":"2026-01-22T12:19:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-711","ktid":1000490,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000490","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"亚美尼亚大使在华盛顿CSIS会议讨论合作议程","title_en":"Armenian ambassador discusses cooperation agenda at CSIS meeting in Washington, D.C.","summary_cn":"亚美尼亚通讯社报道，亚美尼亚驻美国大使纳雷克·姆克尔奇扬访问华盛顿战略与国际研究中心（CSIS），会见该中心欧洲、俄罗斯与欧亚项目主任马克斯·伯格曼及其他代表。据使馆通报，大使介绍了亚美尼亚与美国合作议程，重点提及近期签署的多项协议，为高技术、人工智能、关键矿产、半导体产业和能源等战略领域合作创造新机遇。双方还讨论地区形势、和平进程及美国的作用，并探讨CSIS与亚美尼亚研究分析机构之间的合作机会。","summary_en":"Armenpress reports that Armenian Ambassador to the United States Narek Mkrtchyan visited the Center for Strategic and International Studies (CSIS) in Washington, D.C., meeting Max Bergmann, director of the Europe, Russia, and Eurasia Program, and other representatives. According to the embassy readout, the ambassador presented the Armenia-U.S. cooperation agenda, highlighting recently signed agreements creating opportunities in high technology, artificial intelligence, critical minerals, the semiconductor industry and energy. Discussions also covered regional developments, the peace process and the U.S. role, as well as possible cooperation between CSIS and Armenian research centers.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:35:05.820068+00:00","url":"https://armenpress.am/en/article/1253587","content":"U. S.14:00, 20 June 2026Armenian ambassador discusses cooperation agenda at CSIS meeting in Washington, D.C.1 minute readArmenian Ambassador to the United States Narek Mkrtchyan visited the Center for Strategic and International Studies (CSIS) in Washington, D.C., where he met with Max Bergmann, Director of the Europe, Russia, and Eurasia Program, as well as other representatives of the center.According to the embassy’s readout, during the meeting the Ambassador presented the Armenia–United States cooperation agenda, with particular emphasis on several recently signed agreements that create new opportunities for collaboration in high technology, artificial intelligence, critical minerals, the semiconductor industry, energy, and other strategic sectors.The discussions also focused on regional developments and issues related to the ongoing peace process, including the role and contribution of the United States in supporting it.The participants also explored opportunities for cooperation between CSIS and Armenian research and analytical centers.Read the article in: FrançaisՀայերենРусскийLocation U. S. ArmeniaPerson Narek Mkrtchyan","content_cn":"美国 14:00，2026年6月20日 亚美尼亚大使在华盛顿特区战略与国际研究中心会议上讨论合作议程 阅读时间1分钟 亚美尼亚驻美国大使纳雷克·姆克尔奇扬访问了位于华盛顿特区的战略与国际研究中心（CSIS），在那里他会见了欧洲、俄罗斯和欧亚项目主任马克斯·伯格曼以及该中心的其他代表。据使馆通报，会议期间，大使介绍了亚美尼亚—美国合作议程，特别强调了几项近期签署的协议，这些协议为高技术、人工智能、关键矿产、半导体产业、能源及其他战略领域的合作创造了新机遇。讨论还聚焦于地区事态发展以及与正在进行的和平进程相关的问题，包括美国在支持该进程中的作用和贡献。与会者还探讨了CSIS与亚美尼亚研究和分析中心之间的合作机会。阅读本文的其他语言版本：法语、亚美尼亚语、俄语 地点：美国、亚美尼亚 人物：纳雷克·姆克尔奇扬","publish_source":"armenpress.am","publish_time":"2026-06-20T14:00:00+04:00"}},{"id":"news-2691","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"联邦调查局继续追查哈德利男子涉嫌出售钚一案","title_en":"FBI continues to track down plutonium allegedly sold by Hadley man - Center for Arms Control and Non-Proliferation","summary_cn":"军控与不扩散中心网站刊文称，该中心生物与化学安全科学家工作组高级科学研究员约翰·吉尔伯特就联邦调查局调查非法出售钚一事接受MassLive采访。吉尔伯特表示，涉案男子据称出售的少量钚远不足以制造核弹，但钚若处理不当具有致命危险，其粉末被吸入即使量很小也会导致极严重的呼吸窘迫。他还认为检方所称来自烟雾探测器的材料不太可能是钚，因为苏联当年需要所有能获得的钚，而更适合用于烟雾探测器的是危险性较低的镅。","summary_en":"The Center for Arms Control and Non-Proliferation reports that John Gilbert, a senior science fellow of its Scientists Working Group on Biological and Chemical Security, spoke with MassLive about the FBI's investigation into the illegal selling of plutonium. Gilbert said the small amounts allegedly sold by Miller are nowhere near the amount needed for a nuclear bomb, but plutonium is deadly if handled incorrectly, causing extremely bad respiratory distress if its powder is inhaled even in small amounts. He said it is unlikely the material prosecutors said came from smoke detectors was plutonium, since the Soviets needed all the plutonium they could get; americium is better suited for smoke detectors and less dangerous.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:13:09.110128+00:00","url":"https://armscontrolcenter.org/fbi-continues-to-track-down-plutonium-allegedly-sold-by-hadley-man","content":"You are here: Home / Press Room / Center in the News / FBI continues to track down plutonium allegedly sold by Hadley manJune 25, 2025FBI continues to track down plutonium allegedly sold by Hadley man\nJohn Gilbert, Senior Science Fellow of the Center’s Scientists Working Group on Biological and Chemical Security, spoke with MassLive about the FBI’s investigation of the illegal selling of plutonium.\nJohn Gilbert, a senior science fellow at the Center for Arms Control and Non-Proliferation, while the small amounts allegedly sold by Miller is nowhere near the amount needed for a nuclear bomb, plutonium is deadly if handled incorrectly.\nIf its powder is breathed in — even in small amounts — it causes “extremely, extremely bad respiratory distress,” he said.\nGilbert said it is unlikely the material prosecutors said came from smoke detectors was plutonium, as the Soviets “needed all the plutonium they could get.” Rather, another radioactive element — americium — is good for use in smoke detectors, and it is not as dangerous, he said. Read more\nPosted in: Center in the News, Nuclear Security, Press Room, United States","content_cn":"当前位置：首页 / 新闻室 / 中心新闻 / FBI继续追查据称由哈德利男子出售的钚\n2025年6月25日\nFBI继续追查据称由哈德利男子出售的钚\n该中心生物与化学安全科学家工作组的高级科学研究员John Gilbert接受了MassLive采访，谈及FBI对非法出售钚一事的调查。\n军备控制与防扩散中心高级科学研究员John Gilbert表示，Miller据称出售的少量钚远未达到制造核弹所需的数量，但如果处理不当，钚具有致命危险。\n他说，即使吸入少量粉末，也会造成“极其、极其严重的呼吸窘迫”。\nGilbert说，检察官称来自烟雾探测器的材料不太可能是钚，因为苏联人“需要得到他们能获得的所有钚”。相反，另一种放射性元素——镅——适合用于烟雾探测器，而且没有那么危险，他说。阅读更多\n发布于：中心新闻、核安全、新闻室、美国","publish_source":"armscontrolcenter.org","publish_time":"2025-06-25T16:43:40+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3022","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿灵顿赞扬FBI/司法部在西得克萨斯打击贩毒集团行动","title_en":"Arrington Praises FBI/DOJ Anti-Cartel Operation in West Texas | U.S. Representative Jodey Arrington","summary_cn":"美国众议员乔迪·阿灵顿发表声明，赞扬联邦调查局与司法部在西得克萨斯州卢伯克开展的一次打击与墨西哥贩毒集团有关联的贩毒网络行动。FBI局长卡什·帕特尔表示，行动中逮捕了22名贩毒网络成员，其中一人据信与墨西哥贩毒集团合作。阿灵顿还提到FBI近期逮捕了多名十大通缉犯，并在弗吉尼亚州抓获MS-13东海岸头目。","summary_en":"U.S. Rep. Jodey Arrington praised an FBI and DOJ operation in Lubbock, Texas, that dismantled a narcotics trafficking ring affiliated with Mexican drug cartels. FBI Director Kash Patel said 22 members were arrested, one believed to be working with Mexican cartels. Arrington also noted recent arrests of top 10 most wanted fugitives and the capture of the MS-13 East Coast leader in Virginia.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:17:18.611835+00:00","url":"https://arrington.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=2684","content":"news\nPress Releases\nArrington Praises FBI/DOJ Anti-Cartel Operation in West Texas\nShare on Facebook\nShare on X\nPrint this Page\nShare by Email\nWashington,\nMarch 27, 2025\nRep. Arrington and Director Patel celebrated a large operation to take down a narcotics trafficking ring affiliated with Mexican Drug Cartels in Lubbock, Texas.\nLubbock, TX – House Budget Chairman Jodey Arrington (TX-19) celebrated a large operation to take down a narcotics trafficking ring affiliated with Mexican Drug Cartels in Lubbock, Texas.\n“The Biden Administration willingly ceded operational control of our southern border to narco-terrorists drug cartels killing hundreds of thousands of our citizens and wreaking havoc across the country - and West Texas is on the front lines,” said Chairman Arrington. “President Trump has been clear - the days of surrendering the safety and security of our communities are over. I’m grateful for the leadership and resolve of FBI Director Kash Patel, Attorney General Pam Bondi, and Border Czar Tom Homan for last night’s successful mission in West Texas, and I’m praying for continued safety and success for our law enforcement officers on the front lines.”\n“BREAKING: Tonight I can report yet another successful operation from our brave field agents and regional partners in our ongoing mission to break the drug Cartels,” said FBI Director Kash Patel. “Earlier today, our teams executed a takedown and arrested 22 members of a narcotics trafficking ring in Lubbock, Texas — one who we believe to be working with the Mexican Cartels. Our FBI Dallas team did incredible work, partnering with Texas LEO, DEA HQ, and others. These are the operations that mean safer streets for American families. And we are just getting started.”\nBackground:\nThe operation in Lubbock is part of broader operations that have targeted top-level members of gangs and drug-trafficking rings operating in the United States.\nJust in the past two months, the FBI has arrested three individuals on its top 10 most wanted list.\nIn addition to the operation in Lubbock, Director Patel and AG Bondi oversaw the arrest of the top MS-13 leader for the U.S. East Coast in an operation in Woodbridge, Virginia, just south of Washington, D.C.\nFollowing the operations, AG Bondi said the “DOJ will not rest until we make America safe again.”\n###","content_cn":"新闻\n新闻稿\nArrington赞扬FBI/司法部在西德州开展的反卡特尔行动\n分享到Facebook\n分享到X\n打印此页面\n通过电子邮件分享\n\n华盛顿\n2025年3月27日\n\nArrington议员和Patel局长庆祝在得克萨斯州拉伯克市开展大规模行动，捣毁一个与墨西哥贩毒集团有关联的毒品贩运团伙。\n\n得克萨斯州拉伯克市——众议院预算委员会主席Jodey Arrington（得克萨斯州第19选区）庆祝在得克萨斯州拉伯克市开展大规模行动，捣毁一个与墨西哥贩毒集团有关联的毒品贩运团伙。\n\n“拜登政府甘愿把我国南部边境的行动控制权拱手让给毒品恐怖分子贩毒集团，这些集团杀害了数十万美国公民，并在全国各地造成混乱，而西德州正处于最前线，”Arrington主席说。“特朗普总统已经明确表示——屈服、放弃社区安全保障的日子结束了。我感谢FBI局长Kash Patel、司法部长Pam Bondi和边境事务主管Tom Homan的领导力与决心，感谢他们促成昨晚在西德州的成功行动；我也祈祷前线执法人员能够继续安全并取得成功。”\n\n“突发消息：今晚我可以报告，我们勇敢的一线特工和地区合作伙伴在持续打击毒品卡特尔的任务中又取得了一次成功行动，”FBI局长Kash Patel说。“今天早些时候，我们的团队在得克萨斯州拉伯克市实施抓捕行动，逮捕了一个毒品贩运团伙的22名成员，其中一人我们认为正在与墨西哥卡特尔合作。我们的FBI达拉斯团队与得克萨斯州执法部门、缉毒局总部及其他机构合作，完成了令人难以置信的工作。这些行动意味着美国民众家庭的街道更加安全。而我们才刚刚开始。”\n\n背景：\n\n拉伯克行动是更广泛行动的一部分，这些行动针对在美国境内活动的帮派和毒品贩运团伙的高层成员。\n\n仅在过去两个月里，FBI就逮捕了其十大通缉名单上的三名人员。\n\n除拉伯克行动外，Patel局长和Bondi司法部长还在弗吉尼亚州伍德布里奇的一次行动中监督逮捕了MS-13在美国东海岸的最高级别头目；伍德布里奇位于华盛顿特区以南。\n\n行动结束后，Bondi司法部长表示：“司法部在让美国重新安全之前不会停歇。”\n\n###","publish_source":"arrington.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-03-27T00:00:00"}},{"id":"news-2509","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿林顿庆祝得州理工系统与联邦调查局建立合作","title_en":"Arrington Celebrates Texas Tech System Partnership with FBI | U.S. Representative Jodey Arrington","summary_cn":"美国众议员乔迪·阿林顿发布新闻稿，宣布出席得克萨斯理工大学系统与联邦调查局签署合作研发协议（CRADA）的仪式，该协议旨在推进美国国家安全、网络安全和关键基础设施保护。阿林顿称针对关键基础设施的网络攻击是经济稳定、公共安全和国家安全面临的重大风险之一。联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔、得州理工系统校监米切尔、得州理工大学校长肖瓦内克及联邦调查局官员亚尔布勒等均发表声明，强调学术界与执法机构合作应对外国和国内威胁的重要性。","summary_en":"U.S. Representative Jodey Arrington issued a press release announcing his attendance at a signing ceremony for a Cooperative Research & Development Agreement (CRADA) between the Texas Tech University System and the Federal Bureau of Investigation to advance U.S. national security, cybersecurity, and critical infrastructure protection. Arrington called cyber attacks on critical infrastructure one of the most significant risks to economic stability, public safety, and national security. Statements from FBI Director Kash Patel, Texas Tech System Chancellor Tedd Mitchell, Texas Tech President Lawrence Schovanec, and FBI official Chad Yarbrough emphasized the importance of academic-law enforcement partnership against foreign and domestic threats.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:58:26.405083+00:00","url":"https://arrington.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=3991","content":"news\nPress Releases\nArrington Celebrates Texas Tech System Partnership with FBI\nShare on Facebook\nShare on X\nPrint this Page\nShare by Email\nLubbock ,\nAugust 18, 2025\nTags:\nConservative Values\n,\nEconomy\nLubbock, TX – Today, House Budget Chairman Jodey Arrington (TX-19) attended a signing ceremony for a Cooperative Research & Development Agreement (CRADA) between the Texas Tech University System and the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) to advance U.S. national security, cybersecurity, and critical infrastructure protection.\n“Cyber attacks on our critical infrastructure present one of the most significant risks to our economic stability, public safety, and national security, and I’m very proud Texas Tech is lending its expertise in partnership with the FBI to confront this threat,” said Chairman Arrington. “No one translates discovery and innovation for solving real-world problems like the faculty at Texas Tech. Unlike many universities today, Texas Tech’s laboratory isn’t in the Ivory Tower, it’s in the marketplace where we work, the communities where we live, and with our government partners working to address our national priorities.”\n“Protecting U.S. critical infrastructure is essential to our national security, and the state of Texas is helping lead the charge with the Critical Infrastructure Security Institute at the Texas Tech University System,\" said Kash Patel, FBI Director. “Today, we celebrate the signing of a landmark agreement between Texas Tech and the FBI – an agreement that will benefit the entire country and facilitate the kind of innovation key to securing America. We will continue to work closely with our partners in government, academia, and the private sector to detect and counter diverse threats from foreign and domestic adversaries.”\n“Among institutions of higher education, the Texas Tech University System has been a longtime leader in research and security studies, and we are excited to join the FBI in this ambitious endeavor,” said Tedd L. Mitchell, M.D., Chancellor of the Texas Tech University System. “This partnership is a testament to the commitment of our universities to identify our world’s most pressing needs and create innovative, collaborative and sustainable solutions. We are grateful for this opportunity and look forward to all we will accomplish together.”\n“Texas Tech University is proud to stand alongside the FBI and Angelo State University in this important partnership to strengthen the security of our nation's critical infrastructure,” said Lawrence Schovanec, President of Texas Tech University. “This collaboration builds on our university's research strengths and our commitment to preparing the next generation of leaders who will protect and serve our country.\"\n“The FBI's mission of protecting the American people includes safeguarding vital assets like U.S. critical infrastructure from all adversaries both foreign and domestic,\" said Chad Yarbrough, Federal Bureau of Investigation. “Working with academic partners like the Texas Tech University System is just one of the many ways the FBI seeks to mitigate these threats and advance cybersecurity and the security of critical infrastructure. The FBI appreciates the forward leaning posture of the TTU System and looks forward to continued partnership to better protect U.S. national security.”\n###\nRelated News\nOPINION: U.S. Rep. Arrington praises Trump administration trade policies\nJune 18, 2026 | Posted in In the News\nSupport for H.Res.50: Affirming States’ Constitutional Right to Defend Against Border Invasion\nMay 15, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases\nOPINION: Texas paid for Biden’s border crisis. Republicans must make sure it never happens again\nMay 13, 2026 | Posted in In the News\nArrington Statement on House Passage of DHS Funding Bill\nApril 30, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases\nArrington Applauds Trump Administration Rolling Back Costly Biden-Era Methane Rule\nApril 7, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases","content_cn":"新闻\n新闻稿\n阿灵顿庆祝德州理工大学系统与联邦调查局建立合作伙伴关系\n在 Facebook 上分享\n在 X 上分享\n打印此页面\n通过电子邮件分享\n卢博克，\n2025年8月18日\n标签：\n保守价值观\n，\n经济\n卢博克，得克萨斯州——今天，众议院预算委员会主席乔迪·阿灵顿（得克萨斯州第19选区）出席了德州理工大学系统与联邦调查局（FBI）签署合作研究与开发协议（CRADA）的仪式，以推进美国国家安全、网络安全和关键基础设施保护。\n“针对我们关键基础设施的网络攻击对经济稳定、公共安全和国家安全构成最重大的风险之一。我非常自豪德州理工大学正与联邦调查局合作，运用自身专业知识应对这一威胁，”阿灵顿主席说。“没有谁能像德州理工大学的教师那样，将发现和创新转化为解决现实世界问题的方案。与如今许多大学不同，德州理工大学的实验室不在象牙塔里，而是在我们工作的市场、我们生活的社区，以及与政府合作伙伴共同解决国家优先事项的地方。”\n“保护美国关键基础设施对国家安全至关重要，得克萨斯州正通过德州理工大学系统的关键基础设施安全研究所带头推进这项工作，”联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔说。“今天，我们庆祝德州理工大学与联邦调查局签署一项具有里程碑意义的协议——这项协议将惠及整个国家，并促进保障美国安全所需的创新。我们将继续与政府、学术界和私营部门的合作伙伴密切协作，侦测并遏制来自外国和国内对手的各种威胁。”\n“在高等教育机构中，德州理工大学系统长期以来一直是研究和安全研究领域的领导者，我们很高兴与联邦调查局共同开展这一雄心勃勃的事业，”德州理工大学系统校长、医学博士特德·L·米切尔说。“这一伙伴关系证明了我们的大学致力于识别世界最紧迫的需求，并创造创新、协作且可持续的解决方案。我们感谢这一机会，并期待我们共同取得的一切成果。”\n“德州理工大学很自豪能与联邦调查局和安杰洛州立大学携手，参与这一加强我国关键基础设施安全的重要伙伴关系，”德州理工大学校长劳伦斯·斯科瓦内克说。“这项合作建立在我们大学的研究优势以及培养下一代领导者、使其能够保护和服务国家的承诺之上。”\n“联邦调查局保护美国人民的使命包括保护美国关键基础设施等重要资产，使其免受外国和国内所有对手的侵害，”联邦调查局的查德·亚伯拉罕说。“与德州理工大学系统这样的学术伙伴合作，只是联邦调查局寻求减轻这些威胁、推进网络安全和关键基础设施安全的众多方式之一。联邦调查局赞赏德州理工大学系统积极进取的姿态，并期待继续合作，更好地保护美国国家安全。”\n###\n相关新闻\n观点：美国众议员阿灵顿赞扬特朗普政府的贸易政策\n2026年6月18日 | 发布于“新闻报道”\n支持H.Res.50：确认各州捍卫宪法权利、抵御边境入侵\n2026年5月15日 | 发布于新闻稿\n观点：得克萨斯州为拜登的边境危机买单。共和党人必须确保这种情况不再发生\n2026年5月13日 | 发布于“新闻报道”\n阿灵顿就众议院通过国土安全部拨款法案发表声明\n2026年4月30日 | 发布于新闻稿\n阿灵顿称赞特朗普政府撤回拜登时期代价高昂的甲烷规定\n2026年4月7日 | 发布于新闻稿","publish_source":"arrington.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-08-18T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1987","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议院预算委员会主席阿灵顿推出SHIELD法案，拟削减庇护城市联邦资金","title_en":"Top Republican rebukes notions to arrest DHS agents with plan to pull funding from problem cities | U.S. Representative Jodey Arrington","summary_cn":"美国众议院预算委员会主席乔迪·阿灵顿（得州共和党人）宣布将提出《SHIELD法案》，禁止地方警察逮捕执行移民执法的联邦探员，并规定任何司法管辖区一旦逮捕、拘留、起诉或阻碍联邦移民官员，将失去整个财年的联邦财政援助，除非其停止相关行为并书面承诺。此举回应了芝加哥、旧金山等地民主党官员的抵制立场。","summary_en":"House Budget Committee Chairman Jodey Arrington (R-Texas) announced the SHIELD Act, which would bar local police from arresting federal immigration agents and cut an entire fiscal year of federal financial assistance to any jurisdiction that arrests, detains, prosecutes or obstructs a federal immigration officer, unless it halts such conduct and attests in writing. The bill responds to resistance from Democratic officials in Chicago and San Francisco.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:54:48.570582+00:00","url":"https://arrington.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=4247","content":"news\nIn the News\nTop Republican rebukes notions to arrest DHS agents with plan to pull funding from problem cities\nHouse Budget Chairman Jodey Arrington's SHIELD Act could target San Francisco, Chicago\nShare on Facebook\nShare on X\nPrint this Page\nShare by Email\nWashington,\nDecember 11, 2025\nTop Republican rebukes notions to arrest DHS agents with plan to pull funding from problem cities\nHouse Budget Chairman Jodey Arrington's SHIELD Act could target San Francisco, Chicago\nBy Charles Creitz\nDecember 11, 2025\nAS SEEN IN FOX NEWS\nEXCLUSIVE: The SHIELD Act — Safeguarding Homeland Immigration Enforcement from Local Detention — would bar local police from arresting federal agents, a response to recent Democratic claims that state and local officials should be able to intervene.\nEfforts from the left to stymie President Donald Trump’s \"mass deportation\" endeavor have often been tied up in court, such as when Obama-appointed Judge William Orrick threw cold water on a prior effort to strip sanctuary cities of federal funding.\nOn Friday, House Budget Committee chairman Jodey Arrington, R-Texas, will introduce the SHIELD Act, which he told Fox News Digital will \"stand up for the rule of law and push back on far-left radicals by cutting off every federal dollar to any jurisdiction that obstructs or prosecutes our officers - even once - carrying out their critical security responsibilities.\"\n\"I’m proud to lead the fight to support our federal officers and hold lawless politicians who undermine the safety and security of the United States fully accountable,\" Arrington said.\nHouse Budget Chairman Jodey Arrington hosts a budget committee hearing at the US Capitol in Washington, DC\nSimilar efforts — including the Trump administration’s bid to penalize sanctuary cities that Orrick blocked — came from the executive branch, while Arrington’s proposal would create a new law.\n\"Any state or local leader who arrests federal agents for enforcing immigration law are abandoning the heart of constitutional order, aiding and abetting criminal illegal aliens, and fueling the perverse incentives that drive illegal immigration,\" Arrington added.\nIn recent weeks, some Democrats pledged varied levels of interference with DHS operations.\nChicago Mayor Brandon Johnson ordered the establishment of \"ICE-Free Zones\" in October, amid \"Operation Midway Blitz\" and DHS’ use of public spaces like a city-owned lot on Kedzie Avenue for staging.\n\"We will not tolerate ICE agents violating our residents’ constitutional rights nor will we allow the federal government to disregard our local authority,\" Johnson said at the time.\n\"ICE agents are detaining elected officials, tear-gassing protestors, children, and Chicago police officers, and abusing Chicago residents,\" he added, claiming his order reflects the Constitutional rights of immigrant communities.\nFederal agents knock on a door of a suspected illegal immigrant in New Orleans, La. (Ryan Murphy/Getty Images)\nTo the west, California lawmakers – some of whom were successful as plaintiffs in the Orrick case – suggested in recent weeks that local authorities may be able to detain federal officers during immigration operations.\nReps. Nancy Pelosi and Kevin Mullin, both Democrats from San Francisco, publicly backed that county’s top prosecutor after a New York Times report said she came up with an idea to prosecute problematic federal agents after-the-fact.\n\"I had lead-time to think about what authority I have and what I can do. This is something I felt very strongly about, and I had my office research it,\" Brooke Jenkins told the paper.\nIn a statement, Pelosi and Mullin said that reports of potential Los Angeles-style raids in the Bay Area would be an \"appalling abuse of law enforcement power.\"\n\"It is important to note that California law protects communities and prevents federal agents from taking certain actions here that we have witnessed in other states.\"\nPelosi, who represents most of San Francisco, and Mullin who represents a small slice of it along with Daly City and part of San Mateo, rebuked Trump’s supposed \"absolute immunity; courtesy of the Supreme Court,\" adding that agents in San Francisco would not enjoy that alleged benefit.\n\"[I]f they break California law — and if they are convicted, the president cannot pardon them,\" Pelosi and Mullin concluded.\nArrington’s bill would directly address San Francisco’s musings and potentially Illinois’ continued oppositional efforts.\nRepresentative Jodey Arrington, a Republican from Texas and chairman of the House Budget Committee, center, speaks during a House Budget Committee\nmeeting at the US Capitol in Washington, DC, US, on Sunday, May 18, 2025.  (Alex Wroblewski/Bloomberg via Getty Images)\nA single instance of arresting, detaining, prosecuting or obstructing a federal immigration officer would trigger a full fiscal-year loss of federal financial assistance.\nThe Justice Department would then only be able to restore federal funding if the municipality halts such behavior and attests to it in writing.\nLegal experts agreed Arrington’s bill would stand up in court.\nHoltzman-Vogel partner Elizabeth Foley — who previously worked for Oregon Democratic Sen. Ron Wyden and later on Republicans’ legal challenge to ObamaCare — told Fox News Digital that Congress has already established this pattern by setting a nationwide 21-year-old drinking age, a policy that withholds portions of USDOT funding from states that drop below that threshold.\nDiffering drinking ages meant a 19-year-old from Allentown, Pennsylvania who could not drink in 1983 could cross the Delaware River into Phillipsburg, New Jersey and legally do so for two extra years.\nFoley noted the Supreme Court upheld the Reagan administration policy in 1987’s Dakota v. Dole.\n\"Putting strings or conditions on the receipt of federal funds is common,\" Foley said.\n\"Because Congress alone has the power of the purse, any conditions on the receipt of federal funds must be made unambiguously by Congress,\" she said, noting that a president lacks that authority by itself – citing the Orrick case.\nFox News Digital reached out to Jenkins’ office as well as Johnson for any comment on the overall idea of withholding funding from their municipalities over their aversion to ICE enforcement.","content_cn":"新闻\n新闻报道\n共和党高层驳斥逮捕国土安全部探员的设想，并计划削减问题城市的资金\n众议院预算委员会主席乔迪·阿灵顿的《SHIELD法案》可能针对旧金山、芝加哥\n在Facebook上分享\n在X上分享\n打印本页\n通过电子邮件分享\n华盛顿，\n2025年12月11日\n共和党高层驳斥逮捕国土安全部探员的设想，并计划削减问题城市的资金\n众议院预算委员会主席乔迪·阿灵顿的《SHIELD法案》可能针对旧金山、芝加哥\n作者：查尔斯·克里茨\n2025年12月11日\n刊于福克斯新闻\n独家报道：《SHIELD法案》——即《保护国土移民执法免受地方拘留法》——将禁止地方警察逮捕联邦探员，此举是对近期民主党声称州和地方官员应有权进行干预的回应。\n左翼阻挠总统唐纳德·特朗普“大规模驱逐”行动的努力往往陷入法庭诉讼，例如奥巴马任命的法官威廉·奥里克曾对先前一项剥夺庇护城市联邦资金的努力泼了冷水。\n周五，德克萨斯州共和党籍众议院预算委员会主席乔迪·阿灵顿将提出《SHIELD法案》。他告诉福克斯新闻数字频道，该法案将“捍卫法治，反击极左激进分子，方法是切断任何阻碍或起诉我们探员——哪怕只有一次——执行其关键安全职责的司法管辖区的每一分联邦资金。”\n阿灵顿说：“我很自豪能领导这场斗争，支持我们的联邦探员，并让那些破坏美国安全与保障的不法政客承担全部责任。”\n众议院预算委员会主席乔迪·阿灵顿在华盛顿特区美国国会大厦主持一场预算委员会听证会\n类似的努力——包括特朗普政府试图惩罚庇护城市但被奥里克阻止——来自行政部门，而阿灵顿的提案将创设一项新法律。\n阿灵顿补充说：“任何因联邦探员执行移民法而将其逮捕的州或地方领导人，都是在抛弃宪法秩序的核心，帮助和教唆犯罪的非法外国人，并助长驱动非法移民的扭曲激励。”\n近几周，一些民主党人承诺对国土安全部行动进行不同程度的干预。\n芝加哥市长布兰登·约翰逊于10月下令设立“无ICE区”，当时正值“中途闪电战行动”，且国土安全部使用公共空间，如凯齐大道上一处市属停车场作为集结地。\n约翰逊当时说：“我们不会容忍ICE探员侵犯我们居民的宪法权利，也不会允许联邦政府无视我们的地方权威。”\n他补充说：“ICE探员正在拘留民选官员，向抗议者、儿童和芝加哥警察喷射催泪瓦斯，并虐待芝加哥居民。”他声称自己的命令体现了移民群体的宪法权利。\n联邦探员在路易斯安那州新奥尔良敲一名疑似非法移民的门。（瑞安·墨菲/盖蒂图片社）\n在西海岸，加利福尼亚州议员——其中一些人作为原告在奥里克案中获胜——近几周暗示，地方当局或许能够在移民行动中拘留联邦探员。\n旧金山民主党众议员南希·佩洛西和凯文·穆林公开支持该县最高检察官，此前《纽约时报》报道称，她提出了在事后起诉有问题联邦探员的想法。\n布鲁克·詹金斯对该报说：“我有提前时间思考我拥有什么权力以及我能做什么。这是我非常强烈感受到的事情，我让我的办公室研究了此事。”\n佩洛西和穆林在一份声明中说，有关湾区可能发生洛杉矶式突袭的报道将是“对执法权力的骇人滥用”。\n“值得注意的是，加利福尼亚州法律保护社区，并阻止联邦探员在这里采取我们在其他州目睹的某些行动。”\n代表旧金山大部分地区的佩洛西，以及代表旧金山一小部分、戴利城和圣马特奥部分地区的穆林，谴责特朗普所谓的“最高法院赐予的绝对豁免权”，并补充说，在旧金山的探员不会享有这一所谓的好处。\n佩洛西和穆林总结道：“[如果]他们违反加利福尼亚州法律——并且如果被定罪，总统不能赦免他们。”\n阿灵顿的法案将直接回应旧金山的盘算，也可能回应伊利诺伊州持续不断的反对行动。\n众议员乔迪·阿灵顿，一位","publish_source":"arrington.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-12-11T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1065","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"阿林顿就众议院通过国土安全部拨款法案发表声明","title_en":"Arrington Statement on House Passage of DHS Funding Bill  | U.S. Representative Jodey Arrington","summary_cn":"美国众议员乔迪·阿林顿官网发布新闻稿，众议院预算委员会主席阿林顿就众议院通过H.R.7147《进一步追加持续拨款法案》发表声明。该法案为第十二项也是最后一项拨款法案，为国土安全部提供资金，涵盖运输安全管理局、联邦应急管理局、网络安全和基础设施安全局、美国海岸警卫队等机构。阿林顿称民主党此前令国土安全部停摆75天，共和党人通过该法案结束停摆，并利用预算调节程序为移民和海关执法局及海关与边境保护局提供未来三年资金。","summary_en":"U.S. Representative Jodey Arrington's official website published a press release in which House Budget Chairman Arrington issued a statement after the House passed H.R. 7147, the Further Additional Continuing Appropriations Act, the twelfth and final appropriations bill, funding the Department of Homeland Security, including TSA, FEMA, CISA and the U.S. Coast Guard. Arrington said Democrats had kept DHS shut down for 75 days, and that Republicans acted to end the shutdown while using reconciliation to fund ICE and CBP for three years, preventing future shutdowns and defunding of ICE.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:29:20.107239+00:00","url":"https://arrington.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=4483","content":"news\nPress Releases\nArrington Statement on House Passage of DHS Funding Bill\nShare on Facebook\nShare on X\nPrint this Page\nShare by Email\nWashington,\nApril 30, 2026\nTags:\nBorder Security\n,\nConservative Values\n,\nDefending America\nWashington, D.C. – Today, House Budget Chairman Jodey Arrington (TX-19) released the following statement after the House of Representatives passed H.R. 7147, the Further Additional Continuing Appropriations Act, the twelfth and final appropriations bill, funding the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) to provide resources to TSA, FEMA, CISA, the U.S. Coast Guard, and other critical agencies:\n“For 75 days, Democrats have kept DHS shut down. House Democrats had 17 opportunities to stand with the men and women who risk their lives for our ports, our borders, and other critical infrastructure.\n“Today, House Republicans acted to end this reckless shutdown and restore critical operations to DHS, while using reconciliation to fund ICE and CBP for the next three years. This will prevent the Democrats from shutting down the government and defunding ICE in the future and provide our agents the resources they need to secure the border, enforce the law, and protect our communities.\n“After four years of lawlessness under Democrats and President Biden and 75 days of Democrat dysfunction, Republicans are restoring order and putting the safety and security of this country first.” – Chairman Arrington.\n###\nRelated News\nOPINION: U.S. Rep. Arrington praises Trump administration trade policies\nJune 18, 2026 | Posted in In the News\nARRINGTON: Securing Record Investment in Dyess Air Force Base\nMay 24, 2026 | Posted in In the News\nSupport for H.Res.50: Affirming States’ Constitutional Right to Defend Against Border Invasion\nMay 15, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases\nTexas GOP House members: What we must do to keep the border secure\nMay 13, 2026 | Posted in In the News\nOPINION: Texas paid for Biden’s border crisis. Republicans must make sure it never happens again\nMay 13, 2026 | Posted in In the News","content_cn":"新闻\n新闻稿\n阿灵顿就众议院通过国土安全部拨款法案发表声明\n在Facebook上分享\n在X上分享\n打印本页\n通过电子邮件分享\n华盛顿，\n2026年4月30日\n标签：\n边境安全\n、\n保守价值观\n、\n捍卫美国\n华盛顿特区——今日，众议院预算委员会主席乔迪·阿灵顿（德克萨斯州第19选区）在众议院通过H.R. 7147号法案《进一步追加持续拨款法案》后发表以下声明。该法案是第十二项也是最后一项拨款法案，为国土安全部（DHS）提供资金，以向运输安全管理局（TSA）、联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）、网络安全和基础设施安全局（CISA）、美国海岸警卫队及其他关键机构提供资源：\n“75天来，民主党人一直让国土安全部处于停摆状态。众议院民主党人有17次机会与那些为我们的港口、边境和其他关键基础设施冒着生命危险的男男女女站在一起。\n“今天，众议院共和党人采取行动，结束了这场鲁莽的停摆，恢复了国土安全部的关键运作，同时利用预算协调程序为移民和海关执法局（ICE）及海关和边境保护局（CBP）提供未来三年的资金。这将防止民主党人今后再次关闭政府并削减ICE的资金，并为我们的人员提供所需资源，以保障边境安全、执行法律、保护我们的社区。\n“在民主党人和拜登总统四年来的无法无天以及民主党人75天的失能之后，共和党人正在恢复秩序，并将这个国家的安全与保障放在首位。”——阿灵顿主席。\n###\n相关新闻\n评论文章：美国众议员阿灵顿赞扬特朗普政府贸易政策\n2026年6月18日 | 发表于新闻报道\n阿灵顿：确保对戴斯空军基地创纪录的投资\n2026年5月24日 | 发表于新闻报道\n支持H.Res.50号决议：确认各州抵御边境入侵的宪法权利\n2026年5月15日 | 发表于新闻稿\n德克萨斯州共和党众议员：我们必须做什么来保持边境安全\n2026年5月13日 | 发表于新闻报道\n评论文章：德克萨斯州为拜登的边境危机付出了代价。共和党人必须确保这种事不再发生\n2026年5月13日 | 发表于新闻报道","publish_source":"arrington.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-04-30T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1227","ktid":1056514,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056514","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"摩根大通以混合型抵押贷款池支持3.492亿美元RMBS发行","title_en":"JP Morgan's pool of hybrid mortgages backs $349.2 million in RMBS | Asset Securitization Report","summary_cn":"摩根大通推出3.492亿美元的住宅抵押贷款支持证券，由混合可调利率抵押贷款池作为担保。该交易名为J.P. Morgan Mortgage Trust 2026-HYB1，采用修正顺序结构偿付票据持有人，共发行八个档级票据，最终到期日为2056年8月。惠誉给予A1A和A1B档AAA评级，借款人加权平均FICO评分为766。","summary_en":"J.P. Morgan is offering $349.2 million in residential mortgage-backed securities backed by a pool of hybrid adjustable-rate mortgages. The deal, J.P. Morgan Mortgage Trust 2026-HYB1, uses a modified sequential structure and issues eight tranches with a final maturity of August 2056. Fitch assigns AAA to classes A1A and A1B; borrowers have a weighted average FICO score of 766.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:38:02.552127+00:00","url":"https://asreport.americanbanker.com/news/jp-morgans-pool-of-hybrid-mortgages-backs-349-2-million-in-rmbs","content":"JPMorgan Chase JP Morgan's pool of hybrid mortgages backs $349.2 million in RMBS By Donna M. Mitchell CloseText About Donna mailto donna.mitchell@arizent.com linkedin https://www.linkedin.com/in/donnamitchellnj/ Published April 02, 2026, 1:17 p.m. EDT 1 Min Read Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Email RH2010 for Adobe Stock JP Morgan is offering the capital markets $349.2 million in residential mortgage-backed securities, from a pool of hybrid adjustable-rate mortgage loans as collateral.The JP Morgan Mortgage Trust 2026-HYB1 will use a modified sequential structure to repay noteholders, instead of the more common senior-subordinate, shifting interest structure in rated deals, according to Fitch Ratings analysts. While the underlying mortgages have a hybrid interest structure, in which all loans initially had a period of fixed rates between 60 and 120 months at origination, none of the 244 loans in the pool are interest-only, Fitch said. Processing ContentFurther, mezzanine and subordinate noteholders will be shut out from receiving principal payments while principal collections are distributed to the class A notes equally until their balances are reduced to zero, Fitch said.The deal will issue the debt through eight tranches of notes, classes A, M and B, according to Fitch.All the notes have a final scheduled maturity date of August 2056, with credit enhancements on the most senior A1A and A1B classes of 15.00% and 8.25%, respectively, Fitch said. The A2 and A3 classes benefit from credit enhancement levels of 6.40% and 2.80%, respectively.Throughout the rest of the deal the M1 through B2 tranches benefit from credit enhancement levels ranging from 1.20% through 0.35%, Fitch analysts said.The deal structure includes two performance triggers to ensure cash flow to the notes—delinquency and cumulative loss, according to Fitch. The delinquency triggers are in place for the life of the transaction. If delinquency rates exceed three pre-set percentages corresponding to three repayment windows, the trigger event will occur, and that will change the principal waterfall from a pro-rata to a sequential structure.Similarly, if cumulative losses are breached, the repayment structure will change from pro-rata to sequential, the rating agency said.The notes also benefit from excess spread of 0.81%, Fitch said.Borrowers are of prime quality with a weighted average (WA) FICO score of 766, and an original loan-to-value (LTV) ratio of 72.5%. Fitch assigns ratings of AAA to classes A1A and A1B; AA- to A2; A- to A3; BBB- to M1; and BB- and B- to classes B1 and B2. ﻿ Donna M. Mitchell Editor Donna M. Mitchell is a financial journalist based in the New York metro area with expertise covering structured finance, commercial real estate, and... Read full bio mailto linkedin For reprint and licensing requests for this article, click here. JPMorgan Chase RMBS Securitization","content_cn":"摩根大通 摩根大通的一池混合型抵押贷款为3.492亿美元住宅抵押贷款支持证券提供支持 作者：Donna M. Mitchell 关闭 关于Donna 邮箱 donna.mitchell@arizent.com 领英 https://www.linkedin.com/in/donnamitchellnj/ 发布于2026年4月2日下午1:17（美国东部时间） 阅读需时1分钟 Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Email RH2010，Adobe Stock 摩根大通正向资本市场发行3.492亿美元的住宅抵押贷款支持证券，其抵押品来自一池混合型可调整利率抵押贷款。根据惠誉评级分析师的说法，JPMorgan Mortgage Trust 2026-HYB1将采用修改后的顺序结构偿还票据持有人，而不是评级交易中更常见的高级—次级、利息转移结构。惠誉表示，尽管基础抵押贷款采用混合利率结构，即所有贷款在发放时最初都有60至120个月的固定利率期限，但该池中的244笔贷款均不是仅付息贷款。处理内容此外，惠誉表示，在本金回收款分配给A类票据且其余额降至零之前，夹层和次级票据持有人将无法获得本金支付。根据惠誉，该交易将通过8个票据档次发行债务，分别为A、M和B类。惠誉表示，所有票据的最终计划到期日均为2056年8月，其中最优先的A1A和A1B类信用增级分别为15.00%和8.25%。A2和A3类受益于分别为6.40%和2.80%的信用增级水平。惠誉分析师表示，在交易的其余部分，M1至B2档次受益于从1.20%至0.35%不等的信用增级水平。根据惠誉，该交易结构包括两个业绩触发机制，以确保向票据支付现金流——拖欠率和累计损失。拖欠率触发机制在整个交易存续期内有效。如果拖欠率超过与三个偿还窗口相对应的三个预设百分比之一，就会发生触发事件，本金分配瀑布将从按比例结构改为顺序结构。评级机构表示，同样，如果累计损失突破阈值，偿还结构也将从按比例改为顺序。惠誉表示，这些票据还受益于0.81%的超额利差。借款人属于优质客户，FICO加权平均（WA）分数为766，原始贷款价值比（LTV）为72.5%。惠誉对A1A和A1B类授予AAA评级；对A2类授予AA-评级；对A3类授予A-评级；对M1类授予BBB-评级；对B1和B2类分别授予BB-和B-评级。﻿ Donna M. Mitchell 编辑 Donna M. Mitchell是一名常驻纽约都会区的金融记者，擅长报道结构化融资、商业房地产以及…… 阅读完整个人简介 邮箱 领英 如需本文转载和许可申请，请点击此处。 摩根大通住宅抵押贷款支持证券证券化","publish_source":"asreport.americanbanker.com","publish_time":"2026-04-02T17:17:34.683000"}},{"id":"news-1904","ktid":1056514,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056514","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"非合格抵押贷款支持摩根大通最新5.876亿美元RMBS发行","title_en":"Non-QM mortgages secure JP Morgan's latest RMBS, offering $587.6 million | Asset Securitization Report","summary_cn":"摩根大通推出5.876亿美元住宅抵押贷款支持证券，由非合格抵押贷款池担保，交易名为J.P. Morgan Mortgage Trust 2025-NQM5。该交易发行约11个档级票据，最终分配日为2066年5月，采用修正顺序结构偿付。约44.5%的贷款为非合格抵押贷款，约50%为投资用途贷款，借款人信用状况总体良好。","summary_en":"J.P. Morgan is bringing a $587.6 million residential mortgage-backed securities offering backed by non-qualified mortgages, named J.P. Morgan Mortgage Trust 2025-NQM5. The deal issues about 11 tranches with a May 2066 final distribution date and a modified-sequential structure. About 44.5% of loans are non-QM and roughly 50% were made for business purposes, with generally strong borrower credit.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:56:36.832156+00:00","url":"https://asreport.americanbanker.com/news/non-qm-mortgages-secure-jp-morgans-latest-rmbs-offering-587-6-million","content":"RMBS Non-QM mortgages secure JP Morgan's latest RMBS, offering $587.6 million By Donna M. Mitchell CloseText About Donna mailto donna.mitchell@arizent.com linkedin https://www.linkedin.com/in/donnamitchellnj/ Published December 29, 2025, 11:57 a.m. EST | Updated December 29, 2025, 5:28 p.m. EST 1 Min Read Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Email Kristina Blokhin for Adobe Stock Non-qualified mortgages will secure the latest J.P. Morgan mortgage issuance, as the J.P. Morgan Mortgage Trust 2025-NQM5 comes to market with $587.6 million in residential mortgage-backed securities.According to Fitch Ratings and Morningstar DBRS, which assessed the deal, the collateral pool is secured by a pool of all first lien mortgages diversified by fixed and adjustable-rates, prime- and non-prime. JPMMT-NQM5 will issue the notes through about 11 tranches of class A, M and B notes, with the class A notes containing the bulk of the notes, the rating agencies said. All the notes have a May 2066 final distribution date.Processing ContentWith J.P. Morgan Securities as lead underwriter, the deal is expected to close on December 30., will repay investors through a modified-sequential structure, with the class A notes being repaid on a pro rata basis, Fitch and DBRS said, although there are limits to the advancing of delinquent principal and interest.A significant portion of the loans in the pool by balance, 44.5%, are designated at non-QM, according to DBRS, adding that about 50% of the loans in the pool were made to investors for business purposes. Only 19.6% of the loans in the collateral pool were underwritten using full documentation, according to Fitch.The underlying loans, however, generally have good credit, with about 72.7% of borrowers having credit scores of 720 and higher. On a weighted average (WA) basis, the underlying loans have a combined loan-to-value (CLTV) ratio of 74.0%, suggesting that borrowers have significant equity in their homes, DBRS said.Some 1,611 loans will secure the certificates issued to investors, as of the deal's December 1, cutoff date. DBRS notes that they benefit from improved underwriting standards. For instance, for borrowers using bank statements as income verification, one borrower must be self-employed, and income must be supported by 12 or 24 months of personal or business bank statements, the rating agency said.Maxex Clearing and United Wholesale Mortgage are the top originators in the pool, while Shellpoint Mortgage and Selene Finance as servicer, Fitch said.Fitch assigns AAA to all the A1A notes; AA- to the A2 notes; A- to the A3 notes and BBB- to the M1A notes.DBRS assigns (P) AAA (sf) to the A1 notes, it says. After that, DBRS' ratings range from (P) AA (high) (sf) on the A2 notes to (P) B (low) (sf) on the B2 notes. ﻿ Donna M. Mitchell Editor Donna M. Mitchell is a financial journalist based in the New York metro area with expertise covering structured finance, commercial real estate, and... Read full bio mailto linkedin For reprint and licensing requests for this article, click here. RMBS Securitization Non-QM J.P. Morgan Securities","content_cn":"非合格抵押贷款为摩根大通最新RMBS提供担保，发行规模5.876亿美元\n作者：Donna M. Mitchell 关闭文本 关于Donna 邮件 donna.mitchell@arizent.com 领英 https://www.linkedin.com/in/donnamitchellnj/\n发表于2025年12月29日上午11:57（美国东部时间）| 更新于2025年12月29日下午5:28（美国东部时间）\n阅读用时1分钟 Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Email\nKristina Blokhin为Adobe Stock拍摄\n非合格抵押贷款将为最新一笔摩根大通抵押贷款发行提供担保。随着J.P. Morgan Mortgage Trust 2025-NQM5进入市场，该交易将发行5.876亿美元住宅抵押贷款支持证券。\n据评估该交易的惠誉评级和Morningstar DBRS称，抵押品池由全部第一留置权抵押贷款构成，并按固定利率和可调整利率、优质和非优质贷款实现多元化。评级机构表示，JPMMT-NQM5将通过约11个A类、M类和B类票据分层发行票据，其中A类票据占票据总量的大部分。所有票据的最终分配日均为2066年5月。\n处理内容\n惠誉和DBRS表示，以J.P. Morgan Securities为主承销商，该交易预计于12月30日完成，并将通过修订后的顺序结构向投资者偿付，其中A类票据按比例偿还，但对拖欠本金和利息的垫付设有限制。\n据DBRS称，按余额计算，贷款池中相当大一部分贷款（44.5%）被指定为非合格贷款；此外，贷款池中约50%的贷款发放给了出于商业目的的投资者。惠誉称，抵押品池中只有19.6%的贷款采用完整文件进行承销。\n然而，基础贷款通常具有良好信用状况，约72.7%的借款人信用评分达到720分及以上。DBRS称，按加权平均（WA）计算，基础贷款的合并贷款价值比（CLTV）为74.0%，这表明借款人在房屋中拥有大量权益。\n截至交易12月1日的截止日，共有1,611笔贷款为向投资者发行的凭证提供担保。DBRS指出，这些贷款受益于改进后的承销标准。评级机构称，例如，对于使用银行对账单进行收入核实的借款人，其中一名借款人必须是自雇人士，且收入必须由12个月或24个月的个人或企业银行对账单予以支持。\n惠誉称，Maxex Clearing和United Wholesale Mortgage是贷款池中的主要发起机构，而Shellpoint Mortgage和Selene Finance担任服务机构。\n惠誉给予所有A1A票据AAA评级；给予A2票据AA-评级；给予A3票据A-评级；给予M1A票据BBB-评级。\nDBRS表示，给予A1票据（P）AAA（sf）评级。此后，DBRS的评级范围从A2票据的（P）AA（高）（sf）到B2票据的（P）B（低）（sf）。\nDonna M. Mitchell 编辑\nDonna M. Mitchell是一名常驻纽约都会区的财经记者，专长于结构化金融、商业房地产以及……\n阅读完整个人简介 mailto linkedin\n如需转载和许可本文，请点击此处。\nRMBS 证券化 非合格贷款 J.P. Morgan Securities","publish_source":"asreport.americanbanker.com","publish_time":"2025-12-29T16:57:37.213000"}},{"id":"news-2815","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike与AARNet合作保护教育行业","title_en":"CrowdStrike Partners With AARNet to Safeguard Education Sector - Australian Cyber Security Magazine","summary_cn":"CrowdStrike与澳大利亚学术与研究网络（AARNet）宣布扩大合作，通过新的托管服务向澳大利亚研究与教育行业提供CrowdStrike Falcon Complete Next-Gen MDR。该服务提供7×24小时托管检测与响应，由AARNet交付，可单独提供或作为现有安全运营中心服务的补充。双方高管表示，该行业持有宝贵数据与知识产权且内部安全资源不足，易受高级威胁攻击，此次合作旨在提供先进技术与行业经验。","summary_en":"CrowdStrike and Australia's Academic and Research Network (AARNet) announced an expanded partnership to deliver CrowdStrike Falcon Complete Next-Gen MDR to Australia's research and education sector through a new managed service. The offering provides 24/7 managed detection and response, delivered by AARNet, available standalone or as an addition to existing AARNet Security Operations Center services. Executives said the sector holds valuable data and intellectual property with under-resourced security programs, making it a prime target for advanced threats.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:20:29.925314+00:00","url":"https://australiancybersecuritymagazine.com.au/crowdstrike-partners-with-aarnet-to-safeguard-education-sector","content":"CrowdStrike Partners With AARNet to Safeguard Education Sector\n0\nBy\nACSM_Accro\non\nMay 30, 2025\nFeatured, Movers & Shakers, Skills & Training, Technology\nCrowdStrike and Australia’s Academic and Research Network (AARNet) today announced an expanded partnership to deliver CrowdStrike Falcon Complete Next-Gen MDR to Australia’s research and education sector through a new managed service.\nThis service will provide institutions with industry-leading, 24/7 managed detection and response to defend against advanced cyber threats powered by CrowdStrike’s Falcon Complete for Service Providers offering and delivered by AARNet.\nThe cyber threat continues to grow while the cybersecurity skills gap widens. Australia’s research and education sector is a prime target for adversaries with the valuable proprietary data and intellectual property they hold – often combined with under-resourced internal security programs.\nFalcon Complete Next-Gen MDR paired with AARNet’s deep experience providing technology services to the research and education sector, provides institutions with the technology, expertise and sector-specific services they need to stay ahead of advanced threats.\nFalcon Complete Next-Gen MDR will be available to AARNet customers through a standalone service or as an addition to a customer’s existing AARNet Security Operations Center managed services.\n“Expanding our partnership with CrowdStrike, cybersecurity’s industry leader, simply makes sense given Australia’s research and education sector is constantly targeted by sophisticated cyber threat actors,” said AARNet CISO Charles Sterner. “Our customers need to be able to protect their vital assets with best-in-class cybersecurity capabilities and expertise. We’re excited to work with CrowdStrike to provide an MDR solution that ensures customers can comprehensively manage, detect and respond to threats.”\n“Falcon Complete Next-Gen MDR sets the standard for MDR while accelerating SOC transformation initiatives in collaboration with innovative services partners like AARNet,” said CrowdStrike’s Jon Fox. “Together, we’re a true force multiplier for Australia’s education and research cybersecurity teams, delivering the advanced technology, expertise, and sector-specific experience they need to combat modern threats.”\n“We’re excited to expand our partnership with AARNet, securing the mission-critical institutions powering Australia’s next generation of innovation and growth,” he said.\nShare.\nTwitter\nFacebook\nPinterest\nLinkedIn\nTumblr\nEmail","content_cn":"CrowdStrike与AARNet合作，保障教育领域安全\n0\n作者\nACSM_Accro\n发表于\n2025年5月30日\n精选、行业领袖、技能与培训、技术\nCrowdStrike和澳大利亚学术与研究网络（AARNet）今天宣布扩大合作，通过一项新的托管服务，向澳大利亚的研究和教育领域提供CrowdStrike Falcon Complete新一代托管检测与响应（MDR）。\n该服务将为各机构提供业内领先的全天候（24/7）托管检测与响应能力，利用CrowdStrike Falcon Complete for Service Providers方案，由AARNet交付，以防御先进网络威胁。\n网络威胁持续增加，而网络安全技能缺口不断扩大。澳大利亚的研究和教育领域是攻击者的主要目标，因为这些机构拥有有价值的专有数据和知识产权，而其内部安全项目往往资源不足。\nFalcon Complete新一代MDR与AARNet在为研究和教育领域提供技术服务方面的深厚经验相结合，为各机构提供了应对先进威胁所需的技术、专业知识和行业特定服务，使其能够保持领先。\nAARNet客户可将Falcon Complete新一代MDR作为独立服务使用，也可以将其添加到客户现有的AARNet安全运营中心托管服务中。\nAARNet首席信息安全官Charles Sterner表示：“扩大我们与网络安全行业领导者CrowdStrike的合作非常合理，因为澳大利亚的研究和教育领域不断受到复杂网络威胁行为者的攻击。我们的客户需要能够凭借一流的网络安全能力和专业知识保护其重要资产。我们很高兴与CrowdStrike合作提供MDR解决方案，确保客户能够全面管理、检测并响应威胁。”\nCrowdStrike的Jon Fox表示：“Falcon Complete新一代MDR树立了MDR的标准，同时与AARNet这样的创新服务合作伙伴协作，加速安全运营中心（SOC）转型计划。我们共同成为澳大利亚教育和研究网络安全团队的真正力量倍增器，为他们提供应对现代威胁所需的先进技术、专业知识和行业特定经验。”\n“我们很高兴扩大与AARNet的合作，为推动澳大利亚下一代创新与增长的关键任务机构提供安全保障。”他补充道。\n分享。\nTwitter\nFacebook\nPinterest\nLinkedIn\nTumblr\n电子邮件","publish_source":"australiancybersecuritymagazine.com.au","publish_time":"2025-05-30T00:10:20+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2038","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"通过AWS Marketplace部署CrowdStrike Falcon下一代SIEM","title_en":"Deploy CrowdStrike Falcon Next-Gen SIEM for AWS through AWS Marketplace | AWS Marketplace","summary_cn":"AWS官方博客介绍如何在AWS Marketplace中订阅并部署CrowdStrike Falcon下一代SIEM。该方案采用按需付费模式，通过AWS IAM跨账户只读角色和CloudFormation实现自动化部署，并集成AWS CloudTrail、Amazon GuardDuty和AWS Security Hub等数据连接器，帮助客户在数分钟内完成跨组织账户的安全监控与响应配置。","summary_en":"An AWS blog explains how to subscribe to and deploy CrowdStrike Falcon Next-Gen SIEM through AWS Marketplace. The pay-as-you-go offering uses IAM cross-account read-only roles and CloudFormation for automated deployment, integrating connectors for AWS CloudTrail, Amazon GuardDuty and AWS Security Hub, enabling customers to set up security monitoring and response across AWS Organization accounts in minutes.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:29:22.927565+00:00","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/awsmarketplace/deploy-crowdstrike-falcon-next-gen-siem-aws-through-aws-marketplace","content":"AWS Marketplace\nDeploy CrowdStrike Falcon Next-Gen SIEM for AWS through AWS Marketplace\nby Jenn Reed and Kunjal Botadra on 01 DEC 2025 in Amazon EventBridge, Amazon GuardDuty, Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3), Announcements, Architecture, AWS CloudTrail, AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM), AWS Key Management Service, AWS Marketplace, AWS re:Invent, AWS Security Hub, Configuration, compliance, and auditing, Security, Technical How-to Permalink Share\nCrowdStrike Falcon for AWS in AWS Marketplace is a pay-as-you-go offering AWS customers can use to help protect their cloud workloads using the CrowdStrike Falcon platform and only pay for what they use. The Falcon platform on Amazon Web Services (AWS) is a unified security platform for enterprise-grade security solutions at scale. This offering includes security information event management (SIEM) and cloud security modules, CrowdStrike Falcon Next-Gen SIEM and CrowdStrike Falcon Cloud Security. Falcon Next-Gen SIEM includes a new automation experience that simplifies the onboarding of the complex configurations of AWS Organizations to provide visibility and security monitoring, analysis, detection, and response all within one platform. It does this by using AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) cross-account read-only asset discovery roles using AWS CloudFormation. In addition to IAM, AWS Marketplace deploys the Falcon Next-Gen SIEM connectors for AWS CloudTrail, Amazon GuardDuty and AWS Security Hub.\nIn this post, we show you how to use the automation experience in AWS Marketplace to deploy Falcon Next-Gen SIEM for AWS across all AWS Accounts in your AWS Organization. We then demonstrate how to connect AWS CloudTrail, AWS Security Hub, and Amazon GuardDuty.\nSolution overview\nCrowdStrike and AWS have created an enhanced version of SaaS Quick Launch for Falcon Next-Gen SIEM in AWS Marketplace, delivering a streamlined deployment experience so customers can quickly deploy and access Falcon Next-Gen SIEM for AWS in minutes.\nCrowdStrike Falcon Next-Gen SIEM for AWS architecture\nFalcon Next-Gen SIEM is a security software-as-a-service (SaaS) hosted on AWS. It uses AWS services running in a customer’s AWS accounts to deploy customer data connectors using Amazon EventBridge, Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS), and Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) to send AWS event and security data to Falcon Next-Gen SIEM. The customer’s Falcon Next-Gen SIEM infrastructure is fully managed by CrowdStrike using IAM using cross-account roles and AWS CloudFormation.\nThe following diagram shows the solution architecture.\nFigure 1: CrowdStrike Falcon Next-Gen SIEM for AWS architecture\nSolution walkthrough: Deploy CrowdStrike Next-Gen SIEM for AWS through AWS Marketplace\nIn the following steps, we show you how to subscribe to CrowdStrike Falcon for AWS in AWS Marketplace. We then use the new launch experience to deploy Falcon Next-Gen SIEM. The solution follows a two-step process:\nStart your CrowdStrike Falcon for AWS subscription\nDeploy CrowdStrike Falcon Next-Gen SIEM for AWS\nStart your CrowdStrike Falcon for AWS subscription\nFollow these steps to subscribe to CrowdStrike Falcon for AWS in AWS Marketplace:\nIn your AWS management account, open the CrowdStrike Falcon for AWS product detail page and choose View purchase options.\nChoose Subscribe.\nYour subscription might take a couple minutes to process. In the meantime, to begin the deployment integration process, click Set up your account (Figure 2).\nIf you receive a dialog box to Enable AWS Marketplace deployment integration, choose Enable and continue.\nFigure 2: Set up your account redirect\nDeploy CrowdStrike Falcon Next-Gen SIEM for AWS\nYou will be taken to the new streamlined experience that will guide you through CrowdStrike authentication, Falcon Next-Gen SIEM for AWS configuration, and launch. Follow these steps:\nYou will be redirected to the CrowdStrike account registration page. Follow the on-screen prompts to register with CrowdStrike. This can take 15 minutes for activation. Wait until you receive the account activation email before you proceed to the next step. .\nReturn to AWS Marketplace and notice the success message indicating that your CrowdStrike account has been linked, as shown in the following screenshot. Choose Next.\nFigure 3: CrowdStrike account linking confirmation message\nIn the Configure deployment Rand access role section, keep the default parameters. Choose Next.\nIn the Configure AWS CloudTrail i section, it will have selected the location where your organizational AWS CloudTrail for management events is configured. Keep the default parameters. Choose Next.\nIn the Configure AWS Security Hub integration section, it will have selected the AWS account and home Region where either AWS Security Hub cloud security posture management (CSPM) or AWS Security Hub is configured. It will then create an Amazon EventBridge rule to send AWS Security Hub events to the CrowdStrike Amazon EventBridge event-bus for Falcon Next-Gen SIEM. Keep the default. Choose Next.\nIn the Configure Amazon GuardDuty integration section, it will have selected the AWS account and Regions where Amazon GuardDuty is configured. It will then create an Amazon EventBridge rule to send Amazon GuardDuty events to the CrowdStrike Amazon EventBridge event-bus for Falcon Next-Gen SIEM. Keep the default parameters. Choose Next.\nIn the Review and launch section, choose Deploy resources. During the next few minutes, the application integration and identity resources necessary to deploy Falcon Next-Gen SIEM, will be installed across all AWS accounts in your AWS Organization. Follow the on-screen prompts to access your new Falcon Next-Gen SIEM quick start connectors page, as shown in the following screenshot.\nFigure 4: CrowdStrike Falcon Next-Gen SIEM quick start connectors page\nConclusion\nIn this post, we demonstrated how to subscribe to and use CrowdStrike Next-Gen SIEM for AWS available in AWS Marketplace. For more information, visit CrowdStrike Falcon for AWS.\nAbout Authors\nJenn Reed\nJenn Reed is a Global Principal Security Solutions Architect at AWS with over 25 years of deep experience working in cyber security and software development. She is based out of Ann Arbor MI. At AWS, she is focused on helping customers build securely with AWS.\nKunjal Botadra\nKunjal Botadra is a Senior Product Manager at Amazon Web Services (AWS), focusing on software delivery and procurement solutions. He drives the strategy and roadmap for enterprise software deployment. Previously at Akamai Technologies, Kunjal developed web performance optimization products and services. He specializes in customer-centric product development and building high-performing cross-functional teams.\nTAGS: AWS Marketplace, aws marketplace security, AWS Marketplace Solutions, Cloud Security, cybersecurity, pay as you go, saas, security","content_cn":"AWS Marketplace\n通过 AWS Marketplace 为 AWS 部署 CrowdStrike Falcon 下一代 SIEM\n作者：Jenn Reed 和 Kunjal Botadra，2025 年 12 月 1 日，分类：Amazon EventBridge、Amazon GuardDuty、Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)、公告、架构、AWS CloudTrail、AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM)、AWS Key Management Service、AWS Marketplace、AWS re:Invent、AWS Security Hub、配置、合规与审计、安全、技术操作指南 永久链接 分享\n\nAWS Marketplace 中的 CrowdStrike Falcon for AWS 是一项按需付费（pay-as-you-go）产品，AWS 客户可以使用它，借助 CrowdStrike Falcon 平台帮助保护其云工作负载，并且只需按实际使用量付费。Amazon Web Services (AWS) 上的 Falcon 平台是一个统一的安全平台，可大规模提供企业级安全解决方案。该产品包含安全信息事件管理（SIEM）和云安全模块，即 CrowdStrike Falcon 下一代 SIEM 和 CrowdStrike Falcon 云安全。Falcon 下一代 SIEM 包含全新的自动化体验，可简化 AWS Organizations 复杂配置的入门流程，从而在一个平台内提供可见性以及安全监控、分析、检测和响应。它通过使用 AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) 跨账户只读资产发现角色，并借助 AWS CloudFormation 来实现这一点。除 IAM 外，AWS Marketplace 还部署适用于 AWS CloudTrail、Amazon GuardDuty 和 AWS Security Hub 的 Falcon 下一代 SIEM 连接器。\n\n在本文中，我们将向您展示如何使用 AWS Marketplace 中的自动化体验，在您的 AWS Organization 中的所有 AWS 账户中部署适用于 AWS 的 Falcon 下一代 SIEM。随后，我们将演示如何连接 AWS CloudTrail、AWS Security Hub 和 Amazon GuardDuty。\n\n解决方案概览\nCrowdStrike 和 AWS 为 AWS Marketplace 中的 Falcon 下一代 SIEM 创建了增强版 SaaS Quick Launch，提供简化的部署体验，使客户能够在几分钟内快速部署并访问适用于 AWS 的 Falcon 下一代 SIEM。\n\nCrowdStrike Falcon 下一代 SIEM for AWS 架构\nFalcon 下一代 SIEM 是托管在 AWS 上的安全软件即服务（SaaS）。它使用在客户 AWS 账户中运行的 AWS 服务，通过 Amazon EventBridge、Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) 和 Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) 部署客户数据连接器，将 AWS 事件和安全数据发送到 Falcon 下一代 SIEM。客户的 Falcon 下一代 SIEM 基础设施由 CrowdStrike 使用 IAM（通过跨账户角色）和 AWS CloudFormation 进行完全托管。\n\n下图展示了解决方案架构。\n图 1：CrowdStrike Falcon 下一代 SIEM for AWS 架构\n\n解决方案演练：通过 AWS Marketplace 为 AWS 部署 CrowdStrike 下一代 SIEM\n在以下步骤中，我们将向您展示如何在 AWS Marketplace 中订阅 CrowdStrike Falcon for AWS。然后，我们使用全新的启动体验来部署 Falcon 下一代 SIEM。该解决方案遵循两步流程：\n1. 开始您的 CrowdStrike Falcon for AWS 订阅\n2. 为 AWS 部署 CrowdStrike Falcon 下一代 SIEM\n\n开始您的 CrowdStrike Falcon for AWS 订阅\n按照以下步骤在 AWS Marketplace 中订阅 CrowdStrike Falcon for AWS：\n1. 在您的 AWS 管理账户中，打开 CrowdStrike Falcon for AWS 产品详情页面，然后选择 View purchase options（查看购买选项）。\n2. 选择 Subscribe（订阅）。\n3. 您的订阅可能需要几分钟来处理。在此期间，要开始部署集成流程，请点击 Set up your account（设置您的账户）（图 2）。\n4. 如果出现 Enable AWS Marketplace deployment integration（启用 AWS Marketplace 部署集成）对话框，请选择 Enable（启用）并继续。\n图 2：设置您的账户重定向\n\n为 AWS 部署 CrowdStrike Falcon 下一代 SIEM\n您将被带到全新的简化体验，该体验将引导您完成 CrowdStrike 身份验证、Falcon 下一代 SIEM for AWS 配置以及启动。请按照以下步骤操作：\n1. 您将被重定向到 CrowdStrike 账户注册页面。按照屏幕上的提示向 CrowdStrike 注册。激活可能需要 15 分钟。请等待收到账户激活电子邮件后，再继续下一步。\n2. 返回 AWS Marketplace，注意显示您的 CrowdStrike 账户已关联的成功消息，如下方截图所示。选择 Next（下一步）。\n图 3：CrowdStrike 账户关联确认消息\n3. 在 Configure deployment Rand access role（配置部署随机访问角色）部分，保留默认参数。选择 Next（下一步）。\n4. 在 Configure AWS CloudTra\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"aws.amazon.com","publish_time":"2025-12-01T00:00:39+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1623","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike任命Jonathon Dixon领导JAPAC地区AI安全业务","title_en":"CrowdStrike names Jonathon Dixon to lead AI security initiatives | Back End News","summary_cn":"网络安全公司CrowdStrike宣布任命Jonathon Dixon为日本及亚太区（JAPAC）副总裁兼董事总经理，负责推动该地区AI驱动的网络安全方案落地，重点推广CrowdStrike Falcon平台。Dixon拥有逾25年网络安全与IT领导经验，此前在Verkada、Cloudflare任职，并曾在AWS、思科和IBM担任管理职务。CrowdStrike总裁Michael Sentonas表示，JAPAC是公司在AI时代的重要增长市场。","summary_en":"Cybersecurity firm CrowdStrike has appointed Jonathon Dixon as vice president and managing director for Japan and Asia Pacific (JAPAC), tasking him with driving AI-powered cybersecurity adoption across the region, with a focus on expanding use of the CrowdStrike Falcon platform. Dixon brings more than 25 years of cybersecurity and IT leadership experience, most recently at Verkada and previously at Cloudflare, AWS, Cisco and IBM. CrowdStrike President Michael Sentonas called JAPAC an important growth theater in the AI era.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:32:38.983760+00:00","url":"https://backendnews.net/crowdstrike-names-jonathon-dixon-to-lead-ai-security-initiatives-in-japac","content":"Appointments\nCrowdStrike names Jonathon Dixon to lead AI security initiatives in JAPAC\nByBack End News\nFeb 11, 2026\nCybersecurity solutions firm CrowdStrike has appointed Jonathon Dixon as vice president and managing director for the Japan and Asia Pacific (JAPAC), tasking him to help drive artificial intelligence (AI)-powered cybersecurity adoption across the region.\nDixon will focus on expanding the use of the CrowdStrike Falcon platform and supporting organizations as they strengthen their cybersecurity programs amid evolving digital threats.\nDixon brings more than 25 years of experience in cybersecurity and information technology leadership. He most recently served as vice president and managing director of Japan and Asia-Pacific at Verkada, where he led go-to-market and operational teams and expanded the company’s presence across the region.\nCrowdStrike report shows AI tools both targeted and used in new cyberattacks\nBefore joining Verkada, Dixon served as vice president and managing director for Asia Pacific, Japan, and Greater China at Cloudflare. The region became the company’s fastest-growing theater during his leadership. Earlier in his career, Dixon held leadership roles at global technology firms AWS, Cisco, and IBM, managing multi-billion-dollar regional business segments and driving revenue growth through channel development and go-to-market strategies.\n“Jonathan brings a rare mix of regional insight and experience scaling businesses, which will be critical to our continued growth in the region,” said Michael Sentonas, president of CrowdStrike. “JAPAC is an important growth theater as organizations modernize their security for the AI era. Under Jonathon’s leadership, we will continue to expand our presence across the region and support more organizations in strengthening their security posture, as traditional approaches struggle to keep pace with today’s threat landscape.”\n“CrowdStrike is leading cybersecurity in the AI era, delivering the game-changing technology that organizations throughout JAPAC need to secure a rapidly evolving threat landscape,” said Dixon. “I am thrilled to be joining CrowdStrike as the company continues to revolutionize cybersecurity and define AI-native platform protection.”\nSHARE\nShare on Facebook (Opens in new window)\nFacebook\nShare on X (Opens in new window)\nX\nShare on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\nLinkedIn\nShare on Reddit (Opens in new window)\nReddit\nShare on Tumblr (Opens in new window)\nTumblr\nShare on Pinterest (Opens in new window)\nPinterest\nShare on Telegram (Opens in new window)\nTelegram\nShare on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\nWhatsApp\nLike this:Like Loading…\nRelated Stories\nPost navigation\nFedEx appoints new Asia Pacific president Dr. Gay Jane Perez takes oath as PhilSA ad interim director general\nBy Back End News\nRelated Post\nAppointments\nIndustry veteran Caroline Foo to lead Microsoft Philippines\nSep 2, 2026\nBack End News\nAppointments\nFortinet names Luca Simonelli as SVP for APAC\nJul 9, 2026\nBack End News\nAppointments\nSAP taps Verena Siow to lead Asia Pacific\nJul 3, 2026\nBack End News\nrealme P4 Litehttps://youtu.be/fFo528dYx3E?si=coaBtcyDF4fS-bQ6\nWeekly Newsletter\nSubscribe on LinkedInSubscribe via Email\nEnter your email address to subscribe and receive notifications of new posts.\nEmail Address\nSubscribe\nPrivacy & Cookies: This site uses cookies. By continuing to use this website, you agree to their use.\nTo find out more, including how to control cookies, see here:\nCookie Policy","content_cn":"人事任命\nCrowdStrike任命乔纳森·迪克森（Jonathon Dixon）领导日本及亚太地区的人工智能安全计划\n作者：Back End News\n2026年2月11日\n网络安全解决方案公司CrowdStrike已任命乔纳森·迪克森（Jonathon Dixon）为日本及亚太地区（JAPAC）副总裁兼董事总经理，委任其协助推动人工智能（AI）驱动的网络安全解决方案在该地区的普及。\n迪克森将专注于扩大CrowdStrike Falcon平台的应用，并在数字威胁不断演变之际，支持各组织加强其网络安全计划。\n迪克森在网络安全和信息技术领导领域拥有超过25年的经验。他最近担任Verkada日本及亚太地区副总裁兼董事总经理，负责领导市场推广和运营团队，并扩大了公司在该地区的业务版图。\nCrowdStrike报告显示AI工具既被攻击者瞄准也被用于新型网络攻击\n在加入Verkada之前，迪克森曾担任Cloudflare亚太、日本及大中华区副总裁兼董事总经理。在其领导期间，该地区成为公司增长最快的市场。在其职业生涯早期，迪克森曾在全球科技公司AWS、思科（Cisco）和IBM担任领导职务，管理数十亿美元规模的区域业务板块，并通过渠道开发和市场推广策略推动收入增长。\n“乔纳森带来了区域洞察力和业务规模化经验的罕见组合，这对我们在该地区的持续增长至关重要，”CrowdStrike总裁迈克尔·森托纳斯（Michael Sentonas）表示。“日本及亚太地区是一个重要的增长市场，各组织正在为AI时代实现安全现代化。在乔纳森的领导下，我们将继续扩大在该地区的业务版图，并支持更多组织加强其安全态势，因为传统方法已难以跟上当今的威胁形势。”\n“CrowdStrike正在引领AI时代的网络安全，提供颠覆性技术，帮助整个日本及亚太地区的组织应对快速演变的威胁形势，”迪克森表示。“我很高兴能加入CrowdStrike，公司正在持续革新网络安全，并定义AI原生平台保护。”\n分享\n在Facebook上分享（在新窗口中打开）\nFacebook\n在X上分享（在新窗口中打开）\nX\n在LinkedIn上分享（在新窗口中打开）\nLinkedIn\n在Reddit上分享（在新窗口中打开）\nReddit\n在Tumblr上分享（在新窗口中打开）\nTumblr\n在Pinterest上分享（在新窗口中打开）\nPinterest\n在Telegram上分享（在新窗口中打开）\nTelegram\n在WhatsApp上分享（在新窗口中打开）\nWhatsApp\n喜欢这个：喜欢加载中……\n相关报道\n文章导航\n联邦快递任命新的亚太区总裁 盖伊·简·佩雷斯博士宣誓就任菲律宾航天局临时局长\n作者：Back End News\n相关文章\n人事任命\n行业资深人士卡罗琳·傅（Caroline Foo）将领导微软菲律宾\n2026年9月2日\nBack End News\n人事任命\nFortinet任命卢卡·西蒙内利（Luca Simonelli）为亚太区高级副总裁\n2026年7月9日\nBack End News\n人事任命\nSAP聘请维雷娜·萧（Verena Siow）领导亚太区\n2026年7月3日\nBack End News\nrealme P4 Lite https://youtu.be/fFo528dYx3E?si=coaBtcyDF4fS-bQ6\n每周通讯\n在LinkedIn上订阅 通过电子邮件订阅\n输入您的电子邮件地址以订阅并接收新文章通知。\n电子邮件地址\n订阅\n隐私与Cookie：本网站使用Cookie。继续使用本网站即表示您同意其使用。\n如需了解更多信息，包括如何控制Cookie，请参阅：\nCookie政策","publish_source":"backendnews.net","publish_time":"2026-02-11T09:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2084","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国会议员方文思获任命加入第119届国会国土安全委员会","title_en":"Congressman Vince Fong appointed to House Homeland Security Committee for 119th Congress","summary_cn":"加州第20选区联邦众议员方文思（Vince Fong）被任命为第119届国会国土安全委员会成员，将负责反恐、应急准备、网络安全以及非法移民和外国对手威胁等议题。方文思表示将把公共安全作为首要任务，委员会主席加拉巴里诺对其加入表示欢迎。","summary_en":"Congressman Vince Fong (CA-20) was appointed to the House Homeland Security Committee for the 119th Congress, covering counterterrorism, emergency preparedness, cybersecurity, and threats from illegal immigration and foreign adversaries. Fong said public safety must be a top priority, and Chairman Andrew Garbarino welcomed his addition to the committee.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:11:10.746903+00:00","url":"https://bakersfieldnow.com/news/local/congressman-vince-fong-appointed-to-house-homeland-security-committee-for-119th-congress-counterterrorism-emergency-cybersecurity-illegal-immigration-borders-ports-bakersfield-kern-county","content":"Congressman Vince Fong appointed to House Homeland Security Committee for 119th Congressby BakersfieldNow StaffWed, November 19, 2025 at 4:17 PMUpdated Wed, November 19, 2025 at 4:18 PM4VIEW ALL PHOTOSFILE -Congressman Vince Fong praised the Federal Railroad Administration for its recent report, which he said exposes the California High-Speed Rail project as a significant example of government waste. (Photo: Rep. Vince Fong)1CommentSharetopics: Vince FongHomeland SecurityCongressCounterterrorismCybersecurityEmergency PreparednessIllegal ImmigrationChinaBAKERSFIELD, Calif.(KBAK/KBFX) — On Wednesday, Congressman Vince Fong (CA-20) was appointed to the House Homeland Security Committee for the 119th Congress.Fong's position will cover issues of importance to the safety of Californians and Americans, which include counterterrorism, emergency preparedness, cybersecurity, as well as threats posed by illegal immigration and foreign adversaries such as China, according to a press release.Fong stated, “I’m honored to have been selected to serve on the Homeland Security Committee. A secure California is critical to protecting our homeland. From our borders and ports to our cybersecurity and defense assets – we must make public safety a top priority and be ready to confront the ever-evolving threats facing our nation. I look forward to working with my colleagues on the Committee to advance policies that safeguard our communities, strengthen our preparedness, and ensure the security of the American people.”Chairman Andrew Garbarino stated, “I am proud to welcome Congressman Fong to the Committee on Homeland Security. Throughout his years of service at the local, state, and federal levels of government, he has consistently demonstrated a deep commitment to improving the lives of his constituents and the American people. His experience and perspective will strengthen our efforts to protect our supply chains, safeguard critical infrastructure, combat evolving threats in and out of cyberspace, and enhance public safety. I look forward to working alongside Congressman Fong to keep our homeland secure.”TrendingDistrict cites injury policy as mom seeks review of Loudon Elementary incidentA mother is questioning how Loudon Elementary School handled her 4-year-old daughter’s injury after she says the child fell during the school day and was not ta42-year-old woman awaiting trial dies in custody at Kern County jailAccording to the Kern County Sheriff’s Office records, a person died while in custody on Monday, September 14.According to records, the person was identified asBPD: Bakersfield man arrested in kidnapping and rape of missing 11-year-old girlA 29-year-old man was arrested after investigators said Flock Safety cameras helped identify his vehicle in connection with the kidnapping and rape of an 11-yeaDriver dead after truck hits tree, catches on fire along Highway 99A driver died after a truck struck a tree and caught on fire on Highway 99 Wednesday afternoon.The California Highway Patrol said on Wednesday, September 16, 20Ross Stores, Inc. to build processing and distribution center in southeast BakersfieldThe City of Bakersfield announced that a Ross Stores, Inc. processing and distribution center will be coming. It is expected to bring hundreds of jobs and milliNEWS IN PHOTOS:\"Local\"3District cites injury policy as mom seeks review of Loudon Elementary incident3Diesel prices keep climbing in California, squeezing Bakersfield drivers and truckers5Driver dead after truck hits tree, catches on fire along Highway 995Federal prosecutors charge 3 with stealing $12M in homeless aid fraud in Los Angeles","content_cn":"国会议员文斯·方被任命为第119届国会众议院国土安全委员会成员\n作者：BakersfieldNow 工作人员\n2025年11月19日星期三下午4:17\n更新于2025年11月19日星期三下午4:18\n4 查看所有照片\n资料图——国会议员文斯·方赞扬联邦铁路管理局近期的报告，称该报告揭露加州高铁项目是政府浪费的重大例证。（照片：国会议员文斯·方）\n1条评论 分享\n话题：文斯·方 国土安全 国会 反恐 网络安全 应急准备 非法移民 中国\n加州贝克斯菲尔德（KBAK/KBFX）——周三，国会议员文斯·方（加州第20选区）被任命为第119届国会众议院国土安全委员会成员。\n据一份新闻稿称，方的职位将负责对加州人和美国人安全至关重要的问题，包括反恐、应急准备、网络安全，以及非法移民和诸如中国等外国对手带来的威胁。\n方表示：“我很荣幸被选中在国土安全委员会任职。一个安全的加州对于保护我们的国土至关重要。从我们的边境和港口到我们的网络安全和国防资产——我们必须将公共安全作为首要任务，并准备好应对我们国家面临的不断演变的威胁。我期待与委员会的同仁合作，推进保护我们社区、加强我们的准备工作并确保美国人民安全的政策。”\n主席安德鲁·加巴里诺表示：“我很自豪地欢迎方国会议员加入国土安全委员会。他在地方、州和联邦各级政府多年的服务中，始终展现出对改善其选民和美国人民生活的坚定承诺。他的经验和视角将加强我们保护供应链、保障关键基础设施、打击网络空间内外的不断演变威胁以及提升公共安全的努力。我期待与方国会议员并肩合作，维护我们的国土安全。”\n热门\n学区援引伤害政策，母亲寻求审查劳登小学事件\n一位母亲质疑劳登小学如何处理她4岁女儿的受伤事件，她说孩子在当天上学期间摔倒，却没有被……\n42岁女子候审期间在克恩县监狱羁押中死亡\n根据克恩县治安官办公室记录，9月14日星期一有一人在羁押中死亡。\n记录显示，该人被确认为……\n贝克斯菲尔德警方：贝克斯菲尔德男子因绑架并强奸失踪的11岁女孩被捕\n一名29岁男子被捕，调查人员称Flock Safety摄像头帮助识别出他的车辆，该车与一名11岁女孩被绑架并强奸一案有关……\n司机在99号公路上卡车撞树起火后死亡\n周三下午，一名司机在99号公路上卡车撞树起火后死亡。\n加州公路巡警称，9月16日星期三，20……\n罗斯百货公司将在贝克斯菲尔德东南部建设加工和配送中心\n贝克斯菲尔德市宣布，罗斯百货公司将建设一个加工和配送中心。预计将带来数百个工作岗位和数百万……\n新闻图片：\n“本地”\n3 学区援引伤害政策，母亲寻求审查劳登小学事件\n3 加州柴油价格持续攀升，令贝克斯菲尔德司机和卡车司机承压\n5 司机在99号公路上卡车撞树起火后死亡\n5 联邦检察官指控3人在洛杉矶盗窃1200万美元无家可归者援助欺诈案","publish_source":"bakersfieldnow.com","publish_time":"2025-11-20T00:17:26+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2824","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"联邦调查局悬赏2万美元征集1999年克恩县谋杀案逃犯线索","title_en":"FBI offers $20,000 reward for fugitive wanted for 1999 Kern County murder","summary_cn":"联邦调查局萨克拉门托分局悬赏最高2万美元，征集有助于逮捕并定罪赫苏斯·何塞·阿斯托尔加的线索。阿斯托尔加涉嫌1999年10月15日在加州沙夫特一处公寓持刀杀害一名男子，1999年11月被克恩县地检署以一级谋杀罪起诉，2000年6月因非法逃避起诉被联邦法院发出逮捕令。据称他已逃往墨西哥，与杜兰戈和索诺拉两地有关联。","summary_en":"The FBI Sacramento Field Office is offering a reward of up to $20,000 for information leading to the arrest and conviction of Jesus Jose Astorga, who allegedly fled to Mexico to avoid prosecution for a 1999 Kern County murder. Astorga was charged with first-degree murder in the fatal stabbing of a man at a Shafter apartment on October 15, 1999, and a federal arrest warrant for unlawful flight to avoid prosecution was issued in June 2000. He reportedly has ties to Durango and Sonora, Mexico.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:24:25.722533+00:00","url":"https://bakersfieldnow.com/news/local/fbi-offers-20000-reward-for-fugitive-wanted-for-1999-kern-county-murder-shafter-california","content":"FBI offers $20,000 reward for fugitive wanted for 1999 Kern County murderby BakersfieldNow StaffTue, May 27, 2025 at 11:09 AM6VIEW ALL PHOTOSThe Federal Bureau of Investigation Sacramento Field Office is offering a reward of up to $20,000 for information leading to the arrest and conviction of Jesus Jose Astorga, who allegedly went to Mexico to avoid prosecution for murder in Kern County. PHOTO: FBI Sacramento1CommentSharetopics: FBIRewardFugitiveMurderKern CountyJesus Jose AstorgaArrestMexicoBAKERSFIELD, Calif. (KBAK/KBFX) — The Federal Bureau of Investigation Sacramento Field Office is offering a reward of up to $20,000 for information leading to the arrest and conviction of Jesus Jose Astorga, who allegedly went to Mexico to avoid prosecution for murder in Kern County.Anyone with information regarding the location of Astorga is asked to call the local FBI office, nearest United States embassy, or submit a tip at tips.fbi.gov. All information can be submitted anonymously.FBI Sacramento said Astorga has ties to the cities of Durango and Sonora in Mexico. He is described as Hispanic, 5’7” tall, with black hair and brown eyes. He also has scars on his head and face.jesus-jose-astorgaPDF previewPreview PDFView PDFThe Shafter Police Department said Astorga was allegedly involved in the fatal stabbing of a man at a Shafter apartment on October 15, 1999. Shafter police said on November 2, 1999, the Kern County District Attorney’s Office charged Astorga with one count of murder in the first degree in the Bakersfield Municipal Court District in Kern County.On June 20, 2000, a federal arrest warrant for unlawful flight to avoid prosecution was issued for Astorga in the United States District Court in the Eastern District of California.“The FBI has a long-standing commitment to aiding our law enforcement partners and ensuring defendants face the charges brought against them—no matter how far they may run,” said Sid Patel, Special Agent in Charge of the FBI Sacramento Field Office. “Every family deserves an opportunity to seek justice for their lost loved ones.”TrendingJackknifed semi blocks northbound Interstate 5 lanes near GormanMotorists traveling from SoCal to Kern County can expect delays on northbound Interstate 5 after a semi-truck jackknifed early Thursday morning.The CHP&rsquo;s websitWhat you need to know before you go to the 2026 Kern County FairFrom hours, tickets, and wristbands to concerts, here's what you need to know before heading to the Kern County Fair.The 2026 Kern County Fair is running from SShelter-in-place LIFTED for east Bakersfield zone after hydrochloric acid leakA shelter-in-place order for a zone in east Bakersfield has been lifted. The advisory was issued due to a hazardous leak involving hydrochloric acid.The Kern CoBakersfield Search and Rescue seeks meal donations as volunteers patrol fair parking lotsBakersfield Search and Rescue Team is seeking meal donations for their volunteer members as they patrol the Kern County Fair parking lots every night.&ldquo;Our team Delano PD: 47-year-old man wanted for attempted murder after High Street shootingThe Delano Police Department is asking for the community&rsquo;s help in finding 47-year-old Manuel Robert Lema, who is wanted for attempted murder and assault with aNEWS IN PHOTOS:\"Local\"8KCSO: 4 arrested after 679 pounds of meth, guns and cash seized, two meth labs dismantled3Jackknifed semi blocks northbound Interstate 5 lanes near Gorman9Kern County Fair shares child safety tips for families4Kern County Fair boosts security with magnetometers, AI, and police partnership","content_cn":"FBI 悬赏20,000美元，征集有关一名因1999年克恩县谋杀案被通缉逃犯的信息\nBakersfieldNow 工作人员\n2025年5月27日，星期二，上午11:09\n6\n查看所有照片\n联邦调查局萨克拉门托外地办事处悬赏最高20,000美元，征集能够促成 Jesus Jose Astorga 被逮捕并定罪的信息；他涉嫌前往墨西哥以逃避因克恩县谋杀案而受到起诉。照片：FBI 萨克拉门托\n1条评论\n分享\n主题：FBI、悬赏、逃犯、谋杀、克恩县、Jesus Jose Astorga、逮捕、墨西哥\n加利福尼亚州贝克斯菲尔德（KBAK/KBFX）——联邦调查局萨克拉门托外地办事处悬赏最高20,000美元，征集能够促成 Jesus Jose Astorga 被逮捕并定罪的信息；他涉嫌前往墨西哥以逃避因克恩县谋杀案而受到起诉。\n\n任何掌握 Astorga 所在地点信息的人，请致电当地 FBI 办事处、最近的美国大使馆，或在 tips.fbi.gov 提交线索。所有信息均可匿名提交。\n\nFBI 萨克拉门托表示，Astorga 与墨西哥的杜兰戈市和索诺拉市有联系。他被描述为西班牙裔，身高5英尺7英寸，黑发棕眼。他的头部和面部还有伤疤。\n\njesus-jose-astorga\nPDF 预览\n预览 PDF\n查看 PDF\n\n沙夫特警察局表示，Astorga 涉嫌参与于1999年10月15日在沙夫特一间公寓内发生的一名男子被刺身亡案件。沙夫特警方表示，1999年11月2日，克恩县地方检察官办公室在克恩县贝克斯菲尔德市法院辖区以一级谋杀罪一项罪名起诉 Astorga。\n\n2000年6月20日，美国加利福尼亚东区联邦地区法院对 Astorga 签发了因非法逃亡以逃避起诉的联邦逮捕令。\n\n“FBI 长期致力于协助我们的执法合作伙伴，并确保被告面对针对他们提出的指控——无论他们逃得多远，”FBI 萨克拉门托外地办事处主管特别探员 Sid Patel 表示。“每个家庭都应有机会为失去的亲人寻求正义。”\n\n热门\n折叠式半挂车阻塞戈尔曼附近5号州际公路北行车道\n从南加州前往克恩县的驾车者可预计5号州际公路北行方向出现延误，原因是一辆半挂卡车于周四清晨发生折叠式侧滑。\nCHP 的网站\n\n前往2026年克恩县博览会前须知\n从开放时间、门票和腕带到音乐会，以下是前往克恩县博览会前需要了解的事项。\n2026年克恩县博览会从\n\n盐酸泄漏后，贝克斯菲尔德东区的就地避难令已解除\n贝克斯菲尔德东区一片区域的就地避难令已解除。该警告因涉及盐酸的危险泄漏而发布。\n克恩县\n\n贝克斯菲尔德搜救队在志愿者巡逻博览会停车场期间征集餐食捐赠\n贝克斯菲尔德搜救队正在为其志愿成员征集餐食捐赠；他们每晚都会巡逻克恩县博览会停车场。“我们的团队\n\n德拉诺警察局：高街枪击案后，47岁男子因涉嫌谋杀未遂被通缉\n德拉诺警察局正请求社区协助寻找47岁的 Manuel Robert Lema；他因涉嫌谋杀未遂和袭击而被通缉。\n\n图片新闻：\n“本地”\n8\nKCSO：缴获679磅冰毒、枪支和现金并捣毁两处制毒实验室后，4人被捕\n3\n折叠式半挂车阻塞戈尔曼附近5号州际公路北行车道\n9\n克恩县博览会向家庭分享儿童安全提示\n4\n克恩县博览会通过磁力计、人工智能和警方合作加强安保","publish_source":"bakersfieldnow.com","publish_time":"2025-05-27T18:09:49+00:00"}},{"id":"news-535","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"被解雇FBI员工促法院审查帕特尔的“反同性恋运动”","title_en":"Fired FBI agent urges court to examine Patel's anti-gay crusade","summary_cn":"一名FBI实习特工大卫·马尔廷斯基在2025年因在工作站展示骄傲旗被FBI局长卡什·帕特尔解雇，距其从匡蒂科FBI学院毕业仅三周。他此前为FBI工作逾16年。其律师团队请求法院允许取证程序推进，以公开帕特尔及司法部的内部文件和投诉员工姓名，并称政府试图阻挠取证的理由毫无根据。","summary_en":"FBI agent trainee David Maltinsky was fired in 2025 by FBI Director Kash Patel for displaying a Pride flag at his workstation, three weeks before graduating from the FBI Academy at Quantico, after more than 16 years with the bureau. His legal team is asking the court to allow discovery to proceed, seeking internal documents and statements from Patel and the DOJ, calling the government's efforts to block discovery meritless.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:43:08.750666+00:00","url":"https://baptistnews.com/article/fired-fbi-employee-urges-court-to-examine-patels-anti-gay-crusade","content":"An FBI agent trainee is challenging the Trump administration and FBI Director Kash Patel’s attempts to quash his lawsuit against them for wrongful termination.\nDavid Maltinsky was fired in 2025 for displaying a Pride flag at his workstation — a flag the FBI had given to him and sanctioned the display of. He was terminated from employment by Patel three weeks before he was to graduate from the FBI Academy at Quantico.\nMaltinsky had worked for the bureau more than 16 years and completed 16 weeks of its 19-week special agent training program. Patel’s termination letter said Maltinsky exercised “poor judgment” by displaying “political signage” at his workstation.\nThe “political signage” in question was a progress Pride flag previously flown outside the Wilshire Federal Building in Los Angeles and later given to him in recognition of his work supporting LGBTQ employees. He displayed it with a small placard describing its history.\nFBI Director Kash Patel speaks at a news conference July 1, 2026, at Briefing Room/DOJ in Washington DC, USA. (Lenin Nolly/Sipa USA via AP Images)\nWhile Patel found the Pride flag offensive, the Trump administration allows other FBI employees to display Thin Blue Line flags, Gadsden flags and Punisher skull imagery, Maltinsky’s lawyers said.\nMaltinsky’s lawsuit in U.S. District Court for the District of Columbia began in November 2025 but recently was stalled by the administration’s attempt to dismiss key parts of the suit. His latest motion asks the court to allow discovery to proceed, which would make public internal documents and statements by Patel, as well as the names of FBI employees who complained about the presence of the Pride flag.\nMaltinsky’s legal team says the government’s attempt to subvert discovery are meritless.\n“David Maltinsky served the FBI and this country with honor for more than 16 years, only to be fired for displaying a Pride flag that the FBI gave him in recognition of his efforts to strengthen the bureau,” said Christopher M. Mattei, a partner at Koskoff Koskoff & Bieder and counsel for Maltinsky. “Instead of answering for their unlawful actions, Director Patel and the DOJ are making baseless arguments in an effort to delay justice and shield from public view the cruel discrimination that led to David’s firing.”\n“David was boldly moved to a life of public service after the Pulse nightclub shooting claimed 49 lives in 2016, and in the years that followed he was an exceptional employee on track to become a special agent. Then Kash Patel and the Trump administration targeted him not just for his speech, but for who he is,” said Nathaniel Zelinsky of the Washington Litigation Group. “This shocking abuse of an honorable member of the federal law enforcement community cries out for justice.”\nThe Trump administration is beholden to a conservative evangelical voting bloc that generally opposes the LGBTQ community and disdains Pride flags and Pride celebrations.\nTags:LGBTQFBITrump AdministrationPride flagKash PatelDavid MaltinskyMore byMark Wingfield","content_cn":"一名联邦调查局（FBI）特工学员正在挑战特朗普政府和FBI局长卡什·帕特尔试图压制他针对两者提起的非法解雇诉讼的行为。\n\n大卫·马尔廷斯基因在工作站展示彩虹旗而于2025年被解雇——这面旗帜是FBI提供给他的，且FBI批准展示。他在原本还差三周即将从弗吉尼亚州匡蒂科的FBI学院毕业时，被帕特尔终止了雇佣关系。\n\n马尔廷斯基在该局工作了16年多，并完成了为期19周的特工培训项目中的16周。帕特尔的解雇信称，马尔廷斯基在工作站展示“政治标语”是“判断力不佳”的表现。\n\n所称的“政治标语”是一面进步彩虹旗，此前曾悬挂在洛杉矶威尔希尔联邦大楼外，后来为表彰他支持LGBTQ员工的工作而赠予他。他展示这面旗帜时，还放置了一块小牌子介绍其历史。\n\n2026年7月1日，美国华盛顿特区司法部简报室，FBI局长卡什·帕特尔在新闻发布会上发言。（Lenin Nolly/Sipa USA via AP Images）\n\n马尔廷斯基的律师称，尽管帕特尔认为彩虹旗令人反感，特朗普政府却允许其他FBI员工展示“蓝线”旗、加兹登旗和《惩罚者》骷髅图案。\n\n马尔廷斯基于2025年11月在美国哥伦比亚特区联邦地区法院提起诉讼，但政府近期试图驳回诉讼中的关键部分，导致案件陷入停滞。他最新提交的动议请求法院允许继续证据开示，这将使帕特尔的内部文件和陈述，以及投诉彩虹旗存在的FBI员工姓名公开。\n\n马尔廷斯基的法律团队表示，政府试图破坏证据开示的做法毫无依据。\n\n“戴维·马尔廷斯基以荣誉为FBI和这个国家服务了16年多，却仅仅因为展示FBI为表彰他努力加强该局而赠予他的彩虹旗而被解雇，”Koskoff Koskoff & Bieder律师事务所合伙人、马尔廷斯基代理律师克里斯托弗·M·马泰说。“帕特尔局长和司法部没有为其违法行为作出解释，反而提出毫无根据的论点，企图拖延正义，并掩盖导致戴维被解雇的残酷歧视，不让公众看到。”\n\n“2016年Pulse夜总会枪击事件夺走49条生命后，戴维毅然投身公共服务；在此后的岁月里，他是一名出色的员工，正朝着成为特工的目标前进。随后，卡什·帕特尔和特朗普政府针对的不仅是他的言论，还有他的身份，”华盛顿诉讼集团的纳撒尼尔·泽林斯基说。“这起对一名受人尊敬的联邦执法界成员令人震惊的滥权行为，迫切需要得到公正处理。”\n\n特朗普政府依赖一个保守的福音派选民群体，该群体通常反对LGBTQ群体，并鄙视彩虹旗和彩虹庆祝活动。\n\n标签：LGBTQ、FBI、特朗普政府、彩虹旗、卡什·帕特尔、大卫·马尔廷斯基；作者：马克·温菲尔德","publish_source":"baptistnews.com","publish_time":"2026-07-22T02:32:48+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3590","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike因全球宕机事件被股东起诉","title_en":"CrowdStrike sued by shareholders over global outage - Barbados Today","summary_cn":"网络安全公司CrowdStrike因一次故障软件更新导致全球超800万台电脑崩溃，被股东起诉。诉讼指控公司就其软件测试作出“虚假和误导性”陈述，称事件后12天内股价下跌32%，市值损失250亿美元。CrowdStrike否认指控并表示将抗辩。公司称截至7月29日宕机已修复。达美航空CEO表示宕机造成该航司5亿美元损失，正寻求赔偿。故障更新于7月19日导致全球微软Windows电脑崩溃，扰乱航空、银行和医院等服务。","summary_en":"Cybersecurity firm CrowdStrike is being sued by shareholders after a faulty software update crashed more than eight million computers worldwide. The lawsuit accuses the company of making false and misleading statements about its software testing, saying its share price dropped 32 percent in the 12 days after the incident, a loss of $25bn in market value. CrowdStrike denies the allegations and says it will defend itself. The company said the outage was fixed as of July 29. Delta Air Lines' CEO said the disruption cost the airline $500m and it is preparing to seek compensation. The faulty July 19 update crashed 8.5 million Microsoft Windows computers, disrupting airlines, banks and hospitals.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:21:12.024453+00:00","url":"https://barbadostoday.bb/2024/08/01/crowdstrike-sued-by-shareholders-over-global-outage/amp","content":"Technology World\nCrowdStrike sued by shareholders over global outage\nSandy Deane01/08/202401.7K views\nCrowdStrike is being sued by its shareholders after a faulty software update by the cybersecurity firm crashed more than eight million computers and caused chaos around the world.\nThe lawsuit accuses the company of making “false and misleading” statements about its software testing.\nIt also says the company’s share price dropped 32 per cent in the 12 days after the incident, causing a loss in market value of $25bn (£14.5bn).\nCrowdStrike denies the allegations and says it will defend itself against the proposed class action lawsuit.\nMeanwhile, the firm has said computers affected by the massive global IT outage are effectively now back to normal.\nThe US-based company stated that as of 5 p.m. local time on Monday, 29 July (00:00, Tuesday GMT), the outage had been fixed – ten days after the incident began.\nThe suit filed in the Austin, Texas federal court, alleges that CrowdStrike executives defrauded investors by making them believe the company’s software updates were adequately tested.\nThe lawsuit is seeking an unspecified amount of compensation for investors who owned CrowdStrike shares between 29 November and 29 July.\nIt cites chief executive George Kurtz, who said in a conference call on 5 March that the firm’s software was “validated, tested and certified.”\nCrowdStrike told BBC News that it disputes the claims.\n“We believe this case lacks merit and we will vigorously defend the company,” a spokesperson said.\nMeanwhile, the chief executive of Delta Air Lines, Ed Bastian, has said in an interview with business news channel CNBC that the disruption caused by the outage cost the airline $500m, including lost revenue and compensation to passengers.\nDelta has reportedly hired a prominent lawyer and is preparing to seek compensation from CrowdStrike.\nThe faulty update on 19 July crashed 8.5 million Microsoft Windows computers around the world. The outage disrupted businesses and services, including airlines, banks and hospitals.\nIn a detailed review of the incident, CrowdStrike said there was a “bug” in a system designed to ensure software updates worked properly.\nCrowdStrike said the glitch meant “problematic content data” in a file went undetected.\nThe company said it could prevent a repeat of the incident with better software testing and checks, including more scrutiny from developers. (BBC)\nShareFacebookTwitterPinterestEmail","content_cn":"科技世界\nCrowdStrike因全球宕机被股东起诉\nSandy Deane\n2024年08月01日\n1.7K次观看\n在这家网络安全公司的错误软件更新导致逾800万台电脑崩溃、并在全球引发混乱后，CrowdStrike正遭其股东起诉。\n该诉讼指控该公司就其软件测试作出“虚假且误导性”的陈述。\n诉讼还称，事件发生后的12天内，该公司股价下跌32%，造成250亿美元（145亿英镑）的市值损失。\nCrowdStrike否认这些指控，并表示将为自己应对这起拟议的集体诉讼。\n与此同时，该公司表示，受这次大规模全球IT宕机影响的电脑如今实际上已恢复正常。\n这家总部位于美国的公司称，截至7月29日星期一当地时间下午5点（格林尼治时间星期二00:00），宕机问题已得到修复——距离事件开始已有10天。\n提交至得克萨斯州奥斯汀联邦法院的诉状称，CrowdStrike高管让投资者相信公司的软件更新经过充分测试，从而欺诈了投资者。\n该诉讼寻求为在11月29日至7月29日期间持有CrowdStrike股票的投资者获得数额未披露的赔偿。\n诉讼援引首席执行官George Kurtz的话，他在3月5日的一次电话会议上称，该公司的软件“已经过验证、测试和认证”。\nCrowdStrike告诉BBC新闻，其对这些主张提出异议。\n一名发言人表示：“我们认为此案缺乏依据，并将积极为公司辩护。”\n与此同时，达美航空首席执行官Ed Bastian在接受商业新闻频道CNBC采访时表示，这次宕机造成的干扰使该航空公司损失5亿美元，其中包括收入损失以及向乘客支付的赔偿。\n据报道，达美航空已聘请一名知名律师，并正准备向CrowdStrike寻求赔偿。\n7月19日的错误更新导致全球850万台微软Windows电脑崩溃。这次宕机扰乱了包括航空公司、银行和医院在内的企业和服务。\nCrowdStrike在对该事件的详细审查中表示，一个旨在确保软件更新正常运行的系统中存在一个“漏洞”。\nCrowdStrike称，这一故障意味着文件中的“有问题的内容数据”未被检测到。\n该公司表示，通过改进软件测试和检查措施，包括让开发人员进行更严格审查，可以防止此类事件再次发生。（BBC）\n分享\nFacebook\nTwitter\nPinterest\n电子邮件","publish_source":"barbadostoday.bb","publish_time":"2024-08-01T19:21:22+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2469","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI突袭坦帕豪宅，以共谋与强迫劳动罪名逮捕两人","title_en":"FBI raids Tampa mansion, arresting two on conspiracy charges","summary_cn":"2025年8月27日，美国联邦调查局证实突袭了坦帕Avila高档社区一处价值逾800万美元的豪宅，该房产属于“Kingdom of God Global Church”领导人。56岁的Michelle Brannon在坦帕被捕，53岁的David Taylor在北卡罗来纳州被捕，两人被控共谋洗钱和强迫劳动。检方称他们通过身心虐待受害者索取数千万美元，十多年间筹得逾5000万美元，若罪名成立最高面临二十余年监禁及100万美元罚款。","summary_en":"On Aug. 27, 2025, the FBI confirmed it raided a mansion worth more than $8 million in Tampa's Avila neighborhood, owned by leaders of the \"Kingdom of God Global Church.\" Michelle Brannon, 56, was arrested in Tampa and David Taylor, 53, in North Carolina, both charged with conspiracy to commit money laundering and forced labor. Authorities say they abused victims physically and mentally to solicit tens of millions of dollars, raising over $50 million in a scheme lasting more than a decade. If convicted, they face over two decades in prison and up to $1 million in fines.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:52:45.626875+00:00","url":"https://baynews9.com/fl/tampa/news/2025/08/27/fbi-raids-tampa-mansion--arresting-two-on-conspiracy--forced-labor-charges","content":"FBI raids Tampa mansion, arresting two 'religious leaders' on conspiracy, forced labor charges\nBY\nSpectrum News Staff\nHillsborough County\nUPDATED 5:08 PM ET Aug. 27, 2025\nPUBLISHED 12:52 PM ET Aug. 27, 2025\nPUBLISHED 12:52 PM EDT Aug. 27, 2025\nSHARE\nTAMPA, Fla. — Federal agents raided a north Tampa mansion Wednesday morning and arrested two self-proclaimed religious leaders. One of them was being held in jail overnight.\nThe FBI confirmed they raided a mansion valued at more than $8 million in Tampa’s luxury Avila neighborhood owned by the leaders of “Kingdom of God Global Church.”\nWhat You Need To Know\nFBI raids mansion in Tampa's Avila neighborhood\nFBI confirmed they raided a mansion in Tampa’s luxury Avila neighborhood owned by the leaders of \"Kingdom of God Global Church”\nMichelle Brannon, 56, was arrested in Tampa and 53-year-old David Taylor was arrested in North Carolina. The two are charged with conspiracy to commit money laundering and forced labor\nAuthorities said the leaders are accused of physically and mentally abusing victims to solicit tens of millions of dollars.\nMichelle Brannon, 56, was arrested in Tampa and 53-year-old David Taylor was arrested in North Carolina. Brannon was being held overnight in Hillsborough County with no bond because she had no attorney present in court.\nKingdom of God Global Church is formerly known as Joshua Media Ministries. According to JMMI's website, Brannon was listed online as Taylor's spiritual daughter and executive to the ministry. But court documents refer to her as his second in command. She is accused of making sure victims followed orders from Taylor under the threat of violence and condemnation\nAccording to an indictment, Brannon was listed online as Taylor's spiritual daughter and executive to the ministry. But court documents refer to her as his second in command. She is accused of making sure victims followed orders from Taylor under the threat of violence and condemnation.\nVictims were cut off from their families, according to documents, and weren't allowed to leave the properties without permission.\nThe indictment alleges the pair forced victims to work long hours without pay at their call centers and to act as personal servants for Taylor.\nInvestigators say he also demanded those servants bring him women from ministry houses, airports and other locations. Taylor would also force those women to take Plan B contraceptives, according to authorities.\nThe suspects reportedly raised more than $50 million in a scheme that lasted more than a decade.\nBoth Taylor and Brannon are facing multiple charges, including conspiracy to commit money laundering and forced labor.\nBoth could face more than two decades in prison and up to $1 million in fines if convicted.","content_cn":"FBI突袭坦帕豪宅，以共谋和强迫劳动罪名逮捕两名“宗教领袖”\n作者\nSpectrum News Staff\n希尔斯伯勒县\n更新于美国东部时间2025年8月27日下午5:08\n发布于美国东部时间2025年8月27日中午12:52\n发布于美国东部夏令时间2025年8月27日中午12:52\n分享\n佛罗里达州坦帕——联邦特工周三上午突袭了坦帕北部的一座豪宅，并逮捕了两名自封的宗教领袖。其中一人被羁押过夜。\nFBI证实，他们突袭了坦帕高档阿维拉社区一座价值逾800万美元的豪宅，该宅属于“上帝国度全球教会”的领导人。\n你需要了解的内容\nFBI突袭坦帕阿维拉社区豪宅\nFBI证实，他们突袭了坦帕高档阿维拉社区一座属于“上帝国度全球教会”领导人的豪宅\n56岁的Michelle Brannon在坦帕被捕，53岁的David Taylor在北卡罗来纳州被捕。两人被控洗钱共谋和强迫劳动\n当局称，这些领导人被指控对受害者实施身体和精神虐待，以募集数千万美元。\n56岁的Michelle Brannon在坦帕被捕，53岁的David Taylor在北卡罗来纳州被捕。由于Brannon出庭时没有律师在场，她在希尔斯伯勒县被无保释羁押过夜。\n上帝国度全球教会原名Joshua Media Ministries。根据JMMI网站，Brannon在网上被列为Taylor的属灵女儿及该事工的管理人员。但法庭文件称她是他的二把手。她被指控以暴力和谴责相威胁，确保受害者服从Taylor的命令。\n根据起诉书，Brannon在网上被列为Taylor的属灵女儿及该事工的管理人员。但法庭文件称她是他的二把手。她被指控以暴力和谴责相威胁，确保受害者服从Taylor的命令。\n文件显示，受害者与家人断绝联系，且未经许可不得离开这些房产。\n起诉书指控两人强迫受害者在其呼叫中心长时间无偿工作，并充当Taylor的私人仆从。\n调查人员称，他还要求这些仆从从事工住所、机场及其他地点为他带来女性。当局称，Taylor还会强迫这些女性服用Plan B避孕药。\n据报道，这些嫌疑人通过一项持续十余年的计划筹集了逾5000万美元。\nTaylor和Brannon均面临多项指控，包括洗钱共谋和强迫劳动。\n若被定罪，两人均可能面临二十多年监禁及最高100万美元罚款。","publish_source":"baynews9.com","publish_time":"2025-08-27T12:52:00-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2238","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部长诺姆在布雷登顿停留期间赞扬ICE工作","title_en":"In Bradenton stop, Homeland Security Secretary touts ICE","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆在佛罗里达州萨拉索塔和布雷登顿停留，强调移民与海关执法局及国土安全官员将所谓顽固犯罪分子清除出社区的成果。诺姆称特朗普执政九个月以来已有超过48万无证移民被捕，并重申支持佛罗里达州的驱逐设施。她还回应了有关其花费2亿美元购买两架私人飞机的报道，称这些飞机是海岸警卫队用于替换老旧机型。","summary_en":"Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem visited Sarasota and Bradenton, Florida, highlighting ICE and homeland officials' work in removing what she called hardened criminals from communities. Noem said over 480,000 undocumented immigrants have been arrested in nine months under Trump, and reaffirmed support for Florida deportation facilities. She also addressed reports of $200 million spent on two private jets, saying they replace 25-year-old Coast Guard aircraft.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:38:39.337747+00:00","url":"https://baynews9.com/fl/tampa/news/2025/10/20/in-sarasota-stop--homeland-security-secretary-noem-touts-ice-efforts","content":"In Bradenton stop, Homeland Security Secretary Noem touts ICE efforts\nBY\nSpectrum News Staff\nFlorida\nUPDATED 5:23 PM ET Oct. 20, 2025\nPUBLISHED 11:49 AM ET Oct. 20, 2025\nPUBLISHED 11:49 AM EDT Oct. 20, 2025\nSHARE\nBRADENTON, Fla. — Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem was in Sarasota and Bradenton on Monday, highlighting the work of ICE and homeland officials in getting what she said are hardened criminals off the streets.\nNoem said Monday marks nine months since President Donald Trump took office, and since then more than 480,000 undocumented immigrants have been arrested.\n\"Across the country we are making communities safer so that families can thrive and they can prosper and enjoy the freedoms that this country was established to provide,\" she said.\nShe also reaffirmed support for Florida’s deportation facilities, including “Alligator Alcatraz” and “Deportation Depot.”\n“It’s been fantastic to see the partnerships that we’ve had here in Florida, in this community and throughout the entire state,” Noem said.\nThe secretary stood in front of a table full of firearms and narcotics and addressed violence against ICE agents, saying that it won’t be tolerated.\nNoem was asked about recent reports that she had spent $200 million of taxpayer money on two private jets. Noem said they are for the Coast Guard to replace 25-year-old aircrafts.\nA few days ago, a member of the House Appropriations Committee wrote a letter to Noem, claiming she didn’t have the protocol to obtain those jets. Noem said the funds were appropriated from the Big Beautiful Bill and were approved by Congress.","content_cn":"在布雷登顿停留期间，国土安全部长诺姆称赞ICE的工作\n作者\nSpectrum News工作人员\n佛罗里达州\n更新：2025年10月20日美国东部时间下午5:23\n发布：2025年10月20日美国东部时间上午11:49\n发布：2025年10月20日美国东部夏令时间上午11:49\n分享\n佛罗里达州布雷登顿——国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆周一到访萨拉索塔和布雷登顿，强调ICE和国土安全官员所做的工作，即将她所称的顽固罪犯从街头清除。\n诺姆说，周一是唐纳德·特朗普总统上任九个月纪念日，自那以来已有超过48万名无证移民被逮捕。\n“在全国各地，我们正在使社区更安全，让家庭能够蓬勃发展、实现繁荣，并享有这个国家建立时旨在提供的自由。”她说。\n她还重申支持佛罗里达州的驱逐设施，包括“鳄鱼恶魔岛”和“驱逐站”。\n诺姆说：“看到我们在佛罗里达州、在这个社区以及整个州建立的伙伴关系，真是太棒了。”\n这位部长站在一张摆满枪支和毒品的桌子前，谈及针对ICE特工的暴力行为，并表示这不会被容忍。\n诺姆被问及近期报道称她花费2亿美元纳税人资金购买两架私人飞机。诺姆称，这些飞机供海岸警卫队使用，用以替换已有25年机龄的飞机。\n几天前，众议院拨款委员会的一名成员致信诺姆，称她没有获得这些飞机所需的程序授权。诺姆表示，资金来自《美丽大法案》的拨款，并已获国会批准。","publish_source":"baynews9.com","publish_time":"2025-10-20T11:49:00-04:00"}},{"id":"news-98","ktid":5775050,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"5775050","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"Shopify 成为 OpenAI 首个电商合作伙伴，接入 ChatGPT 广告","title_en":"Shopify becomes OpenAI’s first e-commerce partner with ChatGPT Ads integration | BetaKit","summary_cn":"BetaKit 报道，OpenAI 已在 Shopify 应用商店上线 ChatGPT Ads，Shopify 商家可将店铺同步至 ChatGPT、设置广告预算并在聊天机器人中投放标注广告，目前仅限美国商家，9 月 23 日起扩展至 ChatGPT Ads 可用的国际市场。Shopify 总裁称其为 OpenAI 首个商务合作伙伴。OpenAI 同时推出赞助代理和 AI 营销工具，显示大模型正改变在线购物与电商格局。","summary_en":"BetaKit reports that OpenAI has launched ChatGPT Ads in Shopify's App Store, letting Shopify merchants sync storefronts to ChatGPT, set ad budgets, and run marked ads inside the chatbot, initially only for US merchants and expanding from Sept. 23 to international markets where ChatGPT Ads is available. Shopify's president called it OpenAI's first commerce partner. OpenAI also introduced sponsored agents and AI marketing tools, signaling how large language models are changing online shopping and e-commerce.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T13:16:09.555196+00:00","url":"https://betakit.com/shopify-becomes-openais-first-e-commerce-partner-with-chatgpt-ads-integration/","content":"Shopify becomes OpenAI’s first e-commerce partner with ChatGPT Ads integration\nBy Alex Riehl\nSeptember 18, 2026\nEmail\nShare on LinkedIn\nShare on X\nShare on Reddit\nShare on BlueSky\nIntegration allows merchants to sync storefronts and advertise directly inside ChatGPT in the US.\nSome Shopify merchants can now directly advertise in the world’s most popular AI chatbot.\nThe news: US AI giant OpenAI has launched ChatGPT Ads inside Canadian e-commerce giant Shopify’s App Store. The free-to-install integration allows Shopify merchants to sync their storefronts to ChatGPT, set ad campaigns within a budget, and feature their products in marked ads inside the chatbot.\nAt the moment, ChatGPT Ads is only available for Shopify merchants in the United States. According to OpenAI, the app will be available in international markets where ChatGPT Ads are available starting September 23. BetaKit has reached out to OpenAI to confirm if this includes Canada.\nFrom the source: ChatGPT leads the AI assistant market, and became the fastest mobile app to reach one billion monthly active users this past May, according to a June report from analytics firm Sensor Tower. While the report also says ChatGPT’s market share dipped below 50 percent for the first time earlier this year, it’s still a massive market for Shopify merchants to advertise to.\nThe context: Shopify is OpenAI’s first commerce partner, according to Shopify president Harley Finkelstein. Outside of advertising, Shopify has been working on allowing merchants to sell their products across popular AI chatbots since last year, and much of its product updates since then have been focused on bolstering the platform’s agentic commerce capabilities. Shopify has also struck similar partnerships with Google and Microsoft to increase merchant discoverability in their chatbots.\nFinal thought: Alongside the Shopify app release, OpenAI introduced sponsored agents, which let users start a conversation with a business-sponsored agent after clicking an ad in ChatGPT, and AI-powered marketing tools to ChatGPT Ads. These features are early indications of how large language models are (potentially dramatically) changing online shopping and e-commerce, and by getting in early, Shopify appears to be embracing that change.\nDisclosure: BetaKit majority owner Good Future is the family office of two former Shopify leaders, Arati Sharma and Satish Kanwar.\nFeature image courtesy Burst. Photo by Avelino Calvary Martinez.\nAI\nBriefs\nOntario\nOttawa\nRetail\nEmail\nShare on LinkedIn\nShare on X\nShare on Reddit\nShare on BlueSky\n0 replies on “Shopify becomes OpenAI’s first e-commerce partner with ChatGPT Ads integration”\nLatest Posts\nHow founders are rethinking capital in the AI era\nIsabelle Kirkwood\nSeptember 24, 2026\nWoveo partners with BDC on business microlending program\nJesse Cole\nSeptember 23, 2026\nFemtech Connect conference puts femtech funding under the microscope\nJesse Cole\nSeptember 23, 2026","content_cn":"Shopify通过整合ChatGPT Ads成为OpenAI首个电子商务合作伙伴\n作者：Alex Riehl\n2026年9月18日\n电子邮件\n在LinkedIn上分享\n在X上分享\n在Reddit上分享\n在BlueSky上分享\n该整合允许商家在美国同步店铺，并直接在ChatGPT内投放广告。\n一些Shopify商家现在可以直接在全球最受欢迎的AI聊天机器人中投放广告。\n新闻：美国AI巨头OpenAI已在加拿大电子商务巨头Shopify的应用商店中推出ChatGPT Ads。这一可免费安装的整合工具允许Shopify商家将店铺同步至ChatGPT，在预算范围内设置广告活动，并在聊天机器人内以标注广告的形式展示其产品。\n目前，ChatGPT Ads仅向美国的Shopify商家提供。OpenAI表示，自9月23日起，该应用将在提供ChatGPT Ads的国际市场上线。BetaKit已联系OpenAI，以确认这是否包括加拿大。\n来源信息：根据分析公司Sensor Tower在6月发布的一份报告，ChatGPT引领AI助手市场，并在今年5月成为达到每月10亿活跃用户速度最快的移动应用。报告还称，ChatGPT的市场份额在今年早些时候首次跌破50%，但对Shopify商家而言，这仍是一个规模巨大的广告市场。\n背景：据Shopify总裁Harley Finkelstein称，Shopify是OpenAI的首个商业合作伙伴。除广告业务外，Shopify自去年以来一直在努力让商家能够通过热门AI聊天机器人销售产品，此后的许多产品更新都专注于强化平台的代理式商务能力。Shopify还与Google和Microsoft达成了类似合作，以提高商家在它们聊天机器人中的可发现性。\n最后想法：在发布Shopify应用的同时，OpenAI推出了赞助代理，用户点击ChatGPT中的广告后，可以与由企业赞助的代理开始对话；同时还为ChatGPT Ads推出了AI驱动的营销工具。这些功能初步显示，大型语言模型正在（可能是大幅）改变在线购物和电子商务，而Shopify通过抢先布局，似乎正在拥抱这一变化。\n披露：BetaKit的大股东Good Future是两位前Shopify领导者Arati Sharma和Satish Kanwar的家族办公室。\n特色图片由Burst提供。照片由Avelino Calvary Martinez拍摄。\n人工智能\n简报\n安大略省\n渥太华\n零售\n电子邮件\n在LinkedIn上分享\n在X上分享\n在Reddit上分享\n在BlueSky上分享\n“Shopify通过整合ChatGPT Ads成为OpenAI首个电子商务合作伙伴”下有0条回复\n最新文章\n创始人在AI时代如何重新思考资本\nIsabelle Kirkwood\n2026年9月24日\nWoveo与BDC合作开展商业小额贷款项目\nJesse Cole\n2026年9月23日\nFemtech Connect大会深入审视女性科技融资\nJesse Cole\n2026年9月23日","publish_source":"betakit.com","publish_time":"2026-09-18T16:51:56+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2972","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国国土安全部与USCIS面临人员裁减","title_en":"DHS and USCIS Facing Staffing Cuts - International Legal and Business Services Group","summary_cn":"文章报道美国国土安全部（DHS）与USCIS正鼓励员工辞职或退休，以配合特朗普政府缩减联邦雇员规模的计划。2025年4月7日发给DHS员工的邮件提供延迟辞职、提前退休或最高2.5万美元自愿离职补偿三种选项。DHS发言人称此举旨在让机构重新聚焦边境安全与移民执法。USCIS可能有多达2万名员工被裁，或将加剧美国移民系统积压与审理延误。","summary_en":"The article reports that the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and USCIS are encouraging staff to resign or retire as part of the Trump administration's effort to shrink the federal workforce. An April 7, 2025 email offered DHS employees deferred resignation, early retirement, or a voluntary separation payment of up to $25,000. A DHS spokesperson said the move aims to refocus the agency on border security and immigration enforcement. Up to 20,000 USCIS employees could be laid off, potentially worsening immigration backlogs and processing delays.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:52:20.869083+00:00","url":"https://bizlegalservices.com/2025/04/15/dhs-and-uscis-facing-staffing-cuts","content":"Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS) staff are being encouraged to resign or retire amid a new wave of staffing cuts. These cutbacks, announced in an email to DHS staff on April 7, 2025, marks the latest effort by the Trump administration to reduce the size of the federal workforce. This decision marks a sharp turn in the Trump administration’s efforts to reduce the size of federal agencies, as Homeland Security and ICE had seemingly avoided the widespread layoffs seen in other agencies.\nThe email, titled “Reshaping the DHS Workforce,” offered DHS staff three options for leaving their current roles: a deferred resignation, early retirement, or a voluntary separation payment. The latter offers employees a lump-sum payment of up to twenty-five thousand dollars.\nDHS spokesperson Tricia McLaughlin explained the DHS and USCIS staffing cuts are the result of a plan to help the organization refocus its efforts on border security and immigration enforcement. Downsizing, according to Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi Noem, allows the department to fulfill the immigration enforcement efforts of the Trump administration while still supporting its’ employees.\nUSCIS staff received a similar email. Up to 20,000 employees from their agency alone could get laid off. This action will increase the backlog in the U.S. immigration system, increasing wait times and delays on document processing.\nIt’s currently unclear whether mandatory DHS and USCIS staffing cuts will be made if not enough employees accept one of the options.\nSince the start of his second term, President Trump has made numerous efforts to reduce the size and scale of federal agencies and their workforce. This was mainly to reduce unnecessary spending, a key promise of Trump’s re-election campaign. However, the first wave of layoffs faced legal challenges from resistant employees, some upheld by the courts. Providing compensation could be a more indirect way of getting federal staff.\nAs always, ILBSG actively monitors ongoing U.S. immigration news. If you have questions about any U.S. immigration related issue, contact us. Working with an experienced attorney ensures you get the right advice based on the most recent laws. In an ever-evolving immigration policy landscape, it’s particularly critical.\ndhs\nImmigration backlog\nU.S. immigration backlog\nUSCIS\nUSCIS backlog\nPrevNext","content_cn":"国土安全部（DHS）和美国公民及移民服务局（USCIS）的工作人员被鼓励辞职或退休，此时正值新一轮裁员。此次裁员措施于2025年4月7日通过发给国土安全部员工的一封电子邮件宣布，标志着特朗普政府削减联邦 workforce规模的最新举措。这一决定标志着特朗普政府削减联邦机构规模努力的急剧转变，因为国土安全部和移民及海关执法局（ICE）似乎避开了其他机构所经历的大范围裁员。\n这封标题为“重塑国土安全部 workforce”的电子邮件向国土安全部员工提供了三种离开当前职位的选择：延期辞职、提前退休或自愿离职补偿。后者向员工提供最高两万五千美元的一次性付款。\n国土安全部发言人特里西娅·麦克劳林解释说，国土安全部和美国公民及移民服务局的裁员是一个帮助该机构重新聚焦边境安全和移民执法工作的计划的一部分。国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆表示，缩编使该部门能够落实特朗普政府的移民执法工作，同时继续支持其员工。\n美国公民及移民服务局的工作人员也收到了一封类似的电子邮件。仅该机构就可能有多达20,000名员工被裁。这一行动将增加美国移民系统的积压，延长等待时间并拖延文件处理。\n目前尚不清楚，如果没有足够多的员工接受其中一个选项，是否会实施强制性的国土安全部和美国公民及移民服务局裁员。\n自第二任期开始以来，特朗普总统已多次努力缩减联邦机构及其 workforce的规模和范围。这主要是为了减少不必要的支出，这是特朗普竞选连任时的一项重要承诺。然而，第一轮裁员遭到了不愿离职员工的法律挑战，其中一些挑战得到法院支持。提供补偿可能是一种更间接地让联邦工作人员离职的方式。\n一如既往，ILBSG积极监控美国移民新闻的最新动态。如果你对任何与美国移民相关的问题有疑问，请联系我们。与经验丰富的律师合作，可以确保你根据最新法律获得正确建议。在不断变化的移民政策环境中，这一点尤其重要。\ndhs\n移民积压\n美国移民积压\nUSCIS\nUSCIS积压\n上一篇\n下一篇","publish_source":"bizlegalservices.com","publish_time":"2025-04-15T16:28:03+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1303","ktid":1056630,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056630","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"RSAC 2026：IBM聚焦Q-Day与后量子就绪","title_en":"RSAC 2026: IBM Sets Its Sights on Q-Day and Post-Quantum Readiness","summary_cn":"在RSAC 2026上，IBM技术副总裁Suja Viswesan表示量子计算威胁已非理论，Q-Day不可避免，组织应持续适应而非等待单一期限，强调“加密敏捷性”。她指出监管压力正加速紧迫感，证书轮换周期可能缩短至47天。首要步骤是梳理加密资产实现可见性，再引入代理层等控制措施。她还提到AI驱动的非人类身份扩大攻击面，并建议中小企业向供应商追问量子安全路线图。","summary_en":"At RSAC 2026, IBM vice president of technology Suja Viswesan said the quantum threat is no longer theoretical and Q-Day is inevitable, arguing organizations must adapt continuously rather than wait for a single deadline, stressing 'crypto-agility.' She noted regulatory pressure is accelerating urgency, with certificate rotation cycles potentially shrinking to 47 days. The first step is mapping cryptographic assets for visibility, then introducing controls such as proxy layers. She also cited AI-driven nonhuman identities expanding the attack surface and advised smaller firms to ask vendors about quantum-safe roadmaps.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T12:51:22.442172+00:00","url":"https://biztechmagazine.com/article/2026/03/rsac-2026-ibm-sets-its-sights-q-day-and-post-quantum-readiness","content":"Home»Security\nMar\n26\n2026\nSecurity\nRSAC 2026: IBM Sets Its Sights on Q-Day and Post-Quantum Readiness\nIBM’s Suja Viswesan explains why post-quantum cryptography is a continuous journey, not a single deadline. And IBM’s RSAC discussions show why urgency is accelerating.\nby Joe Kuehne\nJoe Kuehne is an Associate Editorial Director at BizTech magazine.\nListen\nPause\nThe idea of Q-Day — the theoretical moment when quantum computers will be able to break modern cryptography — has long hovered at the edge of cybersecurity discussions. But according to Suja Viswesan, IBM’s vice president of technology, that moment is no longer theoretical. It’s inevitable, and many organizations are already behind.\n“Quantum compute is coming,” Viswesan said in a conversation at RSAC 2026. “We were talking about it for the last two years. What happened last year was more regulators, and everybody like, ‘OK, this is not some far-fetched dream. It’s coming in a few years.’”\nThat uncertainty is precisely what makes the threat so challenging. While estimates often place Q-Day sometime between 2030 and 2033, Viswesan emphasized that waiting for a precise date is the wrong approach. The shift underway isn’t about a single breaking point; it’s about continuous adaptation.\n“This is not a Y2K problem that you fix after Q-day,” she explained. “It’s continuous work. ‘Crypto-agility’ is the word.”\nClick the banner below for deeper insight into modern cyber resilience.\nFrom Theory to Urgency\nWhat changed over the past year, Viswesan noted, is not the science, but the response. Regulators, financial institutions and healthcare organizations are now treating quantum risk as immediate: “Customers are coming to us and saying, ‘I don’t know what to do. How do I get ready?’”\nRegulatory pressure is accelerating that urgency. For example, certificate rotation cycles — once measured in months — are expected to shrink dramatically. By the end of the decade, organizations may need to rotate cryptographic certificates every 47 days, forcing a shift toward automation and visibility.\nRSAC 2026 also reflected this growing momentum. Across sessions and vendor discussions, the focus shifted from awareness to execution, particularly around crypto-agility and quantum-safe architectures.\nIndustry leaders at the event emphasized practical steps such as gaining visibility into cryptographic assets, implementing agile encryption frameworks and aligning with emerging post-quantum standards from the National Institute of Standards and Technology.\nWATCH: Check out the cybersecurity trends to watch in 2026.\nThe “‘Harvest Now, Decrypt Later'” Problem\nOne of the most pressing concerns discussed both by IBM and across RSAC sessions is the “harvest now, decrypt later” strategy. Attackers can capture encrypted data today and decrypt it once quantum capabilities mature.\nThis aligns with academic research showing that widely used cryptosystems such as RSA and elliptic curve cryptography could eventually be broken by Shor’s algorithm, which enables efficient factorization on quantum machines.\nWhile today’s quantum hardware still faces limitations — including instability and scale challenges — researchers agree that the trajectory is clear.\nThat reality is why organizations must act before Q-Day arrives.\nDIVE DEEPER: What your cybersecurity leaders need to know about quantum readiness.\nVisibility Before Protection\nFor Viswesan, the first step isn’t replacing algorithms — it’s understanding where cryptography exists in the first place.\n“I cannot fix things that I don’t know,” she said. “Visibility is the most important thing.”\nIBM’s approach focuses on mapping cryptographic assets — including certificates, secrets and application programming interface keys — across environments. Once identified, organizations can begin prioritizing risk and introducing controls such as proxy layers to “buy time” before full post-quantum upgrades are available.\nThis mirrors broader industry guidance. RSAC discussions repeatedly highlighted encryption visibility and governance as foundational capabilities for quantum readiness.\nI cannot fix things that I don’t know. Visibility is the most important thing.”\nSuja Viswesan\nVice President of Technology, IBM\nThe Role of AI and Nonhuman Identities\nComplicating the challenge is the rise of AI-driven systems and agentic identities — nonhuman actors that interact with systems autonomously.\n“The nonhuman identity, part of it is not helping this cause, because with everything that we were doing before, you could have biometrics and multifactor authentication. What do you do with agents?” Viswesan asked.\n“Now, it's nondeterministic. I don’t know what it’s going to do, because each agent has their own agency to go do something on your behalf.”\nThese systems expand the attack surface significantly. Secrets, certificates and embedded credentials — once static — are now being accessed and exploited at machine speed. AI-driven attackers can identify vulnerabilities far faster than human adversaries.\nEmerging research reinforces this concern, proposing “quantumsecure by construction” architectures that embed post-quantum protections directly into AI systems rather than retrofitting them later.\nWATCH: Learn how to secure agentic artificial intelligence.\nWhat Small Businesses Should Do\nWhile much of the conversation focuses on large enterprises, Viswesan stressed that smaller organizations are not exempt.\nHer advice was straightforward: Rely on vendors, but ask the right questions.\n“Are you quantum safe? If not, what is your roadmap?” she said.\nThis shift mirrors earlier security transitions, but with higher stakes. Organizations that delay may face not only higher costs but also competitive disadvantage.\n“The longer they wait, the bigger the problem is going to be,” she warned.\nasbe/Getty Images\nMore On\nAgentic AI\nAI Strategy\nData protection\nIdentity Management\nRelated Articles\nSecurity\nHow Banks Should Prioritize Cybersecurity Spending\nSecurity\nComprehensive Security Platforms Move Strategic Defense Forward\nSecurity\nWhy Financial Institutions Are Turning to SOC as a Service\nClose\nNew Research from CDW Explores AI and Cybersecurity\nLearn how AI is helping IT teams manage risk and improve resilience.\nGet the Report\nLatest Articles\nAI Production Readiness: Build the Foundation Before You Scale\nHow ManpowerGroup and Other Companies Measure AI’s ROI\nThe Minnesota Wild Score Big With a Phone and Contact Center Upgrade\nHow Banks Should Prioritize Cybersecurity Spending\nArtificial Intelligence\nAI Production Readiness: Build the Foundation Before You Scale\nArtificial Intelligence\nHow ManpowerGroup and Other Companies Measure AI’s ROI\nTrending Now\nHow Do You Choose Between CAT 6, CAT 7 and CAT 8 Cables?","content_cn":"首页»安全\n2026年\n3月\n26日\n安全\nRSAC 2026：IBM将目光投向Q-Day与后量子就绪\nIBM的苏佳·维斯韦桑（Suja Viswesan）解释了为什么后量子密码学是一段持续的旅程，而非一个单一的截止日期。IBM在RSAC上的讨论也表明，为何紧迫性正在加速。\n作者：乔·库内（Joe Kuehne）\n乔·库内是BizTech杂志的副编辑总监。\n收听\n暂停\nQ-Day——即量子计算机能够破解现代密码学的理论时刻——这一概念长期以来一直徘徊在网络安全讨论的边缘。但据IBM技术副总裁苏佳·维斯韦桑所言，那个时刻已不再是理论。它不可避免，而许多组织已经落后了。\n“量子计算正在到来，”维斯韦桑在RSAC 2026的一次对话中表示。“过去两年我们一直在谈论它。去年发生的变化是，更多的监管机构，以及所有人都说，‘好吧，这不是什么遥不可及的梦想。它几年内就会到来。’”\n正是这种不确定性，使得这一威胁如此具有挑战性。虽然估计通常将Q-Day定在2030年至2033年之间的某个时候，但维斯韦桑强调，等待一个精确的日期是错误的做法。正在发生的转变并非关乎某个单一的临界点，而是关乎持续的适应。\n“这不是一个在Q-Day之后才去修复的千年虫问题，”她解释道。“这是持续的工作。‘密码敏捷性’（crypto-agility）才是关键词。”\n点击下方横幅，深入了解现代网络韧性。\n从理论到紧迫性\n维斯韦桑指出，过去一年改变的不是科学，而是应对方式。监管机构、金融机构和医疗机构如今都将量子风险视为迫在眉睫的问题：“客户来找我们说，‘我不知道该怎么办。我该如何做好准备？’”\n监管压力正在加速这种紧迫性。例如，证书轮换周期——曾经以月为单位——预计将大幅缩短。到本十年末，组织可能需要每47天轮换一次密码证书，从而迫使它们转向自动化和可视化。\nRSAC 2026也反映了这种日益增长的势头。在各场会议和厂商讨论中，焦点已从意识转向执行，尤其是围绕密码敏捷性和量子安全架构。\n活动中的行业领袖强调了诸如了解密码资产可见性、实施敏捷加密框架以及与美国国家标准与技术研究院（NIST）新兴的后量子标准保持一致等实际步骤。\n观看：了解2026年值得关注的那些网络安全趋势。\n“先收集，后解密”问题\nIBM以及RSAC各场会议讨论的最紧迫关切之一，是“先收集，后解密”策略。攻击者可以在今天捕获加密数据，待量子能力成熟后再将其解密。\n这与学术研究一致，研究表明，诸如RSA和椭圆曲线密码学等广泛使用的密码系统，最终可能被Shor算法破解，该算法能够在量子机器上实现高效因式分解。\n尽管当今的量子硬件仍面临局限——包括不稳定性和规模挑战——但研究人员一致认为，其发展轨迹是明确的。\n正是这一现实，使得组织必须在Q-Day到来之前采取行动。\n深入探究：你的网络安全领导者需要了解哪些关于量子就绪的知识。\n先可见，后防护\n对维斯韦桑而言，第一步不是替换算法——而是首先了解密码学存在于何处。\n“我无法修复我不知道的东西，”她说。“可见性是最重要的。”\nIBM的方法侧重于绘制跨环境的密码资产图谱——包括证书、密钥和应用程序编程接口密钥。一旦识别出来，组织就可以开始对风险进行优先级排序，并引入诸如代理层之类的控制措施，以便在全面的后量子升级可用之前“争取时间”。\n这与更广泛的行业指导一致。RSAC的讨论一再强调，加密可见性和治理是量子就绪的基础能力。\n我无法修复我不知道的东西。可见性是最重要的。”\n苏佳·维斯韦桑\nIBM技术副总裁\nAI与非人类身份的角色\n使挑战更加复杂的是AI驱动系统和代理身份——即自主与系统交互的非人类行为者——的兴起。\n“非人类身份，其中一部分对此事并无帮助，因为随着每一……\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"biztechmagazine.com","publish_time":"2026-03-26T15:44:34+00:00"}},{"id":"news-239","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026：应对智能体时代身份管理新挑战","title_en":"CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026: Confronting the New Challenges of Identity in the Agentic Era","summary_cn":"在CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026大会上，CrowdStrike推出Agentic身份提供商（IdP），旨在将AI智能体确立为可信身份并实现持续授权。公司总裁Michael Sentonas指出，多数智能体拥有过度权限并继承人类权限，部署速度快于治理速度。该方案通过短期令牌按任务授予访问权限，并已与Okta、Microsoft Entra集成，未来将扩展至GitHub、Salesforce及ServiceNow、Jira等系统。","summary_en":"At CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026, CrowdStrike introduced its Agentic Identity Provider (IdP), designed to establish AI agents as trusted identities and enable continuous authorization. President Michael Sentonas noted that most agents are overprivileged and inherit human permissions, and are deployed faster than they can be governed. The solution issues short-lived, task-based tokens and integrates with Okta and Microsoft Entra, with planned expansion to GitHub, Salesforce, ServiceNow and Jira.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:36:28.078283+00:00","url":"https://biztechmagazine.com/article/2026/09/crowdstrike-falcon-2026-confronting-new-challenges-identity-agentic-era","content":"Home»Security\nSep\n09\n2026\nSecurity\nCrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026: Confronting the New Challenges of Identity in the Agentic Era\nWith artificial intelligence agents being created and deployed at the enterprise level, managing identities and access becomes more complex and increasingly critical to cybersecurity.\nby Joe Kuehne\nJoe Kuehne is an Associate Editorial Director at BizTech magazine.\nListen\nPause\nArtificial intelligence is changing the needs of organizations to restrict and control access within their environments because of an ever-increasing number of identities, both human and nonhuman. AI agents are adding new wrinkles to the challenge of identity, and they’re forcing organizations to seek out new tools for assistance.\nAt last week’s CrowdStrike Fal.Con, CrowdStrike introduced its Agentic Identity Provider (IdP). As the cybersecurity provider noted in a Sept. 2 press release, “Identity is the front line of modern attacks, and AI agents accelerate the threat at scale. They execute code, access systems, and move data with real credentials, at machine speed, with no one watching. Before they can be continuously authorized, they must first be established as trusted identities, something traditional identity providers were never built to do.”\nSpeaking at a Sept. 3 keynote session, CrowdStrike President Michael Sentonas told attendees, “Every agent has an identity, and in most cases, it’s an overprivileged identity. And in too many cases, it inherits the human permissions, and you are all deploying them faster than you can govern them.”\nSentonas emphasized the importance of asking who or what created each agent in your environment. But that’s just the tip of the iceberg in establishing identity and authorizing access. “Who is it shared with? What third-party systems can it access? What permissions does it have, and where can it go? The challenge isn’t granting access to that agent once; it’s knowing what it should be allowed to do at every moment it’s running and every step. And we have to make a big change here. Trust cannot stop at authentication.”\nClick the banner below to read the recent CDW Cybersecurity Research Report.\nHow Does CrowdStrike Agentic IdP Establish Continuous Identity?\nAccording to the company’s press release, “Agentic IdP establishes every agent as a trusted identity, brokers only the access needed for as long as needed and ties every action back to the human or system behind it. This is the foundation that makes continuous identity possible.”\n“Securing AI agents demands solutions built for how they operate,” said Scott Kriz, general manager of continuous identity at CrowdStrike. “Continuous Identity modernized identity security for the agentic era, but you cannot continuously authorize an identity you were never able to establish, and traditional identity providers break the moment an agent acts on its own. Agentic IdP is the identity provider for AI agents.”\n“A lot of the concepts that exist around identity are different for agents because they operate at such machine speed,” said Kriz, speaking with BizTech during CrowdStrike Fal.Con. “They don’t have boundaries, and they often inherit the ability to get to things that their creators granted them.”\nDISCOVER: Find out how mature your security posture is with a self-assessment.\nAgentic Identity and Access Should Be Task-Based\nAs Sentonas explained in his keynote, “We now have the ability to give people one-time access, but importantly, to remove it and give access on demand, to give access when they need it, access by role type, access to carry out a specific task and to make sure that you remove all standing privilege.”\nKriz pointed out some key partnerships in refining identity-based access. “We’ve integrated with identity providers such as Okta and Microsoft Entra on giving the ability for certain users to get access to infrastructure. Being able to rightsize that access to a specific role based on business context is really important for humans.”\nBut while it’s necessary to restrict access for human users, it’s becoming even more important to do the same for nonhuman identities. “What happens when the agent can get to your AWS environment?” Kriz asked. CrowdStrike has developed a way to issue tokens — for humans and agents alike — for specific tasks based on business context.\nKriz said these short-lived tokens have already been in use for a while under a part of the Falcon platform called Falcon Privileged Access. “It started out as really just access to Entra, and now we’re expanding it. So, in the next quarter, we’ll be adding GitHub. We’ll be adding Salesforce. We’ll be adding context from ticketing systems like ServiceNow and Jira,” which, he said, would give companies the ability to justify or deny access as soon as a ticket closes, depending on the context.\nWe have to make a big change here. Trust cannot stop at authentication.”\nMichael Sentonas\nPresident, CrowdStrike\nEstablishing Identity Becomes More Complicated With Shadow AI\nAs organizations encourage their employees to learn AI skills and spin up their own agents, the occurrence of shadow AI has increased, and more vulnerabilities have opened up.\nKriz said he thinks business leaders initially saw agentic AI as a productivity tool, so they’ve been pushing employees to use it before thinking through the important issues of identity, access and governance. “But then you start seeing things that could be existential threats to a company,” Kriz said. “You have to know the identities to be able to manage them, right? And Guardian was the clear first step in doing that.”\nAnd with Agentic IdP, he said, “we can now look at what’s going on. We can catalog it. We can identify it. We can actually prevent activity happening off machines, so you don’t give agents access to things on your machine.”\nThe next step is securing the actions being taken by agents, Kriz noted: “What happens off the machine? What happens when they’re trying to get to these other resources?” Agentic IdP can establish a clear identity thread throughout.\n“I think identity and security have been at odds for a long time,” he added. “Identity is all about reducing friction: Let people get in so they can do their jobs. And security is about stopping people from doing things. And those things have been converging organically.”\nPhotography by Joe Kuehne\nMore On\nArtificial Intelligence\nAgentic AI\nAI Security\nEndpoint Security\nIdentity Management\nRisk Assessment\nThreat Prevention\nRelated Articles\nArtificial Intelligence\nAI Production Readiness: Build the Foundation Before You Scale\nArtificial Intelligence\nHow ManpowerGroup and Other Companies Measure AI’s ROI\nSecurity\nHow Banks Should Prioritize Cybersecurity Spending\nClose\nNew Research from CDW Explores AI and Cybersecurity\nLearn how AI is helping IT teams manage risk and improve resilience.\nGet the Report\nLatest Articles\nAI Production Readiness: Build the Foundation Before You Scale\nHow ManpowerGroup and Other Companies Measure AI’s ROI\nThe Minnesota Wild Score Big With a Phone and Contact Center Upgrade\nHow Banks Should Prioritize Cybersecurity Spending\nArtificial Intelligence\nAI Production Readiness: Build the Foundation Before You Scale\nArtificial Intelligence\nHow ManpowerGroup and Other Companies Measure AI’s ROI\nTrending Now\nHow Do You Choose Between CAT 6, CAT 7 and CAT 8 Cables?","content_cn":"首页»安全\n9月\n09\n2026\n安全\nCrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026：直面智能体时代身份管理的新挑战\n随着人工智能智能体在企业层面被创建和部署，管理身份与访问权限变得更加复杂，对网络安全也愈发关键。\n作者：Joe Kuehne\nJoe Kuehne 是 BizTech 杂志的副编辑总监。\n收听\n暂停\n人工智能正在改变组织限制和控制其环境内访问权限的需求，因为身份数量——无论是人类还是非人类——都在不断增加。AI 智能体为身份挑战增添了新的难题，并迫使组织寻求新的工具来协助应对。\n在上周举行的 CrowdStrike Fal.Con 大会上，CrowdStrike 推出了其智能体身份提供商（IdP）。正如这家网络安全提供商在 9 月 2 日的一份新闻稿中所指出的：“身份是现代攻击的前线，而 AI 智能体以规模化方式加速了这一威胁。它们使用真实凭证、以机器速度执行代码、访问系统并移动数据，且无人看管。在它们能够被持续授权之前，必须先被确立为可信身份，而传统身份提供商从未为此而构建。”\n在 9 月 3 日的一场主题演讲中，CrowdStrike 总裁 Michael Sentonas 对与会者表示：“每个智能体都有一个身份，而且在大多数情况下，它是一个权限过高的身份。在太多情况下，它继承了人类的权限，而你们部署它们的速度超过了你们治理它们的速度。”\nSentonas 强调了询问环境中每个智能体由谁或由什么创建的重要性。但这只是确立身份和授权访问的冰山一角。“它与谁共享？它可以访问哪些第三方系统？它拥有什么权限，又能去往哪里？挑战不在于一次性授予该智能体访问权限；而在于知道它在运行的每一刻、每一步应该被允许做什么。我们必须在这里做出重大改变。信任不能止步于身份验证。”\n点击下方横幅，阅读最新的 CDW 网络安全研究报告。\nCrowdStrike 智能体 IdP 如何建立持续身份？\n根据该公司的新闻稿，“智能体 IdP 将每个智能体确立为可信身份，仅在所需时间内代理所需的访问权限，并将每个操作追溯至其背后的人类或系统。这是使持续身份成为可能的基础。”\n“保护 AI 智能体需要为其运作方式量身打造的解决方案，”CrowdStrike 持续身份业务总经理 Scott Kriz 表示。“持续身份为智能体时代实现了身份安全的现代化，但你无法持续授权一个你从未能够确立的身份，而传统身份提供商在智能体自主行动的那一刻就会失效。智能体 IdP 是面向 AI 智能体的身份提供商。”\n“围绕身份的许多概念对智能体而言是不同的，因为它们以如此之快的机器速度运作，”Kriz 在 CrowdStrike Fal.Con 期间接受 BizTech 采访时表示。“它们没有边界，而且它们往往继承了其创建者授予它们的访问能力。”\n探索：通过自我评估了解你的安全态势有多成熟。\n智能体身份与访问应基于任务\n正如 Sentonas 在其主题演讲中所解释的：“我们现在有能力为人们提供一次性访问权限，但更重要的是，能够移除它并按需授予访问权限，在他们需要时授予访问权限，按角色类型授予访问权限，为执行特定任务授予访问权限，并确保移除所有常设特权。”\nKriz 指出了在完善基于身份的访问方面的一些关键合作伙伴关系。“我们已与 Okta 和 Microsoft Entra 等身份提供商集成，使某些用户能够获得对基础设施的访问权限。能够根据业务情境将访问权限合理调整到特定角色，对人类而言非常重要。”\n但是，尽管限制人类用户的访问权限是必要的，对非人类身份做同样的事情正变得更加重要。“当智能体能够进入你的 AWS 环境时会发生什么？”Kriz 问道。CrowdStrike 已开发出一种方法，可根据业务情境为特定任务签发令牌——无论对人类还是智能体都是如此。\nKriz 表示，这些短期令牌已经在 Falcon 平台中一个名为 Falcon Privileged Access 的部分下使用了一段时间。“它最初真的只是……\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"biztechmagazine.com","publish_time":"2026-09-09T17:11:30+00:00"}},{"id":"news-254","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026：CrowdStrike发布Falcon Guardian与SafeMind，聚焦AI检测与响应","title_en":"CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026: CrowdStrike Announces Falcon Guardian and Safe Mind for AIDR","summary_cn":"在CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026大会上，CEO George Kurtz宣布推出Falcon Guardian，为AI代理提供AI检测与响应（AIDR）能力，可发现并映射企业内“影子AI”代理，实现运行时可见性。同时，CrowdStrike与NVIDIA合作推出SafeMind，称其为面向防御者的首个代理式系统，基于NVIDIA Nemotron构建。Kurtz引用2026全球威胁报告称AI驱动攻击增加89%。","summary_en":"At CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026, CEO George Kurtz announced Falcon Guardian, delivering AI detection and response (AIDR) to discover and map shadow AI agents across endpoints with runtime visibility. CrowdStrike also unveiled SafeMind, described as the first agentic system for defenders, built with NVIDIA Nemotron in partnership with NVIDIA. Kurtz cited the 2026 Global Threat Report noting an 89% increase in AI-enabled adversary attacks.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T05:45:40.039333+00:00","url":"https://biztechmagazine.com/article/2026/09/crowdstrike-falcon-2026-crowdstrike-announces-falcon-guardian-and-safe-mind-aidr","content":"Home»Security\nSep\n04\n2026\nSecurity\nCrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026: CrowdStrike Announces Falcon Guardian and Safe Mind for AIDR\nWith the rapid proliferation of agentic artificial intelligence, businesses need solutions that can detect and respond to threats at machine speed.\nby Joe Kuehne\nJoe Kuehne is an Associate Editorial Director at BizTech magazine.\nListen\nPause\nArtificial intelligence agents are being spun up for every imaginable use case, but not every agent is developed to deliver greater efficiency and productivity. Malicious actors are leveraging AI for faster attack methods, and many organizations are discovering they aren’t adequately prepared to defend themselves.\nAccording to the CrowdStrike 2026 Global Threat Report, the last year has seen an 89% increase in attacks by AI-enabled adversaries. Recent research by CDW also indicates high rates of AI-fueled attacks: 43% of respondents to the company’s survey said their organization had experienced phishing attacks either enhanced or generated by AI, while 37% reported having been hit by AI-powered malware in the past year.\nAt this week’s CrowdStrike Fal.Con, the theme was “Securing the AI Revolution.” CrowdStrike CEO George Kurtz presented the opening keynote session with a comprehensive consideration of the ways in which agentic AI is reshaping cybersecurity. Attackers are using agents to uncover and exploit vulnerabilities, but as Kurtz said, “No one has built AI for the defender.” Until now.\nClick the banner below to read the recent CDW Cybersecurity Research Report.\nAI Demands Its Own Form of Detection and Response\n“Today, AI is the new battleground,” Kurtz said in the at the outset of the event, noting that every major period of growth in computing brings about an expansion of the attack landscape. “We’ve been there for some of the most consequential attack surface changes in the world, and the AI agent is the next one.”\nTo palpable excitement, Kurtz announced the launch of Falcon Guardian, designed to deliver AI detection and response (AIDR) to help organizations “not only understand their risk, understand what’s running, but more importantly, accelerate AI adoption in your own organizations.”\n“CrowdStrike pioneered EDR by making the endpoint the control point for stopping attacks. AI demands the same approach,” Kurtz said in a press release the same day. “AI hasn’t changed the attack, it has changed its speed. Governance alone can’t stop an agent already in motion. Falcon Guardian turns policy into protection, stopping threats where AI agents execute and before they can cause harm.”\nDISCOVER: Find out how mature your security posture is with a self-assessment.\nGuardian Offers Help in Identifying and Securing Shadow AI\nOne of the greatest cybersecurity challenges arising from the surge in agentic AI is the lack of visibility. As companies encourage their employees to learn about, leverage and deploy agents of their own creation, they aren’t always aware of what’s in their ecosystem.\nKurtz presented a video introducing Falcon Guardian, which explained that many organizations don’t know where their own AI agents are running, who deployed them or what risks they might introduce. “Guardian changes that. It starts with discovery. Guardian maps your entire AI agent fleet, known as shadow AI, across every endpoint,” he said.\nIn a separate keynote, CrowdStrike President Michael Sentonas explained why Guardian will be so valuable: “Once AI becomes part of the enterprise, visibility is no longer enough. You need to know what’s running, what it can access, what it is doing, where to draw the line. That is Guardian.”\n“It gives you runtime visibility across the entire AI estate,” Sentonas said. “What your agents are doing, what they’re accessing, what actions they’re taking, whether you know about it or not, and where you need to step in.”\nOnce AI becomes part of the enterprise, visibility is no longer enough.”\nMichael Sentonas\nPresident, CrowdStrike\nCrowdStrike Introduces SafeMind for Greater AI Security\nKurtz continued to highlight CrowdStrike’s new innovations with an offering developed through a partnership with NVIDIA.\n“Together with NVIDIA, we built cybersecurity’s first complete agentic system for cybersecurity, including the first frontier models and harnesses purpose-built for defenders,” he announced. According to an accompanying press release, CrowdStrike SafeMind is the first agentic system for defenders, and it was built with NVIDIA Nemotron.\nKurtz presented SafeMind at the event alongside Jensen Huang, president and CEO of NVIDIA. “Our AI researchers love working with yours,” Huang told Kurtz. “Together with our domain expertise — your decade and a half of security data that we can train on — we can create Nemotron, take a frontier model and make it essentially a super AGI that is incredibly good at cybersecurity. And then, you put it into a system called SafeMind, with red-teaming, blue-teaming, the two adversarially working against each other in a digital twin of NVIDIA and testing it against that. I mean, that’s completely brilliant.”\nHuang said he thinks we need SafeMind everywhere. “We need it obviously inside our companies. We need it in the cloud. We’re going to need it at the edge. We’re going to need it at the distributed edge.”\nHe said the basic framework of SafeMind applies to robotics, edge computing, enterprise computing and more. “In every single one of these systems, we could create something like SafeMind. We could use the SafeMind framework and create essentially a cybersecurity agent that runs alongside the AI model itself.”\nSentonas summed up the potential of an innovation such as SafeMind by saying, “This is incredibly important. Our world is changing, and we’re going to have to start to think differently. We’re always going to have a human in the loop, but that model is going to change. Adversaries will use autonomous AI to find weaknesses, to adapt, to attack. I challenge everyone to think the same.”\n“Defenders need AI that can do the same,” he said. “Defenders need to start to think about AI working against AI continuously, autonomously, many times before a human even knows there’s a fight. This is where this is all going, and I believe AI is going to move us faster and give us a really powerful thing: trust, where trust can become an advantage.”\nPhotography by Joe Kuehne\nMore On\nArtificial Intelligence\nAgentic AI\nAI Governance\nAI Security\nAI Strategy\nSecurity\nEndpoint Security\nRelated Articles\nArtificial Intelligence\nAI Production Readiness: Build the Foundation Before You Scale\nArtificial Intelligence\nHow ManpowerGroup and Other Companies Measure AI’s ROI\nSecurity\nHow Banks Should Prioritize Cybersecurity Spending\nClose\nNew Research from CDW Explores AI and Cybersecurity\nLearn how AI is helping IT teams manage risk and improve resilience.\nGet the Report\nLatest Articles\nAI Production Readiness: Build the Foundation Before You Scale\nHow ManpowerGroup and Other Companies Measure AI’s ROI\nThe Minnesota Wild Score Big With a Phone and Contact Center Upgrade\nHow Banks Should Prioritize Cybersecurity Spending\nArtificial Intelligence\nAI Production Readiness: Build the Foundation Before You Scale\nArtificial Intelligence\nHow ManpowerGroup and Other Companies Measure AI’s ROI\nTrending Now\nHow Do You Choose Between CAT 6, CAT 7 and CAT 8 Cables?","content_cn":"首页»安全\n9月\n04\n2026\n安全\nCrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026：CrowdStrike发布Falcon Guardian与Safe Mind，用于AIDR\n随着代理式人工智能迅速普及，企业需要能够以机器速度检测和响应威胁的解决方案。\n作者：Joe Kuehne\nJoe Kuehne是BizTech杂志的副编辑总监。\n收听\n暂停\n人工智能代理正被用于各种可以想象的用例，但并非每个代理的开发都是为了带来更高的效率和生产力。恶意行为者正利用AI实现更快的攻击方法，许多组织发现自身并未做好充分防御准备。\n根据《CrowdStrike 2026全球威胁报告》，过去一年中，由AI赋能的对手发起的攻击增加了89%。CDW最近的研究也表明，AI驱动的攻击发生率很高：该公司调查中43%的受访者表示，其组织遭遇过由AI增强或生成的网络钓鱼攻击，而37%的受访者报告称在过去一年中受到过AI驱动恶意软件的打击。\n在本周的CrowdStrike Fal.Con上，主题是“保障AI革命的安全”。CrowdStrike首席执行官George Kurtz发表了开幕主题演讲，全面审视了代理式AI正在重塑网络安全的种种方式。攻击者正在利用代理发现并利用漏洞，但正如Kurtz所说，“还没有人为防御者构建AI。”直到现在。\n点击下方横幅，阅读最新的CDW网络安全研究报告。\nAI需要其自身形式的检测与响应\n“今天，AI是新的战场，”Kurtz在活动开始时表示，并指出计算领域的每一个重大增长时期都会带来攻击面的扩张。“我们曾经历过世界上一些最具后果性的攻击面变化，而AI代理就是下一个。”\n在显而易见的兴奋气氛中，Kurtz宣布推出Falcon Guardian，旨在提供AI检测与响应（AIDR），帮助组织“不仅了解其风险、了解正在运行的内容，更重要的是，加速AI在你们自己组织中的采用。”\n“CrowdStrike通过让端点成为阻止攻击的控制点，开创了EDR。AI需要同样的方法，”Kurtz在当天的一份新闻稿中表示。“AI没有改变攻击，它改变了攻击的速度。仅靠治理无法阻止一个已经在行动的代理。Falcon Guardian将策略转化为保护，在AI代理执行之处、在其造成伤害之前阻止威胁。”\n探索：通过自我评估了解你的安全态势有多成熟。\nGuardian帮助识别和保护影子AI\n代理式AI激增带来的最大网络安全挑战之一是缺乏可见性。当公司鼓励员工了解、利用和部署他们自己创建的代理时，他们并不总是知道其生态系统中有什么。\nKurtz播放了一段介绍Falcon Guardian的视频，其中解释说，许多组织不知道自己的AI代理在哪里运行、是谁部署了它们，或者它们可能引入什么风险。“Guardian改变了这一点。它从发现开始。Guardian会映射你整个AI代理舰队，也就是所谓的影子AI，覆盖每一个端点，”他说。\n在另一场主题演讲中，CrowdStrike总裁Michael Sentonas解释了为什么Guardian将如此有价值：“一旦AI成为企业的一部分，可见性就不再足够。你需要知道正在运行什么、它可以访问什么、它正在做什么、在哪里划清界限。这就是Guardian。”\n“它为你提供整个AI资产范围的运行时可见性，”Sentonas说。“你的代理正在做什么、正在访问什么、正在采取什么行动，无论你是否知道，以及你需要在何处介入。”\n一旦AI成为企业的一部分，可见性就不再足够。”\nMichael Sentonas\nCrowdStrike总裁\nCrowdStrike推出SafeMind，以提升AI安全\nKurtz继续强调CrowdStrike通过与NVIDIA合作开发的一项新创新。\n“我们与NVIDIA一起，构建了网络安全领域首个完整的代理式网络安全系统，包括首个专为防御者打造的前沿模型和框架，”他宣布。根据随附的一份新闻稿，CrowdStrike SafeMind是首个面向防御者的代理式系统，并且是使用NVIDIA Nemotron构建的。\nKurtz展示\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"biztechmagazine.com","publish_time":"2026-09-04T20:26:44+00:00"}},{"id":"news-247","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026：你的SOC准备好迎接AI代理了吗？","title_en":"CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026: Is Your SOC Ready for AI Agents?","summary_cn":"在CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026大会上，总裁Michael Sentonas指出，随着攻击者突破时间趋近于零，传统SOC模式已难以为继，需转向“代理式SOC”，让端点、身份与云安全代理协同共享信息。CrowdStrike托管服务副总裁Austin Murphy介绍其代理式工作流已研发一年多，由Falcon Complete驱动，并提出“human on the loop”概念以持续训练代理。","summary_en":"At CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026, President Michael Sentonas argued that with breakout time approaching zero, the traditional SOC model is broken and organizations need an agentic SOC where endpoint, identity and cloud agents collaborate in a shared space. Austin Murphy, VP of managed services, said CrowdStrike has worked on agentic workflows for over a year, powered by Falcon Complete, and introduced a 'human on the loop' concept to keep training agents.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T05:45:39.779618+00:00","url":"https://biztechmagazine.com/article/2026/09/crowdstrike-falcon-2026-your-soc-ready-ai-agents","content":"Home»Security\nSep\n08\n2026\nSecurity\nCrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026: Is Your SOC Ready for AI Agents?\nAs attackers continue to evolve techniques and strategies, defenders must be able to respond at machine speed. The agentic security operations center might be the answer.\nby Joe Kuehne\nJoe Kuehne is an Associate Editorial Director at BizTech magazine.\nListen\nPause\nArtificial intelligence is dramatically reducing the amount of time it takes an attacker to compromise an organization’s security. And cybersecurity leaders recognize the need to match that speed by appropriately arming their security operations centers (SOCs).\nAccording to CrowdStrike’s 2026 Global Threat Report, “The average eCrime breakout time” — the period between initial access and lateral movement onto another system — “dropped to 29 minutes, a 65% increase in speed from 2024.”\nAt last week’s CrowdStrike Fal.Con, CrowdStrike President Michael Sentonas told attendees at a keynote session, “I will argue that the breakout time is over. Think about what that means. We now live in a world where a model finds a vulnerability and weaponizes it at the same time.”\n“You’re not going to be scanning vulnerabilities and spending weeks to think about where to deal with an issue,” he continued. “There’s no gap left to measure. There’s no window. We’re living in a world where the breakout time is zero.”\nClick the banner below to read the recent CDW Cybersecurity Research Report.\nReduced Breakout Time Demands an Agentic SOC\nFor security teams to keep up with their adversaries, it’s becoming clear they must enable AI agents within the SOC. “We need to start to move to investigations at machine speed,” Sentonas said. “This is why the old SOC model is broken in many ways.”\nCurrent models frequently involve separate human agents tackling endpoint security, identity security and cloud security. When an attacker has the capability to move in minutes or less, organizations can’t afford to spend hours on an investigation. That’s where the agentic SOC comes in.\nWith an agentic SOC, there would still be agents working on endpoint, identity and cloud security. But they would work simultaneously and collaboratively, speeding up the process because they’re sharing memory and information.\n“No handoffs, no waiting, no starting over,” Sentonas said. “That’s the difference between a collection of agents and an agentic SOC. Not working independently, but working together in that shared space, giving you the ability to stay in control.”\nDISCOVER: Find out how mature your security posture is with a self-assessment.\nCrowdStrike Is Already Helping Organizations Create Agentic SOCs\nAccording to Austin Murphy, vice president of managed services at CrowdStrike, “We started working on our agentic workflows over a year ago.”\n“The agents that are powering the agentic SOC are created by Falcon Complete because it’s what we’ve been using behind the scenes for us, and now there’s an opportunity to expand the number of customers that can benefit from what we’ve built to help ourselves become more efficient, more consistent,” Murphy said.\nMurphy anticipates that the agentic SOC will change the roles of defenders and the ways they interact with agents. He referenced the often-repeated phrase “human in the loop,” which he said means that “agents can only take you so far, and then it escalates to a human to finish up if it ever gets stuck.”\nBut he also mentioned “human on the loop,” which is a concept he said CrowdStrike is working on internally. He noted that the current state of AI was trained on data produced when humans were performing the work. “Well, if they stop performing the work, we’re going to lose the data to train the next version. So, when we refer to human on the loop, we have a human analyst parallel working the same detection that an agent does.” This approach allows CrowdStrike to perform data comparisons between the human and the agent and continually maintain and improve the agents.\nThere’s no gap left to measure. There’s no window. We’re living in a world where the breakout time is zero.”\nMichael Sentonas\nPresident, CrowdStrike\nHow Can the Agentic SOC Benefit a Security Team?\nMurphy said he envisions agents allowing human analysts to delegate some of their normal tasks to an investigative harness, transforming the analyst role into more of a managerial position. “Instead of actually doing log analysis, you’re directing the log analysis,” he explained. “You’re directing the work instead of running the actual work. It’s still the same discipline, it’s just more of a supervisory role.”\nMurphy added that agents will also allow analysts to work at the next level up, addressing some of the skills gaps that have persisted in the cybersecurity workforce for years. Analysts who are skilled at writing a particular type of query or working in one language can rely on agents to elevate their abilities.\nHe admitted that some traditional analysts are responding to the use of agents differently. “There’s a lot of apprehension, but what we find is that kind of melts away when the analysts start in good faith interacting with some of the technology. That quickly turns into excitement.”\nDespite some initial reservations about AI potentially eliminating jobs, familiarity with the technology can ease those concerns. Once analysts start working with agents, they frequently discover “it just means that I can do my job faster,” Murphy said. “I don’t have to be doing seven tasks one after another. I can have these seven tasks be done at the same time, and I’m working at a higher level.”\nPhotography by Joe Kuehne\nMore On\nArtificial Intelligence\nAgentic AI\nAI Security\nEndpoint Security\nRisk Assessment\nThreat Prevention\nRelated Articles\nArtificial Intelligence\nAI Production Readiness: Build the Foundation Before You Scale\nArtificial Intelligence\nHow ManpowerGroup and Other Companies Measure AI’s ROI\nSecurity\nHow Banks Should Prioritize Cybersecurity Spending\nClose\nNew Research from CDW Explores AI and Cybersecurity\nLearn how AI is helping IT teams manage risk and improve resilience.\nGet the Report\nLatest Articles\nAI Production Readiness: Build the Foundation Before You Scale\nHow ManpowerGroup and Other Companies Measure AI’s ROI\nThe Minnesota Wild Score Big With a Phone and Contact Center Upgrade\nHow Banks Should Prioritize Cybersecurity Spending\nArtificial Intelligence\nAI Production Readiness: Build the Foundation Before You Scale\nArtificial Intelligence\nHow ManpowerGroup and Other Companies Measure AI’s ROI\nTrending Now\nHow Do You Choose Between CAT 6, CAT 7 and CAT 8 Cables?","content_cn":"首页»安全\n2026年9月8日\n安全\nCrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026：你的安全运营中心准备好迎接AI智能体了吗？\n随着攻击者不断演进其技术和策略，防御者必须能够以机器速度做出响应。智能体化安全运营中心或许就是答案。\n作者：Joe Kuehne\nJoe Kuehne是BizTech杂志的副编辑总监。\n收听\n暂停\n人工智能正在大幅缩短攻击者攻破组织安全所需的时间。网络安全领域的领导者们认识到，必须通过适当武装其安全运营中心（SOC）来匹配这种速度。\n根据CrowdStrike的《2026年全球威胁报告》，“网络犯罪的平均突破时间”——即从初始访问到横向移动到另一系统的这段时间——“降至29分钟，速度较2024年提升了65%。”\n在上周举行的CrowdStrike Fal.Con大会上，CrowdStrike总裁Michael Sentonas在主题演讲中对与会者表示：“我认为突破时间已经不复存在了。想想这意味着什么。我们现在生活在一个模型发现漏洞并同时将其武器化的世界里。”\n“你不再需要扫描漏洞并花数周时间思考在哪里处理问题，”他继续说道，“已经没有可衡量的间隙了。没有窗口期了。我们生活在一个突破时间为零的世界里。”\n点击下方横幅阅读最新的CDW网络安全研究报告。\n突破时间缩短要求智能体化SOC\n为了让安全团队跟上对手的步伐，越来越明显的是，他们必须在SOC中启用AI智能体。“我们需要开始以机器速度进行调查，”Sentonas说，“这就是为什么旧的SOC模式在很多方面已经行不通了。”\n当前的模式通常涉及不同的人工智能体分别处理终端安全、身份安全和云安全。当攻击者有能力在几分钟甚至更短时间内移动时，组织无法承受在调查上花费数小时。这正是智能体化SOC的用武之地。\n在智能体化SOC中，仍然会有智能体负责终端、身份和云安全。但它们会同时协作运行，因为共享记忆和信息而加快流程。\n“没有交接，没有等待，没有从头开始，”Sentonas说，“这就是一组智能体与一个智能体化SOC之间的区别。不是独立工作，而是在那个共享空间中协同工作，让你有能力保持控制。”\n探索：通过自我评估了解你的安全态势有多成熟。\nCrowdStrike已在帮助组织创建智能体化SOC\n据CrowdStrike托管服务副总裁Austin Murphy介绍，“我们一年多前就开始研究智能体化工作流了。”\n“驱动智能体化SOC的智能体是由Falcon Complete创建的，因为这一直是我们在幕后使用的东西，现在有机会扩大能够受益于我们所构建成果的客户数量，帮助我们变得更高效、更一致，”Murphy说。\nMurphy预计，智能体化SOC将改变防御者的角色及其与智能体互动的方式。他提到了常被重复的“人在回路中”这一说法，他说这意味着“智能体只能带你走到一定程度，然后如果卡住了，就会升级给人类来完成。”\n但他也提到了“人在回路上”，他说这是CrowdStrike正在内部研究的一个概念。他指出，当前AI的状态是基于人类执行工作时产生的数据训练的。“那么，如果他们停止执行这些工作，我们就会失去用于训练下一版本的数据。所以，当我们提到人在回路上时，我们让一名人类分析师与智能体并行处理同一个检测任务。”这种方法使CrowdStrike能够在人类和智能体之间进行数据比较，并持续维护和改进智能体。\n已经没有可衡量的间隙了。没有窗口期了。我们生活在一个突破时间为零的世界里。”\nMichael Sentonas\nCrowdStrike总裁\n智能体化SOC如何惠及安全团队？\nMurphy说，他设想智能体允许人类分析师将一些日常任务委托给调查框架，将分析师的角色转变为更像管理者的职位。“你不是在做日志分析，而是在指挥日志分析，”他解释道，“你在指挥工作，而不是","publish_source":"biztechmagazine.com","publish_time":"2026-09-08T17:46:58+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2526","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike、Uber、Zoom等企业采用NVIDIA Nemotron与Cosmos推理模型构建智能体","title_en":"CrowdStrike, Uber, Zoom Among Industry Pioneers Building Smarter Agents With NVIDIA Nemotron and Cosmos Reasoning Models for Enterprise and Physical AI Applications | NVIDIA Blog","summary_cn":"NVIDIA在SIGGRAPH上宣布扩展Nemotron与Cosmos两大模型系列的推理能力，用于企业级AI智能体与物理AI应用。CrowdStrike、Uber、Zoom、Magna、NetApp等企业已采用这些模型。其中CrowdStrike正测试Nemotron模型，以支持其Charlotte AI智能体在Falcon平台上编写查询；Uber则探索用Cosmos Reason分析自动驾驶车辆行为。","summary_en":"At SIGGRAPH, NVIDIA announced expanded reasoning capabilities for its Nemotron and Cosmos model families, targeting enterprise AI agents and physical AI. CrowdStrike, Uber, Zoom, Magna and NetApp are among the adopters. CrowdStrike is testing Nemotron models to let its Charlotte AI agents write queries on the CrowdStrike Falcon platform, while Uber is exploring Cosmos Reason to analyze autonomous vehicle behavior and summarize visual data.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:52:10.177307+00:00","url":"https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/nemotron-cosmos-reasoning-enterprise-physical-ai","content":"CrowdStrike, Uber, Zoom Among Industry Pioneers Building Smarter Agents With NVIDIA Nemotron and Cosmos Reasoning Models for Enterprise and Physical AI Applications\nOpen reasoning models provide faster and extended thinking to generate smarter outcomes for AI agents across customer service, cybersecurity, manufacturing, logistics and robotics.\nAugust 11, 2025 by Kari Briski\n0 Comments\nShare\nShare This Article\nX\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\nCopy link\nLink copied!\nAI agents are poised to deliver as much as $450 billion from revenue gains and cost savings by 2028, according to Capgemini. Developers building these agents are turning to higher-performing reasoning models to improve AI agent platforms and physical AI systems.\nAt SIGGRAPH, NVIDIA today announced an expansion of two model families with reasoning capabilities — NVIDIA Nemotron and NVIDIA Cosmos — that leaders across industries are using to drive productivity via teams of AI agents and humanoid robots.\nCrowdStrike, Uber, Magna, NetApp and Zoom are among some of the enterprises tapping into these model families.\nNew NVIDIA Nemotron Nano 2 and Llama Nemotron Super 1.5 models offer the highest accuracy in their size categories for scientific reasoning, math, coding, tool-calling, instruction-following and chat. These new models give AI agents the power to think more deeply and work more efficiently — exploring broader options, speeding up research and delivering smarter results within set time limits.\nThink of the model as the brain of an AI agent — it provides the core intelligence. But to make that brain useful for a business, it must be embedded into an agent that understands specific workflows, in addition to industry and business jargon, and operates safely. NVIDIA helps enterprises bridge that gap with leading libraries and AI blueprints for onboarding, customizing and governing AI agents at scale.\nCosmos Reason is a new reasoning vision language model (VLM) for physical AI applications that excels in understanding how the real world works, using structured reasoning to understand concepts like physics, object permanence and space-time alignment. The VLM topped the Physical Reasoning Leaderboard on Hugging Face.\nCosmos Reason is purpose-built to serve as the reasoning backbone to a robot vision language action (VLA) model, or critique and caption training data for robotics and autonomous vehicles, and equip runtime visual AI agents with spatial-temporal understanding and reasoning of physical operations, like in factories or cities.\nNemotron: Highest Accuracy and Efficiency for Agentic Enterprise AI\nAs enterprises develop AI agents to tackle complex, multistep tasks, models that can provide strong reasoning accuracy with efficient token generation enable intelligent, autonomous decision-making at scale.\nNVIDIA Nemotron is a family of advanced open reasoning models that use leading models, NVIDIA-curated open datasets and advanced AI techniques to provide an accurate and efficient starting point for AI agents.\nThe latest Nemotron models deliver leading efficiency in three ways: a new hybrid model architecture, compact quantized models and a configurable thinking budget that provides developers with control over token generation, resulting in 60% lower reasoning costs. This combination lets the models reason more deeply and respond faster, without needing more time or computing power. This means better results at a lower cost.\nNemotron Nano 2 provides as much as 6x higher token generation compared with other leading models of its size.\nLlama Nemotron Super 1.5 achieves leading performance and the highest reasoning accuracy in its class, empowering AI agents to reason better, make smarter decisions and handle complex tasks independently. It’s now available in NVFP4, or 4-bit floating point, which delivers as much as 6x higher throughput on NVIDIA B200 GPUs compared with NVIDIA H100 GPUs.\nThe chart above shows the Nemotron model delivers top reasoning accuracy in the same timeframe and on the same compute budget, delivering the highest accuracy per dollar.\nAlong with the two new Nemotron models, NVIDIA is also announcing its first open VLM training dataset — Llama Nemotron VLM dataset v1 — with 3 million samples of optical character recognition, visual QA and captioning data that power the previously released Llama 3.1 Nemotron Nano VL 8B model.\nIn addition to the accuracy of the reasoning models, agents also rely on retrieval-augmented generation to fetch the latest and most relevant information from connected data across disparate sources to make informed decisions. The recently released Llama 3.2 NeMo Retriever embedding model tops three visual document retrieval leaderboards — ViDoRe V1, ViDoRe V2 and MTEB VisualDocumentRetrieval — for boosting agentic system accuracy.\nUsing these reasoning and information retrieval models, a deep research agent built using the AI-Q NVIDIA Blueprint is currently No. 1 for open and portable agents on DeepResearch Bench.\nNVIDIA NeMo and NVIDIA NIM microservices support the entire AI agent lifecycle — from development and deployment to monitoring and optimization of the agentic systems.\nCosmos Reason: A Breakthrough in Physical AI\nVLMs marked a breakthrough for computer vision and robotics, empowering machines to identify objects and patterns. However, nonreasoning VLMs lack the ability to understand and interact with the real world — meaning they can’t handle ambiguity or novel experiences, nor solve complex multistep tasks.\nNVIDIA Cosmos Reason is a new open, customizable, 7-billion-parameter reasoning VLM for physical AI and robotics. Cosmos Reason lets robots and vision AI agents reason like humans, using prior knowledge, physics understanding and common sense to understand and act in the physical world.\nCosmos Reason enables advanced capabilities across robotics and physical AI applications such as training data critiquing and captioning, robot decision-making and video analytics AI agents.\nIt can help automate the curation and annotation of large, diverse training datasets, accelerating the development of high-accuracy AI models. It can also serve as a sophisticated reasoning engine for robot planning, parsing complex instructions into actionable steps for VLA models, even in new environments.\nIt also powers video analytics AI agents built on the NVIDIA Blueprint for video search and summarization (VSS), enabled by the NVIDIA Metropolis platform, gleaning valuable insights from massive volumes of stored or live video data. These visually perceptive and interactive AI agents can help streamline operations in factories, warehouses, retail stores, airports, traffic intersections and more by spotting anomalies.\nNVIDIA’s robotics research team uses Cosmos Reason for data filtration and curation, and as the “System 2” reasoning VLM behind VLA models such as the next versions of NVIDIA Isaac GR00T NX.\nNow Serving: NVIDIA Reasoning Models for AI Agents and Robots Everywhere\nDiverse enterprises and consulting leaders are adopting NVIDIA’s latest reasoning models. Leaders spanning cybersecurity to telecommunications are among those working with Nemotron to build enterprise AI agents.\nZoom plans to harness Nemotron reasoning models with Zoom AI Companion to make decisions and manage multistep tasks to take action for users across Zoom Meetings, Zoom Chat and Zoom documents.\nCrowdStrike is testing Nemotron models to enable its Charlotte AI agents to write queries on the CrowdStrike Falcon platform.\nAmdocs is using NVIDIA Nemotron models in its amAIz Suite to drive AI agents to handle complex, multistep automation spanning care, sales, network and customer support.\nEY is adopting Nemotron Nano 2, given its high throughput, to support agentic AI in large organizations for tax, risk management and finance use cases.\nNetApp is currently testing Nemotron reasoning models so that AI agents can search and analyze business data\nDataRobot is working with Nemotron models for its Agent Workforce Platform for end-to-end agent lifecycle management.\nTabnine is working with Nemotron models for suggesting and automating coding tasks on behalf of developers.\nAutomation Anywhere, CrewAI and Dataiku are among the additional agentic AI software developers integrating Nemotron models into their platforms.\nLeading companies across transportation, safety and AI intelligence are using Cosmos Reason to advance autonomous driving, video analytics, and road and workplace safety.\nUber is exploring Cosmos Reason to analyze autonomous vehicle behavior. In addition, Uber is post-training Cosmos Reason to summarize visual data and analyze scenarios like pedestrians walking across highways to perform quality analysis and inform autonomous driving behavior.\nCosmos Reason can also serve as the brain of autonomous vehicles. It lets robots interpret environments and, given complex commands, break them down into tasks and execute them using common sense, even in unfamiliar environments.\nCentific is testing Cosmos Reason to enhance its AI-powered video intelligence platform. The VLM enables the platform to process complex video data into actionable insights, helping reduce false positives and improve decision-making efficiency.\nVAST is advancing real-time urban intelligence using NVIDIA Cosmos Reason with its AI operating system to process massive video streams at scale. With the VSS Blueprint, VAST can build agents that can identify incidents and trigger responses, turning video streams and metadata into actionable, proactive public safety tools.\nAmbient.ai is working with Cosmos Reason’s temporal, physics-aware reasoning, to enable automated detection of missing personal protection equipment and monitoring of hazardous conditions, helping enhance environmental health and safety across construction, manufacturing, logistics and other industrial settings.\nMagna is developing with Cosmos Reason as part of its City Delivery Platform — a fully autonomous, low-cost solution for instant delivery — to help vehicles adapt more quickly to new cities. The model adds world understanding to the vehicles’ long-term trajectory planning.\nThese models are expected to be available as NVIDIA NIM microservices for secure, reliable deployment on any NVIDIA-accelerated infrastructure for maximum privacy and control. They are planned to be available soon through Amazon Bedrock and Amazon SageMaker AI for Nemotron models, as well as through Azure AI Foundry, Oracle Data Science Platform and Google Vertex AI.\nTry Cosmos Reason on build.nvidia.com or download it from Hugging Face or GitHub.\nNemotron Nano 2 and Llama Nemotron Super 1.5 (NVFP4) will be available soon for download. Meanwhile, learn more about Nemotron models and download previous versions.\nDownload the Llama Nemotron VLM Dataset v1 from Hugging Face.\nVisit our Cosmos Cookbook for step-by-step workflows, technical recipes, and concrete examples for building, adapting, and deploying Cosmos WFMs, or join our community to learn with peers.\nSee notice regarding software product information.\nNVIDIA GTC Berlin Registration Is Now Open\nOctober 20-22\nRegister Now\nRecent News\nAI\nAt AI Day Singapore, NVIDIA and Partners Showcase AI Advancements Across Southeast Asia\nSeptember 22, 2026\nRobotics\nNVIDIA Isaac ROS 5.0 Advances Agentic, Open Source Robotics Development\nSeptember 22, 2026\nCorporate\nNVIDIA Launches DSX Ready to Qualify Power and Cooling Products for AI Factories\nSeptember 21, 2026\nRobotics\nWhy Deploying Physical AI at Scale Demands Safety at Every Layer\nSeptember 21, 2026\nView All Recent News\nCategories:\nAI\nTags:\nAgentic AIArtificial IntelligenceCosmosMetropolisNemotronPhysical AISIGGRAPH 2025\nRelated News\nDriving\nPhysical AI Takes the Wheel: How the World’s Robotaxi Leaders Are Building With NVIDIA Technologies\nSep 10, 2026\nDriving\nNVIDIA Alpamayo 2 Super, the Frontier Open Model for Robotaxis and Autonomous Vehicles, Now Available for Commercial Use\nAug 4, 2026\nDriving\nFor Robotaxis, Safety Must Be Built In, Not Bolted On\nJun 10, 2026\nResearch\nNVIDIA Research Unlocks Advanced Grasping, Smarter Autonomous Driving and Agent Training at Scale\nJun 3, 2026","content_cn":"CrowdStrike、Uber、Zoom 等行业先驱正利用 NVIDIA Nemotron 和 Cosmos 推理模型，为企业及物理 AI 应用构建更智能的智能体\n\n开放式推理模型可提供更快且更深入的思考，为客户服务、网络安全、制造、物流和机器人领域的 AI 智能体生成更智能的成果。\n\n2025 年 8 月 11 日，Kari Briski\n0 条评论\n分享\n分享本文\nX\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\n复制链接\n链接已复制！\n\n据 Capgemini 称，到 2028 年，AI 智能体有望通过收入增长和成本节约带来高达 4500 亿美元的收益。构建这些智能体的开发者正转向性能更高的推理模型，以改进 AI 智能体平台和物理 AI 系统。\n\nNVIDIA 今日在 SIGGRAPH 上宣布扩展具备推理能力的两个模型系列——NVIDIA Nemotron 和 NVIDIA Cosmos。各行业的领导者正利用这些模型系列，通过 AI 智能体团队和人形机器人提升生产力。\n\nCrowdStrike、Uber、Magna、NetApp 和 Zoom 等企业都在采用这些模型系列。\n\n全新的 NVIDIA Nemotron Nano 2 和 Llama Nemotron Super 1.5 模型，在科学推理、数学、编码、工具调用、指令遵循和聊天方面，在各自的尺寸类别中提供最高准确率。这些新模型赋予 AI 智能体更深入思考和更高效工作的能力——探索更广泛的选项、加快研究，并在规定时间内交付更智能的结果。\n\n可以把模型看作 AI 智能体的大脑——它提供核心智能。但要让这个大脑对企业有用，就必须将其嵌入一个能够理解特定工作流以及行业和业务术语、并安全运行的智能体中。NVIDIA 通过领先的库和 AI 蓝图，帮助企业大规模完成 AI 智能体的接入、定制和治理，从而弥合这一差距。\n\nCosmos Reason 是一种面向物理 AI 应用的新型推理视觉语言模型（VLM），擅长理解现实世界的运作方式，利用结构化推理理解物理学、物体恒存性和时空对齐等概念。该 VLM 在 Hugging Face 的 Physical Reasoning Leaderboard 上名列第一。\n\nCosmos Reason 专门用于充当机器人视觉语言动作（VLA）模型的推理骨干，或为机器人和自动驾驶汽车的训练数据提供批评和描述，并为运行时视觉 AI 智能体配备对物理操作的时空理解和推理能力，例如工厂或城市中的操作。\n\nNemotron：面向智能企业 AI 的最高准确率与效率\n\n随着企业开发 AI 智能体来处理复杂的多步骤任务，能够以高效的令牌生成提供强大推理准确率的模型，可在大规模范围内实现智能、自主的决策。\n\nNVIDIA Nemotron 是一个先进开放式推理模型系列，采用领先模型、由 NVIDIA 精选的开放数据集和先进 AI 技术，为 AI 智能体提供准确且高效的起点。\n\n最新的 Nemotron 模型通过三种方式实现领先效率：全新的混合模型架构、紧凑的量化模型，以及可配置的思考预算，让开发者能够控制令牌生成，从而将推理成本降低 60%。这种组合让模型无需更多时间或计算能力，就能进行更深入的推理并更快响应。这意味着以更低成本获得更好结果。\n\nNemotron Nano 2 提供高达 6 倍的令牌生成\n与同等规模的其他领先模型相比。\nLlama Nemotron Super 1.5 实现了领先性能和同类产品中最高的推理准确率，使 AI 代理能够更好地推理、更明智地做出决策，并独立处理复杂任务。现在，该模型以 NVFP4（即 4 位浮点格式）提供，在 NVIDIA B200 GPU 上的吞吐量最高可达 NVIDIA H100 GPU 的 6 倍。\n上图显示，在相同时间范围和相同计算预算下，Nemotron 模型提供了顶尖的推理准确率，实现了每美元最高的准确率。\n除这两个新的 Nemotron 模型外，NVIDIA 还宣布推出其首个开放式 VLM 训练数据集——Llama Nemotron VLM dataset v1——其中包含 300 万个光学字符识别、视觉问答和图像描述样本，这些数据为此前发布的 Llama 3.1 Nemotron Nano VL 8B 模型提供支持。\n除了依赖推理模型的准确率外，代理还依靠检索增强生成，从跨不同来源的连接数据中获取最新且最相关的信息，以做出明智决策。近期发布的 Llama 3.2 NeMo Retriever 嵌入模型在三个视觉文档检索排行榜——ViDoRe V1、ViDoRe V2 和 MTEB VisualDocumentRetrieval——上均名列第一，从而提升了代理系统的准确率。\n利用这些推理和信息检索模型，使用 AI-Q NVIDIA Blueprint 构建的深度研究代理目前在 DeepResearch Bench 上排名第一，成为开放且可移植代理中的第一名。\nNVIDIA NeMo 和 NVIDIA NIM 微服务支持 AI 代理的整个生命周期——从开发、部署到代理系统的监控和优化。\n\nCosmos Reason：物理 AI 的突破\n\nVLM 为计算机视觉和机器人技术带来了突破，使机器能够识别物体和模式。然而，非推理型 VLM 缺乏理解和与现实世界互动的能力——这意味着它们无法处理歧义或新颖体验，也无法解决复杂的多步骤任务。\nNVIDIA Cosmos Reason 是一款面向物理 AI 和机器人技术的全新开放、可定制的 70 亿参数推理型 VLM。Cosmos Reason 让机器人和视觉 AI 代理能够像人类一样进行推理，运用先验知识、物理理解和常识来理解并作用于物理世界。\nCosmos Reason 为机器人和物理 AI 应用带来先进能力，例如训练数据批评与描述、机器人决策以及视频分析 AI 代理。\n它可以帮助自动完成大型、多样化训练数据集的整理和标注，加速高准确率 AI 模型的开发。它还可以作为机器人规划的高级推理引擎，将复杂指令解析为可执行步骤，供 VLA 模型使用，即使是在全新的环境中也能如此。\n它还为基于 NVIDIA 视频搜索与摘要（VSS）Blueprint、由 NVIDIA Metropolis 平台支持的视频分析 AI 代理提供动力，从海量存储或实时视频数据中获取有价值的洞察。这些具备视觉感知和交互能力的 AI 代理可以通过发现异常，帮助简化工厂、仓库、零售店、机场、交通路口等场所的运营。\nNVIDIA 的机器人研究团队使用 Cosmos Reason 进行数据筛选和整理，并将其作为 VLA 模型背后的“系统 2”推理 VLM，例如下一代 NVIDIA Isaac GR00T NX。\n\n现已提供：面向各地 AI 代理和机器人的 NVIDIA 推理模型\n\n多样化\n企业和咨询领域的领导者正在采用 NVIDIA 最新的推理模型。从网络安全到电信等领域的领导者，都在使用 Nemotron 构建企业级 AI 代理。\nZoom 计划将 Nemotron 推理模型与 Zoom AI Companion 结合使用，使其能够在 Zoom Meetings、Zoom Chat 和 Zoom 文档中代表用户作出决策并管理多步骤任务以采取行动。\nCrowdStrike 正在测试 Nemotron 模型，以支持其 Charlotte AI 代理在 CrowdStrike Falcon 平台上编写查询。\nAmdocs 正在其 amAIz Suite 中使用 NVIDIA Nemotron 模型，驱动 AI 代理处理涵盖客户服务、销售、网络和客户支持的复杂多步骤自动化任务。\nEY 正在采用 Nemotron Nano 2，凭借其高吞吐量，为大型组织在税务、风险管理和财务用例中提供代理式 AI 支持。\nNetApp 目前正在测试 Nemotron 推理模型，使 AI 代理能够搜索和分析业务数据\nDataRobot 正在为其 Agent Workforce Platform 使用 Nemotron 模型，以实现端到端的代理生命周期管理。\nTabnine 正在使用 Nemotron 模型，代表开发者提出建议并自动完成编码任务。\nAutomation Anywhere、CrewAI 和 Dataiku 等其他代理式 AI 软件开发商也在将 Nemotron 模型集成到其平台中。\n交通运输、安全和 AI 智能领域的领先企业正在使用 Cosmos Reason，推进自动驾驶、视频分析以及道路和工作场所安全。\nUber 正在探索使用 Cosmos Reason 分析自动驾驶车辆的行为。此外，Uber 还在对 Cosmos Reason 进行后训练，以总结视觉数据，并分析行人横穿高速公路等场景，从而开展质量分析并为自动驾驶行为提供信息。\nCosmos Reason 还可以充当自动驾驶车辆的大脑。它能让机器人解读环境，并在接收到复杂指令时，运用常识将其分解为任务并执行，即使身处陌生环境也能如此。\nCentific 正在测试 Cosmos Reason，以增强其 AI 驱动的视频智能平台。该视觉语言模型能够将复杂的视频数据处理为可执行的洞察，帮助减少误报并提高决策效率。\nVAST 正在使用 NVIDIA Cosmos Reason 及其 AI 操作系统推进实时城市智能，以大规模处理海量视频流。借助 VSS Blueprint，VAST 可以构建能够识别事件并触发响应的代理，将视频流和元数据转化为可执行、主动式的公共安全工具。\nAmbient.ai 正在利用 Cosmos Reason 的时间推理和物理感知推理能力，实现对个人防护装备缺失和危险状况的自动检测与监控，帮助提升建筑、制造、物流及其他工业环境中的环境健康与安全。\nMagna 正在将 Cosmos Reason 用于其 City Delivery Platform 的开发，这是一个完全自主、低成本的即时配送解决方案，可帮助车辆更快适应新的城市。该模型为车辆的长期轨迹规划增加了世界理解能力。\n预计这些模型将以 NVIDIA NIM 微服务的形式提供，以便在任何 NVIDIA 加速基础设施上进行安全、可靠的部署，从而实现最大程度的隐私和控制。Nemotron 模型计划很快通过 Amazon Bedrock 和 Amazon SageMaker AI 提供，同时也将通过 Azure AI Foundry、Oracle Data\nScience 平台和 Google Vertex AI。\n在 build.nvidia.com 上试用 Cosmos Reason，或从 Hugging Face 或 GitHub 下载。\nNemotron Nano 2 和 Llama Nemotron Super 1.5（NVFP4）即将开放下载。同时，进一步了解 Nemotron 模型并下载之前的版本。\n从 Hugging Face 下载 Llama Nemotron VLM Dataset v1。\n访问我们的 Cosmos Cookbook，获取用于构建、适配和部署 Cosmos WFM 的分步工作流程、技术配方和具体示例，或加入我们的社区，与同行一起学习。\n请参阅有关软件产品信息的通知。\nNVIDIA GTC Berlin 注册现已开放\n10 月 20 日至 22 日\n立即注册\n最新新闻\nAI\n在新加坡 AI Day 上，NVIDIA 与合作伙伴展示东南亚各地的 AI 进展\n2026 年 9 月 22 日\n机器人\nNVIDIA Isaac ROS 5.0 推进智能体式、开源机器人开发\n2026 年 9 月 22 日\n公司\nNVIDIA 发布 DSX Ready，为 AI 工厂电力和冷却产品提供资格认证\n2026 年 9 月 21 日\n机器人\n为何大规模部署物理 AI 要求每一层都具备安全性\n2026 年 9 月 21 日\n查看所有最新新闻\n类别：\nAI\n标签：\n智能体式 AI人工智能CosmosMetropolisNemotron物理 AISIGGRAPH 2025\n相关新闻\n驾驶\n物理 AI 驾临：全球 Robotaxi 领导者如何利用 NVIDIA 技术进行构建\n2026 年 9 月 10 日\n驾驶\nNVIDIA Alpamayo 2 Super——面向 Robotaxi 和自动驾驶汽车的前沿开放模型——现已可用于商业用途\n2026 年 8 月 4 日\n驾驶\n对于 Robotaxi，安全必须内置，而不是事后补上\n2026 年 6 月 10 日\n研究\nNVIDIA Research 解锁先进抓取、更智能的自动驾驶和大规模智能体训练\n2026 年 6 月 3 日","publish_source":"blogs.nvidia.com","publish_time":"2025-08-11T15:00:13+00:00"}},{"id":"news-273","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"NVIDIA与CrowdStrike强化智能体网络安全前沿","title_en":"NVIDIA and CrowdStrike Strengthen Agentic Cybersecurity Frontier | NVIDIA Blog","summary_cn":"在CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026大会上，NVIDIA与CrowdStrike宣布推出CrowdStrike SafeMind智能体网络安全系统，该系统基于NVIDIA Nemotron开放模型构建，采用攻防持续共同进化循环。NVIDIA创始人黄仁勋与CrowdStrike CEO George Kurtz共同发布，并宣布Falcon IQ及扩展的Guardian AI安全方案。测试显示基于Nemotron 3 Super的Blue Solano模型准确率更高且成本降低99%。","summary_en":"At CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026, NVIDIA and CrowdStrike announced CrowdStrike SafeMind, an agentic cybersecurity system built on NVIDIA Nemotron open models using a continuous offense-defense coevolution loop. NVIDIA founder Jensen Huang and CrowdStrike CEO George Kurtz unveiled it alongside Falcon IQ and an expanded Guardian AI safety solution. Testing showed the Blue Solano model, based on Nemotron 3 Super, delivered higher accuracy at 99% lower cost.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:41:07.556303+00:00","url":"https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/nvidia-crowdstrike-fal-con-2026","content":"NVIDIA and CrowdStrike Strengthen Agentic Cybersecurity Frontier\nNew CrowdStrike SafeMind agentic cybersecurity system built with NVIDIA Nemotron open models delivers greater protection and cost savings for cyber defense.\nSeptember 1, 2026 by Brian Caulfield\n0 Comments\nShare\nShare This Article\nX\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\nCopy link\nLink copied!\n“We’re at an inflection point in cybersecurity,” Jensen Huang told a sold-out crowd at CrowdStrike’s Fal.Con 2026 in Las Vegas Tuesday. Attacks are now automated. Defense has to be, too.\nThe NVIDIA founder and CEO joined CrowdStrike CEO and founder George Kurtz to announce CrowdStrike SafeMind, its agentic cybersecurity system developed by the CrowdStrike Cyber Superintelligence Lab.\n“This is the beginning of a new age of cybersecurity,” Huang told the crowd of 10,000 security professionals. “On the one hand, the adversaries are going to be more armed than ever. On the other hand, all of you are going to be more armed than ever.”\nSafeMind combines CrowdStrike’s purpose-built, beyond frontier-capable models and customized agentic harnesses, with defensive models built on NVIDIA Nemotron, in a continuous coevolution loop where offense and defense repeatedly challenge and improve each other.\nCrowdStrike also announced CrowdStrike Falcon IQ to operationalize Project QuiltWorks through agentic workload automation and expanded its CrowdStrike Guardian AI safety solution.\n“We have asymmetric advantages because we have a large community of cybersecurity experts who want to work with each other and keep the world safe,” Huang told the crowd.\nCrowdStrike’s annual conference drew security leaders from financial services, healthcare, the public sector and critical infrastructure.\n“The real gap that I saw was that the attackers had frontier AI, and the defenders didn’t,” Kurtz told them. “And that changes now.”\nSafeMind\nCrowdStrike built SafeMind’s defensive model using NVIDIA Nemotron open models, post-trained with CrowdStrike’s cyber experience and threat data. The SafeMind models are paired with proprietary cybersecurity harnesses optimized to work as an agentic stack.\nThe result ships natively in the CrowdStrike Falcon platform as SafeMind, CrowdStrike’s agentic cybersecurity system. SafeMind brings offensive and defensive AI together in a continuous coevolution loop, where each side adapts to and strengthens the other. This process continuously hardens the security of the customer environment until attacks are unsuccessful.\n“Your decade and a half of security data that we can train on — we can take a frontier model and make it essentially a super AGI that is incredibly good at cybersecurity,” Huang told Kurtz.\n“Together with NVIDIA, we built cybersecurity’s first complete agentic system for cybersecurity, including the first frontier models and harness purpose-built for defenders,” Kurtz said. “This isn’t a copilot baked into someone else’s intelligence. It’s not a chatbot with a security skin. It is a frontier-class model built and trained by CrowdStrike on our data in partnership with NVIDIA.”\nNVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra orchestrates the defensive agent harness. A fine-tuned Nemotron 3 Super powers SafeMind’s rule-generation sub-agent.\nBy post-training Nemotron with CrowdStrike data, CrowdStrike internal evaluations showed that the Blue Solano model — based on Nemotron 3 Super — delivered higher accuracy rates than leading frontier models at 99% lower cost.\nWhile SafeMind can operate as a complete system, the models can be used independently to empower defenders to stay ahead of the adversary. Security experts can also pair their own models with CrowdStrike’s custom harnesses, giving customers the flexibility to use the right models and capabilities for their environment.\n“The harness is essentially the exoskeleton of the large language model,” Huang said. “The large language model is the brain. The exoskeleton turns it into an agent — and this exoskeleton doesn’t have to be the same shape and capability for every domain.”\nWhen AI Is the Defense\nAI-enabled attacks rose 89% in the past year, and the fastest eCrime breakout time has reached 27 seconds, according to CrowdStrike. Human-speed response isn’t defense. It’s documentation.\n“There are many applications in the world where you must have the ability to fine-tune, to post-train — to create an AI that is super good at a particular domain,” Huang said. “Nemotron was created for precisely that. Completely free. Incredibly fast. You have the ability to have an asymmetric advantage against whatever comes your way.”\nWith open Nemotron as the base, CrowdStrike’s security teams post-trained on their own threat data without sending it to an outside provider, and customized the AI to their environment.\nThat’s not possible with a closed frontier model, and in security, the ability to inspect what’s defending matters.\nRed vs. Blue\nNVIDIA announced its work testing the CrowdStrike SafeMind models and harnesses in a high-fidelity cyber agent environment running as a simulation of the NVIDIA network.\nThe testing runs SafeMind in an offensive-defensive loop for adversarial coevolution. An offensive red-team agent finds the exploit, a blue-team defensive agent closes it and the findings become actionable detections to block attacks.\nThe red-agent harness runs Recon, Assault and Compromise sub-agents executing attack paths inside the cyber agent environment. The blue-agent harness monitors via Falcon sensors, generates detection candidates, validates them and promotes them.\nCrowdStrike built the test environment with NVIDIA: a digital twin of NVIDIA’s own accelerated computing infrastructure, validated against NVIDIA’s real threat landscape.\n“The basic framework of SafeMind — an adversarial model acting on a digital twin of the environment, with a defender model in a continuous cat-and-mouse loop, eventually learning how to secure itself — this basic framework applies to robotics, edge computing, enterprise computing and just about everything,” Huang said.\nCrowdStrike also announced Falcon IQ. NVIDIA Nemotron models help to power the agentic engine at the heart of Charlotte AI AgentWorks, CrowdStrike’s no-code agent development platform where Falcon IQ runs.\nFalcon IQ uses more than 50 agents working together as a unified agentic workforce to automate the most time-intensive workflows in assessment, prioritization and remediation.\nPartners use Falcon IQ to deliver customized findings, recommendations and executive outputs to customers. Charlotte AI AgentWorks enables every Falcon user to build their own agentic security workforce.\nThe Full Stack\nCrowdStrike has thousands of customer organizations generating trillions of daily security events.\nWith NVIDIA’s full-stack accelerated computing platform, the collaboration runs from the chips up through the models to the harnesses acting on what those models find. For Kurtz, that’s the point.\n“The crowd in CrowdStrike,” Kurtz added, “is the asymmetry that puts the defenders in a unique position to defeat the adversary.”\nNVIDIA GTC Berlin Registration Is Now Open\nOctober 20-22\nRegister Now\nRecent News\nGaming\nCute Critters Come to the Cloud: ‘Aniimo’ Launches on GeForce NOW\nSeptember 17, 2026\nAI Infrastructure\nNVIDIA Vera Rubin NVL72 Delivers Leading Performance in MLPerf Inference v6.1 Debut\nSeptember 16, 2026\nAI Infrastructure\nEmerald AI, Google and NVIDIA Launch Alliance to Advance Flexible AI Data Centers\nSeptember 16, 2026\nAI\nUniversity of Manchester Uses NVIDIA Earth-2 to Forecast Air Pollution Across the UK\nSeptember 15, 2026\nView All Recent News\nCategories:\nAICorporateSoftware\nTags:\nCybersecurityNemotronOpen Source\nRelated News\nAI\n‘Now We Can Know Everything and Do Anything,’ Jensen Huang Says at Dreamforce\nSep 15, 2026\nAI\nHeart of the Matter: How a Major Children’s Hospital Uses Open Source NVIDIA AI for Cardiac Care\nSep 15, 2026\nAI\nPerplexity Portable Computer Is Now Available on Windows, Powered by NVIDIA RTX\nSep 14, 2026\nAI\nNVIDIA Brings Real-Time AI to Broadcast, Sports and Global Streaming at IBC\nSep 9, 2026","content_cn":"NVIDIA与CrowdStrike强化智能体网络安全前沿\n全新的CrowdStrike SafeMind智能体网络安全系统基于NVIDIA Nemotron开放模型构建，为网络防御带来更强的保护与成本节约。\n2026年9月1日 作者：Brian Caulfield\n0条评论\n分享\n分享本文\nX\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\n复制链接\n链接已复制！\n“我们正处于网络安全的一个拐点，”黄仁勋周二在拉斯维加斯CrowdStrike Fal.Con 2026大会上面向座无虚席的观众说道。攻击如今已经自动化。防御也必须如此。\n这位NVIDIA创始人兼首席执行官与CrowdStrike首席执行官兼创始人George Kurtz共同宣布了CrowdStrike SafeMind，这是由CrowdStrike网络超级智能实验室开发的智能体网络安全系统。\n“这是网络安全新时代的开端，”黄仁勋对现场1万名安全专业人士说道。“一方面，对手将比以往任何时候都更加武装到牙齿。另一方面，你们所有人也将比以往任何时候都更加强大。”\nSafeMind将CrowdStrike专为超越前沿能力打造的模型和定制化智能体执行框架，与基于NVIDIA Nemotron构建的防御模型相结合，形成一个持续共同进化的循环，让攻防双方反复挑战并改进彼此。\nCrowdStrike还宣布推出CrowdStrike Falcon IQ，通过智能体工作负载自动化将Project QuiltWorks投入运营，并扩展了其CrowdStrike Guardian AI安全解决方案。\n“我们拥有不对称优势，因为我们有一个庞大的网络安全专家社区，他们希望彼此合作，共同守护世界安全，”黄仁勋对观众说道。\nCrowdStrike的年度大会吸引了来自金融服务、医疗健康、公共部门和关键基础设施领域的安全领导者。\n“我看到的真正差距在于，攻击者拥有前沿AI，而防御者没有，”Kurtz对他们说道。“而现在，这种情况将改变。”\nSafeMind\nCrowdStrike使用NVIDIA Nemotron开放模型构建了SafeMind的防御模型，并用CrowdStrike的网络经验和威胁数据进行了后训练。SafeMind模型与专有的网络安全执行框架相配对，并针对作为智能体技术栈运行进行了优化。\n最终成果以SafeMind的形式原生集成在CrowdStrike Falcon平台中，即CrowdStrike的智能体网络安全系统。SafeMind将进攻性AI与防御性AI结合在一个持续共同进化的循环中，双方相互适应、相互强化。这一过程持续加固客户环境的安全性，直到攻击无法得逞。\n“你们积累了15年的安全数据，我们可以基于这些数据进行训练——我们可以拿一个前沿模型，把它打造成一个在网络安全方面极其出色的超级AGI，”黄仁勋对Kurtz说道。\n“与NVIDIA携手，我们构建了网络安全领域首个完整的智能体网络安全系统，包括首个专为防御者打造的前沿模型和执行框架，”Kurtz说道。“这不是嵌入别人智能中的副驾驶。这不是披着安全外衣的聊天机器人。这是一个前沿级模型，由CrowdStrike基于我们的数据、与NVIDIA合作构建和训练。”\nNVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra负责编排防御智能体执行框架。经过微调的Nemotron 3 Super为SafeMind的规则生成子智能体提供支持。\n通过用CrowdStrike数据对Nemotron进行后训练，CrowdStrike的内部评估显示，基于Nemotron 3 Super的Blue Solano模型在准确率上高于领先的前沿模型，而成本降低了99%。\n虽然SafeMind可以作为完整系统运行，但这些模型也可以独立使用，赋能防御者保持对对手的领先。安全专家还可以将自己的模型与CrowdStrike的定制执行框架配对，让客户能够灵活地为其环境选择正确的模型和能力。\n“执行框架本质上是大语言模型的外骨骼，”黄仁勋说道。“大语言模型是大脑。外骨骼将其转变为智能体——而这个外骨骼不必在每个领域都具有相同的形态和能力。”\n当AI成为防御\n据CrowdStrike称，过去一年中AI驱动的攻击上升了89%，最快的网络犯罪突破时间已达到27秒。人类速度的响应不是防御，而是记录。\n“世界上有许多应用场景，你必须具备微调、后训练的能力——打造一个在特定领域极其出色的AI，”黄仁勋说道。“Nemotron正是为此而生。完全免费。极其快速。你拥有这种能力\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"blogs.nvidia.com","publish_time":"2026-09-01T21:19:20+00:00"}},{"id":"news-348","ktid":1001290,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001290","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"北达科他大学首位获任美国外交关系协会教育大使的教授","title_en":"UND professor first in ND to be named Council on Foreign Relations Education Ambassador - UND Today","summary_cn":"北达科他大学太空研究副教授弗朗西斯科·德尔坎托·维特拉莱被选为美国外交关系协会（CFR）教育大使项目成员，成为北达科他州首位获此荣誉的学者。CFR成立于1921年，是全球最具影响力的国际事务智库之一，其教育大使项目每学年从高中教育者和高校教师中各选80人，任期八个月。德尔坎托·维特拉莱表示，获此殊荣是荣誉也是责任，他计划在太空研究系举办信息说明会，并与校内其他院系及北达科他州教育机构合作，推动全球事务素养教育。","summary_en":"Francisco Del Canto Viterale, associate professor of Space Studies at the University of North Dakota, has been selected as a member of the Council on Foreign Relations' Education Ambassador Program, becoming the first scholar from North Dakota to receive the honor. Founded in 1921, CFR is widely considered one of the world's most influential global affairs think tanks. Its Education Ambassador Program selects 160 ambassadors each academic year—80 high school educators and 80 higher education faculty—for eight-month terms. Del Canto Viterale said the distinction is both an honor and a responsibility, and he plans to hold information sessions in his department and collaborate with other UND colleges and North Dakota educational institutions to promote global affairs literacy.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T13:48:44.999862+00:00","url":"https://blogs.und.edu/und-today/2026/08/und-professor-first-in-nd-to-be-named-council-on-foreign-relations-education-ambassador/","content":"UND professor first in ND to be named Council on Foreign Relations Education Ambassador\nAugust 18, 2026\nby Joe Banish\nPublished in: John D. Odegard School of Aerospace Sciences, Learning\nFrancisco Del Canto Viterale, associate professor of Space Studies, will share his expertise in global affairs as one of 80 higher education ambassadors\nFrancisco Del Canto Viterale.\nA UND faculty member has been named an ambassador to a prestigious international think tank – the first scholar representing North Dakota to achieve this honor.\nFrancisco Del Canto Viterale, associate professor of Space Studies, was recently selected to serve as a member of the Council on Foreign Relations’ (CFR) Education Ambassador Program.\nFounded in 1921, the CFR is widely considered one of the most influential global affairs think tanks in the world. Its mission is to promote informed discourse – both among the public and policymakers – on issues of international relations and geopolitics.\nThe Education Ambassador Program serves as the CFR’s educational arm. Each academic year, a new cohort of 160 ambassadors – 80 high school educators and 80 higher education faculty members – is selected to serve eight-month terms.\n“It is a huge honor to become a CFR higher education ambassador for one of the world’s most prestigious think tanks, and to contribute to the mission of promoting global affairs literacy within my community,” Del Canto Viterale said. “Being the first in North Dakota to receive this distinction is an additional honor and responsibility, and I am eager to help UND students make sense of the world around them.”\n“In today’s interconnected global economy and geopolitical landscape, America’s interests are increasingly intertwined with those of other countries and their citizens,” he added. “To ensure that students understand and engage effectively in today’s interconnected world, it is essential that they be literate in global affairs.”\nAn expert in the intersection between the social sciences and Space Studies, Del Canto Viterale asserted that knowledge in one discipline is corollary to understanding the other.\n“The 21st century is witnessing a new space age, with over 100 countries having space programs or engaging in space-related activities,” he said. “There are nearly 80 government space agencies and more than 10,000 space companies worldwide. Studying the policy, diplomatic, economic, and geopolitical aspects of the new space age provide our UND students with a unique perspective to fully understand the complex reality of space activities.”\nAs a CFR Education Ambassador, Del Canto Viterale will receive educational materials to supplement his curriculum and participate in professional development activities with members of his cohort.\n“I am planning to be active in sharing the relevance and need to understand global issues and their connection with our own reality,” he said. “I plan to offer information sessions in my department of Space Studies, and to collaborate with other colleges and departments at UND and other educational institutions in North Dakota to provide these sessions, given the interdisciplinary nature of the international perspective.”","content_cn":"北达科他大学教授成为外交关系委员会教育大使，北达科他州首位获此殊荣者\n2026年8月18日\n作者：Joe Banish\n发表于：John D. Odegard航空航天科学学院、学习\n空间研究副教授Francisco Del Canto Viterale将作为80名高等教育大使之一，分享其全球事务专业知识\nFrancisco Del Canto Viterale。\n北达科他大学一名教职员工被任命为一家享有盛誉的国际智库大使，成为首位代表北达科他州获得这一荣誉的学者。\n空间研究副教授Francisco Del Canto Viterale最近入选外交关系委员会（CFR）教育大使项目成员。\n外交关系委员会成立于1921年，被广泛认为是世界上最具影响力的全球事务智库之一。其使命是促进公众和政策制定者就国际关系与地缘政治问题开展知情讨论。\n教育大使项目是CFR的教育部门。每学年，一个由160名大使组成的新团队——80名高中教育工作者和80名高等教育教师——将被选出，任期八个月。\nDel Canto Viterale说：“能够成为世界上最负盛名的智库之一——CFR的高等教育大使，并为在社区内推广全球事务素养这一使命作出贡献，是巨大的荣誉。成为北达科他州首位获得这一荣誉的人，又增添了一份荣誉和责任，我很期待帮助北达科他大学的学生理解周围的世界。”\n他补充道：“在当今相互联系的全球经济和地缘政治格局中，美国的利益与其他国家及其公民的利益日益交织在一起。为了确保学生理解并有效参与当今相互联系的世界，让他们具备全球事务素养至关重要。”\n作为社会科学与空间研究交叉领域的专家，Del Canto Viterale主张，对一个学科的知识是理解另一个学科的辅助条件。\n他说：“21世纪正见证一个新的太空时代，已有100多个国家拥有太空计划或参与太空相关活动。全球有近80个政府空间机构和超过10,000家航天企业。研究新太空时代的政策、外交、经济和地缘政治层面，将为北达科他大学学生提供独特视角，使他们全面理解太空活动的复杂现实。”\n作为CFR教育大使，Del Canto Viterale将获得用于补充其课程的教育材料，并与同届成员参加专业发展活动。\n他说：“我计划积极分享理解全球问题及其与我们自身现实联系的重要性和必要性。我计划在空间研究系举办信息分享会，并与北达科他大学及北达科他州其他教育机构的其他学院和系合作提供这些活动，因为国际视角具有跨学科性质。”","publish_source":"blogs.und.edu","publish_time":"2026-08-18T19:30:15+00:00"}},{"id":"news-522","ktid":2572960,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"2572960","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"预告：思科Talos亮相2026年美国黑帽大会","title_en":"Preview: Cisco Talos at Black Hat USA 2026","summary_cn":"思科Talos发布2026年美国黑帽大会参会预告，介绍其在Cisco与Splunk展台的展示安排，包括多场15分钟闪电演讲，主题涵盖攻击者提示工程、Warlock勒索软件、代理身份零信任、漏洞发现趋势等。此外还安排了两场研讨会，分别探讨AI加速漏洞发现与修补，以及自主代理作为内部威胁的风险。","summary_en":"Cisco Talos previews its presence at Black Hat USA 2026, outlining activities at the Cisco and Splunk booth, including 15-minute lightning talks on threat actor prompting, Warlock ransomware, zero trust for agent identity, and vulnerability discovery trends. Two workshops cover AI finding vulnerabilities faster than humans can patch and autonomous agents acting as insider threats.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:55:28.901170+00:00","url":"https://blog.talosintelligence.com/preview-cisco-talos-at-black-hat-usa-2026/","content":"Preview: Cisco Talos at Black Hat USA 2026\nBy\nMitch Neff\nThursday, July 23, 2026 06:00\nWe’re looking forward to having some great conversations with those of you heading to the desert for Hacker Summer Camp 2026. We have a presence within the Cisco and Splunk booth (2633) during Black Hat where you can chat to us about our latest threat research, incident response, and how Talos powers the Cisco portfolio with our intelligence.Or, feel free to pretend to want to talk to us about those things while grabbing a new multicolored Snorty. That’s fine, too.Here’s some of the ways we’ll be showing up at Black Hat, alongside our friends at Cisco and Splunk: Meet the researchers: Booth lightning talks Our Talosians have spent a lot of time over the last few months putting together some truly... well, enlightening lightning talks. Throughout Wednesday and Thursday at Black Hat, you can expect to see such topics as:Threat actor prompting and the emerging ways adversaries are using prompts, agents, skills, and tools to improve efficiencyWarlock ransomware, and why this group does not fit neatly into a simple RaaS or state-linked label.Zero trust for agent identityBuilding a \"second brain\" for your second brainPredicting cybersecurity fraudVulnerability discovery trends... and much moreLightning talks are 15 minutes. That’s less than 9% of The Odyssey. Don’t worry, we cut the bit where everyone gets turned into Snorty pigs.Talos workshop: When AI finds vulnerabilities faster than humans can patch Date/Time: Wednesday, August 5 | 1:30 p.m. – 3:00 p.m. (Oceanside E, Level 2)If you're looking for something hands-on and interactive, don't miss our workshop with Talos’ Nick Biasini and Cisco’s Omar Santos. In two parts, they’ll demonstrate practical ways security teams can incorporate AI into SOC workflows to identify sophisticated adversary behavior.In Part 1, Omar will discuss the Foundry Security Spec. He’ll walk through how to deploy, build testing harnesses around its core agent roles, and integrate Project CodeGuard so that findings from autonomous testing can be converted into reusable secure-coding rules and future prevention. In Part 2, Nick will demonstrate how Talos leverages AI to transform threat hunting. We will explore best practices for identifying adversarial AI tactics and provide attendees with insights into how Cisco Talos is leveraging AI for defense. Participants will learn how to integrate these defensive AI strategies into their own SOC workflows.  Splunk workshop: When agents become insider threats Date/Time: Wednesday, August 5 | 10:15 a.m. – 11:00 a.m. (Mandalay Bay I)The Splunk workshop considers the fact that the next insider threat may not be a person; it may be an autonomous agent using valid credentials and delegated authority. Attendees will see real-world attack paths in which agents move sensitive data across tools, distribute brute-force attempts under a single delegation, and manipulate internal systems without triggering traditional SIEM or UEBA alerts. It was Talos all alongOne of the questions we hear often is: \"How do I buy Talos?\"The answer… is that you probably already did.Throughout the Cisco booth you'll see our “It was Talos all along” campaign, highlighting the fact that Talos isn't a standalone product or a threat intelligence feed you bolt onto your security stack. Talos is already embedded across the Cisco security portfolio, which continually benefits from our threat research and intelligence.To build your curiosity, take a look at our new video, “Where Protection Starts,” to see how Cisco Talos Intelligence Integrations help reduce uncertainty in the SOC:See you in Las Vegas.\nShare this post","content_cn":"预告：Cisco Talos亮相Black Hat USA 2026\n作者\nMitch Neff\n2026年7月23日，星期四 06:00\n我们期待与前往沙漠参加2026年黑客夏令营的各位展开精彩交流。在Black Hat期间，我们将在Cisco和Splunk展位（2633）设有展台，您可以在那里与我们聊聊最新的威胁研究、事件响应，以及Talos如何通过我们的情报为Cisco产品组合提供支持。\n或者，您也可以假装想和我们聊这些话题，同时拿走一个全新的彩色Snorty。这样也没问题。\n以下是我们将在Black Hat与Cisco和Splunk的朋友们一起亮相的几种方式：\n与研究人员见面：展位闪电演讲\n我们的Talos团队成员过去几个月投入了大量时间，准备了一些真正……嗯，启发人心的闪电演讲。在Black Hat的周三和周四，您可以期待看到以下主题：\n威胁行为者提示词，以及对手利用提示词、代理、技能和工具提高效率的新兴方式\nWarlock勒索软件，以及为什么该组织无法简单归入RaaS或国家关联标签\n代理身份的零信任\n为你的“第二大脑”打造一个“第二大脑”\n预测网络安全欺诈\n漏洞发现趋势……以及更多\n闪电演讲时长为15分钟。这不到《奥德赛》的9%。别担心，我们删掉了所有人变成Snorty猪的那一段。\nTalos工作坊：当AI发现漏洞的速度超过人类修补漏洞的速度\n日期/时间：8月5日，星期三 | 下午1:30 – 下午3:00（Oceanside E，2层）\n如果您想参加动手实践且具有互动性的活动，不要错过我们与Talos的Nick Biasini和Cisco的Omar Santos共同举办的工作坊。他们将分两部分展示安全团队如何将AI切实融入SOC工作流程，以识别复杂的对手行为。\n第一部分中，Omar将讨论Foundry Security Spec。他将演示如何部署它、围绕其核心代理角色构建测试工具，并集成Project CodeGuard，以便将自主测试的发现转化为可复用的安全编码规则和未来的预防措施。\n第二部分中，Nick将演示Talos如何利用AI改变威胁狩猎。我们将探讨识别对抗性AI战术的最佳实践，并向参加者介绍Cisco Talos如何利用AI进行防御。参加者将学习如何把这些防御性AI策略整合到自己的SOC工作流程中。\nSplunk工作坊：当代理成为内部威胁\n日期/时间：8月5日，星期三 | 上午10:15 – 上午11:00（Mandalay Bay I）\nSplunk工作坊探讨这样一个事实：下一次内部威胁可能不是人，而可能是一个使用有效凭据和受委派权限的自主代理。参加者将看到现实世界中的攻击路径：代理在工具之间传输敏感数据，在单次委派权限下分发暴力破解尝试，并操纵内部系统，而不会触发传统SIEM或UEBA警报。\n原来一直都是Talos\n我们经常听到的一个问题是：“我该如何购买Talos？”\n答案是……你可能已经买过了。\n在整个Cisco展位，您都会看到我们的“原来一直都是Talos”宣传活动，强调Talos并不是一个独立产品，也不是可以附加到安全技术栈上的威胁情报源。Talos已经嵌入Cisco的整个安全产品组合，而该组合持续受益于我们的威胁研究和情报。\n为了激发您的好奇心，请观看我们的新视频《保护从这里开始》，了解Cisco Talos Intelligence Integrations如何帮助减少SOC中的不确定性：\n拉斯维加斯见。\n分享这篇文章","publish_source":"blog.talosintelligence.com","publish_time":"2026-07-23T10:00:14+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1382","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"若获确认，参议员马林将成为国土安全部的下一场灾难？","title_en":"If Confirmed, Will Senator Markwayne Mullin Be DHS’s Next Disaster? - Union of Concerned Scientists","summary_cn":"忧思科学家联盟发文反对参议员马克韦恩·马林出任国土安全部长的提名，认为其缺乏国家安全、移民政策和应急管理经验，且是气候变化否认者。文章重点质疑其对联邦应急管理局（FEMA）的立场，呼吁参议院国土安全与政府事务委员会在3月18日听证会上严格审查并投反对票。","summary_en":"The Union of Concerned Scientists opposes Senator Markwayne Mullin's nomination to lead the Department of Homeland Security, citing his lack of national security, immigration and emergency management experience and his climate denial. The piece focuses on his stance toward FEMA and urges the Senate Homeland Security committee to scrutinize him at the March 18 hearing and vote no.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:22:33.205536+00:00","url":"https://blog.ucs.org/shana-udvardy/if-confirmed-will-senator-markwayne-mullin-will-be-dhss-next-disaster","content":"If Confirmed, Will Senator Markwayne Mullin Be DHS’s Next Disaster?\nMarch 17, 2026 | 2:08 pm\nWin McNamee/Getty Images\nShana Udvardy\nSenior Climate Resilience Policy Analyst\nSenator Markwayne Mullin Is Unqualified to run DHS and its Nine Agencies, Including Diminished FEMA\nOn March 18, the Senate Homeland Security and Government Affairs Committee will hold a confirmation hearing for Senator Markwayne Mullin, a Republican from Oklahoma—President Trump’s nominee for secretary of the Department of Homeland Security (DHS). A vote will follow the next day, when by all accounts he’ll likely be confirmed even though the Senator is uniquely unqualified to lead the third largest federal department with a half a million employees, nine agencies including ICE, FEMA and the Coast Guard among others, and roughly a $100 billion budget.\nThe Union of Concerned Scientists (UCS) strongly opposes Senator Mullin’s nomination, and we ask members of the committee to thoroughly interrogate his qualifications and vote no on Thursday.\nIf confirmed, Senator Mullin would be yet another unqualified member of President Trump’s particularly unqualified cabinet. Senator Mullin could be counted on to continue the same harmful, destructive leadership as his fired predecessor, Kristi Noem, who has been called “the worst DHS Secretary since the agency was formed.” Secretary Noem implemented vicious and deadly immigration policies and called for FEMA to be dismantled, leaving the agency in disarray. We can’t afford to let this happen.\nIt’s critical that senators closely examine Senator Mullin’s qualifications to run DHS and question him regarding the damage done by his predecessor’s extreme, destructive agenda.\nSenator Mullin uniquely unqualified to lead DHS\nSenator Mullin represented Eastern Oklahoma in the US House of Representatives from 2013 until 2023, when he was elected to the US Senate. Senator Mullin has little to no professional experience that makes him qualified to be Secretary of DHS and it is unlikely that he would lead the department in a way that serves the public interest. He has no experience in national security, immigration policy, or emergency management and does not serve on the Senate Homeland Security Committee.\nHe has, however,\nBeen on the record as a climate denier as climate change is accelerating and driving more costly and disruptive extreme weather and disasters nationwide, while receiving more than $1.4 million in fossil fuel industry contributions.\nBacked extreme immigration policies in Congress, such as defending violent actions after immigration agents fatally shot Alex Pretti and Renee Good in Minneapolis, Senator Mullin defended the officers and criticized the victims.\nReportedly used insider knowledge as a member of the US Armed Services Committee to make considerable financial gains to his stock portfolio, increasing his jaw-dropping $66 million net worth which makes him the fourth-richest Senator in Congress.\nVoted against certifying the 2020 elections and defended the pardon of the January 6 rioters.\nQuestions senators should ask Senator Mullin\nThere are questions galore to ask Senator Mullin, particularly about deadly, inhumane, unconstitutional actions taken by ICE. Because I am a senior climate resilience policy analyst who works on safeguarding communities from climate change-related risks and impacts, my focus here is on how the senator would manage FEMA on disaster preparedness, response, and recovery.\nThere were 23 separate billion-dollar extreme weather and climate change-related disasters last year. Recent reports find that global warming is accelerating and the impacts are playing out before our eyes with more frequent and intense flooding, extreme heat, and wildfires. Secretary Noem is leaving FEMA ill-prepared for the upcoming Atlantic Hurricane season that begins this June.\nHere are the questions that I hope members of the Senate Homeland Security and Government Affairs Committee will ask Senator Mullin that reflect my top concerns regarding FEMA:\nWill you continue to implement the goal of President Trump and former Secretary Noem to dismantle FEMA, or will you implement badly needed measures to ensure that FEMA fulfills its essential role and functions?\nOne year ago, former Secretary Noem called for FEMA to be eliminated and then walked it back to say the agency should be dismantled. Noem in many ways met this goal by severely reducing staff by 20%, draining much of the expertise at FEMA headquarters and cutting Cadre of On‑Call Response and Recovery (CORE) staff with plans for 41% cuts in the CORE team, causing a bottleneck on spending approvals, delaying disaster assistance and generally creating a hostile work environment. Based on Senator Mullin’s record, I’m doubtful that he’ll defend FEMA against President Trump’s attacks on the agency.\nThe Union of Concerned Scientists submitted comments to the FEMA review council offering five major buckets of reforms the council should consider, including: 1) Strengthen FEMA and its internal systems; 2) Improve FEMA’s role in disaster response and recovery; 3) Restore resilience programs; 4) Advocate for modernization and reform of National Flood Insurance Program; and 5) Restore climate and equity to all FEMA standards, programs and guidance. Strengthening FEMA requires hiring and rehiring staff, returning FEMA to a cabinet-level agency and nominating a qualified FEMA administrator.\nIf Senator Mullin is confirmed, his first order of business must be to repeal former Secretary Noem’s requirement to review expenditures over $100,000, largely disliked by members on both sides of the aisle who want to see funding allocations speed up significantly to better help communities recover and shore up their resilience efforts.\nUnfortunately, this won’t necessarily change the policies under this administration that push state and local governments to take on more of the costs of disaster response and recovery. This could mean fewer disaster declarations which would hurt those states and local governments with the least resources and those that have been hit with back-to-back disasters the most. While the impacts of such policies could be felt broadly, historically disadvantaged communities, rural areas, people with disabilities and the elderly will be hurt first and worst.\nFEMA has obstructed Congress’ oversight responsibilities by failing to respond to congressional requests for information. Will you ensure transparent and prompt responses to congressional oversight of DHS and FEMA?\nEarlier this month, Senator Welch co-authored a letter to the DHS inspector general (IG) with four other Senators asking the IG to investigate all complaints into FEMA.  The letter speaks to how FEMA whistleblowers have been retaliated against and the lack of a Senate-confirmed FEMA administrator is “fueling widespread employee uncertainty and policy whiplash.” Last summer, many concerns such as these and more rose to such a level that former and current FEMA staff signed a letter to Congress titled the Katrina Declaration to raise alarm that many of the safeguards put into place by Post-Katrina Emergency Management Reform Act of 2006 were not holding up.\nHow will you handle political standoffs such as what is going on currently with the DHS budget given the critical need to fund FEMA, among other agencies, as the Atlantic hurricane season approaches?\nIt’s very concerning that FEMA’s Disaster Relief Fund (DRF) is running low and that it’s caught up in the Department of Homeland Security (DHS)-specific shutdown. Typically, FEMA can withstand these types of funding dips but we’re not talking normal times. The Trump administration has delayed and denied disaster assistance even as communities are still recovering from the record 2024 wildfires and hurricanes and as the Atlantic Hurricane season approaches, it’s essential that FEMA’s mission is protected and concerns about FEMA funding are not used to justify continued funding for DHS without significant reform. The DHS budget fight and issues with former Secretary Noem underscore why FEMA should be re-established as an independent, cabinet-level agency and why it’s long overdue for the president to nominate a FEMA administrator with the requisite emergency management qualifications.\nWill you advise against President Trump’s illegal cancellation of federal grants, withholding and delaying FEMA disaster assistance and continued use of FEMA and other DHS resources to support mass deportations, or withhold them to punish states and localities that refuse to participate in them without due process?\nThe federal government watchdogs, the US Government Accountability Office (GAO) found that former Secretary Noem violated the Impoundment Control Act (ICA) by withholding or delaying the allocation of funding for FEMA programs including the Emergency Food and Shelter Program, the Shelter and Services Program, and the Next Generation Warning System Grants Program.\nThe Trump administration illegally canceled the Building Resilient Infrastructure and Communities (BRIC) program that US District Court Judge Stearns has ordered FEMA to reinstate for the second time. The administration also rescinded the Federal Flood Risk Management Standard (FFRMS) that simply ensured federally funded projects would be built to withstand future flooding, saving federal taxpayer dollars.\nDenials and delays in approval of disaster declarations and cost-sharing with the federal government have added a layer of uncertainty in local and state government budget planning at a time when these local officials are already feeling the impacts of President Trump’s One Big Beautiful Bill Act (OBBBA) passed last July.\nIt’s a Catch-22 when states and local governments need to invest in climate adaptation to be more resilient to climate change while much of the funding they rely on comes from the federal government. A year ago, President Trump released an executive order that called for pushing the burden of disaster response and recovery on to states and local governments, among other things. Most state and local governments don’t have the resources to invest in adequate levels of resilience.\nWe need close oversight of the acting FEMA administrator and the new DHS secretary to ensure the essential funding in the Disaster Recovery Fund isn’t diverted towards other accounts, which has happened previously under this administration.\nWith the impacts of fossil-fueled climate change accelerating, DHS needs a qualified and steady hand at the helm\nCongress must ensure the March 18 confirmation hearing is not a sham. Senator Markwayne Mullin lacks qualifications to lead homeland security, much less FEMA.\nAs extreme weather and disasters are increasingly showing up in people’s everyday lives, communities across the nation need a qualified and steady leader at DHS.\nSenator Mullin has vowed to be open to listening to his colleagues on both sides of the aisle, however his actions to date have proven his allegiance to President Trump and this does not bode well for disaster victims who continue to wait on assistance, the DHS agency staff not being paid during the budget shutdown, or for communities that have suffered at the hands of ICE.\nThe Union of Concerned Scientists strongly opposes Senator Mullin as the nominee for DHS, and we ask members of the Senate’s Homeland Security and Government Affairs Committee to vote NO on this nomination.\nPart of a series on Danger SeasonRead the series\nPosted in:\nClimate Change, Science and Democracy\nTags:\nclimate change and hurricanes, climate impacts, Danger Season, disaster recovery, emergency preparedness, FEMA, Second Trump Administration\nShare\nBlueSky\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\nAbout the author\nMore from Shana\nShana Udvardy is a senior climate resilience policy analyst with the Climate & Energy program at the Union of Concerned Scientists. She conducts research and policy analysis to help inform and build support to increase resilience to climate change impacts.\nMore like this\nEric Thayer/Getty Images\nSeptember 3, 2026\nFossil Fuel-Driven Climate Change is Worsening Wildfire Seasons\nCarly Phillips\nSenior Scientist\nJustin Sullivan/Getty Images\nAugust 25, 2026\n3 Ways Scientists Can Help Hold Major Polluters Accountable Under the Trump Administration\nCarly Phillips\nSenior Scientist\nMario Tama/Getty Images\nAugust 20, 2026\nHow Climate Change Is Drying up the Western US\nUCS Science Network","content_cn":"若获确认，参议员马克韦恩·穆林会成为国土安全部的下一场灾难吗？\n2026年3月17日 | 下午2:08\nWin McNamee/Getty Images\n沙娜·乌德瓦迪\n高级气候韧性政策分析师\n参议员马克韦恩·穆林没有资格执掌国土安全部及其九个机构，包括已被削弱的联邦应急管理署\n3月18日，参议院国土安全与政府事务委员会将就俄克拉荷马州共和党参议员马克韦恩·穆林举行确认听证会——他是特朗普总统提名的国土安全部（DHS）部长人选。次日将进行投票，从各方面来看，他很可能会获得确认，尽管这位参议员格外没有资格领导这个拥有50万雇员、包括移民和海关执法局（ICE）、联邦应急管理署（FEMA）和海岸警卫队等在内的九个机构、预算约1000亿美元的第三大联邦部门。\n忧思科学家联盟（UCS）强烈反对穆林参议员的提名，我们请求委员会成员彻底质询他的资格，并在周四投下反对票。\n若获确认，穆林参议员将成为特朗普总统这个格外不称职的内阁中又一位不称职的成员。可以指望穆林参议员延续其被解职的前任克里斯蒂·诺姆同样有害、破坏性的领导风格——诺姆被称为“该机构成立以来最糟糕的国土安全部部长”。诺姆部长实施了残暴且致命的移民政策，并呼吁解散FEMA，使该机构陷入混乱。我们不能让这种情况发生。\n参议员们必须仔细审查穆林参议员执掌国土安全部的资格，并就其前任极端、破坏性议程所造成的损害对他进行质询，这一点至关重要。\n穆林参议员格外没有资格领导国土安全部\n穆林参议员于2013年至2023年在美国众议院代表俄克拉荷马州东部，随后当选为美国参议员。穆林参议员几乎没有或完全没有能使他胜任国土安全部部长的专业经验，而且他不太可能以符合公共利益的方式领导该部门。他在国家安全、移民政策或应急管理方面没有经验，也不在参议院国土安全委员会任职。\n然而，他确实：\n在气候变化加速、并在全国范围内引发代价更高、破坏性更强的极端天气和灾害之际，公开记录显示他是一名气候变化否认者，同时收受了超过140万美元的化石燃料行业政治献金。\n在国会支持极端移民政策，例如在移民执法人员于明尼阿波利斯致命枪击亚历克斯·普雷蒂和蕾妮·古德之后为暴力行为辩护，穆林参议员为涉事警员辩护并批评受害者。\n据报道，他利用作为美国军事委员会成员的内幕信息为其股票投资组合谋取可观财务收益，使其令人瞠目的6600万美元净资产进一步增加，成为国会中第四富有的参议员。\n投票反对认证2020年选举结果，并为赦免1月6日骚乱者辩护。\n参议员们应当向穆林参议员提出的问题\n有大量问题要问穆林参议员，尤其是关于ICE采取的致命、不人道、违宪的行为。由于我是一名高级气候韧性政策分析师，致力于保护社区免受气候变化相关风险和影响，我在此的关注重点是该参议员将如何管理FEMA在灾害准备、响应和恢复方面的工作。\n去年发生了23起单独的、损失达十亿美元级的极端天气和气候变化相关灾害。近期报告发现，全球变暖正在加速，其影响正呈现在我们眼前，表现为更频繁、更强烈的洪水、极端高温和野火。诺姆部长让FEMA对即将于今年6月开始的大西洋飓风季准备不足。\n以下是我希望参议院国土安全与政府事务委员会成员向穆林参议员提出的问题，它们反映了我对FEMA最关切的几个方面：\n你会继续执行特朗普总统和前部长诺姆解散FEMA的目标，还是会采取亟需的措施，确保FEMA履行其基本职责和职能？\n一年前，前部长诺姆呼吁取消FEMA，随后又改口称该机构应被解散。诺姆在许多方面实现了这一目标，将人员大幅削减20%，抽空了FEMA总部的大量专业力量\n[正文过长，翻译截断；对象库保留全文]","publish_source":"blog.ucs.org","publish_time":"2026-03-17T14:08:26-04:00"}},{"id":"news-3249","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"联邦调查局称上月已关闭多元化与包容办公室","title_en":"FBI closed DEI office last month, says the agency","summary_cn":"BNO News报道，美国联邦调查局（FBI）证实已于2024年12月关闭其多元化与包容办公室（ODI），但未说明原因。此举发生在共和党议员推动取消联邦机构DEI项目、众议院监督委员会通过相关法案之后，也与当选总统特朗普承诺取消政府DEI计划的表态一致。特朗普随后在社交平台要求FBI保留该办公室全部记录。","summary_en":"BNO News reports that the FBI confirmed it closed its Office of Diversity and Inclusion in December 2024 without giving a reason. The move follows Republican pressure to eliminate DEI programs in federal agencies and aligns with President-elect Trump's campaign pledges. Trump later demanded on Truth Social that the FBI preserve all records of the now-closing office.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:31:57.959770+00:00","url":"https://bnonews.com/index.php/2025/01/fbi-closed-dei-office-last-month-says-the-agency","content":"Politics\nFBI closed DEI office last month, says the agency\nPublished on\nJanuary 16, 2025\nBy Carlos Robles\nFile photo: J. Edgar Hoover FBI Building in D.C. (Credit: Billy Hathorn)\nAdvertisment17\nShare\nTweet\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) has confirmed the closure of its Office of Diversity and Inclusion (ODI) in December, according to Fox News. The agency did not provide an explanation for the decision.\n“In recent weeks, the FBI took steps to close the Office of Diversity and Inclusion (ODI), effective by December 2024,” the agency said in a statement provided to Fox News on Thursday.\nAlthough the statement did not specify the reasons for the closure, the decision follows accusations from Republican lawmakers that the FBI was wrongfully prioritizing DEI initiatives. It also comes after a Republican-led push to eliminate DEI programs in federal agencies.\nRepresentative Michael Cloud (R-TX) introduced the “Dismantle DEI Act,” a bill to ban DEI initiatives in federal agencies, in June last year. The bill, sponsored in the Senate by Senator JD Vance, who is set to become Vice President, passed the House Oversight Committee in November. However, it did not proceed to a vote before the conclusion of the previous Congress.\nArticle continues below the player\nThe FBI’s decision aligns with campaign promises made by President-elect Donald Trump, who is set to take office on Monday, to eliminate DEI initiatives across the government, according to the New York Post.\n“We demand that the FBI preserve and retain all records, documents, and information on the now closing DEI Office,” Trump said in a post on his platform, Truth Social, following the news. “Never should have been opened and, if it was, should have closed long ago. Why is it that they’re closing one day before the Inauguration of a new Administration? The reason is, CORRUPTION!”\nDiversity, Equity, and Inclusion (DEI) initiatives have become a polarizing topic in recent years. Critics argue that such programs undermine meritocracy, suppress free expression, or foster reverse discrimination, while proponents view DEI as vital for addressing systemic inequalities.\nRelated Topics:DEI ProgramsFederal Bureau of Investigation (FBI)United States\nAdvertisment15\nAdvertisment5\nLatest\nLegal9 hours ago\nMan accused of funding ISIS recruits extradited to U.S.\nPolitics10 hours ago\nColombia cuts ties with Iran, declares IRGC a terrorist group\nBusiness10 hours ago\nNew York sues Polymarket over alleged illegal gambling\nUS News11 hours ago\nButler Trump rally shooting survivor James Copenhaver dies at 76\nAdvertisment4\nTrending\nUS News1 week ago\n3 killed, 1 injured as NBC Los Angeles helicopter crashes while covering deadly collision\nLegal5 days ago\nMan seriously injured in ICE shooting in Austin, Texas\nWorld1 week ago\nCatholic priest found murdered near road in central Mexico\nAdvertisment6\nMost Viewed\nUS News1 week ago\n3 killed, 1 injured as NBC Los Angeles helicopter crashes while covering deadly collision\nLegal5 days ago\nMan seriously injured in ICE shooting in Austin, Texas\nWorld1 week ago\nCatholic priest found murdered near road in central Mexico\nLegal1 week ago\nPennsylvania man charged over alleged ISIS-inspired mass shooting plot\nLegal5 days ago\n8 shot at social gathering in Sanford, Florida; 2 critically injured\nLegal5 days ago\nDelaware deer hunter charged after fatally shooting woman he mistook for deer\nLegal4 days ago\nGunman opens fire into crowd of 400 juveniles near St. Louis; suspect shot by police\nLegal1 week ago\nISIS-K operative sentenced to 20 years for role in Kabul airport attack\nCopyright © 2026 BNO News, B.V. All rights reserved.\nAbout Us | Privacy Policy | Terms | BNO en Español | Contact Us","content_cn":"政治\nFBI上个月关闭DEI办公室，机构称\n发布于\n2025年1月16日\n作者：Carlos Robles\n资料照片：华盛顿特区的J. Edgar Hoover FBI大楼。（图片来源：Billy Hathorn）\n广告17\n分享\n推文\n据福克斯新闻报道，美国联邦调查局（FBI）已确认于12月关闭其多元化与包容性办公室（ODI）。该机构未就此决定作出解释。\n该机构周四在向福克斯新闻提供的一份声明中表示：“最近几周，FBI采取措施关闭多元化与包容性办公室（ODI），该关闭于2024年12月生效。”\n尽管声明未说明关闭原因，但这一决定是在共和党议员指责FBI不当优先推进DEI倡议之后作出的。此前，共和党人也推动取消联邦机构中的DEI项目。\n得克萨斯州共和党众议员Michael Cloud去年6月提出《拆除DEI法案》，旨在禁止联邦机构开展DEI倡议。该法案由即将出任副总统的参议员JD Vance在参议院发起赞助，并于11月在众议院监督委员会获得通过。然而，在上一届国会结束前，该法案未进入表决程序。\n文章在播放器下方继续\n据《纽约邮报》报道，FBI的决定与当选总统Donald Trump的竞选承诺一致；Trump将于周一就职，并承诺取消政府各部门的DEI倡议。\n消息传出后，Trump在其平台Truth Social发文称：“我们要求FBI保存并保留有关现正关闭的DEI办公室的所有记录、文件和信息。这个办公室本就不该成立，如果成立了，也早该关闭。为什么他们在新政府就职前一天关闭它？原因就是，腐败！”\n近年来，多元化、公平与包容（DEI）倡议已成为一个两极分化的话题。批评者认为，这类项目损害择优原则、压制言论自由，或助长逆向歧视；支持者则认为，DEI对于解决系统性不平等至关重要。\n相关主题：DEI项目；美国联邦调查局（FBI）；美国\n广告15\n广告5\n最新\n法律 9小时前\n被控资助ISIS招募人员的男子被引渡至美国\n政治 10小时前\n哥伦比亚与伊朗断交，宣布伊斯兰革命卫队为恐怖组织\n商业 10小时前\n纽约就涉嫌非法赌博起诉Polymarket\n美国新闻 11小时前\nButler Trump集会枪击案幸存者James Copenhaver去世，享年76岁\n广告4\n热门\n美国新闻 1周前\nNBC洛杉矶直升机在报道致命碰撞事故时坠毁，3人死亡、1人受伤\n法律 5天前\n男子在得克萨斯州奥斯汀ICE枪击事件中重伤\n世界 1周前\n天主教神父被发现遭谋杀，遗体位于墨西哥中部一条道路附近\n广告6\n浏览最多\n美国新闻 1周前\nNBC洛杉矶直升机在报道致命碰撞事故时坠毁，3人死亡、1人受伤\n法律 5天前\n男子在得克萨斯州奥斯汀ICE枪击事件中重伤\n世界 1周前\n天主教神父被发现遭谋杀，遗体位于墨西哥中部一条道路附近\n法律 1周前\n宾夕法尼亚州男子因涉嫌策划受ISIS启发的大规模枪击案被控罪\n法律 5天前\n佛罗里达州Sanford社交聚会发生枪击，8人中枪；2人伤势危重\n法律 5天前\n特拉华州猎鹿人误将女子当作鹿而开枪致其死亡，遭起诉\n法律 4天前\n枪手向圣路易斯附近400名未成年人组成的人群开火；嫌疑人被警方击中\n法律 1周前\nISIS-K成员因在喀布尔机场袭击中所扮演角色被判20年监禁\n版权所有 © 2026 BNO News, B.V. 保留所有权利。\n关于我们 | 隐私政策 | 条款 | BNO西班牙语版 | 联系我们","publish_source":"bnonews.com","publish_time":"2025-01-17T03:21:34+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2613","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"前FBI局长之女莫琳·科米被解职联邦检察官职务","title_en":"Maurene Comey, daughter of former FBI director, fired from federal prosecutor post","summary_cn":"据媒体报道，纽约南区联邦检察官、前FBI局长詹姆斯·科米之女莫琳·科米已被解职。有消息人士向CNN表示“在现政府中身为科米家人难以立足”，并提及詹姆斯·科米对特朗普的公开批评及针对其是否向国会作虚假陈述的调查。莫琳曾参与爱泼斯坦、麦克斯韦尔及肖恩·“吹牛老爹”·库姆斯等案件。FBI在局长卡什·帕特尔领导下正审查詹姆斯·科米5月发布的一条已删除社交媒体帖文。司法部尚未公开回应解职一事。","summary_en":"Maurene Comey, a federal prosecutor in the Southern District of New York and daughter of former FBI Director James Comey, has been fired, according to media reports. A source told CNN that \"being a Comey is untenable in this administration,\" citing James Comey's public criticism of President Trump and an ongoing investigation into whether he made false statements to Congress. Maurene Comey previously worked on high-profile cases including the prosecutions of Jeffrey Epstein, Ghislaine Maxwell and Sean \"Diddy\" Combs. The FBI, under Director Kash Patel, is reviewing a deleted May social media post by James Comey. The Justice Department has not publicly addressed her termination.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:06:19.191179+00:00","url":"https://bnonews.com/index.php/2025/07/maurene-comey-daughter-of-former-fbi-director-fired-from-federal-prosecutor-post","content":"Politics\nMaurene Comey, daughter of former FBI director, fired from federal prosecutor post\nPublished on\nJuly 16, 2025\nBy Carlos Robles\nFile photo (Credit: Associated Press)\nAdvertisment17\nShare\nTweet\nMaurene Comey, a federal prosecutor in the Southern District of New York and the daughter of former FBI Director James Comey, has been fired from her position, according to media outlets.\nA person familiar with the situation told CNN that “being a Comey is untenable in this administration,” referencing James Comey’s public criticism of President Donald Trump and an ongoing investigation into whether the former FBI director made false statements to Congress.\nMaurene Comey was previously involved in several high-profile federal prosecutions, including the investigation and trial of accused sex trafficker Jeffrey Epstein and his associate Ghislaine Maxwell. Maxwell was convicted and sentenced to 20 years in prison, a conviction she has since appealed. More recently, Comey served as a prosecutor in the case against Sean “Diddy” Combs.\nComey and her team faced a partial setback in the Combs case, with the jury acquitting the performer on more serious charges, including racketeering conspiracy and sex trafficking. However, Combs was found guilty on two counts of violating the Mann Act, which prohibits transporting individuals across state lines for prostitution.\nArticle continues below the player\nThe dismissal of Maurene Comey comes amid renewed scrutiny of her father, former FBI Director James Comey. The FBI, under Director Kash Patel, is reviewing a deleted social media post made by James Comey in May that appeared to reference President Trump.\nThe post featured the number “8647” arranged with shells on a beach and was captioned, “Cool shell formation on my beach walk.” While no direct threats were made, the inclusion of “86”—slang for “get rid of”—and “47”—a number often associated with Trump as the potential 47th president—prompted backlash from the Trump administration.\nMaurene Comey’s termination has not been publicly addressed by the Department of Justice.\nRelated Topics:Department of Justice (DOJ)James ComeyMaurene ComeyUnited States\nAdvertisment15\nAdvertisment5\nLatest\nLegal35 mins ago\nFlorida student arrested over school shooting threat on Roblox\nWorld20 hours ago\nSon of Israeli ambassador to U.S. critically injured in West Bank ramming attack\nPolitics21 hours ago\nMilei says Argentina will ‘take matters into its own hands’ over Falklands\nBusiness21 hours ago\nAustralia says OpenAI agent bypassed blocks to access government files\nAdvertisment4\nTrending\nUS News1 week ago\n3 killed, 1 injured as NBC Los Angeles helicopter crashes while covering deadly collision\nLegal4 days ago\nMan seriously injured in ICE shooting in Austin, Texas\nWorld1 week ago\nCatholic priest found murdered near road in central Mexico\nAdvertisment6\nMost Viewed\nUS News1 week ago\n3 killed, 1 injured as NBC Los Angeles helicopter crashes while covering deadly collision\nLegal4 days ago\nMan seriously injured in ICE shooting in Austin, Texas\nWorld1 week ago\nCatholic priest found murdered near road in central Mexico\nLegal1 week ago\nPennsylvania man charged over alleged ISIS-inspired mass shooting plot\nLegal4 days ago\n8 shot at social gathering in Sanford, Florida; 2 critically injured\nLegal4 days ago\nDelaware deer hunter charged after fatally shooting woman he mistook for deer\nLegal4 days ago\nGunman opens fire into crowd of 400 juveniles near St. Louis; suspect shot by police\nLegal1 week ago\nISIS-K operative sentenced to 20 years for role in Kabul airport attack\nCopyright © 2026 BNO News, B.V. All rights reserved.\nAbout Us | Privacy Policy | Terms | BNO en Español | Contact Us","content_cn":"政治\n前联邦调查局局长之女莫琳·科米被解雇，失去联邦检察官职位\n发布于\n2025年7月16日\n作者 Carlos Robles\n资料照片（图片来源：美联社）\n广告17\n分享\n推文\n据媒体报道，纽约南区联邦检察官、前联邦调查局局长詹姆斯·科米的女儿莫琳·科米已被解雇。\n一名熟悉情况的人士告诉CNN：“在本届政府任职，身为科米是无法接受的”，此话指的是詹姆斯·科米公开批评唐纳德·特朗普总统，以及针对这名前联邦调查局局长是否向国会作出虚假陈述的持续调查。\n莫琳·科米此前参与过数起备受关注的联邦起诉案件，包括对被指控从事性交易的杰弗里·爱泼斯坦及其同伙吉斯兰·麦克斯韦的调查和审判。麦克斯韦被判有罪并获刑20年，此后已提出上诉。最近，科米还担任肖恩·“吹牛老爹”·科姆斯案件的检察官。\n科米及其团队在科姆斯案中遭遇部分挫折，陪审团宣判这名艺人较严重的敲诈勒索共谋和性交易等指控不成立。不过，科姆斯被判两项违反《曼恩法》罪名成立；该法禁止为卖淫目的将个人跨州运输。\n文章在播放器下方继续\n莫琳·科米被解雇之际，其父亲、前联邦调查局局长詹姆斯·科米再次受到审查。在局长卡什·帕特尔领导下，联邦调查局正在审查詹姆斯·科米5月发布的一条已删除社交媒体帖子，该帖子似乎影射特朗普总统。\n帖子展示了用贝壳在海滩上排列成的数字“8647”，配文为：“在海滩散步时看到的酷贝壳图案。”尽管没有直接威胁，但“86”包含“摆脱掉”的俚语含义，而“47”常被用来指代特朗普可能成为第47任总统，这引发了特朗普政府的反弹。\n司法部尚未公开回应莫琳·科米被解雇一事。\n相关主题：司法部（DOJ）、詹姆斯·科米、莫琳·科米、美国\n广告15\n广告5\n最新\n法律 35分钟前\n佛罗里达州学生因在Roblox上发布校园枪击威胁被捕\n世界 20小时前\n以色列驻美大使之子在约旦河西岸冲撞袭击中受重伤\n政治 21小时前\n米莱称阿根廷将就福克兰群岛“自行采取行动”\n商业 21小时前\n澳大利亚称OpenAI代理绕过拦截访问政府文件\n广告4\n热门\n美国新闻 1周前\nNBC洛杉矶直升机在报道致命碰撞事故时坠毁，3人死亡、1人受伤\n法律 4天前\n男子在得克萨斯州奥斯汀遭移民与海关执法局枪击，受重伤\n世界 1周前\n天主教牧师被发现遭谋杀，地点在墨西哥中部一条道路附近\n广告6\n最多浏览\n美国新闻 1周前\nNBC洛杉矶直升机在报道致命碰撞事故时坠毁，3人死亡、1人受伤\n法律 4天前\n男子在得克萨斯州奥斯汀遭移民与海关执法局枪击，受重伤\n世界 1周前\n天主教牧师被发现遭谋杀，地点在墨西哥中部一条道路附近\n法律 1周前\n宾夕法尼亚州男子因涉嫌策划受“伊斯兰国”启发的大规模枪击被控罪\n法律 4天前\n佛罗里达州桑福德社交聚会上8人中枪，2人重伤\n法律 4天前\n特拉华州猎鹿人误将女子当作鹿射杀后被控罪\n法律 4天前\n枪手在圣路易斯附近向400名青少年人群开火；嫌疑人遭警方击中\n法律 1周前\n“呼罗珊省伊斯兰国”成员因参与喀布尔机场袭击被判20年\n版权所有 © 2026 BNO News, B.V. 保留所有权利。\n关于我们 | 隐私政策 | 条款 | BNO西班牙语 | 联系我们","publish_source":"bnonews.com","publish_time":"2025-07-17T01:47:16+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1816","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"明尼阿波利斯联邦车辆遭破坏，FBI悬赏10万美元","title_en":"FBI offers $100,000 reward after vandalism of federal vehicles in Minneapolis","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局（FBI）悬赏最高10万美元，征集有关明尼阿波利斯联邦政府车辆遭破坏和财物被盗事件的信息。FBI称周三探员在北明尼阿波利斯调查一起袭击联邦官员案件时，多辆政府车辆被破坏、闯入，车内财物被盗。此前当地因ICE探员枪杀蕾妮·古德引发抗议和骚乱。","summary_en":"The FBI is offering a reward of up to $100,000 for information on the vandalism and theft of federal government vehicles in Minneapolis. The agency said agents responded to an assault on a federal officer investigation in North Minneapolis on Wednesday, where several government vehicles were damaged, broken into and property stolen. The unrest follows protests over an ICE agent's fatal shooting of Renee Good.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:31:50.302815+00:00","url":"https://bnonews.com/index.php/2026/01/fbi-offers-100000-reward-after-vandalism-of-federal-vehicles-in-minneapolis","content":"Legal\nFBI offers $100,000 reward after vandalism of federal vehicles in Minneapolis\nPublished on\nJanuary 15, 2026\nBy Carlos Robles\nCredit: CNN\nAdvertisment17\nShare\nTweet\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) is offering a reward of up to $100,000 for information leading to the recovery of stolen government property and the arrest of individuals responsible for vandalism and theft of federal property in Minneapolis, Minnesota, the agency said.\nThe FBI posted a seeking information bulletin Thursday showing photos of heavily damaged vehicles and saying that on Wednesday, agents responded to an assault on a federal officer investigation in North Minneapolis.\nSeveral government vehicles were vandalized and broken into, and government property was reported stolen from inside them, the announcement said. The FBI is offering a reward of up to $100,000 for information related to the incident.\n“If you harm law enforcement or destroy/steal federal property this FBI will not hesitate to pursue you, find you, and bring you to the fullest extent of justice,” FBI Director Kash Patel said in a social media post.\nArticle continues below the player\nMinneapolis has seen multiple confrontations involving U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) and other federal law enforcement officers in recent days following a fatal shooting of Renee Nicole Good by an ICE agent on January 7, which led to protests and community unrest.\nOn Wednesday night, another shooting involving federal agents was reported in North Minneapolis when a Venezuelan man was shot in the leg by an ICE agent during an enforcement operation, officials said.\nThe Department of Homeland Security said the man resisted arrest and attacked the agent with objects during a struggle before he was struck in the leg; he was taken to a hospital with non-life-threatening injuries.\nThat incident sparked protests and unrest in the area, during which federal forces deployed flash bangs and tear gas against crowds.\nRelated Topics:featuredFederal deployment during the Trump administrationMinneapolis (Minnesota)MinnesotaShooting of Renee GoodTrump administration protestsUnited States\nAdvertisment15\nAdvertisment5\nLatest\nLegal14 hours ago\nFormer Assad regime prison chief sentenced to 60 years in U.S. for torture\nLegal14 hours ago\nGeorgia middle school student arrested over “credible” shooting threat\nLegal15 hours ago\nTeen arrested over school shooting threat in California’s Central Valley\nPolitics15 hours ago\nFlorida GOP Rep. Salazar tells Trump immigration enforcement has ‘gone too far’\nAdvertisment4\nTrending\nUS News3 days ago\n3 killed, 1 injured as NBC Los Angeles helicopter crashes while covering deadly collision\nWorld6 days ago\n16 elderly residents killed in fire at Chilean nursing home\nLegal6 days ago\nFormer officer arrested after threats to shoot police station in southern Florida\nAdvertisment6\nMost Viewed\nUS News3 days ago\n3 killed, 1 injured as NBC Los Angeles helicopter crashes while covering deadly collision\nWorld6 days ago\n16 elderly residents killed in fire at Chilean nursing home\nLegal6 days ago\nFormer officer arrested after threats to shoot police station in southern Florida\nLegal7 days ago\nU.S. uses secretive terrorism court for the first time to deport Afghan woman\nWorld2 days ago\nCatholic priest found murdered near road in central Mexico\nLegal3 days ago\nPennsylvania man charged over alleged ISIS-inspired mass shooting plot\nLegal4 days ago\nColorado man charged with threatening to kill police, FBI agents and Muslims\nLegal2 days ago\nISIS-K operative sentenced to 20 years for role in Kabul airport attack\nCopyright © 2026 BNO News, B.V. All rights reserved.\nAbout Us | Privacy Policy | Terms | BNO en Español | Contact Us","content_cn":"法律\n明尼阿波利斯联邦车辆遭破坏后，FBI悬赏10万美元\n发布于\n2026年1月15日\n作者：卡洛斯·罗布尔斯\n图片来源：CNN\n广告17\n分享\n推文\n美国联邦调查局（FBI）表示，该局悬赏最高10万美元，征集有助于追回被盗政府财产以及逮捕在明尼苏达州明尼阿波利斯破坏和盗窃联邦财产责任人的信息。\nFBI周四发布了一份征集信息公告，展示了严重受损车辆的照片，并称周三，探员们对北明尼阿波利斯一起袭击联邦官员的调查作出了响应。\n公告称，多辆政府车辆遭到破坏和撬窃，据报车内政府财产被盗。FBI悬赏最高10万美元，征集与此事件有关的信息。\nFBI局长卡什·帕特尔在社交媒体帖子中表示：“如果你伤害执法人员或破坏/盗窃联邦财产，这个FBI将毫不犹豫地追查你、找到你，并将你绳之以法，追究最严厉的责任。”\n文章在播放器下方继续\n在1月7日ICE探员致命枪击蕾妮·妮可·古德后，明尼阿波利斯近日出现了多起涉及美国移民和海关执法局（ICE）及其他联邦执法人员的对峙，并引发了抗议和社区动荡。\n官员称，周三晚间，北明尼阿波利斯又报告了一起涉及联邦探员的枪击事件，一名委内瑞拉男子在一次执法行动中被ICE探员击中腿部。\n美国国土安全部表示，该男子拒捕，并在搏斗中用物品袭击探员，随后腿部中弹；他被送往医院，伤势没有生命危险。\n该事件在当地引发了抗议和骚乱，期间联邦力量对人群使用了闪光弹和催泪瓦斯。\n相关主题：精选特朗普政府期间的联邦部署明尼阿波利斯（明尼苏达州）明尼苏达州蕾妮·古德枪击案特朗普政府抗议活动美国\n广告15\n广告5\n最新\n法律14小时前\n前阿萨德政权监狱负责人因酷刑在美国被判处60年监禁\n法律14小时前\n佐治亚州一名中学生因“可信的”枪击威胁被捕\n法律15小时前\n加州中央谷地一名青少年因学校枪击威胁被捕\n政治15小时前\n佛罗里达州共和党众议员萨拉萨尔告诉特朗普，移民执法“做得太过头了”\n广告4\n热门\n美国新闻3天前\nNBC洛杉矶直升机在报道致命碰撞时坠毁，3人死亡、1人受伤\n世界6天前\n智利一家养老院发生火灾，16名老年居民死亡\n法律6天前\n前警官因威胁枪击南佛罗里达警察局后被捕\n广告6\n浏览量最高\n美国新闻3天前\nNBC洛杉矶直升机在报道致命碰撞时坠毁，3人死亡、1人受伤\n世界6天前\n智利一家养老院发生火灾，16名老年居民死亡\n法律6天前\n前警官因威胁枪击南佛罗里达警察局后被捕\n法律7天前\n美国首次使用秘密恐怖主义法庭驱逐一名阿富汗女子\n世界2天前\n天主教神父在墨西哥中部一条道路附近被发现遭谋杀\n法律3天前\n宾夕法尼亚州一名男子因涉嫌受ISIS启发策划大规模枪击被起诉\n法律4天前\n科罗拉多州一名男子因威胁杀害警察、FBI探员和穆斯林被起诉\n法律2天前\nISIS-K特工因参与喀布尔机场袭击被判处20年监禁\n版权所有 © 2026 BNO News, B.V. 保留所有权利。\n关于我们 | 隐私政策 | 条款 | BNO西班牙语 | 联系我们","publish_source":"bnonews.com","publish_time":"2026-01-15T23:21:14+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2274","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike发布Windows版Falcon Sensor安全更新（CVE-2025-42701、CVE-2025-42706）","title_en":"CrowdStrike: Security update for Falcon Sensor for Windows (CVE-2025-42701, CVE-2025-42706)Born's Tech and Windows World","summary_cn":"CrowdStrike发布安全公告，修复Windows版Falcon Sensor中两个中危漏洞。CVE-2025-42701为TOCTOU竞争条件，CVSS 3.1评分5.6；CVE-2025-42706为逻辑错误，评分6.5。两者均需攻击者先在主机上执行代码，随后可删除任意文件。修复包含在Falcon Sensor 7.29版及7.24至7.28热修复版中，Windows 7/2008 R2主机使用7.16热修复。CrowdStrike称未发现实际利用迹象，但因其将漏洞称为“问题”而引发争议，安全专家凯文·博蒙特批评这是粉饰。","summary_en":"CrowdStrike released a security advisory fixing two medium-severity vulnerabilities in Falcon Sensor for Windows. CVE-2025-42701 is a TOCTOU race condition with a CVSS 3.1 score of 5.6; CVE-2025-42706 is a logic error scored 6.5. Both require an attacker to first execute code on the host, after which arbitrary files could be deleted. Fixes are included in Falcon Sensor version 7.29, hotfixes for versions 7.24 to 7.28, and a 7.16 hotfix for Windows 7/2008 R2 hosts. CrowdStrike said there are no signs of exploitation, but its labeling of the flaws as \"issues\" sparked controversy, with security expert Kevin Beaumont calling it sugarcoating.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:45:44.670158+00:00","url":"https://borncity.com/win/2025/10/09/crowdstrike-security-update-for-falcon-sensor-for-windows-cve-2025-42701-cve-2025-42706","content":"← Microsoft 365: Outage blocks Teams and Exchange Online (Oct. 8, 2025)\nMicrosoft Admin Center down – there are certificate errors (Oct. 9, 2025) →\nCrowdStrike: Security update for Falcon Sensor for Windows (CVE-2025-42701, CVE-2025-42706)\nPosted on 2025-10-09 by guenni\n[German]There are two medium-score vulnerabilities in CrowdStrike Falcon Sensors for Windows that have been patched by the manufacturer via an update. A discussion is currently raging because CrowdStrike refers to this as an \"issue,\" while security researchers refer to it as \"closing vulnerabilities.\"\nCrowdStrike information about an \"issue\"\nCrowdStrike has published a security advisory entitled Issues Affecting CrowdStrike Falcon Sensor for Windows on the matter. It states that \"fixes for two issues\" affecting the Falcon sensor for Windows have been released.\nIn both cases, an attacker would first have to create the possibility of executing code on the host. Then they could use the \"two problems\" to delete any files.\nCVE-2025-42701: A Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) race condition in Falcon Sensor for Windows that could allow an attacker who has previously been able to execute code on a host to delete arbitrary files; CVSS 3.1 Score 5.6 (Medium)\nCVE-2025-42706: A logic error exists in Falcon Sensor for Windows that could allow an attacker who has previously been able to execute code on a host to delete arbitrary files. CVSS 3.1 Score 6.5 (Medium)\nCrowdStrike has released fixes for these two vulnerabilities, which it has classified as \"problems.\" The fixes only affect the Falcon sensor for Windows; the sensors for Linux and macOS are not affected.\nThe fixes for both issues are included in the latest version 7.29 of the Falcon sensor for Windows, in hotfix versions for versions 7.24 to 7.28, and in a hotfix 7.16 for hosts running Windows 7/2008 R2. The hotfix for version 7.24 is also an update for the current Long-Term Visibility (LTV) sensor for Windows IoT.\nThere are no signs that \"these issues\" are being exploited in practice, CrowdStrike writes. Their threat detection and analysis teams are actively monitoring whether these \"issues\" are being exploited, according to the security advisory.\nControversy over \"issues versus vulnerabilities\"\nThe wording \"issues\" chosen by CrowdStrike in the security advisory immediately sparked controversy.\nSecurity expert Kevin Beaumont points out in the above tweet that CrowdStrike's description of a \"problem\" is simply sugarcoating. Security vulnerabilities have been found in the Falcon sensors, and they should be referred to as such.\nThis entry was posted in Security, Software and tagged Security, Software. Bookmark the permalink.\n← Microsoft 365: Outage blocks Teams and Exchange Online (Oct. 8, 2025)\nMicrosoft Admin Center down – there are certificate errors (Oct. 9, 2025) →\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name\nEmail\nWebsite\nI have read and accepted the Privacy Policy\n*\nNote: Please note the rules for commenting on the blog (first comments and linked posts end up in moderation, I release them every few hours, I rigorously delete SEO posts/SPAM).","content_cn":"← Microsoft 365：故障导致Teams和Exchange Online中断（2025年10月8日）\nMicrosoft管理中心宕机——出现证书错误（2025年10月9日）→\nCrowdStrike：适用于Windows的Falcon Sensor安全更新（CVE-2025-42701、CVE-2025-42706）\n发表于2025年10月9日，作者：guenni\n[CrowdStrike Falcon Sensor for Windows]（适用于Windows的CrowdStrike Falcon传感器）存在两个中等评分的漏洞，制造商已通过更新修复。当前争论正激烈展开，因为CrowdStrike称其为“问题”，而安全研究人员称其为“修复漏洞”。\nCrowdStrike关于“问题”的信息\nCrowdStrike就此发布了一份题为《影响Windows版CrowdStrike Falcon Sensor的问题》的安全公告。公告称，影响Windows版Falcon传感器的“两个问题”的修复程序已经发布。\n在两种情况下，攻击者都必须先创造在主机上执行代码的条件。随后，他们可以利用这“两个问题”删除任何文件。\nCVE-2025-42701：Windows版Falcon Sensor中存在一次检查时机与使用时机（TOCTOU）竞争条件，可能允许此前已能够在主机上执行代码的攻击者删除任意文件；CVSS 3.1评分5.6（中等）\nCVE-2025-42706：Windows版Falcon Sensor存在逻辑错误，可能允许此前已能够在主机上执行代码的攻击者删除任意文件。CVSS 3.1评分6.5（中等）\nCrowdStrike已发布这两个漏洞的修复程序，但将其归类为“问题”。修复程序仅影响Windows版Falcon传感器；Linux和macOS版传感器不受影响。\n这两个问题的修复程序包含在Windows版Falcon传感器最新的7.29版本中、7.24至7.28版本的热修复版本中，以及适用于运行Windows 7/2008 R2主机的7.16热修复中。7.24版本的热修复同时也是当前Windows IoT长期可见性（LTV）传感器的更新。\nCrowdStrike写道，目前没有迹象表明“这些问题”正在实际遭到利用。根据安全公告，其威胁检测和分析团队正在积极监控这些“问题”是否遭到利用。\n“问题”与“漏洞”之争\nCrowdStrike在安全公告中选择使用“问题”一词，立即引发争议。\n安全专家Kevin Beaumont在上方推文中指出，CrowdStrike对“问题”的描述只是在粉饰。Falcon传感器中已经发现安全漏洞，应当如此称呼。\n此条目发布于“安全”“软件”分类，并标记为“安全”“软件”。收藏固定链接。\n← Microsoft 365：故障导致Teams和Exchange Online中断（2025年10月8日）\nMicrosoft管理中心宕机——出现证书错误（2025年10月9日）→\n发表评论 取消回复\n您的电子邮件地址不会公开。必填字段标有*号\n评论 * 姓名\n电子邮件\n网站\n我已阅读并接受隐私政策\n*\n注意：请注意博客评论规则（首次评论和包含链接的帖子会进入审核，我每隔几小时发布一次；我会严格删除SEO帖子/垃圾邮件）。","publish_source":"borncity.com","publish_time":"2025-10-09T04:27:09+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2980","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike任命前AWS印度首席营销官Karthik Sathuragiri负责印度市场营销业务","title_en":"CrowdStrike appoints former AWS India CMO Karthik Sathuragiri to lead India marketing operations, ETBrandEquity","summary_cn":"网络安全公司CrowdStrike任命前AWS印度及南亚市场营销负责人Karthik Sathuragiri为印度市场总监兼营销负责人。Sathuragiri拥有近二十年全球科技企业经验，曾任职SAP、Akamai、Freshworks和Automation Anywhere。此举显示CrowdStrike加大印度市场投入，意在借助其B2B科技营销经验，推动企业在网络安全、数字韧性和零信任框架需求上升背景下的区域增长。","summary_en":"Cybersecurity firm CrowdStrike has appointed Karthik Sathuragiri, formerly head of marketing for AWS India and South Asia, as director and head of marketing for India. Sathuragiri brings nearly two decades of experience at global tech firms including SAP, Akamai, Freshworks and Automation Anywhere. The move signals CrowdStrike's intensified focus on the Indian market, aiming to leverage his B2B tech marketing expertise to drive regional growth amid rising demand for enterprise cybersecurity, digital resilience and zero-trust frameworks.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:26:27.029232+00:00","url":"https://brandequity.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/the-people-report/crowdstrike-appoints-former-aws-india-cmo-karthik-sathuragiri-to-lead-india-marketing-operations/120270655","content":"The People Report 2 min read\nCrowdStrike appoints former AWS India CMO Karthik Sathuragiri to lead India marketing operations\nCrowdStrike has appointed Karthik Sathuragiri, former AWS India CMO, as its new director and head of marketing for India. This move signals CrowdStrike's intensified focus on the Indian market, aiming to leverage Sathuragiri's extensive B2B tech marketing experience to drive growth in the region's burgeoning cybersecurity sector.\nAnirban Roy Choudhury\nETBrandEquity\nUpdated On Apr 14, 2025 at 11:04 AM IST\nSelect ETBrandEquity as Preferred Choice on Google\nCopy Link\nShare on WhatsApp\nShare on Linkedin\nShare on X\nShare on Telegram\nShare on Facebook\nGlobal cybersecurity major CrowdStrike has appointed Karthik Sathuragiri as director and head of marketing for India, marking a significant step in its strategy to scale operations and deepen market engagement in the region, according to a source close to the development.Sathuragiri, who most recently served as head of marketing for Amazon Web Services (AWS) in India and South Asia, brings nearly two decades of experience across global tech firms including SAP, Akamai, Freshworks, and Automation Anywhere. Known for his strategic marketing acumen and ability to link brand vision to business outcomes, Sathuragiri is widely regarded as one of the leading voices in B2B tech marketing.\nAdvt\n“He’s among the rare marketers who can build narrative, drive demand, and scale operations with equal fluency,” said an executive familiar with his work. “His ability to bridge brand, technology, and business impact has set a high bar.”The move comes as CrowdStrike sharpens its focus on the Indian market, amid heightened demand for enterprise cybersecurity, digital resilience, and zero-trust frameworks.Sathuragiri had recently announced his departure from AWS in a heartfelt note on LinkedIn, reflecting on his 4.5-year journey with the company. “Over the next month, I'll be transitioning out of AWS to take a break and reflect before exploring what's next,” he wrote. “This isn't goodbye to the cloud or the ecosystem I love—just a short pause to breathe, reset, and reimagine.”In his note, he credited AWS’s “tech-first DNA” and customer-obsessed culture as key learning experiences. “At AWS, everyone—from sales to solution architects—know the tech inside out and are obsessed about customer problems... It’s not just about good intentions. It’s about operationalising them as mechanisms. I got a masterclass in that,” he noted.Sathuragiri is an alumnus of the UCLA Anderson School of Management. His appointment at CrowdStrike is expected to further accelerate the company’s positioning in India, especially as cybersecurity emerges as a boardroom imperative across industries.\nAdvt\nBy\nAnirban Roy Choudhury\n,\nETBrandEquity\nPublished On Apr 14, 2025 at 11:04 AM IST\nSee more on:\nCrowdStrike,\nKarthik Sathuragiri,\ncybersecurity,\nAWS India,\nB2B tech marketing,\nhead of marketing appointment,\nAWS,\nIndia market\nTelegram\nFacebook\nCopy Link\nComments\nWhat are your thoughts?\nComment Now\nRead Comment (1)\nAll Comments\nBy commenting, you agree to the Prohibited Content Policy\nPost\nBy commenting, you agree to the Prohibited Content Policy\nPost\nFind this Comment Offensive?\nChoose your reason below and click on the submit button. This will alert our moderators to take actions\nREASONS FOR REPORTING\nFoul Language\nDefamatory\nInciting hatred against a certain community\nOut of Context / Spam\nOthers\nReport\nJoin the community of 2M+ industry professionals.\nSubscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights & analysis in your inbox.\nAll about ETBrandEquity industry right on your smartphone!\nDownload the ETBrandEquity App and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles.\nHomeNewsThe People ReportCrowdStrike appoints former AWS India CMO Karthik Sathuragiri to lead India marketing operations","content_cn":"人民报道 阅读时长2分钟\nCrowdStrike任命前AWS印度首席营销官Karthik Sathuragiri领导印度市场营销业务\nCrowdStrike已任命前AWS印度首席营销官Karthik Sathuragiri为其新任印度市场营销总监兼负责人。此举表明CrowdStrike正加大对印度市场的关注，旨在利用Sathuragiri丰富的B2B科技营销经验，推动该地区蓬勃发展的网络安全领域增长。\nAnirban Roy Choudhury\nETBrandEquity\n更新于2025年4月14日印度标准时间上午11:04\n在Google上将ETBrandEquity设为首选\n复制链接\n分享到WhatsApp\n分享到LinkedIn\n分享到X\n分享到Telegram\n分享到Facebook\n据一位接近此事的消息人士称，全球网络安全巨头CrowdStrike已任命Karthik Sathuragiri为印度市场营销总监兼负责人，这标志着其扩大业务规模并深化在该地区市场参与战略的重要一步。Sathuragiri最近担任亚马逊云科技（AWS）印度及南亚市场营销负责人，在SAP、Akamai、Freshworks和Automation Anywhere等全球科技公司拥有近二十年的经验。Sathuragiri以其战略营销才能以及将品牌愿景与业务成果相连的能力而闻名，被广泛视为B2B科技营销领域的领军人物之一。\n广告\n一位熟悉其工作情况的高管表示：“他是少数能够同样娴熟地构建叙事、推动需求并扩大业务运营的营销人员之一。他弥合品牌、技术与业务影响之间鸿沟的能力，树立了很高的标准。”此举正值CrowdStrike加强对印度市场的关注之际，企业网络安全、数字韧性和零信任框架的需求不断上升。\nSathuragiri最近在LinkedIn上发表了一则真挚的帖子，宣布离开AWS，并回顾了自己在该公司4年半的历程。他写道：“在接下来的一个月里，我将逐步离开AWS，先休息和反思，然后再探索下一步。我并非要告别云或我所热爱的生态系统——只是短暂停下来，喘口气、重新调整并重新想象。”\n在帖子中，他将AWS“技术优先的DNA”和以客户为中心的文化视为重要的学习经历。他指出：“在AWS，从销售人员到解决方案架构师，每个人都对技术了如指掌，并且痴迷于客户问题……这不仅仅关乎良好意愿，而是要将其运营化为机制。我在这方面上了一堂大师课。”\nSathuragiri毕业于加州大学洛杉矶分校安德森管理学院。预计他在CrowdStrike的任命将进一步加速公司在印度的市场定位，尤其是在网络安全正成为各行业董事会层面要务之际。\n广告\n作者\nAnirban Roy Choudhury\n，\nETBrandEquity\n发布于2025年4月14日印度标准时间上午11:04\n查看更多：\nCrowdStrike，\nKarthik Sathuragiri，\n网络安全，\nAWS印度，\nB2B科技营销，\n市场营销负责人任命，\nAWS，\n印度市场\nTelegram\nFacebook\n复制链接\n评论\n您有什么想法？\n立即评论\n阅读评论（1）\n所有评论\n发表评论即表示您同意《禁止内容政策》\n发布\n发表评论即表示您同意《禁止内容政策》\n发布\n觉得此评论具有冒犯性？\n请在下方选择理由并点击提交按钮。这将提醒我们的审核人员采取行动\n举报理由\n粗俗语言\n诽谤性内容\n煽动针对某一社区的仇恨\n断章取义／垃圾信息\n其他\n举报\n加入由200多万行业专业人士组成的社区。\n订阅新闻通讯，将最新洞见和分析发送至您的收件箱。\nETBrandEquity行业资讯尽在您的智能手机上！\n下载ETBrandEquity应用程序，获取实时更新并保存您喜爱的文章。\n首页新闻人民报道CrowdStrike任命前AWS印度首席营销官Karthik Sathuragiri领导印度市场营销业务","publish_source":"brandequity.economictimes.indiatimes.com","publish_time":"2025-04-14T11:04:27+05:30"}},{"id":"news-3649","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike以西部主题广告重返超级碗","title_en":"CrowdStrike returns to Super Bowl with Wild West-themed spot - Brand Innovators","summary_cn":"CrowdStrike连续第二年登陆超级碗，投放30秒广告，以未来主义西部片风格呈现其对抗网络威胁、守护数字世界未来的品牌信息。品牌副总裁Jess Meyers表示，网络安全对大众而言如同“狂野西部”，因此延续去年特洛伊木马广告的叙事，用观众熟悉的善恶对决概念解释网络安全。公司称去年投放对品牌认知、购买意向和决策产生显著影响，因此决定继续讲述该故事。","summary_en":"CrowdStrike returned to the Super Bowl for a second consecutive year with a 30-second ad styled as a futuristic Western, conveying its message of fighting adversaries to secure the digitally connected world. VP of brand Jess Meyers said cybersecurity can feel like the Wild West, so the spot builds on last year's Trojan horse narrative, using a familiar good-versus-evil showdown to explain cybersecurity to a broad audience. The company cited significant impact on brand awareness, perception and buying intent from last year's buy.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:20:26.336970+00:00","url":"https://brand-innovators.com/crowdstrike-returns-to-super-bowl-with-wild-west-themed-spot","content":"Super Bowl Advertising\nNews\nCrowdStrike returns to Super Bowl with Wild West-themed spot\nBy\nDianna Dilworth\nFebruary 8, 2024\nCrowdStrike is returning to the Super Bowl for the second year in a row to bring its cyber security message to a mainstream audience.\nThis year’s :30 ad is a kind of futuristic Western in which CrowdStrike fights the adversary to secure the future of the digitally-connected world. “Cybersecurity can feel like the Wild West, so we wanted to put that future spin on it and that CrowdStrike is here to protect you into the future,” said Jess Meyers, VP of brand at CrowdStrike.\nThe idea for this year’s spot builds on the brand’s commercial from last year. In that ad, the brand told the story of ancient Troy, imagining what would have happened if CrowdStrike had been there (spoiler: the Trojan horse breach wouldn’t have happened).\n“We introduced the concept of the ancient adversary,”  explained Meyers. “This year, we wanted a creative concept that was still relatable. Cybersecurity is hard to explain to a broad audience, so we want to bring in things that people really understand. It’s the concept of good versus evil on the set of an old Western. People understand that face-off, they understand adversaries riding into town.”\nLast year, the brand had success with the media buy. “From a brand standpoint, it was very positively received,” said Meyers. One of the biggest comments they heard in the industry was that the ad made cybersecurity relatable for the first time.\n“We had this big tentpole moment last year from a brand awareness standpoint, brand perception, buying intent, decision-making, we saw just a huge impact from this advertising platform and we wanted to continue the story,” said Meyers. “It made sense for us to come back to the Super Bowl and to do another spot.”\nRelated Content\nSee all\nSuper Bowl Advertising\nNews\nBrand Innovators Super Bowl Ad Tracker 2027\nBy\nDianna Dilworth\nNews\nSuper Bowl Advertising\nWatch Every 2026 Super Bowl Ad\nBy\nAaron Baar\nNews\nSuper Bowl Advertising\nBrand Innovators Event Coverage\nSports marketing has to give 110%: BI Summit Speakers\nBy\nMercedes Cardona\nNews\nSuper Bowl Advertising\nBehind Squarespace’s Super Bowl ad\nBy\nDianna Dilworth","content_cn":"超级碗广告\n新闻\nCrowdStrike携西部荒野主题广告重返超级碗\n作者\nDianna Dilworth\n2024年2月8日\nCrowdStrike连续第二年重返超级碗，向主流受众传递其网络安全信息。\n今年这支30秒广告是一部带有未来色彩的西部片，CrowdStrike在其中与对手交锋，以保障数字互联世界的未来。“网络安全可能让人感觉像是西部荒野，因此我们希望为它加入未来感，并传达CrowdStrike将在未来保护你的信息，”CrowdStrike品牌副总裁Jess Meyers说。\n今年广告的创意建立在该品牌去年的广告基础之上。在那支广告中，品牌讲述了古代特洛伊的故事，设想如果当时CrowdStrike在场会发生什么（剧透：特洛伊木马造成的入侵不会发生）。\n“我们引入了‘古老对手’这一概念，”Meyers解释道。“今年，我们希望创意概念仍然具有共鸣。网络安全很难向广泛受众解释，因此我们希望引入人们真正理解的事物。这是在一部老式西部片场景中的善恶对决概念。人们理解那种正面交锋，也理解对手骑马进城。”\n去年，该品牌的媒体投放取得成功。“从品牌角度看，反响非常积极，”Meyers说。他们在业内听到的最大评价之一是，这支广告首次让网络安全变得易于理解。\n“从品牌认知、品牌观感、购买意向和决策制定的角度来看，去年我们迎来了一个重要的标志性时刻；我们看到这个广告平台带来了巨大影响，因此希望延续这个故事，”Meyers说。“我们重返超级碗并再推出一支广告是合理的。”\n相关内容\n查看全部\n超级碗广告\n新闻\nBrand Innovators 2027年超级碗广告追踪器\n作者\nDianna Dilworth\n新闻\n超级碗广告\n观看每一支2026年超级碗广告\n作者\nAaron Baar\n新闻\n超级碗广告\nBrand Innovators活动报道\n体育营销必须全力以赴：BI峰会演讲嘉宾\n作者\nMercedes Cardona\n新闻\n超级碗广告\nSquarespace超级碗广告幕后故事\n作者\nDianna Dilworth","publish_source":"brand-innovators.com","publish_time":"2024-02-08T12:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3552","ktid":1000490,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000490","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CSIS报告警告中国对全球海底光缆构成威胁","title_en":"CSIS Report Warns of Chinese Threat to Global Subsea Cables","summary_cn":"美国战略与国际研究中心（CSIS）发布报告，警告承载全球近98%互联网流量的海底光缆正面临中国和俄罗斯的蓄意破坏风险。报告称2018年以来已有27起中国船只干扰台湾海底光缆事件，并指出全球对中国光缆维修船的过度依赖构成隐患。报告建议美国及盟友避免依赖不可信实体进行光缆修复，加强电子监控并深化国际合作。","summary_en":"A new report from the Center for Strategic and International Studies (CSIS) warns that subsea fiber-optic cables, which carry nearly 98% of global internet traffic, face deliberate sabotage risks from China and Russia. The report cites 27 recorded incidents since 2018 of Chinese vessels disrupting Taiwan's undersea cables, and highlights global overreliance on Chinese cable repair ships as a key vulnerability. CSIS recommends avoiding untrusted entities for cable restoration, implementing electronic monitoring, and strengthening international cooperation.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:28:22.343914+00:00","url":"https://broadbandbreakfast.com/csis-report-warns-of-chinese-threat-to-global-subsea-cables","content":"China\nCSIS Report Warns of Chinese Threat to Global Subsea Cables\nCSIS warns subsea fiber-optic cables are at risk of sabotage by U.S. foreign adversaries.\nJericho Casper\nAug 28, 2024\n— 2 min read\nPhoto of U.S. Navy diver installing steel armor around a seafloor cable in Kauai, Hawaii, taken by U.S. Navy and used with permission.\nWASHINGTON, August 28, 2024 – Amid escalating concerns in the U.S. about Chinese technology infiltrating telecommunications networks, subsea cables carrying nearly 98% of global internet traffic have surfaced as the latest potential targets for sabotage, with China and Russia identified as primary threats.A new report from the Center for Strategic and International Studies has brought attention to the vulnerabilities of subsea cable systems, revealing a “deliberate” pattern of attacks by China. Amazon, Google, Meta, and Microsoft own or lease around half of all undersea bandwidth worldwide.Since 2018, there have been 27 recorded instances of Chinese vessels disrupting Taiwan’s undersea cables. One such incident in 2023 left 14,000 residents in digital isolation for six weeks.\nThe report notes that the vast scale and exposure of undersea infrastructure made it an easy target for saboteurs operating in the gray zone of “deniable attacks short of war.”One significant vulnerability included the global overreliance on Chinese cable repair ships. This dependence could become a particular concern if, during a military conflict, the Chinese government restricted access to its repair vessels, potentially crippling global communications.Although the data transmitted through subsea cables has been encrypted, the overreliance on Chinese infrastructure has raised alarms in the U.S., leading to a blockade of Chinese companies from subsea projects involving U.S. investments due to national security concerns. Simultaneously, Chinese authorities have delayed or denied the approval of subsea cables passing through the South China Sea, hindering north-south connectivity in the Pacific region. The CSIS report emphasized the need for a more cohesive legal framework to protect subsea cables, recommending that the U.S. and its allies prioritize both security and efficiency in repairs and installations. Key recommendations included avoiding reliance on untrusted entities for cable restoration, implementing electronic monitoring systems for enhanced security, and collaborating with international partners to strengthen global infrastructure resilience. While the U.S. and its allies consider these critical steps, China has already been aggressively pursuing its own strategy to dominate the global subsea cable market, the CSIS report said. In 2015, China set an ambitious goal to capture 60 percent of the global fiber-optic cable market through its Digital Silk Road initiative. By targeting emerging economies in Asia, Africa, the Middle East, and the Pacific, Chinese firms like HMN Technologies have rapidly increased their share of the global subsea cable market.HMN Technologies, formerly Huawei Marine Networks, held 11 percent of the global market in 2021, while U.S. company SubCom, French firm Alcatel Submarine Networks, and Japanese firm Nippon Electric Company collectively held 87 percent. However, HMN Technologies has become the fastest-growing subsea cable builder over the past decade, laying 18 percent of the world’s subsea cables in the last four years.\nPost tagged in\nChina\nPublic Safety\nRussia\nCSIS\nAmazon\nGoogle\nMeta\nMicrosoft\nTaiwan\nDigital Silk Road\nHMN Technologies\nHuawei Marine Networks\nSubCom\nAlcatel Submarine Networks\nNippon Electric Company\nYou have run out of free posts for the moment, sign up to read more.\nSubscribe now\nAlready have an account? Sign in\nYou have run out of free posts for the moment, upgrade to a paid account for unlimited reading.\nSubscribe now\nAlready have an account? Sign in","content_cn":"中国\nCSIS 报告警告中国对全球海底电缆构成威胁\nCSIS 警告，海底光纤电缆面临美国境外对手破坏的风险。\nJericho Casper\n2024年8月28日\n— 阅读时长 2 分钟\n美国海军潜水员在夏威夷考艾岛海底电缆周围安装钢制装甲的照片，由美国海军拍摄并获许可使用。\n\n华盛顿，2024年8月28日——随着美国日益担忧中国技术渗透电信网络，承载全球近98%互联网流量的海底电缆已成为最新的潜在破坏目标，其中中国和俄罗斯被认定为主要威胁。战略与国际问题研究中心的一份新报告使人们注意到海底电缆系统的脆弱性，揭示了中国“蓄意”发动攻击的模式。亚马逊、谷歌、Meta 和微软拥有或租赁全球约一半的海底带宽。\n\n自2018年以来，已有27起记录在案的中国船只扰乱台湾海底电缆的事件。其中一起发生在2023年的事件，令14,000名居民陷入长达六周的数字孤立。\n\n报告指出，海底基础设施规模庞大且暴露在外，使其成为在“低于战争门槛、可否认攻击”灰色地带活动的破坏者的容易目标。一项重大脆弱性是全球对中国电缆维修船的过度依赖。若在军事冲突期间，中国政府限制使用其维修船只，这种依赖可能会成为特别令人担忧的问题，并可能严重削弱全球通信。\n\n尽管通过海底电缆传输的数据已被加密，但对中国基础设施的过度依赖已在美国引发警觉。出于国家安全考虑，美国已阻止中国公司参与涉及美国投资的海底项目。同时，中国当局拖延或拒绝批准穿越南海的海底电缆，阻碍了太平洋地区的南北连通性。\n\nCSIS 报告强调，需要建立更协调一致的法律框架来保护海底电缆，并建议美国及其盟友在维修和安装中同时优先考虑安全与效率。主要建议包括：避免依赖不可信实体进行电缆修复；实施电子监测系统以增强安全；以及与国际伙伴合作，加强全球基础设施韧性。\n\n报告称，在美国及其盟友考虑这些关键步骤之际，中国已积极推行自身战略，以主导全球海底电缆市场。\n\n2015年，中国通过其数字丝绸之路倡议设定了雄心勃勃的目标，即占据全球光纤电缆市场的60%。通过瞄准亚洲、非洲、中东和太平洋地区的新兴经济体，HMN Technologies 等中国企业迅速提高了其在全球海底电缆市场的份额。HMN Technologies 原名华为海洋网络，2021年占全球市场的11%；而美国公司 SubCom、法国公司阿尔卡特海底网络和日本公司日本电气公司合计占87%。不过，在过去十年中，HMN Technologies 已成为增长最快的海底电缆建设商，并在最近四年铺设了全球18%的海底电缆。\n\n文章标签\n中国\n公共安全\n俄罗斯\nCSIS\n亚马逊\n谷歌\nMeta\n微软\n台湾\n数字丝绸之路\nHMN Technologies\n华为海洋网络\nSubCom\n阿尔卡特海底网络\n日本电气公司\n\n您目前的免费文章阅读额度已用完，注册以阅读更多内容。\n立即订阅\n已有账户？登录\n您的免费文章阅读额度已用完，升级至付费账户即可无限阅读。\n立即订阅\n已有账户？登录","publish_source":"broadbandbreakfast.com","publish_time":"2024-08-28T17:41:52+00:00"}},{"id":"news-876","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI查获超80亿美元加密货币","title_en":"FBI Seizes Over $8 Billion In Cryptocurrency","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局（FBI）在一次国际行动中查获超过80亿美元加密货币，解救近2000名被贩运工人并逮捕近300人，关闭了柬埔寨太子集团、迪拜“沙元行动”及缅甸民主克伦仁爱军等诈骗窝点和犯罪组织。FBI局长卡什·帕特尔在X上宣布了行动结果。文章还提及2025年美国加密货币诈骗损失创纪录，FBI互联网犯罪投诉中心收到超百万起投诉。","summary_en":"The FBI seized over $8 billion in cryptocurrency, freed nearly 2,000 trafficked workers and arrested nearly 300 people in an international operation, shutting down scam compounds and criminal groups including the Prince Group in Cambodia, Operation Sand Dollar in Dubai and the Democratic Karen Benevolent Army in Myanmar. FBI Director Kash Patel announced the results on X. The article also notes record U.S. crypto scam losses in 2025 and over one million complaints to the FBI's IC3.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:46:49.184425+00:00","url":"https://brobible.com/culture/article/fbi-seizes-8-billion-cryptocurrency","content":"Culture\nFBI Seizes Over $8 Billion In Cryptocurrency As Part Of The Largest Forfeiture In US Government History\nFollow Us\nAdd as preferred source on Google\n1 Comment\nAdd as preferred source on Google\n1 Comment\nby Douglas CharlesMay 28, 2026 5:10 pm\niStockphoto composite\nThe FBI seized over $8 billion in cryptocurrency, freed nearly 2,000 trafficked workers, and arrested nearly 300 people in a recent international operation.\nAs part of the operation, authorities shut down several “scam compounds” and crime organizations, including groups known as the Prince Group in Cambodia, Operation Sand Dollar in Dubai, and the Democratic Karen Benevolent Army in Myanmar.\n“Scam compounds are modern-day criminal enterprises built to steal from Americans, launder money, and exploit trafficked workers,” FBI director Kash Patel wrote on X announcing the results of the operation.\nFox News reports that the U.S. The Democratic Karen Benevolent Army, an armed militia named after a region in Myanmar that is allegedly connected to the Chinese mob, faces sanctions imposed by the U.S. Treasury. The government has classified it as a transnational criminal organization.\nImages from an operation in Thailand reveal that the FBI confiscated office supplies and thousands of smartphones.\nFBI\nThe FBI in Dubai will extradite six of the 275 individuals they and local police detained there to the United States to face federal charges, according to the FBI. The authorities raided nine “scam compounds” in Dubai, each allegedly generating $6 million in fraud proceeds annually.\nCryptocurrency scams in the US reached a record high in 2025\nIn April, an FBI report revealed that cryptocurrency scams in the U.S. reached a record high in 2025, with reported losses of almost $11.4 billion. According to the FBI, cyber-enabled crimes defrauded Americans of almost $21 billion in 2025, with the costliest complaints involving cryptocurrency and artificial intelligence (AI).\n“The FBI’s 2025 Internet Crime Complaint Report highlights the ever-evolving tactics of internet scammers,” the FBI’s Baltimore office wrote on X. “From fake social media profiles to voice cloning and AI-generated content, cyber criminals are evolving.”\nThe Internet Crime Complaint Center (IC3) received over one million complaints in 2025, up from 859,532 in 2024. The most common complaints were about investment schemes, extortion, and phishing/spoofing.\nDouglas Charles\nDouglas Charles is a Senior Editor for BroBible with two decades of expertise writing about sports, science, and pop culture with a particular focus on the weird news and events that capture the internet's attention. He is a graduate from the University of Iowa.\nTags CryptocurrencyFBIPoliceScams\nWant more news like this? Add BroBible as a preferred source on Google!\nPreferred sources are prioritized in Top Stories, ensuring you never miss any of our editorial team's hard work.\nAdd as preferred source on Google\nLatest Posts\nMan Hacks Woman’s Southwest Account And Cancels Her Trip. Then He Uses The Flight Credit To Fly Dallas To Orlando On Her Dime: ‘Give Me My Refund’\nFormer Flight Attendant Says Not To Book Another Flight Until Hearing This—It Could Save You Hundreds\nBehemoth Hollywood Powerbroker Trying To Get Pat McAfee In One Of The Most-Anticipated Films Of Next Few Years: ‘Ending It All’\nBouncer Overhears Customer’s Unhinged Order. He Can’t Believe His Ears: ‘Had To Throw [Him] Out’","content_cn":"文化\n作为美国政府历史上最大规模没收行动的一部分，联邦调查局扣押超过80亿美元加密货币\n关注我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n1条评论\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n1条评论\nDouglas Charles 于2026年5月28日下午5:10\niStockphoto 合成图\n联邦调查局在最近的一次国际行动中扣押了超过80亿美元的加密货币，解救了近2000名被贩运的工人，并逮捕了近300人。\n作为行动的一部分，当局关闭了多个“诈骗园区”和犯罪组织，包括柬埔寨的 Prince Group、迪拜的 Operation Sand Dollar 以及缅甸的民主克伦慈善军。\n“诈骗园区是现代犯罪企业，旨在窃取美国人的钱、洗钱并剥削被贩运的工人，”联邦调查局局长 Kash Patel 在 X 上宣布行动结果时写道。\n福克斯新闻报道称，美国。缅甸民主克伦慈善军是一个以缅甸某地区命名的武装民兵组织，据称与中国黑帮有关，目前面临美国财政部实施的制裁。美国政府已将其列为跨国犯罪组织。\n泰国一场行动的图片显示，联邦调查局没收了办公用品和数千部智能手机。\n联邦调查局\n据联邦调查局称，联邦调查局驻迪拜机构将把他们与当地警方在那里拘留的275人中的6人引渡到美国，以面对联邦指控。有关部门突袭了迪拜的9个“诈骗园区”，据称每个园区每年产生600万美元的诈骗收益。\n2025年美国加密货币诈骗达到历史新高\n4月，联邦调查局的一份报告披露，美国加密货币诈骗在2025年达到历史新高，报告损失金额接近114亿美元。据联邦调查局称，网络犯罪在2025年从美国人手中骗走近210亿美元，其中损失最严重的投诉涉及加密货币和人工智能（AI）。\n“联邦调查局2025年互联网犯罪投诉报告凸显了网络诈骗者不断演变的策略，”联邦调查局巴尔的摩办公室在 X 上写道。“从虚假社交媒体资料到语音克隆和人工智能生成内容，网络犯罪分子正在不断进化。”\n互联网犯罪投诉中心（IC3）在2025年收到超过100万起投诉，高于2024年的859,532起。最常见的投诉涉及投资骗局、敲诈勒索以及网络钓鱼/欺骗。\nDouglas Charles\nDouglas Charles 是 BroBible 的高级编辑，拥有二十年撰写体育、科学和流行文化内容的经验，尤其关注吸引互联网注意力的奇闻和事件。他毕业于爱荷华大学。\n标签 加密货币 联邦调查局 警察 诈骗\n想要获取更多此类新闻？在 Google 上将 BroBible 添加为首选来源！\n首选来源会在“头条新闻”中优先显示，确保你不会错过我们编辑团队的辛勤工作。\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n最新文章\n男子入侵女子的西南航空账户并取消她的行程。随后，他用航班积分自费从达拉斯飞往奥兰多：“把退款给我”\n前空乘人员称，在听到这件事之前不要再预订航班——这可能为你省下数百美元\n好莱坞巨头掮客试图让 Pat McAfee 参演未来几年最受期待的电影之一：“彻底结束这一切”\n保镖无意中听到顾客离谱的点单。他简直不敢相信自己的耳朵：“不得不把他赶出去”","publish_source":"brobible.com","publish_time":"2026-05-28T21:10:53+00:00"}}];
